(297,1,'Genesis','OT',11,30,'But Sarai was barren; she {had} no child.'),
(298,1,'Genesis','OT',11,31,'And Terah took Abram his son, and Lot the son of Haran his son\'s son, and Sarai his daughter in law, his son Abram\'s wife; and they went forth with them from Ur of the Chaldees, to go into the land of Canaan; and they came unto Haran, and dwelt there.'),
(299,1,'Genesis','OT',11,32,'And the days of Terah were two hundred and five years: and Terah died in Haran.'),
(300,1,'Genesis','OT',12,1,'Now the LORD had said unto Abram, Get thee out of thy country, and from thy kindred, and from thy father\'s house, unto a land that I will shew thee:'),
(301,1,'Genesis','OT',12,2,'And I will make of thee a great nation, and I will bless thee, and make thy name great; and thou shalt be a blessing:'),
(302,1,'Genesis','OT',12,3,'And I will bless them that bless thee, and curse him that curseth thee: and in thee shall all families of the earth be blessed.'),
(303,1,'Genesis','OT',12,4,'So Abram departed, as the LORD had spoken unto him; and Lot went with him: and Abram {was} seventy and five years old when he departed out of Haran.'),
(304,1,'Genesis','OT',12,5,'And Abram took Sarai his wife, and Lot his brother\'s son, and all their substance that they had gathered, and the souls that they had gotten in Haran; and they went forth to go into the land of Canaan; and into the land of Canaan they came.'),
