(327,1,'Genesis','OT',13,8,'And Abram said unto Lot, Let there be no strife, I pray thee, between me and thee, and between my herdmen and thy herdmen; for we {be} brethren. {brethren: Heb. men brethren}'),
(328,1,'Genesis','OT',13,9,'{Is} not the whole land before thee? separate thyself, I pray thee, from me: if {thou wilt take} the left hand, then I will go to the right; or if {thou depart} to the right hand, then I will go to the left.'),
(329,1,'Genesis','OT',13,10,'And Lot lifted up his eyes, and beheld all the plain of Jordan, that it {was} well watered every where, before the LORD destroyed Sodom and Gomorrah, {even} as the garden of the LORD, like the land of Egypt, as thou comest unto Zoar.'),
(330,1,'Genesis','OT',13,11,'Then Lot chose him all the plain of Jordan; and Lot journeyed east: and they separated themselves the one from the other.'),
