(415,1,'Genesis','OT',17,17,'Then Abraham fell upon his face, and laughed, and said in his heart, Shall {a child} be born unto him that is an hundred years old? and shall Sarah, that is ninety years old, bear?'),
(416,1,'Genesis','OT',17,18,'And Abraham said unto God, O that Ishmael might live before thee!'),
(417,1,'Genesis','OT',17,19,'And God said, Sarah thy wife shall bear thee a son indeed; and thou shalt call his name Isaac: and I will establish my covenant with him for an everlasting covenant, {and} with his seed after him.'),
(418,1,'Genesis','OT',17,20,'And as for Ishmael, I have heard thee: Behold, I have blessed him, and will make him fruitful, and will multiply him exceedingly; twelve princes shall he beget, and I will make him a great nation.'),
