(555,1,'Genesis','OT',22,7,'And Isaac spake unto Abraham his father, and said, My father: and he said, Here {am} I, my son. And he said, Behold the fire and the wood: but where {is} the lamb for a burnt offering? {lamb: or, kid}'),
(556,1,'Genesis','OT',22,8,'And Abraham said, My son, God will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering: so they went both of them together.'),
(557,1,'Genesis','OT',22,9,'And they came to the place which God had told him of; and Abraham built an altar there, and laid the wood in order, and bound Isaac his son, and laid him on the altar upon the wood.'),
(558,1,'Genesis','OT',22,10,'And Abraham stretched forth his hand, and took the knife to slay his son.'),
(559,1,'Genesis','OT',22,11,'And the angel of the LORD called unto him out of heaven, and said, Abraham, Abraham: and he said, Here {am} I.'),
(560,1,'Genesis','OT',22,12,'And he said, Lay not thine hand upon the lad, neither do thou any thing unto him: for now I know that thou fearest God, seeing thou hast not withheld thy son, thine only {son} from me.'),
(561,1,'Genesis','OT',22,13,'And Abraham lifted up his eyes, and looked, and behold behind {him} a ram caught in a thicket by his horns: and Abraham went and took the ram, and offered him up for a burnt offering in the stead of his son.'),
(562,1,'Genesis','OT',22,14,'And Abraham called the name of that place Jehovahjireh: as it is said {to} this day, In the mount of the LORD it shall be seen. {Jehovahjireh: that is, The Lord will see, or, provide}'),
(563,1,'Genesis','OT',22,15,'And the angel of the LORD called unto Abraham out of heaven the second time,'),
(564,1,'Genesis','OT',22,16,'And said, By myself have I sworn, saith the LORD, for because thou hast done this thing, and hast not withheld thy son, thine only {son}:'),
(565,1,'Genesis','OT',22,17,'That in blessing I will bless thee, and in multiplying I will multiply thy seed as the stars of the heaven, and as the sand which {is} upon the sea shore; and thy seed shall possess the gate of his enemies; {shore: Heb. lip}'),
(566,1,'Genesis','OT',22,18,'And in thy seed shall all the nations of the earth be blessed; because thou hast obeyed my voice.'),
(567,1,'Genesis','OT',22,19,'So Abraham returned unto his young men, and they rose up and went together to Beersheba; and Abraham dwelt at Beersheba.'),
