(1148,1,'Genesis','OT',38,28,'And it came to pass, when she travailed, that {the one} put out {his} hand: and the midwife took and bound upon his hand a scarlet thread, saying, This came out first.'),
(1149,1,'Genesis','OT',38,29,'And it came to pass, as he drew back his hand, that, behold, his brother came out: and she said, How hast thou broken forth? {this} breach {be} upon thee: therefore his name was called Pharez. {How hast...: or, Wherefore hast thou made this breach against thee?} {Pharez: that is A breach}'),
(1150,1,'Genesis','OT',38,30,'And afterward came out his brother, that had the scarlet thread upon his hand: and his name was called Zarah.'),
