(3659,4,'Numbers','OT',1,54,'And the children of Israel did according to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so did they.'),
(3660,4,'Numbers','OT',2,1,'And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,'),
(3661,4,'Numbers','OT',2,2,'Every man of the children of Israel shall pitch by his own standard, with the ensign of their father\'s house: far off about the tabernacle of the congregation shall they pitch. {far...: Heb. over against}'),
(3662,4,'Numbers','OT',2,3,'And on the east side toward the rising of the sun shall they of the standard of the camp of Judah pitch throughout their armies: and Nahshon the son of Amminadab {shall be} captain of the children of Judah.'),
(3663,4,'Numbers','OT',2,4,'And his host, and those that were numbered of them, {were} threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred.'),
(3664,4,'Numbers','OT',2,5,'And those that do pitch next unto him {shall be} the tribe of Issachar: and Nethaneel the son of Zuar {shall be} captain of the children of Issachar.'),
