(4536,4,'Numbers','OT',26,46,'And the name of the daughter of Asher {was} Sarah.'),
(4537,4,'Numbers','OT',26,47,'These {are} the families of the sons of Asher according to those that were numbered of them; {who were} fifty and three thousand and four hundred.'),
(4538,4,'Numbers','OT',26,48,'{Of} the sons of Naphtali after their families: of Jahzeel, the family of the Jahzeelites: of Guni, the family of the Gunites:'),
(4539,4,'Numbers','OT',26,49,'Of Jezer, the family of the Jezerites: of Shillem, the family of the Shillemites. {Shillem: also called, Shallum}'),
(4540,4,'Numbers','OT',26,50,'These {are} the families of Naphtali according to their families: and they that were numbered of them {were} forty and five thousand and four hundred.'),
(4541,4,'Numbers','OT',26,51,'These {were} the numbered of the children of Israel, six hundred thousand and a thousand seven hundred and thirty.'),
(4542,4,'Numbers','OT',26,52,'And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,'),
(4543,4,'Numbers','OT',26,53,'Unto these the land shall be divided for an inheritance according to the number of names.'),
(4544,4,'Numbers','OT',26,54,'To many thou shalt give the more inheritance, and to few thou shalt give the less inheritance: to every one shall his inheritance be given according to those that were numbered of him. {give the more...: Heb. multiply his inheritance} {give the less...: Heb. diminish his inheritance}'),
(4545,4,'Numbers','OT',26,55,'Notwithstanding the land shall be divided by lot: according to the names of the tribes of their fathers they shall inherit.'),
(4546,4,'Numbers','OT',26,56,'According to the lot shall the possession thereof be divided between many and few.'),
(4547,4,'Numbers','OT',26,57,'And these {are} they that were numbered of the Levites after their families: of Gershon, the family of the Gershonites: of Kohath, the family of the Kohathites: of Merari, the family of the Merarites.'),
(4548,4,'Numbers','OT',26,58,'These {are} the families of the Levites: the family of the Libnites, the family of the Hebronites, the family of the Mahlites, the family of the Mushites, the family of the Korathites. And Kohath begat Amram.'),
(4549,4,'Numbers','OT',26,59,'And the name of Amram\'s wife {was} Jochebed, the daughter of Levi, whom {her mother} bare to Levi in Egypt: and she bare unto Amram Aaron and Moses, and Miriam their sister.'),
(4550,4,'Numbers','OT',26,60,'And unto Aaron was born Nadab, and Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.'),
(4551,4,'Numbers','OT',26,61,'And Nadab and Abihu died, when they offered strange fire before the LORD.'),
(4552,4,'Numbers','OT',26,62,'And those that were numbered of them were twenty and three thousand, all males from a month old and upward: for they were not numbered among the children of Israel, because there was no inheritance given them among the children of Israel.'),
(4553,4,'Numbers','OT',26,63,'These {are} they that were numbered by Moses and Eleazar the priest, who numbered the children of Israel in the plains of Moab by Jordan {near} Jericho.'),
(4554,4,'Numbers','OT',26,64,'But among these there was not a man of them whom Moses and Aaron the priest numbered, when they numbered the children of Israel in the wilderness of Sinai.'),
(4555,4,'Numbers','OT',26,65,'For the LORD had said of them, They shall surely die in the wilderness. And there was not left a man of them, save Caleb the son of Jephunneh, and Joshua the son of Nun.'),
(4556,4,'Numbers','OT',27,1,'Then came the daughters of Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, of the families of Manasseh the son of Joseph: and these {are} the names of his daughters; Mahlah, Noah, and Hoglah, and Milcah, and Tirzah.'),
(4557,4,'Numbers','OT',27,2,'And they stood before Moses, and before Eleazar the priest, and before the princes and all the congregation, {by} the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, saying,'),
(4558,4,'Numbers','OT',27,3,'Our father died in the wilderness, and he was not in the company of them that gathered themselves together against the LORD in the company of Korah; but died in his own sin, and had no sons.'),
(4559,4,'Numbers','OT',27,4,'Why should the name of our father be done away from among his family, because he hath no son? Give unto us {therefore} a possession among the brethren of our father. {done...: Heb. diminished}'),
(4560,4,'Numbers','OT',27,5,'And Moses brought their cause before the LORD.'),
(4561,4,'Numbers','OT',27,6,'And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,'),
(4562,4,'Numbers','OT',27,7,'The daughters of Zelophehad speak right: thou shalt surely give them a possession of an inheritance among their father\'s brethren; and thou shalt cause the inheritance of their father to pass unto them.'),
(4563,4,'Numbers','OT',27,8,'And thou shalt speak unto the children of Israel, saying, If a man die, and have no son, then ye shall cause his inheritance to pass unto his daughter.'),
(4564,4,'Numbers','OT',27,9,'And if he have no daughter, then ye shall give his inheritance unto his brethren.'),
(4565,4,'Numbers','OT',27,10,'And if he have no brethren, then ye shall give his inheritance unto his father\'s brethren.'),
(4566,4,'Numbers','OT',27,11,'And if his father have no brethren, then ye shall give his inheritance unto his kinsman that is next to him of his family, and he shall possess it: and it shall be unto the children of Israel a statute of judgment, as the LORD commanded Moses.'),
(4567,4,'Numbers','OT',27,12,'And the LORD said unto Moses, Get thee up into this mount Abarim, and see the land which I have given unto the children of Israel.'),
(4568,4,'Numbers','OT',27,13,'And when thou hast seen it, thou also shalt be gathered unto thy people, as Aaron thy brother was gathered.'),
(4569,4,'Numbers','OT',27,14,'For ye rebelled against my commandment in the desert of Zin, in the strife of the congregation, to sanctify me at the water before their eyes: that {is} the water of Meribah in Kadesh in the wilderness of Zin.'),
(4570,4,'Numbers','OT',27,15,'And Moses spake unto the LORD, saying,'),
(4571,4,'Numbers','OT',27,16,'Let the LORD, the God of the spirits of all flesh, set a man over the congregation,'),
(4572,4,'Numbers','OT',27,17,'Which may go out before them, and which may go in before them, and which may lead them out, and which may bring them in; that the congregation of the LORD be not as sheep which have no shepherd.'),
(4573,4,'Numbers','OT',27,18,'And the LORD said unto Moses, Take thee Joshua the son of Nun, a man in whom {is} the spirit, and lay thine hand upon him;'),
(4574,4,'Numbers','OT',27,19,'And set him before Eleazar the priest, and before all the congregation; and give him a charge in their sight.'),
(4575,4,'Numbers','OT',27,20,'And thou shalt put {some} of thine honour upon him, that all the congregation of the children of Israel may be obedient.'),
(4576,4,'Numbers','OT',27,21,'And he shall stand before Eleazar the priest, who shall ask {counsel} for him after the judgment of Urim before the LORD: at his word shall they go out, and at his word they shall come in, {both} he, and all the children of Israel with him, even all the congregation.'),
(4577,4,'Numbers','OT',27,22,'And Moses did as the LORD commanded him: and he took Joshua, and set him before Eleazar the priest, and before all the congregation:'),
(4578,4,'Numbers','OT',27,23,'And he laid his hands upon him, and gave him a charge, as the LORD commanded by the hand of Moses.'),
(4579,4,'Numbers','OT',28,1,'And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,'),
(4580,4,'Numbers','OT',28,2,'Command the children of Israel, and say unto them, My offering, {and} my bread for my sacrifices made by fire, {for} a sweet savour unto me, shall ye observe to offer unto me in their due season. {a sweet...: Heb. a savour of my rest}'),
(4581,4,'Numbers','OT',28,3,'And thou shalt say unto them, This {is} the offering made by fire which ye shall offer unto the LORD; two lambs of the first year without spot day by day, {for} a continual burnt offering. {day by day: Heb. in a day}'),
(4582,4,'Numbers','OT',28,4,'The one lamb shalt thou offer in the morning, and the other lamb shalt thou offer at even; {at even: Heb. between the two evenings}'),
(4583,4,'Numbers','OT',28,5,'And a tenth {part} of an ephah of flour for a meat offering, mingled with the fourth {part} of an hin of beaten oil.'),
(4584,4,'Numbers','OT',28,6,'{It is} a continual burnt offering, which was ordained in mount Sinai for a sweet savour, a sacrifice made by fire unto the LORD.'),
(4585,4,'Numbers','OT',28,7,'And the drink offering thereof {shall be} the fourth {part} of an hin for the one lamb: in the holy {place} shalt thou cause the strong wine to be poured unto the LORD {for} a drink offering.'),
(4586,4,'Numbers','OT',28,8,'And the other lamb shalt thou offer at even: as the meat offering of the morning, and as the drink offering thereof, thou shalt offer {it}, a sacrifice made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.'),
(4587,4,'Numbers','OT',28,9,'And on the sabbath day two lambs of the first year without spot, and two tenth deals of flour {for} a meat offering, mingled with oil, and the drink offering thereof:'),
(4588,4,'Numbers','OT',28,10,'{This is} the burnt offering of every sabbath, beside the continual burnt offering, and his drink offering.'),
(4589,4,'Numbers','OT',28,11,'And in the beginnings of your months ye shall offer a burnt offering unto the LORD; two young bullocks, and one ram, seven lambs of the first year without spot;'),
(4590,4,'Numbers','OT',28,12,'And three tenth deals of flour {for} a meat offering, mingled with oil, for one bullock; and two tenth deals of flour {for} a meat offering, mingled with oil, for one ram;'),
(4591,4,'Numbers','OT',28,13,'And a several tenth deal of flour mingled with oil {for} a meat offering unto one lamb; {for} a burnt offering of a sweet savour, a sacrifice made by fire unto the LORD.'),
(4592,4,'Numbers','OT',28,14,'And their drink offerings shall be half an hin of wine unto a bullock, and the third {part} of an hin unto a ram, and a fourth {part} of an hin unto a lamb: this {is} the burnt offering of every month throughout the months of the year.'),
(4593,4,'Numbers','OT',28,15,'And one kid of the goats for a sin offering unto the LORD shall be offered, beside the continual burnt offering, and his drink offering.'),
(4594,4,'Numbers','OT',28,16,'And in the fourteenth day of the first month {is} the passover of the LORD.'),
(4595,4,'Numbers','OT',28,17,'And in the fifteenth day of this month {is} the feast: seven days shall unleavened bread be eaten.'),
(4596,4,'Numbers','OT',28,18,'In the first day {shall be} an holy convocation; ye shall do no manner of servile work {therein}:'),
(4597,4,'Numbers','OT',28,19,'But ye shall offer a sacrifice made by fire {for} a burnt offering unto the LORD; two young bullocks, and one ram, and seven lambs of the first year: they shall be unto you without blemish:'),
(4598,4,'Numbers','OT',28,20,'And their meat offering {shall be of} flour mingled with oil: three tenth deals shall ye offer for a bullock, and two tenth deals for a ram;'),
(4599,4,'Numbers','OT',28,21,'A several tenth deal shalt thou offer for every lamb, throughout the seven lambs:'),
(4600,4,'Numbers','OT',28,22,'And one goat {for} a sin offering, to make an atonement for you.'),
(4601,4,'Numbers','OT',28,23,'Ye shall offer these beside the burnt offering in the morning, which {is} for a continual burnt offering.'),
(4602,4,'Numbers','OT',28,24,'After this manner ye shall offer daily, throughout the seven days, the meat of the sacrifice made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD: it shall be offered beside the continual burnt offering, and his drink offering.'),
(4603,4,'Numbers','OT',28,25,'And on the seventh day ye shall have an holy convocation; ye shall do no servile work.'),
(4604,4,'Numbers','OT',28,26,'Also in the day of the firstfruits, when ye bring a new meat offering unto the LORD, after your weeks {be out}, ye shall have an holy convocation; ye shall do no servile work:'),
(4605,4,'Numbers','OT',28,27,'But ye shall offer the burnt offering for a sweet savour unto the LORD; two young bullocks, one ram, seven lambs of the first year;'),
(4606,4,'Numbers','OT',28,28,'And their meat offering of flour mingled with oil, three tenth deals unto one bullock, two tenth deals unto one ram,'),
(4607,4,'Numbers','OT',28,29,'A several tenth deal unto one lamb, throughout the seven lambs;'),
(4608,4,'Numbers','OT',28,30,'{And} one kid of the goats, to make an atonement for you.'),
(4609,4,'Numbers','OT',28,31,'Ye shall offer {them} beside the continual burnt offering, and his meat offering, (they shall be unto you without blemish) and their drink offerings.'),
(4610,4,'Numbers','OT',29,1,'And in the seventh month, on the first {day} of the month, ye shall have an holy convocation; ye shall do no servile work: it is a day of blowing the trumpets unto you.'),
(4611,4,'Numbers','OT',29,2,'And ye shall offer a burnt offering for a sweet savour unto the LORD; one young bullock, one ram, {and} seven lambs of the first year without blemish:'),
(4612,4,'Numbers','OT',29,3,'And their meat offering {shall be of} flour mingled with oil, three tenth deals for a bullock, {and} two tenth deals for a ram,'),
(4613,4,'Numbers','OT',29,4,'And one tenth deal for one lamb, throughout the seven lambs:'),
(4614,4,'Numbers','OT',29,5,'And one kid of the goats {for} a sin offering, to make an atonement for you:'),
(4615,4,'Numbers','OT',29,6,'Beside the burnt offering of the month, and his meat offering, and the daily burnt offering, and his meat offering, and their drink offerings, according unto their manner, for a sweet savour, a sacrifice made by fire unto the LORD.'),
