(7760,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,29,'And he said, Let me go, I pray thee; for our family hath a sacrifice in the city; and my brother, he hath commanded me {to be there}: and now, if I have found favour in thine eyes, let me get away, I pray thee, and see my brethren. Therefore he cometh not unto the king\'s table.'),
(7761,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,30,'Then Saul\'s anger was kindled against Jonathan, and he said unto him, Thou son of the perverse rebellious {woman}, do not I know that thou hast chosen the son of Jesse to thine own confusion, and unto the confusion of thy mother\'s nakedness? {Thou...: or, Thou perverse rebel: Heb. Son of perverse rebellion}'),
(7762,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,31,'For as long as the son of Jesse liveth upon the ground, thou shalt not be established, nor thy kingdom. Wherefore now send and fetch him unto me, for he shall surely die. {shall...: Heb. is the son of death}'),
(7763,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,32,'And Jonathan answered Saul his father, and said unto him, Wherefore shall he be slain? what hath he done?'),
(7764,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,33,'And Saul cast a javelin at him to smite him: whereby Jonathan knew that it was determined of his father to slay David.'),
(7765,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,34,'So Jonathan arose from the table in fierce anger, and did eat no meat the second day of the month: for he was grieved for David, because his father had done him shame.'),
(7766,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,35,'And it came to pass in the morning, that Jonathan went out into the field at the time appointed with David, and a little lad with him.'),
(7767,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,36,'And he said unto his lad, Run, find out now the arrows which I shoot. {And} as the lad ran, he shot an arrow beyond him. {beyond...: Heb. to pass over him}'),
(7768,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,37,'And when the lad was come to the place of the arrow which Jonathan had shot, Jonathan cried after the lad, and said, {Is} not the arrow beyond thee?'),
(7769,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,38,'And Jonathan cried after the lad, Make speed, haste, stay not. And Jonathan\'s lad gathered up the arrows, and came to his master.'),
(7770,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,39,'But the lad knew not any thing: only Jonathan and David knew the matter.'),
(7771,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,40,'And Jonathan gave his artillery unto his lad, and said unto him, Go, carry {them} to the city. {artillery: Heb. instruments} {his lad: Heb. the lad that was his}'),
(7772,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,41,'{And} as soon as the lad was gone, David arose out of {a place} toward the south, and fell on his face to the ground, and bowed himself three times: and they kissed one another, and wept one with another, until David exceeded.'),
(7773,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,42,'And Jonathan said to David, Go in peace, forasmuch as we have sworn both of us in the name of the LORD, saying, The LORD be between me and thee, and between my seed and thy seed for ever. {forasmuch...: or, the LORD be witness of that which etc}'),
(7774,9,'1 Samuel','OT',20,43,'And he arose and departed: and Jonathan went into the city.'),
(7775,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,1,'Then came David to Nob to Ahimelech the priest: and Ahimelech was afraid at the meeting of David, and said unto him, Why {art} thou alone, and no man with thee? {Ahimelech: also called Ahiah}'),
(7776,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,2,'And David said unto Ahimelech the priest, The king hath commanded me a business, and hath said unto me, Let no man know any thing of the business whereabout I send thee, and what I have commanded thee: and I have appointed {my} servants to such and such a place.'),
(7777,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,3,'Now therefore what is under thine hand? give {me} five {loaves of} bread in mine hand, or what there is present. {present: Heb. found}'),
(7778,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,4,'And the priest answered David, and said, {There is} no common bread under mine hand, but there is hallowed bread; if the young men have kept themselves at least from women.'),
(7779,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,5,'And David answered the priest, and said unto him, Of a truth women {have been} kept from us about these three days, since I came out, and the vessels of the young men are holy, and {the bread is} in a manner common, yea, though it were sanctified this day in the vessel. {yea...: or, especially when this day there is other sanctified in the vessel}'),
(7780,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,6,'So the priest gave him hallowed {bread}: for there was no bread there but the shewbread, that was taken from before the LORD, to put hot bread in the day when it was taken away.'),
(7781,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,7,'Now a certain man of the servants of Saul {was} there that day, detained before the LORD; and his name {was} Doeg, an Edomite, the chiefest of the herdmen that {belonged} to Saul.'),
(7782,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,8,'And David said unto Ahimelech, And is there not here under thine hand spear or sword? for I have neither brought my sword nor my weapons with me, because the king\'s business required haste.'),
(7783,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,9,'And the priest said, The sword of Goliath the Philistine, whom thou slewest in the valley of Elah, behold, it {is here} wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod: if thou wilt take that, take {it}: for {there is} no other save that here. And David said, {There is} none like that; give it me.'),
(7784,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,10,'And David arose, and fled that day for fear of Saul, and went to Achish the king of Gath.'),
(7785,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,11,'And the servants of Achish said unto him, {Is} not this David the king of the land? did they not sing one to another of him in dances, saying, Saul hath slain his thousands, and David his ten thousands?'),
(7786,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,12,'And David laid up these words in his heart, and was sore afraid of Achish the king of Gath.'),
(7787,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,13,'And he changed his behaviour before them, and feigned himself mad in their hands, and scrabbled on the doors of the gate, and let his spittle fall down upon his beard. {scrabbled: or, made marks}'),
(7788,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,14,'Then said Achish unto his servants, Lo, ye see the man is mad: wherefore {then} have ye brought him to me? {is mad: or, playeth the mad man}'),
(7789,9,'1 Samuel','OT',21,15,'Have I need of mad men, that ye have brought this {fellow} to play the mad man in my presence? shall this {fellow} come into my house?'),
(7790,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,1,'David therefore departed thence, and escaped to the cave Adullam: and when his brethren and all his father\'s house heard {it}, they went down thither to him.'),
(7791,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,2,'And every one {that was} in distress, and every one that {was} in debt, and every one {that was} discontented, gathered themselves unto him; and he became a captain over them: and there were with him about four hundred men. {was in debt: Heb. had a creditor} {discontented: Heb. bitter of soul}'),
(7792,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,3,'And David went thence to Mizpeh of Moab: and he said unto the king of Moab, Let my father and my mother, I pray thee, come forth, {and be} with you, till I know what God will do for me.'),
(7793,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,4,'And he brought them before the king of Moab: and they dwelt with him all the while that David was in the hold.'),
(7794,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,5,'And the prophet Gad said unto David, Abide not in the hold; depart, and get thee into the land of Judah. Then David departed, and came into the forest of Hareth.'),
(7795,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,6,'When Saul heard that David was discovered, and the men that {were} with him, (now Saul abode in Gibeah under a tree in Ramah, having his spear in his hand, and all his servants {were} standing about him;) {tree...: or, grove in a high place}'),
(7796,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,7,'Then Saul said unto his servants that stood about him, Hear now, ye Benjamites; will the son of Jesse give every one of you fields and vineyards, {and} make you all captains of thousands, and captains of hundreds;'),
(7797,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,8,'That all of you have conspired against me, and {there is} none that sheweth me that my son hath made a league with the son of Jesse, and {there is} none of you that is sorry for me, or sheweth unto me that my son hath stirred up my servant against me, to lie in wait, as at this day? {sheweth...: Heb. uncovereth mine ear}'),
(7798,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,9,'Then answered Doeg the Edomite, which was set over the servants of Saul, and said, I saw the son of Jesse coming to Nob, to Ahimelech the son of Ahitub.'),
(7799,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,10,'And he enquired of the LORD for him, and gave him victuals, and gave him the sword of Goliath the Philistine.'),
(7800,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,11,'Then the king sent to call Ahimelech the priest, the son of Ahitub, and all his father\'s house, the priests that {were} in Nob: and they came all of them to the king.'),
(7801,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,12,'And Saul said, Hear now, thou son of Ahitub. And he answered, Here I {am}, my lord. {Here...: Heb. Behold me}'),
(7802,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,13,'And Saul said unto him, Why have ye conspired against me, thou and the son of Jesse, in that thou hast given him bread, and a sword, and hast enquired of God for him, that he should rise against me, to lie in wait, as at this day?'),
(7803,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,14,'Then Ahimelech answered the king, and said, And who {is so} faithful among all thy servants as David, which is the king\'s son in law, and goeth at thy bidding, and is honourable in thine house?'),
(7804,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,15,'Did I then begin to enquire of God for him? be it far from me: let not the king impute {any} thing unto his servant, {nor} to all the house of my father: for thy servant knew nothing of all this, less or more. {less...: Heb. little or great}'),
(7805,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,16,'And the king said, Thou shalt surely die, Ahimelech, thou, and all thy father\'s house.'),
(7806,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,17,'And the king said unto the footmen that stood about him, Turn, and slay the priests of the LORD; because their hand also {is} with David, and because they knew when he fled, and did not shew it to me. But the servants of the king would not put forth their hand to fall upon the priests of the LORD. {footmen: or, guard: Heb. runners}'),
(7807,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,18,'And the king said to Doeg, Turn thou, and fall upon the priests. And Doeg the Edomite turned, and he fell upon the priests, and slew on that day fourscore and five persons that did wear a linen ephod.'),
(7808,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,19,'And Nob, the city of the priests, smote he with the edge of the sword, both men and women, children and sucklings, and oxen, and asses, and sheep, with the edge of the sword.'),
(7809,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,20,'And one of the sons of Ahimelech the son of Ahitub, named Abiathar, escaped, and fled after David.'),
(7810,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,21,'And Abiathar shewed David that Saul had slain the LORD\'S priests.'),
(7811,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,22,'And David said unto Abiathar, I knew {it} that day, when Doeg the Edomite {was} there, that he would surely tell Saul: I have occasioned {the death} of all the persons of thy father\'s house.'),
(7812,9,'1 Samuel','OT',22,23,'Abide thou with me, fear not: for he that seeketh my life seeketh thy life: but with me thou {shalt be} in safeguard.'),
(7813,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,1,'Then they told David, saying, Behold, the Philistines fight against Keilah, and they rob the threshingfloors.'),
(7814,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,2,'Therefore David enquired of the LORD, saying, Shall I go and smite these Philistines? And the LORD said unto David, Go, and smite the Philistines, and save Keilah.'),
(7815,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,3,'And David\'s men said unto him, Behold, we be afraid here in Judah: how much more then if we come to Keilah against the armies of the Philistines?'),
(7816,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,4,'Then David enquired of the LORD yet again. And the LORD answered him and said, Arise, go down to Keilah; for I will deliver the Philistines into thine hand.'),
(7817,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,5,'So David and his men went to Keilah, and fought with the Philistines, and brought away their cattle, and smote them with a great slaughter. So David saved the inhabitants of Keilah.'),
(7818,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,6,'And it came to pass, when Abiathar the son of Ahimelech fled to David to Keilah, {that} he came down {with} an ephod in his hand.'),
(7819,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,7,'And it was told Saul that David was come to Keilah. And Saul said, God hath delivered him into mine hand; for he is shut in, by entering into a town that hath gates and bars.'),
(7820,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,8,'And Saul called all the people together to war, to go down to Keilah, to besiege David and his men.'),
(7821,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,9,'And David knew that Saul secretly practised mischief against him; and he said to Abiathar the priest, Bring hither the ephod.'),
(7822,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,10,'Then said David, O LORD God of Israel, thy servant hath certainly heard that Saul seeketh to come to Keilah, to destroy the city for my sake.'),
(7823,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,11,'Will the men of Keilah deliver me up into his hand? will Saul come down, as thy servant hath heard? O LORD God of Israel, I beseech thee, tell thy servant. And the LORD said, He will come down.'),
(7824,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,12,'Then said David, Will the men of Keilah deliver me and my men into the hand of Saul? And the LORD said, They will deliver {thee} up. {deliver: Heb. shut up}'),
(7825,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,13,'Then David and his men, {which were} about six hundred, arose and departed out of Keilah, and went whithersoever they could go. And it was told Saul that David was escaped from Keilah; and he forbare to go forth.'),
(7826,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,14,'And David abode in the wilderness in strong holds, and remained in a mountain in the wilderness of Ziph. And Saul sought him every day, but God delivered him not into his hand.'),
(7827,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,15,'And David saw that Saul was come out to seek his life: and David {was} in the wilderness of Ziph in a wood.'),
(7828,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,16,'And Jonathan Saul\'s son arose, and went to David into the wood, and strengthened his hand in God.'),
(7829,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,17,'And he said unto him, Fear not: for the hand of Saul my father shall not find thee; and thou shalt be king over Israel, and I shall be next unto thee; and that also Saul my father knoweth.'),
(7830,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,18,'And they two made a covenant before the LORD: and David abode in the wood, and Jonathan went to his house.'),
(7831,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,19,'Then came up the Ziphites to Saul to Gibeah, saying, Doth not David hide himself with us in strong holds in the wood, in the hill of Hachilah, which {is} on the south of Jeshimon? {on...: Heb. on the right hand} {Jeshimon: or, the wilderness}'),
(7832,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,20,'Now therefore, O king, come down according to all the desire of thy soul to come down; and our part {shall be} to deliver him into the king\'s hand.'),
(7833,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,21,'And Saul said, Blessed {be} ye of the LORD; for ye have compassion on me.'),
(7834,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,22,'Go, I pray you, prepare yet, and know and see his place where his haunt is, {and} who hath seen him there: for it is told me {that} he dealeth very subtilly. {haunt...: Heb. foot shall be}'),
(7835,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,23,'See therefore, and take knowledge of all the lurking places where he hideth himself, and come ye again to me with the certainty, and I will go with you: and it shall come to pass, if he be in the land, that I will search him out throughout all the thousands of Judah.'),
(7836,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,24,'And they arose, and went to Ziph before Saul: but David and his men {were} in the wilderness of Maon, in the plain on the south of Jeshimon.'),
(7837,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,25,'Saul also and his men went to seek {him}. And they told David: wherefore he came down into a rock, and abode in the wilderness of Maon. And when Saul heard {that}, he pursued after David in the wilderness of Maon. {into...: or, from the rock}'),
(7838,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,26,'And Saul went on this side of the mountain, and David and his men on that side of the mountain: and David made haste to get away for fear of Saul; for Saul and his men compassed David and his men round about to take them.'),
(7839,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,27,'But there came a messenger unto Saul, saying, Haste thee, and come; for the Philistines have invaded the land. {invaded...: Heb. spread themselves upon, etc}'),
(7840,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,28,'Wherefore Saul returned from pursuing after David, and went against the Philistines: therefore they called that place Selahammahlekoth. {Selahammahlekoth: that is, The rock of divisions}'),
(7841,9,'1 Samuel','OT',23,29,'And David went up from thence, and dwelt in strong holds at Engedi.'),
(7842,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,1,'And it came to pass, when Saul was returned from following the Philistines, that it was told him, saying, Behold, David {is} in the wilderness of Engedi. {following: Heb. after}'),
(7843,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,2,'Then Saul took three thousand chosen men out of all Israel, and went to seek David and his men upon the rocks of the wild goats.'),
(7844,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,3,'And he came to the sheepcotes by the way, where {was} a cave; and Saul went in to cover his feet: and David and his men remained in the sides of the cave.'),
(7845,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,4,'And the men of David said unto him, Behold the day of which the LORD said unto thee, Behold, I will deliver thine enemy into thine hand, that thou mayest do to him as it shall seem good unto thee. Then David arose, and cut off the skirt of Saul\'s robe privily. {Saul\'s...: Heb. the robe which was Saul\'s}'),
(7846,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,5,'And it came to pass afterward, that David\'s heart smote him, because he had cut off Saul\'s skirt.'),
(7847,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,6,'And he said unto his men, The LORD forbid that I should do this thing unto my master, the LORD\'S anointed, to stretch forth mine hand against him, seeing he {is} the anointed of the LORD.'),
(7848,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,7,'So David stayed his servants with these words, and suffered them not to rise against Saul. But Saul rose up out of the cave, and went on {his} way. {stayed: Heb. cut off}'),
(7849,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,8,'David also arose afterward, and went out of the cave, and cried after Saul, saying, My lord the king. And when Saul looked behind him, David stooped with his face to the earth, and bowed himself.'),
(7850,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,9,'And David said to Saul, Wherefore hearest thou men\'s words, saying, Behold, David seeketh thy hurt?'),
(7851,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,10,'Behold, this day thine eyes have seen how that the LORD had delivered thee to day into mine hand in the cave: and {some} bade {me} kill thee: but {mine eye} spared thee; and I said, I will not put forth mine hand against my lord; for he {is} the LORD\'S anointed.'),
(7852,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,11,'Moreover, my father, see, yea, see the skirt of thy robe in my hand: for in that I cut off the skirt of thy robe, and killed thee not, know thou and see that {there is} neither evil nor transgression in mine hand, and I have not sinned against thee; yet thou huntest my soul to take it.'),
(7853,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,12,'The LORD judge between me and thee, and the LORD avenge me of thee: but mine hand shall not be upon thee.'),
(7854,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,13,'As saith the proverb of the ancients, Wickedness proceedeth from the wicked: but mine hand shall not be upon thee.'),
(7855,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,14,'After whom is the king of Israel come out? after whom dost thou pursue? after a dead dog, after a flea.'),
(7856,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,15,'The LORD therefore be judge, and judge between me and thee, and see, and plead my cause, and deliver me out of thine hand. {deliver: Heb. judge}'),
(7857,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,16,'And it came to pass, when David had made an end of speaking these words unto Saul, that Saul said, {Is} this thy voice, my son David? And Saul lifted up his voice, and wept.'),
(7858,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,17,'And he said to David, Thou {art} more righteous than I: for thou hast rewarded me good, whereas I have rewarded thee evil.'),
(7859,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,18,'And thou hast shewed this day how that thou hast dealt well with me: forasmuch as when the LORD had delivered me into thine hand, thou killedst me not. {delivered: Heb. shut up}'),
(7860,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,19,'For if a man find his enemy, will he let him go well away? wherefore the LORD reward thee good for that thou hast done unto me this day.'),
(7861,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,20,'And now, behold, I know well that thou shalt surely be king, and that the kingdom of Israel shall be established in thine hand.'),
(7862,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,21,'Swear now therefore unto me by the LORD, that thou wilt not cut off my seed after me, and that thou wilt not destroy my name out of my father\'s house.'),
(7863,9,'1 Samuel','OT',24,22,'And David sware unto Saul. And Saul went home; but David and his men gat them up unto the hold.'),
(7864,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,1,'And Samuel died; and all the Israelites were gathered together, and lamented him, and buried him in his house at Ramah. And David arose, and went down to the wilderness of Paran.'),
(7865,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,2,'And {there was} a man in Maon, whose possessions {were} in Carmel; and the man {was} very great, and he had three thousand sheep, and a thousand goats: and he was shearing his sheep in Carmel. {possessions: or, business}'),
(7866,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,3,'Now the name of the man {was} Nabal; and the name of his wife Abigail: and {she was} a woman of good understanding, and of a beautiful countenance: but the man {was} churlish and evil in his doings; and he {was} of the house of Caleb.'),
(7867,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,4,'And David heard in the wilderness that Nabal did shear his sheep.'),
(7868,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,5,'And David sent out ten young men, and David said unto the young men, Get you up to Carmel, and go to Nabal, and greet him in my name: {greet...: Heb. ask him in my name of peace}'),
(7869,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,6,'And thus shall ye say to him that liveth {in prosperity}, Peace {be} both to thee, and peace {be} to thine house, and peace {be} unto all that thou hast.'),
(7870,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,7,'And now I have heard that thou hast shearers: now thy shepherds which were with us, we hurt them not, neither was there ought missing unto them, all the while they were in Carmel. {hurt: Heb. shamed}'),
(7871,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,8,'Ask thy young men, and they will shew thee. Wherefore let the young men find favour in thine eyes: for we come in a good day: give, I pray thee, whatsoever cometh to thine hand unto thy servants, and to thy son David.'),
(7872,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,9,'And when David\'s young men came, they spake to Nabal according to all those words in the name of David, and ceased. {ceased: Heb. rested}'),
(7873,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,10,'And Nabal answered David\'s servants, and said, Who {is} David? and who {is} the son of Jesse? there be many servants now a days that break away every man from his master.'),
(7874,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,11,'Shall I then take my bread, and my water, and my flesh that I have killed for my shearers, and give {it} unto men, whom I know not whence they {be}? {flesh: Heb. slaughter}'),
(7875,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,12,'So David\'s young men turned their way, and went again, and came and told him all those sayings.'),
(7876,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,13,'And David said unto his men, Gird ye on every man his sword. And they girded on every man his sword; and David also girded on his sword: and there went up after David about four hundred men; and two hundred abode by the stuff.'),
(7877,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,14,'But one of the young men told Abigail, Nabal\'s wife, saying, Behold, David sent messengers out of the wilderness to salute our master; and he railed on them. {railed...: Heb. flew upon them}'),
(7878,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,15,'But the men {were} very good unto us, and we were not hurt, neither missed we any thing, as long as we were conversant with them, when we were in the fields: {hurt: Heb. shamed}'),
(7879,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,16,'They were a wall unto us both by night and day, all the while we were with them keeping the sheep.'),
(7880,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,17,'Now therefore know and consider what thou wilt do; for evil is determined against our master, and against all his household: for he {is such} a son of Belial, that {a man} cannot speak to him.'),
(7881,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,18,'Then Abigail made haste, and took two hundred loaves, and two bottles of wine, and five sheep ready dressed, and five measures of parched {corn}, and an hundred clusters of raisins, and two hundred cakes of figs, and laid {them} on asses. {clusters: or, lumps}'),
(7882,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,19,'And she said unto her servants, Go on before me; behold, I come after you. But she told not her husband Nabal.'),
(7883,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,20,'And it was {so, as} she rode on the ass, that she came down by the covert of the hill, and, behold, David and his men came down against her; and she met them.'),
(7884,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,21,'Now David had said, Surely in vain have I kept all that this {fellow} hath in the wilderness, so that nothing was missed of all that {pertained} unto him: and he hath requited me evil for good.'),
(7885,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,22,'So and more also do God unto the enemies of David, if I leave of all that {pertain} to him by the morning light any that pisseth against the wall.'),
(7886,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,23,'And when Abigail saw David, she hasted, and lighted off the ass, and fell before David on her face, and bowed herself to the ground,'),
(7887,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,24,'And fell at his feet, and said, Upon me, my lord, {upon} me {let this} iniquity {be}: and let thine handmaid, I pray thee, speak in thine audience, and hear the words of thine handmaid. {audience: Heb. ears}'),
(7888,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,25,'Let not my lord, I pray thee, regard this man of Belial, {even} Nabal: for as his name {is}, so {is} he; Nabal {is} his name, and folly {is} with him: but I thine handmaid saw not the young men of my lord, whom thou didst send. {regard: Heb. lay it to his heart} {Nabal: that is, Fool}'),
(7889,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,26,'Now therefore, my lord, {as} the LORD liveth, and {as} thy soul liveth, seeing the LORD hath withholden thee from coming to {shed} blood, and from avenging thyself with thine own hand, now let thine enemies, and they that seek evil to my lord, be as Nabal. {avenging...: Heb. saving thyself}'),
(7890,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,27,'And now this blessing which thine handmaid hath brought unto my lord, let it even be given unto the young men that follow my lord. {blessing: or, present} {follow...: Heb. walk at the feet of, etc}'),
(7891,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,28,'I pray thee, forgive the trespass of thine handmaid: for the LORD will certainly make my lord a sure house; because my lord fighteth the battles of the LORD, and evil hath not been found in thee {all} thy days.'),
(7892,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,29,'Yet a man is risen to pursue thee, and to seek thy soul: but the soul of my lord shall be bound in the bundle of life with the LORD thy God; and the souls of thine enemies, them shall he sling out, {as out} of the middle of a sling. {as out...: Heb. in the midst of the bought of a sling}'),
(7893,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,30,'And it shall come to pass, when the LORD shall have done to my lord according to all the good that he hath spoken concerning thee, and shall have appointed thee ruler over Israel;'),
(7894,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,31,'That this shall be no grief unto thee, nor offence of heart unto my lord, either that thou hast shed blood causeless, or that my lord hath avenged himself: but when the LORD shall have dealt well with my lord, then remember thine handmaid. {no grief: Heb. no staggering, or, stumbling}'),
(7895,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,32,'And David said to Abigail, Blessed {be} the LORD God of Israel, which sent thee this day to meet me:'),
(7896,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,33,'And blessed {be} thy advice, and blessed {be} thou, which hast kept me this day from coming to {shed} blood, and from avenging myself with mine own hand.'),
(7897,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,34,'For in very deed, {as} the LORD God of Israel liveth, which hath kept me back from hurting thee, except thou hadst hasted and come to meet me, surely there had not been left unto Nabal by the morning light any that pisseth against the wall.'),
(7898,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,35,'So David received of her hand {that} which she had brought him, and said unto her, Go up in peace to thine house; see, I have hearkened to thy voice, and have accepted thy person.'),
(7899,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,36,'And Abigail came to Nabal; and, behold, he held a feast in his house, like the feast of a king; and Nabal\'s heart {was} merry within him, for he {was} very drunken: wherefore she told him nothing, less or more, until the morning light.'),
(7900,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,37,'But it came to pass in the morning, when the wine was gone out of Nabal, and his wife had told him these things, that his heart died within him, and he became {as} a stone.'),
(7901,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,38,'And it came to pass about ten days {after}, that the LORD smote Nabal, that he died.'),
(7902,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,39,'And when David heard that Nabal was dead, he said, Blessed {be} the LORD, that hath pleaded the cause of my reproach from the hand of Nabal, and hath kept his servant from evil: for the LORD hath returned the wickedness of Nabal upon his own head. And David sent and communed with Abigail, to take her to him to wife.'),
(7903,9,'1 Samuel','OT',25,40,'And when the servants of David were come to Abigail to Carmel, they spake unto her, saying, David sent us unto thee, to take thee to him to wife.'),
