(7918,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,11,'The LORD forbid that I should stretch forth mine hand against the LORD\'S anointed: but, I pray thee, take thou now the spear that {is} at his bolster, and the cruse of water, and let us go.'),
(7919,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,12,'So David took the spear and the cruse of water from Saul\'s bolster; and they gat them away, and no man saw {it}, nor knew {it}, neither awaked: for they {were} all asleep; because a deep sleep from the LORD was fallen upon them.'),
