(7921,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,14,'And David cried to the people, and to Abner the son of Ner, saying, Answerest thou not, Abner? Then Abner answered and said, Who {art} thou {that} criest to the king?'),
(7922,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,15,'And David said to Abner, {Art} not thou a {valiant} man? and who {is} like to thee in Israel? wherefore then hast thou not kept thy lord the king? for there came one of the people in to destroy the king thy lord.'),
(7923,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,16,'This thing {is} not good that thou hast done. {As} the LORD liveth, ye {are} worthy to die, because ye have not kept your master, the LORD\'S anointed. And now see where the king\'s spear {is}, and the cruse of water that {was} at his bolster. {worthy to die: Heb. the sons of death}'),
(7924,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,17,'And Saul knew David\'s voice, and said, {Is} this thy voice, my son David? And David said, {It is} my voice, my lord, O king.'),
(7925,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,18,'And he said, Wherefore doth my lord thus pursue after his servant? for what have I done? or what evil {is} in mine hand?'),
(7926,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,19,'Now therefore, I pray thee, let my lord the king hear the words of his servant. If the LORD have stirred thee up against me, let him accept an offering: but if {they be} the children of men, cursed {be} they before the LORD; for they have driven me out this day from abiding in the inheritance of the LORD, saying, Go, serve other gods. {accept: Heb. smell} {abiding: Heb. cleaving}'),
(7927,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,20,'Now therefore, let not my blood fall to the earth before the face of the LORD: for the king of Israel is come out to seek a flea, as when one doth hunt a partridge in the mountains.'),
(7928,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,21,'Then said Saul, I have sinned: return, my son David: for I will no more do thee harm, because my soul was precious in thine eyes this day: behold, I have played the fool, and have erred exceedingly.'),
(7929,9,'1 Samuel','OT',26,22,'And David answered and said, Behold the king\'s spear! and let one of the young men come over and fetch it.'),
