(8022,9,'1 Samuel','OT',31,11,'And when the inhabitants of Jabeshgilead heard of that which the Philistines had done to Saul; {of that: or, concerning him that}'),
(8023,9,'1 Samuel','OT',31,12,'All the valiant men arose, and went all night, and took the body of Saul and the bodies of his sons from the wall of Bethshan, and came to Jabesh, and burnt them there.'),
(8024,9,'1 Samuel','OT',31,13,'And they took their bones, and buried {them} under a tree at Jabesh, and fasted seven days.'),
(8025,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,1,'Now it came to pass after the death of Saul, when David was returned from the slaughter of the Amalekites, and David had abode two days in Ziklag;'),
(8026,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,2,'It came even to pass on the third day, that, behold, a man came out of the camp from Saul with his clothes rent, and earth upon his head: and {so} it was, when he came to David, that he fell to the earth, and did obeisance.'),
(8027,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,3,'And David said unto him, From whence comest thou? And he said unto him, Out of the camp of Israel am I escaped.'),
(8028,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,4,'And David said unto him, How went the matter? I pray thee, tell me. And he answered, That the people are fled from the battle, and many of the people also are fallen and dead; and Saul and Jonathan his son are dead also. {How...: Heb. What was, etc}'),
(8029,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,5,'And David said unto the young man that told him, How knowest thou that Saul and Jonathan his son be dead?'),
(8030,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,6,'And the young man that told him said, As I happened by chance upon mount Gilboa, behold, Saul leaned upon his spear; and, lo, the chariots and horsemen followed hard after him.'),
(8031,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,7,'And when he looked behind him, he saw me, and called unto me. And I answered, Here {am} I. {Here...: Heb. Behold me}'),
(8032,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,8,'And he said unto me, Who {art} thou? And I answered him, I {am} an Amalekite.'),
(8033,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,9,'He said unto me again, Stand, I pray thee, upon me, and slay me: for anguish is come upon me, because my life {is} yet whole in me. {anguish...: or, my coat of mail (or, my embroidered coat) hindereth me, that my, etc}'),
(8034,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,10,'So I stood upon him, and slew him, because I was sure that he could not live after that he was fallen: and I took the crown that {was} upon his head, and the bracelet that {was} on his arm, and have brought them hither unto my lord.'),
(8035,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,11,'Then David took hold on his clothes, and rent them; and likewise all the men that {were} with him:'),
(8036,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,12,'And they mourned, and wept, and fasted until even, for Saul, and for Jonathan his son, and for the people of the LORD, and for the house of Israel; because they were fallen by the sword.'),
(8037,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,13,'And David said unto the young man that told him, Whence {art} thou? And he answered, I {am} the son of a stranger, an Amalekite.'),
(8038,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,14,'And David said unto him, How wast thou not afraid to stretch forth thine hand to destroy the LORD\'S anointed?'),
(8039,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,15,'And David called one of the young men, and said, Go near, {and} fall upon him. And he smote him that he died.'),
(8040,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,16,'And David said unto him, Thy blood {be} upon thy head; for thy mouth hath testified against thee, saying, I have slain the LORD\'S anointed.'),
(8041,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,17,'And David lamented with this lamentation over Saul and over Jonathan his son:'),
(8042,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,18,'(Also he bade them teach the children of Judah {the use of} the bow: behold, {it is} written in the book of Jasher.) {of Jasher: or, of the upright}'),
(8043,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,19,'The beauty of Israel is slain upon thy high places: how are the mighty fallen!'),
(8044,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,20,'Tell {it} not in Gath, publish {it} not in the streets of Askelon; lest the daughters of the Philistines rejoice, lest the daughters of the uncircumcised triumph.'),
(8045,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,21,'Ye mountains of Gilboa, {let there be} no dew, neither {let there be} rain, upon you, nor fields of offerings: for there the shield of the mighty is vilely cast away, the shield of Saul, {as though he had} not {been} anointed with oil.'),
(8046,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,22,'From the blood of the slain, from the fat of the mighty, the bow of Jonathan turned not back, and the sword of Saul returned not empty.'),
(8047,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,23,'Saul and Jonathan {were} lovely and pleasant in their lives, and in their death they were not divided: they were swifter than eagles, they were stronger than lions. {pleasant: or, sweet}'),
(8048,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,24,'Ye daughters of Israel, weep over Saul, who clothed you in scarlet, with {other} delights, who put on ornaments of gold upon your apparel.'),
(8049,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,25,'How are the mighty fallen in the midst of the battle! O Jonathan, {thou wast} slain in thine high places.'),
(8050,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,26,'I am distressed for thee, my brother Jonathan: very pleasant hast thou been unto me: thy love to me was wonderful, passing the love of women.'),
(8051,10,'2 Samuel','OT',1,27,'How are the mighty fallen, and the weapons of war perished!'),
(8052,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,1,'And it came to pass after this, that David enquired of the LORD, saying, Shall I go up into any of the cities of Judah? And the LORD said unto him, Go up. And David said, Whither shall I go up? And he said, Unto Hebron.'),
(8053,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,2,'So David went up thither, and his two wives also, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail Nabal\'s wife the Carmelite.'),
(8054,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,3,'And his men that {were} with him did David bring up, every man with his household: and they dwelt in the cities of Hebron.'),
(8055,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,4,'And the men of Judah came, and there they anointed David king over the house of Judah. And they told David, saying, {That} the men of Jabeshgilead {were they} that buried Saul.'),
(8056,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,5,'And David sent messengers unto the men of Jabeshgilead, and said unto them, Blessed {be} ye of the LORD, that ye have shewed this kindness unto your lord, {even} unto Saul, and have buried him.'),
(8057,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,6,'And now the LORD shew kindness and truth unto you: and I also will requite you this kindness, because ye have done this thing.'),
(8058,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,7,'Therefore now let your hands be strengthened, and be ye valiant: for your master Saul is dead, and also the house of Judah have anointed me king over them. {be ye...: Heb. be ye the sons of valour}'),
(8059,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,8,'But Abner the son of Ner, captain of Saul\'s host, took Ishbosheth the son of Saul, and brought him over to Mahanaim; {Saul\'s host: Heb. the host which was Saul\'s} {Ishbosheth: or, Eshbaal}'),
(8060,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,9,'And made him king over Gilead, and over the Ashurites, and over Jezreel, and over Ephraim, and over Benjamin, and over all Israel.'),
(8061,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,10,'Ishbosheth Saul\'s son {was} forty years old when he began to reign over Israel, and reigned two years. But the house of Judah followed David.'),
(8062,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,11,'And the time that David was king in Hebron over the house of Judah was seven years and six months. {time: Heb. number of days}'),
(8063,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,12,'And Abner the son of Ner, and the servants of Ishbosheth the son of Saul, went out from Mahanaim to Gibeon.'),
(8064,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,13,'And Joab the son of Zeruiah, and the servants of David, went out, and met together by the pool of Gibeon: and they sat down, the one on the one side of the pool, and the other on the other side of the pool. {together: Heb. them together}'),
(8065,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,14,'And Abner said to Joab, Let the young men now arise, and play before us. And Joab said, Let them arise.'),
(8066,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,15,'Then there arose and went over by number twelve of Benjamin, which {pertained} to Ishbosheth the son of Saul, and twelve of the servants of David.'),
(8067,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,16,'And they caught every one his fellow by the head, and {thrust} his sword in his fellow\'s side; so they fell down together: wherefore that place was called Helkathhazzurim, which {is} in Gibeon. {Helkathhazzurim: that is, The field of strong men}'),
(8068,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,17,'And there was a very sore battle that day; and Abner was beaten, and the men of Israel, before the servants of David.'),
(8069,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,18,'And there were three sons of Zeruiah there, Joab, and Abishai, and Asahel: and Asahel {was as} light of foot as a wild roe. {of foot: Heb. of his feet} {as a wild...: Heb. as one of the roes that is in the field}'),
(8070,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,19,'And Asahel pursued after Abner; and in going he turned not to the right hand nor to the left from following Abner. {from...: Heb. from after Abner}'),
(8071,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,20,'Then Abner looked behind him, and said, {Art} thou Asahel? And he answered, I {am}.'),
(8072,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,21,'And Abner said to him, Turn thee aside to thy right hand or to thy left, and lay thee hold on one of the young men, and take thee his armour. But Asahel would not turn aside from following of him. {armour: or, spoil}'),
(8073,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,22,'And Abner said again to Asahel, Turn thee aside from following me: wherefore should I smite thee to the ground? how then should I hold up my face to Joab thy brother?'),
(8074,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,23,'Howbeit he refused to turn aside: wherefore Abner with the hinder end of the spear smote him under the fifth {rib}, that the spear came out behind him; and he fell down there, and died in the same place: and it came to pass, {that} as many as came to the place where Asahel fell down and died stood still.'),
(8075,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,24,'Joab also and Abishai pursued after Abner: and the sun went down when they were come to the hill of Ammah, that {lieth} before Giah by the way of the wilderness of Gibeon.'),
(8076,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,25,'And the children of Benjamin gathered themselves together after Abner, and became one troop, and stood on the top of an hill.'),
(8077,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,26,'Then Abner called to Joab, and said, Shall the sword devour for ever? knowest thou not that it will be bitterness in the latter end? how long shall it be then, ere thou bid the people return from following their brethren?'),
(8078,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,27,'And Joab said, {As} God liveth, unless thou hadst spoken, surely then in the morning the people had gone up every one from following his brother. {in the...: Heb. from the morning} {gone...: or, gone away}'),
(8079,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,28,'So Joab blew a trumpet, and all the people stood still, and pursued after Israel no more, neither fought they any more.'),
(8080,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,29,'And Abner and his men walked all that night through the plain, and passed over Jordan, and went through all Bithron, and they came to Mahanaim.'),
(8081,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,30,'And Joab returned from following Abner: and when he had gathered all the people together, there lacked of David\'s servants nineteen men and Asahel.'),
