(8083,10,'2 Samuel','OT',2,32,'And they took up Asahel, and buried him in the sepulchre of his father, which {was in} Bethlehem. And Joab and his men went all night, and they came to Hebron at break of day.'),
(8084,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,1,'Now there was long war between the house of Saul and the house of David: but David waxed stronger and stronger, and the house of Saul waxed weaker and weaker.'),
(8085,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,2,'And unto David were sons born in Hebron: and his firstborn was Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess;'),
(8086,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,3,'And his second, Chileab, of Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite; and the third, Absalom the son of Maacah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur; {Chileab: or, Daniel}'),
(8087,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,4,'And the fourth, Adonijah the son of Haggith; and the fifth, Shephatiah the son of Abital;'),
(8088,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,5,'And the sixth, Ithream, by Eglah David\'s wife. These were born to David in Hebron.'),
(8089,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,6,'And it came to pass, while there was war between the house of Saul and the house of David, that Abner made himself strong for the house of Saul.'),
(8090,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,7,'And Saul had a concubine, whose name {was} Rizpah, the daughter of Aiah: and {Ishbosheth} said to Abner, Wherefore hast thou gone in unto my father\'s concubine?'),
(8091,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,8,'Then was Abner very wroth for the words of Ishbosheth, and said, {Am} I a dog\'s head, which against Judah do shew kindness this day unto the house of Saul thy father, to his brethren, and to his friends, and have not delivered thee into the hand of David, that thou chargest me to day with a fault concerning this woman?'),
(8092,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,9,'So do God to Abner, and more also, except, as the LORD hath sworn to David, even so I do to him;'),
(8093,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,10,'To translate the kingdom from the house of Saul, and to set up the throne of David over Israel and over Judah, from Dan even to Beersheba.'),
(8094,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,11,'And he could not answer Abner a word again, because he feared him.'),
(8095,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,12,'And Abner sent messengers to David on his behalf, saying, Whose {is} the land? saying {also}, Make thy league with me, and, behold, my hand {shall be} with thee, to bring about all Israel unto thee.'),
(8096,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,13,'And he said, Well; I will make a league with thee: but one thing I require of thee, that is, Thou shalt not see my face, except thou first bring Michal Saul\'s daughter, when thou comest to see my face. {that is: Heb. saying}'),
(8097,10,'2 Samuel','OT',3,14,'And David sent messengers to Ishbosheth Saul\'s son, saying, Deliver {me} my wife Michal, which I espoused to me for an hundred foreskins of the Philistines.'),
