(9350,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,7,'And as Obadiah was in the way, behold, Elijah met him: and he knew him, and fell on his face, and said, {Art} thou that my lord Elijah?'),
(9351,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,8,'And he answered him, I {am}: go, tell thy lord, Behold, Elijah {is here}.'),
(9352,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,9,'And he said, What have I sinned, that thou wouldest deliver thy servant into the hand of Ahab, to slay me?'),
(9353,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,10,'{As} the LORD thy God liveth, there is no nation or kingdom, whither my lord hath not sent to seek thee: and when they said, {He is} not {there}; he took an oath of the kingdom and nation, that they found thee not.'),
(9354,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,11,'And now thou sayest, Go, tell thy lord, Behold, Elijah {is here}.'),
(9355,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,12,'And it shall come to pass, {as soon as} I am gone from thee, that the Spirit of the LORD shall carry thee whither I know not; and {so} when I come and tell Ahab, and he cannot find thee, he shall slay me: but I thy servant fear the LORD from my youth.'),
(9356,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,13,'Was it not told my lord what I did when Jezebel slew the prophets of the LORD, how I hid an hundred men of the LORD\'S prophets by fifty in a cave, and fed them with bread and water?'),
(9357,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,14,'And now thou sayest, Go, tell thy lord, Behold, Elijah {is here}: and he shall slay me.'),
(9358,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,15,'And Elijah said, {As} the LORD of hosts liveth, before whom I stand, I will surely shew myself unto him to day.'),
(9359,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,16,'So Obadiah went to meet Ahab, and told him: and Ahab went to meet Elijah.'),
(9360,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,17,'And it came to pass, when Ahab saw Elijah, that Ahab said unto him, {Art} thou he that troubleth Israel?'),
(9361,11,'1 Kings','OT',18,18,'And he answered, I have not troubled Israel; but thou, and thy father\'s house, in that ye have forsaken the commandments of the LORD, and thou hast followed Baalim.'),
