(9414,11,'1 Kings','OT',20,4,'And the king of Israel answered and said, My lord, O king, according to thy saying, I {am} thine, and all that I have.'),
(9415,11,'1 Kings','OT',20,5,'And the messengers came again, and said, Thus speaketh Benhadad, saying, Although I have sent unto thee, saying, Thou shalt deliver me thy silver, and thy gold, and thy wives, and thy children;'),
(9416,11,'1 Kings','OT',20,6,'Yet I will send my servants unto thee to morrow about this time, and they shall search thine house, and the houses of thy servants; and it shall be, {that} whatsoever is pleasant in thine eyes, they shall put {it} in their hand, and take {it} away. {pleasant: Heb. desirable}'),
(9417,11,'1 Kings','OT',20,7,'Then the king of Israel called all the elders of the land, and said, Mark, I pray you, and see how this {man} seeketh mischief: for he sent unto me for my wives, and for my children, and for my silver, and for my gold; and I denied him not. {I denied...: Heb. I kept not back from him}'),
(9418,11,'1 Kings','OT',20,8,'And all the elders and all the people said unto him, Hearken not {unto him}, nor consent.'),
(9419,11,'1 Kings','OT',20,9,'Wherefore he said unto the messengers of Benhadad, Tell my lord the king, All that thou didst send for to thy servant at the first I will do: but this thing I may not do. And the messengers departed, and brought him word again.'),
(9420,11,'1 Kings','OT',20,10,'And Benhadad sent unto him, and said, The gods do so unto me, and more also, if the dust of Samaria shall suffice for handfuls for all the people that follow me. {follow...: Heb. are at my feet}'),
