(9453,11,'1 Kings','OT',20,43,'And the king of Israel went to his house heavy and displeased, and came to Samaria.'),
(9454,11,'1 Kings','OT',21,1,'And it came to pass after these things, {that} Naboth the Jezreelite had a vineyard, which {was} in Jezreel, hard by the palace of Ahab king of Samaria.'),
(9455,11,'1 Kings','OT',21,2,'And Ahab spake unto Naboth, saying, Give me thy vineyard, that I may have it for a garden of herbs, because it {is} near unto my house: and I will give thee for it a better vineyard than it; {or}, if it seem good to thee, I will give thee the worth of it in money. {seem...: Heb. be good in thine eyes}'),
