(12575,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,23,'Hoshea, Hananiah, Hashub,'),
(12576,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,24,'Hallohesh, Pileha, Shobek,'),
(12577,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,25,'Rehum, Hashabnah, Maaseiah,'),
(12578,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,26,'And Ahijah, Hanan, Anan,'),
(12579,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,27,'Malluch, Harim, Baanah.'),
(12580,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,28,'And the rest of the people, the priests, the Levites, the porters, the singers, the Nethinims, and all they that had separated themselves from the people of the lands unto the law of God, their wives, their sons, and their daughters, every one having knowledge, and having understanding;'),
(12581,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,29,'They clave to their brethren, their nobles, and entered into a curse, and into an oath, to walk in God\'s law, which was given by Moses the servant of God, and to observe and do all the commandments of the LORD our Lord, and his judgments and his statutes; {by: Heb. by the hand of}'),
(12582,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,30,'And that we would not give our daughters unto the people of the land, nor take their daughters for our sons:'),
(12583,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,31,'And {if} the people of the land bring ware or any victuals on the sabbath day to sell, {that} we would not buy it of them on the sabbath, or on the holy day: and {that} we would leave the seventh year, and the exaction of every debt. {every...: Heb. every hand}'),
(12584,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,32,'Also we made ordinances for us, to charge ourselves yearly with the third part of a shekel for the service of the house of our God;'),
(12585,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,33,'For the shewbread, and for the continual meat offering, and for the continual burnt offering, of the sabbaths, of the new moons, for the set feasts, and for the holy {things}, and for the sin offerings to make an atonement for Israel, and {for} all the work of the house of our God.'),
(12586,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,34,'And we cast the lots among the priests, the Levites, and the people, for the wood offering, to bring {it} into the house of our God, after the houses of our fathers, at times appointed year by year, to burn upon the altar of the LORD our God, as {it is} written in the law:'),
(12587,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,35,'And to bring the firstfruits of our ground, and the firstfruits of all fruit of all trees, year by year, unto the house of the LORD:'),
(12588,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,36,'Also the firstborn of our sons, and of our cattle, as {it is} written in the law, and the firstlings of our herds and of our flocks, to bring to the house of our God, unto the priests that minister in the house of our God:'),
(12589,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,37,'And {that} we should bring the firstfruits of our dough, and our offerings, and the fruit of all manner of trees, of wine and of oil, unto the priests, to the chambers of the house of our God; and the tithes of our ground unto the Levites, that the same Levites might have the tithes in all the cities of our tillage.'),
(12590,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,38,'And the priest the son of Aaron shall be with the Levites, when the Levites take tithes: and the Levites shall bring up the tithe of the tithes unto the house of our God, to the chambers, into the treasure house.'),
(12591,16,'Nehemiah','OT',10,39,'For the children of Israel and the children of Levi shall bring the offering of the corn, of the new wine, and the oil, unto the chambers, where {are} the vessels of the sanctuary, and the priests that minister, and the porters, and the singers: and we will not forsake the house of our God.'),
(12592,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,1,'And the rulers of the people dwelt at Jerusalem: the rest of the people also cast lots, to bring one of ten to dwell in Jerusalem the holy city, and nine parts {to dwell} in {other} cities.'),
(12593,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,2,'And the people blessed all the men, that willingly offered themselves to dwell at Jerusalem.'),
(12594,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,3,'Now these {are} the chief of the province that dwelt in Jerusalem: but in the cities of Judah dwelt every one in his possession in their cities, {to wit}, Israel, the priests, and the Levites, and the Nethinims, and the children of Solomon\'s servants.'),
(12595,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,4,'And at Jerusalem dwelt {certain} of the children of Judah, and of the children of Benjamin. Of the children of Judah; Athaiah the son of Uzziah, the son of Zechariah, the son of Amariah, the son of Shephatiah, the son of Mahalaleel, of the children of Perez; {Perez: also called, Pharez}'),
(12596,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,5,'And Maaseiah the son of Baruch, the son of Colhozeh, the son of Hazaiah, the son of Adaiah, the son of Joiarib, the son of Zechariah, the son of Shiloni.'),
(12597,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,6,'All the sons of Perez that dwelt at Jerusalem {were} four hundred threescore and eight valiant men.'),
(12598,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,7,'And these {are} the sons of Benjamin; Sallu the son of Meshullam, the son of Joed, the son of Pedaiah, the son of Kolaiah, the son of Maaseiah, the son of Ithiel, the son of Jesaiah.'),
(12599,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,8,'And after him Gabbai, Sallai, nine hundred twenty and eight.'),
(12600,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,9,'And Joel the son of Zichri {was} their overseer: and Judah the son of Senuah {was} second over the city.'),
(12601,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,10,'Of the priests: Jedaiah the son of Joiarib, Jachin.'),
(12602,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,11,'Seraiah the son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, {was} the ruler of the house of God.'),
(12603,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,12,'And their brethren that did the work of the house {were} eight hundred twenty and two: and Adaiah the son of Jeroham, the son of Pelaliah, the son of Amzi, the son of Zechariah, the son of Pashur, the son of Malchiah,'),
(12604,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,13,'And his brethren, chief of the fathers, two hundred forty and two: and Amashai the son of Azareel, the son of Ahasai, the son of Meshillemoth, the son of Immer,'),
(12605,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,14,'And their brethren, mighty men of valour, an hundred twenty and eight: and their overseer {was} Zabdiel, the son of {one of} the great men. {the son...: or, the son of Haggedolim}'),
(12606,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,15,'Also of the Levites: Shemaiah the son of Hashub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Bunni;'),
(12607,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,16,'And Shabbethai and Jozabad, of the chief of the Levites, {had} the oversight of the outward business of the house of God. {had...: Heb. were over}'),
(12608,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,17,'And Mattaniah the son of Micha, the son of Zabdi, the son of Asaph, {was} the principal to begin the thanksgiving in prayer: and Bakbukiah the second among his brethren, and Abda the son of Shammua, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun.'),
(12609,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,18,'All the Levites in the holy city {were} two hundred fourscore and four.'),
(12610,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,19,'Moreover the porters, Akkub, Talmon, and their brethren that kept the gates, {were} an hundred seventy and two. {the gates: Heb. at the gates}'),
(12611,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,20,'And the residue of Israel, of the priests, {and} the Levites, {were} in all the cities of Judah, every one in his inheritance.'),
(12612,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,21,'But the Nethinims dwelt in Ophel: and Ziha and Gispa {were} over the Nethinims. {Ophel: or, the tower}'),
(12613,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,22,'The overseer also of the Levites at Jerusalem {was} Uzzi the son of Bani, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Micha. Of the sons of Asaph, the singers {were} over the business of the house of God.'),
(12614,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,23,'For {it was} the king\'s commandment concerning them, that a certain portion should be for the singers, due for every day. {a certain...: or, a sure ordinance}'),
(12615,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,24,'And Pethahiah the son of Meshezabeel, of the children of Zerah the son of Judah, {was} at the king\'s hand in all matters concerning the people. {Zerah: also called, Zarah}'),
(12616,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,25,'And for the villages, with their fields, {some} of the children of Judah dwelt at Kirjatharba, and {in} the villages thereof, and at Dibon, and {in} the villages thereof, and at Jekabzeel, and {in} the villages thereof,'),
(12617,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,26,'And at Jeshua, and at Moladah, and at Bethphelet,'),
(12618,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,27,'And at Hazarshual, and at Beersheba, and {in} the villages thereof,'),
(12619,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,28,'And at Ziklag, and at Mekonah, and in the villages thereof,'),
(12620,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,29,'And at Enrimmon, and at Zareah, and at Jarmuth,'),
(12621,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,30,'Zanoah, Adullam, and {in} their villages, at Lachish, and the fields thereof, at Azekah, and {in} the villages thereof. And they dwelt from Beersheba unto the valley of Hinnom.'),
(12622,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,31,'The children also of Benjamin from Geba {dwelt} at Michmash, and Aija, and Bethel, and {in} their villages, {from: or, of} {at: or, to}'),
(12623,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,32,'{And} at Anathoth, Nob, Ananiah,'),
(12624,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,33,'Hazor, Ramah, Gittaim,'),
(12625,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,34,'Hadid, Zeboim, Neballat,'),
(12626,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,35,'Lod, and Ono, the valley of craftsmen.'),
(12627,16,'Nehemiah','OT',11,36,'And of the Levites {were} divisions {in} Judah, {and} in Benjamin.'),
(12628,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,1,'Now these {are} the priests and the Levites that went up with Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua: Seraiah, Jeremiah, Ezra,'),
(12629,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,2,'Amariah, Malluch, Hattush, {Malluch: also called, Melicu}'),
(12630,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,3,'Shechaniah, Rehum, Meremoth, {Shechaniah: also called, Shebaniah} {Rehum: also called, Harim} {Meremoth: also called, Meraioth}'),
(12631,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,4,'Iddo, Ginnetho, Abijah, {Ginnetho: also called, Ginnethon}'),
(12632,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,5,'Miamin, Maadiah, Bilgah, {Miamin: also called, Miniamin} {Maadiah: also called, Moadiah}'),
(12633,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,6,'Shemaiah, and Joiarib, Jedaiah,'),
(12634,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,7,'Sallu, Amok, Hilkiah, Jedaiah. These {were} the chief of the priests and of their brethren in the days of Jeshua. {Sallu: also called, Sallai}'),
(12635,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,8,'Moreover the Levites: Jeshua, Binnui, Kadmiel, Sherebiah, Judah, {and} Mattaniah, {which was} over the thanksgiving, he and his brethren. {the thanksgiving: that is, the psalms of thanksgiving}'),
(12636,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,9,'Also Bakbukiah and Unni, their brethren, {were} over against them in the watches.'),
(12637,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,10,'And Jeshua begat Joiakim, Joiakim also begat Eliashib, and Eliashib begat Joiada,'),
(12638,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,11,'And Joiada begat Jonathan, and Jonathan begat Jaddua.'),
(12639,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,12,'And in the days of Joiakim were priests, the chief of the fathers: of Seraiah, Meraiah; of Jeremiah, Hananiah;'),
(12640,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,13,'Of Ezra, Meshullam; of Amariah, Jehohanan;'),
(12641,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,14,'Of Melicu, Jonathan; of Shebaniah, Joseph;'),
(12642,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,15,'Of Harim, Adna; of Meraioth, Helkai;'),
(12643,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,16,'Of Iddo, Zechariah; of Ginnethon, Meshullam;'),
(12644,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,17,'Of Abijah, Zichri; of Miniamin, of Moadiah, Piltai;'),
(12645,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,18,'Of Bilgah, Shammua; of Shemaiah, Jehonathan;'),
(12646,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,19,'And of Joiarib, Mattenai; of Jedaiah, Uzzi;'),
(12647,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,20,'Of Sallai, Kallai; of Amok, Eber;'),
(12648,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,21,'Of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; of Jedaiah, Nethaneel.'),
(12649,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,22,'The Levites in the days of Eliashib, Joiada, and Johanan, and Jaddua, {were} recorded chief of the fathers: also the priests, to the reign of Darius the Persian.'),
(12650,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,23,'The sons of Levi, the chief of the fathers, {were} written in the book of the chronicles, even until the days of Johanan the son of Eliashib.'),
(12651,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,24,'And the chief of the Levites: Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua the son of Kadmiel, with their brethren over against them, to praise {and} to give thanks, according to the commandment of David the man of God, ward over against ward.'),
(12652,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,25,'Mattaniah, and Bakbukiah, Obadiah, Meshullam, Talmon, Akkub, {were} porters keeping the ward at the thresholds of the gates. {thresholds: or, treasuries, or, assemblies}'),
(12653,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,26,'These {were} in the days of Joiakim the son of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and in the days of Nehemiah the governor, and of Ezra the priest, the scribe.'),
(12654,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,27,'And at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem they sought the Levites out of all their places, to bring them to Jerusalem, to keep the dedication with gladness, both with thanksgivings, and with singing, {with} cymbals, psalteries, and with harps.'),
(12655,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,28,'And the sons of the singers gathered themselves together, both out of the plain country round about Jerusalem, and from the villages of Netophathi;'),
(12656,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,29,'Also from the house of Gilgal, and out of the fields of Geba and Azmaveth: for the singers had builded them villages round about Jerusalem.'),
(12657,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,30,'And the priests and the Levites purified themselves, and purified the people, and the gates, and the wall.'),
(12658,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,31,'Then I brought up the princes of Judah upon the wall, and appointed two great {companies of them that gave} thanks, {whereof one} went on the right hand upon the wall toward the dung gate:'),
(12659,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,32,'And after them went Hoshaiah, and half of the princes of Judah,'),
(12660,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,33,'And Azariah, Ezra, and Meshullam,'),
(12661,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,34,'Judah, and Benjamin, and Shemaiah, and Jeremiah,'),
(12662,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,35,'And {certain} of the priests\' sons with trumpets; {namely}, Zechariah the son of Jonathan, the son of Shemaiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Michaiah, the son of Zaccur, the son of Asaph:'),
(12663,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,36,'And his brethren, Shemaiah, and Azarael, Milalai, Gilalai, Maai, Nethaneel, and Judah, Hanani, with the musical instruments of David the man of God, and Ezra the scribe before them.'),
(12664,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,37,'And at the fountain gate, which was over against them, they went up by the stairs of the city of David, at the going up of the wall, above the house of David, even unto the water gate eastward.'),
(12665,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,38,'And the other {company of them that gave} thanks went over against {them}, and I after them, and the half of the people upon the wall, from beyond the tower of the furnaces even unto the broad wall;'),
(12666,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,39,'And from above the gate of Ephraim, and above the old gate, and above the fish gate, and the tower of Hananeel, and the tower of Meah, even unto the sheep gate: and they stood still in the prison gate.'),
(12667,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,40,'So stood the two {companies of them that gave} thanks in the house of God, and I, and the half of the rulers with me:'),
(12668,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,41,'And the priests; Eliakim, Maaseiah, Miniamin, Michaiah, Elioenai, Zechariah, {and} Hananiah, with trumpets;'),
(12669,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,42,'And Maaseiah, and Shemaiah, and Eleazar, and Uzzi, and Jehohanan, and Malchijah, and Elam, and Ezer. And the singers sang loud, with Jezrahiah {their} overseer. {sang...: Heb. made their voice to be heard}'),
(12670,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,43,'Also that day they offered great sacrifices, and rejoiced: for God had made them rejoice with great joy: the wives also and the children rejoiced: so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard even afar off.'),
(12671,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,44,'And at that time were some appointed over the chambers for the treasures, for the offerings, for the firstfruits, and for the tithes, to gather into them out of the fields of the cities the portions of the law for the priests and Levites: for Judah rejoiced for the priests and for the Levites that waited. {of the law: that is, appointed by the law} {for Judah...: Heb. for the joy of Judah} {waited: Heb. stood}'),
(12672,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,45,'And both the singers and the porters kept the ward of their God, and the ward of the purification, according to the commandment of David, {and} of Solomon his son.'),
(12673,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,46,'For in the days of David and Asaph of old {there were} chief of the singers, and songs of praise and thanksgiving unto God.'),
(12674,16,'Nehemiah','OT',12,47,'And all Israel in the days of Zerubbabel, and in the days of Nehemiah, gave the portions of the singers and the porters, every day his portion: and they sanctified {holy things} unto the Levites; and the Levites sanctified {them} unto the children of Aaron. {sanctified: that is, set apart}'),
(12675,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,1,'On that day they read in the book of Moses in the audience of the people; and therein was found written, that the Ammonite and the Moabite should not come into the congregation of God for ever; {they...: Heb. there was read} {audience: Heb. ears}'),
(12676,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,2,'Because they met not the children of Israel with bread and with water, but hired Balaam against them, that he should curse them: howbeit our God turned the curse into a blessing.'),
(12677,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,3,'Now it came to pass, when they had heard the law, that they separated from Israel all the mixed multitude.'),
(12678,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,4,'And before this, Eliashib the priest, having the oversight of the chamber of the house of our God, {was} allied unto Tobiah: {having...: Heb. being set over}'),
(12679,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,5,'And he had prepared for him a great chamber, where aforetime they laid the meat offerings, the frankincense, and the vessels, and the tithes of the corn, the new wine, and the oil, which was commanded {to be given} to the Levites, and the singers, and the porters; and the offerings of the priests. {which...: Heb. the commandment of the Levites}'),
(12680,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,6,'But in all this {time} was not I at Jerusalem: for in the two and thirtieth year of Artaxerxes king of Babylon came I unto the king, and after certain days obtained I leave of the king: {after...: Heb. at the end of days} {obtained...: or, I earnestly requested}'),
(12681,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,7,'And I came to Jerusalem, and understood of the evil that Eliashib did for Tobiah, in preparing him a chamber in the courts of the house of God.'),
(12682,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,8,'And it grieved me sore: therefore I cast forth all the household stuff of Tobiah out of the chamber.'),
(12683,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,9,'Then I commanded, and they cleansed the chambers: and thither brought I again the vessels of the house of God, with the meat offering and the frankincense.'),
(12684,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,10,'And I perceived that the portions of the Levites had not been given {them}: for the Levites and the singers, that did the work, were fled every one to his field.'),
(12685,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,11,'Then contended I with the rulers, and said, Why is the house of God forsaken? And I gathered them together, and set them in their place. {place: Heb. standing}'),
(12686,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,12,'Then brought all Judah the tithe of the corn and the new wine and the oil unto the treasuries. {treasuries: or, storehouses}'),
(12687,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,13,'And I made treasurers over the treasuries, Shelemiah the priest, and Zadok the scribe, and of the Levites, Pedaiah: and next to them {was} Hanan the son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah: for they were counted faithful, and their office {was} to distribute unto their brethren. {treasuries: or, storehouses} {next...: Heb. at their hand} {their office...: Heb. it was upon them}'),
(12688,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,14,'Remember me, O my God, concerning this, and wipe not out my good deeds that I have done for the house of my God, and for the offices thereof. {good...: Heb. kindnesses} {offices: or, observations}'),
(12689,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,15,'In those days saw I in Judah {some} treading wine presses on the sabbath, and bringing in sheaves, and lading asses; as also wine, grapes, and figs, and all {manner of} burdens, which they brought into Jerusalem on the sabbath day: and I testified {against them} in the day wherein they sold victuals.'),
(12690,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,16,'There dwelt men of Tyre also therein, which brought fish, and all manner of ware, and sold on the sabbath unto the children of Judah, and in Jerusalem.'),
(12691,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,17,'Then I contended with the nobles of Judah, and said unto them, What evil thing {is} this that ye do, and profane the sabbath day?'),
(12692,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,18,'Did not your fathers thus, and did not our God bring all this evil upon us, and upon this city? yet ye bring more wrath upon Israel by profaning the sabbath.'),
(12693,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,19,'And it came to pass, that when the gates of Jerusalem began to be dark before the sabbath, I commanded that the gates should be shut, and charged that they should not be opened till after the sabbath: and {some} of my servants set I at the gates, {that} there should no burden be brought in on the sabbath day.'),
(12694,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,20,'So the merchants and sellers of all kind of ware lodged without Jerusalem once or twice.'),
(12695,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,21,'Then I testified against them, and said unto them, Why lodge ye about the wall? if ye do {so} again, I will lay hands on you. From that time forth came they no {more} on the sabbath. {about: Heb. before}'),
(12696,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,22,'And I commanded the Levites that they should cleanse themselves, and {that} they should come {and} keep the gates, to sanctify the sabbath day. Remember me, O my God, {concerning} this also, and spare me according to the greatness of thy mercy. {greatness: or, multitude}'),
(12697,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,23,'In those days also saw I Jews {that} had married wives of Ashdod, of Ammon, {and} of Moab: {had...: Heb. had made to dwell with them}'),
(12698,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,24,'And their children spake half in the speech of Ashdod, and could not speak in the Jews\' language, but according to the language of each people. {could...: Heb. they discerned not to speak} {of each...: Heb. of people and people}'),
(12699,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,25,'And I contended with them, and cursed them, and smote certain of them, and plucked off their hair, and made them swear by God, {saying}, Ye shall not give your daughters unto their sons, nor take their daughters unto your sons, or for yourselves. {cursed: or, reviled}'),
(12700,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,26,'Did not Solomon king of Israel sin by these things? yet among many nations was there no king like him, who was beloved of his God, and God made him king over all Israel: nevertheless even him did outlandish women cause to sin.'),
(12701,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,27,'Shall we then hearken unto you to do all this great evil, to transgress against our God in marrying strange wives?'),
(12702,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,28,'And {one} of the sons of Joiada, the son of Eliashib the high priest, {was} son in law to Sanballat the Horonite: therefore I chased him from me.'),
(12703,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,29,'Remember them, O my God, because they have defiled the priesthood, and the covenant of the priesthood, and of the Levites. {because...: Heb. for the defilings}'),
(12704,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,30,'Thus cleansed I them from all strangers, and appointed the wards of the priests and the Levites, every one in his business;'),
(12705,16,'Nehemiah','OT',13,31,'And for the wood offering, at times appointed, and for the firstfruits. Remember me, O my God, for good.'),
(12706,17,'Esther','OT',1,1,'Now it came to pass in the days of Ahasuerus, (this {is} Ahasuerus which reigned, from India even unto Ethiopia, {over} an hundred and seven and twenty provinces:)'),
(12707,17,'Esther','OT',1,2,'{That} in those days, when the king Ahasuerus sat on the throne of his kingdom, which {was} in Shushan the palace,'),
(12708,17,'Esther','OT',1,3,'In the third year of his reign, he made a feast unto all his princes and his servants; the power of Persia and Media, the nobles and princes of the provinces, {being} before him:'),
(12709,17,'Esther','OT',1,4,'When he shewed the riches of his glorious kingdom and the honour of his excellent majesty many days, {even} an hundred and fourscore days.'),
(12710,17,'Esther','OT',1,5,'And when these days were expired, the king made a feast unto all the people that were present in Shushan the palace, both unto great and small, seven days, in the court of the garden of the king\'s palace; {present: Heb. found}'),
(12711,17,'Esther','OT',1,6,'{Where were} white, green, and blue, {hangings}, fastened with cords of fine linen and purple to silver rings and pillars of marble: the beds {were of} gold and silver, upon a pavement of red, and blue, and white, and black, marble. {blue, hangings: or, violet, etc} {of red...: or, of porphyre, and marble and alabaster, and stone of blue colour}'),
(12712,17,'Esther','OT',1,7,'And they gave {them} drink in vessels of gold, (the vessels being diverse one from another,) and royal wine in abundance, according to the state of the king. {royal...: Heb. wine of the kingdom} {state: Heb. hand}'),
(12713,17,'Esther','OT',1,8,'And the drinking {was} according to the law; none did compel: for so the king had appointed to all the officers of his house, that they should do according to every man\'s pleasure.'),
(12714,17,'Esther','OT',1,9,'Also Vashti the queen made a feast for the women {in} the royal house which {belonged} to king Ahasuerus.'),
(12715,17,'Esther','OT',1,10,'On the seventh day, when the heart of the king was merry with wine, he commanded Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, and Abagtha, Zethar, and Carcas, the seven chamberlains that served in the presence of Ahasuerus the king, {chamberlains: or, eunuchs}'),
(12716,17,'Esther','OT',1,11,'To bring Vashti the queen before the king with the crown royal, to shew the people and the princes her beauty: for she {was} fair to look on. {fair...: Heb. good of countenance}'),
(12717,17,'Esther','OT',1,12,'But the queen Vashti refused to come at the king\'s commandment by {his} chamberlains: therefore was the king very wroth, and his anger burned in him. {by his...: Heb. which was by the hand of his eunuchs}'),
(12718,17,'Esther','OT',1,13,'Then the king said to the wise men, which knew the times, (for so {was} the king\'s manner toward all that knew law and judgment:'),
(12719,17,'Esther','OT',1,14,'And the next unto him {was} Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, {and} Memucan, the seven princes of Persia and Media, which saw the king\'s face, {and} which sat the first in the kingdom;)'),
(12720,17,'Esther','OT',1,15,'What shall we do unto the queen Vashti according to law, because she hath not performed the commandment of the king Ahasuerus by the chamberlains? {What...: Heb. What to do}'),
(12721,17,'Esther','OT',1,16,'And Memucan answered before the king and the princes, Vashti the queen hath not done wrong to the king only, but also to all the princes, and to all the people that {are} in all the provinces of the king Ahasuerus.'),
(12722,17,'Esther','OT',1,17,'For {this} deed of the queen shall come abroad unto all women, so that they shall despise their husbands in their eyes, when it shall be reported, The king Ahasuerus commanded Vashti the queen to be brought in before him, but she came not.'),
(12723,17,'Esther','OT',1,18,'{Likewise} shall the ladies of Persia and Media say this day unto all the king\'s princes, which have heard of the deed of the queen. Thus {shall there arise} too much contempt and wrath.'),
(12724,17,'Esther','OT',1,19,'If it please the king, let there go a royal commandment from him, and let it be written among the laws of the Persians and the Medes, that it be not altered, That Vashti come no more before king Ahasuerus; and let the king give her royal estate unto another that is better than she. {If it...: Heb. If it be good with the king} {unto...: Heb. unto her companion} {from him: Heb. from before him} {be not...: Heb. pass not away}'),
(12725,17,'Esther','OT',1,20,'And when the king\'s decree which he shall make shall be published throughout all his empire, (for it is great,) all the wives shall give to their husbands honour, both to great and small.'),
(12726,17,'Esther','OT',1,21,'And the saying pleased the king and the princes; and the king did according to the word of Memucan: {pleased...: Heb. was good in the eyes of the king}'),
(12727,17,'Esther','OT',1,22,'For he sent letters into all the king\'s provinces, into every province according to the writing thereof, and to every people after their language, that every man should bear rule in his own house, and that {it} should be published according to the language of every people. {that it...: Heb. that one should publish it according to the language of his people}'),
(12728,17,'Esther','OT',2,1,'After these things, when the wrath of king Ahasuerus was appeased, he remembered Vashti, and what she had done, and what was decreed against her.'),
(12729,17,'Esther','OT',2,2,'Then said the king\'s servants that ministered unto him, Let there be fair young virgins sought for the king:'),
(12730,17,'Esther','OT',2,3,'And let the king appoint officers in all the provinces of his kingdom, that they may gather together all the fair young virgins unto Shushan the palace, to the house of the women, unto the custody of Hege the king\'s chamberlain, keeper of the women; and let their things for purification be given {them}: {unto the...: Heb. unto the hand} {Hege: also called, Hegai}'),
(12731,17,'Esther','OT',2,4,'And let the maiden which pleaseth the king be queen instead of Vashti. And the thing pleased the king; and he did so.'),
(12732,17,'Esther','OT',2,5,'{Now} in Shushan the palace there was a certain Jew, whose name {was} Mordecai, the son of Jair, the son of Shimei, the son of Kish, a Benjamite;'),
(12733,17,'Esther','OT',2,6,'Who had been carried away from Jerusalem with the captivity which had been carried away with Jeconiah king of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away. {Jeconiah: also called, Jehoiachin}'),
(12734,17,'Esther','OT',2,7,'And he brought up Hadassah, that {is}, Esther, his uncle\'s daughter: for she had neither father nor mother, and the maid {was} fair and beautiful; whom Mordecai, when her father and mother were dead, took for his own daughter. {brought...: Heb. nourished} {fair...: Heb. fair of form, and good of countenance}'),
(12735,17,'Esther','OT',2,8,'So it came to pass, when the king\'s commandment and his decree was heard, and when many maidens were gathered together unto Shushan the palace, to the custody of Hegai, that Esther was brought also unto the king\'s house, to the custody of Hegai, keeper of the women.'),
(12736,17,'Esther','OT',2,9,'And the maiden pleased him, and she obtained kindness of him; and he speedily gave her her things for purification, with such things as belonged to her, and seven maidens, {which were} meet to be given her, out of the king\'s house: and he preferred her and her maids unto the best {place} of the house of the women. {such...: Heb. her portions} {preferred: Heb. changed}'),
(12737,17,'Esther','OT',2,10,'Esther had not shewed her people nor her kindred: for Mordecai had charged her that she should not shew {it}.'),
(12738,17,'Esther','OT',2,11,'And Mordecai walked every day before the court of the women\'s house, to know how Esther did, and what should become of her. {to know...: Heb. to know the peace}'),
(12739,17,'Esther','OT',2,12,'Now when every maid\'s turn was come to go in to king Ahasuerus, after that she had been twelve months, according to the manner of the women, (for so were the days of their purifications accomplished, {to wit}, six months with oil of myrrh, and six months with sweet odours, and with {other} things for the purifying of the women;)'),
(12740,17,'Esther','OT',2,13,'Then thus came {every} maiden unto the king; whatsoever she desired was given her to go with her out of the house of the women unto the king\'s house.'),
(12741,17,'Esther','OT',2,14,'In the evening she went, and on the morrow she returned into the second house of the women, to the custody of Shaashgaz, the king\'s chamberlain, which kept the concubines: she came in unto the king no more, except the king delighted in her, and that she were called by name.'),
(12742,17,'Esther','OT',2,15,'Now when the turn of Esther, the daughter of Abihail the uncle of Mordecai, who had taken her for his daughter, was come to go in unto the king, she required nothing but what Hegai the king\'s chamberlain, the keeper of the women, appointed. And Esther obtained favour in the sight of all them that looked upon her.'),
(12743,17,'Esther','OT',2,16,'So Esther was taken unto king Ahasuerus into his house royal in the tenth month, which {is} the month Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign.'),
(12744,17,'Esther','OT',2,17,'And the king loved Esther above all the women, and she obtained grace and favour in his sight more than all the virgins; so that he set the royal crown upon her head, and made her queen instead of Vashti. {favour: or, kindness} {in his...: Heb. before him}'),
(12745,17,'Esther','OT',2,18,'Then the king made a great feast unto all his princes and his servants, {even} Esther\'s feast; and he made a release to the provinces, and gave gifts, according to the state of the king. {release: Heb. rest}'),
(12746,17,'Esther','OT',2,19,'And when the virgins were gathered together the second time, then Mordecai sat in the king\'s gate.'),
(12747,17,'Esther','OT',2,20,'Esther had not {yet} shewed her kindred nor her people; as Mordecai had charged her: for Esther did the commandment of Mordecai, like as when she was brought up with him.'),
(12748,17,'Esther','OT',2,21,'In those days, while Mordecai sat in the king\'s gate, two of the king\'s chamberlains, Bigthan and Teresh, of those which kept the door, were wroth, and sought to lay hand on the king Ahasuerus. {Bigthan: also called, Bigthana} {the door: Heb. the threshold}'),
(12749,17,'Esther','OT',2,22,'And the thing was known to Mordecai, who told {it} unto Esther the queen; and Esther certified the king {thereof} in Mordecai\'s name.'),
(12750,17,'Esther','OT',2,23,'And when inquisition was made of the matter, it was found out; therefore they were both hanged on a tree: and it was written in the book of the chronicles before the king.'),
(12751,17,'Esther','OT',3,1,'After these things did king Ahasuerus promote Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, and advanced him, and set his seat above all the princes that {were} with him.'),
(12752,17,'Esther','OT',3,2,'And all the king\'s servants, that {were} in the king\'s gate, bowed, and reverenced Haman: for the king had so commanded concerning him. But Mordecai bowed not, nor did {him} reverence.'),
(12753,17,'Esther','OT',3,3,'Then the king\'s servants, which {were} in the king\'s gate, said unto Mordecai, Why transgressest thou the king\'s commandment?'),
(12754,17,'Esther','OT',3,4,'Now it came to pass, when they spake daily unto him, and he hearkened not unto them, that they told Haman, to see whether Mordecai\'s matters would stand: for he had told them that he {was} a Jew.'),
(12755,17,'Esther','OT',3,5,'And when Haman saw that Mordecai bowed not, nor did him reverence, then was Haman full of wrath.'),
(12756,17,'Esther','OT',3,6,'And he thought scorn to lay hands on Mordecai alone; for they had shewed him the people of Mordecai: wherefore Haman sought to destroy all the Jews that {were} throughout the whole kingdom of Ahasuerus, {even} the people of Mordecai.'),
(12757,17,'Esther','OT',3,7,'In the first month, that {is}, the month Nisan, in the twelfth year of king Ahasuerus, they cast Pur, that {is}, the lot, before Haman from day to day, and from month to month, {to} the twelfth {month}, that {is}, the month Adar.'),
(12758,17,'Esther','OT',3,8,'And Haman said unto king Ahasuerus, There is a certain people scattered abroad and dispersed among the people in all the provinces of thy kingdom; and their laws {are} diverse from all people; neither keep they the king\'s laws: therefore it {is} not for the king\'s profit to suffer them. {for the...: Heb. meet or, equal, etc}'),
(12759,17,'Esther','OT',3,9,'If it please the king, let it be written that they may be destroyed: and I will pay ten thousand talents of silver to the hands of those that have the charge of the business, to bring {it} into the king\'s treasuries. {that they...: Heb. to destroy them} {pay: Heb. weigh}'),
(12760,17,'Esther','OT',3,10,'And the king took his ring from his hand, and gave it unto Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, the Jews\' enemy. {enemy: or, oppressor}'),
(12761,17,'Esther','OT',3,11,'And the king said unto Haman, The silver {is} given to thee, the people also, to do with them as it seemeth good to thee.'),
(12762,17,'Esther','OT',3,12,'Then were the king\'s scribes called on the thirteenth day of the first month, and there was written according to all that Haman had commanded unto the king\'s lieutenants, and to the governors that {were} over every province, and to the rulers of every people of every province according to the writing thereof, and {to} every people after their language; in the name of king Ahasuerus was it written, and sealed with the king\'s ring. {scribes: or, secretaries}'),
(12763,17,'Esther','OT',3,13,'And the letters were sent by posts into all the king\'s provinces, to destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish, all Jews, both young and old, little children and women, in one day, {even} upon the thirteenth {day} of the twelfth month, which is the month Adar, and {to take} the spoil of them for a prey.'),
(12764,17,'Esther','OT',3,14,'The copy of the writing for a commandment to be given in every province was published unto all people, that they should be ready against that day.'),
(12765,17,'Esther','OT',3,15,'The posts went out, being hastened by the king\'s commandment, and the decree was given in Shushan the palace. And the king and Haman sat down to drink; but the city Shushan was perplexed.'),
(12766,17,'Esther','OT',4,1,'When Mordecai perceived all that was done, Mordecai rent his clothes, and put on sackcloth with ashes, and went out into the midst of the city, and cried with a loud and a bitter cry;'),
(12767,17,'Esther','OT',4,2,'And came even before the king\'s gate: for none {might} enter into the king\'s gate clothed with sackcloth.'),
(12768,17,'Esther','OT',4,3,'And in every province, whithersoever the king\'s commandment and his decree came, {there was} great mourning among the Jews, and fasting, and weeping, and wailing; and many lay in sackcloth and ashes. {many...: Heb. sackcloth and ashes were laid under many}'),
(12769,17,'Esther','OT',4,4,'So Esther\'s maids and her chamberlains came and told {it} her. Then was the queen exceedingly grieved; and she sent raiment to clothe Mordecai, and to take away his sackcloth from him: but he received {it} not. {chamberlains: Heb. eunuchs}'),
(12770,17,'Esther','OT',4,5,'Then called Esther for Hatach, {one} of the king\'s chamberlains, whom he had appointed to attend upon her, and gave him a commandment to Mordecai, to know what it {was}, and why it {was}. {appointed...: Heb. set before her}'),
(12771,17,'Esther','OT',4,6,'So Hatach went forth to Mordecai unto the street of the city, which {was} before the king\'s gate.'),
(12772,17,'Esther','OT',4,7,'And Mordecai told him of all that had happened unto him, and of the sum of the money that Haman had promised to pay to the king\'s treasuries for the Jews, to destroy them.'),
(12773,17,'Esther','OT',4,8,'Also he gave him the copy of the writing of the decree that was given at Shushan to destroy them, to shew {it} unto Esther, and to declare {it} unto her, and to charge her that she should go in unto the king, to make supplication unto him, and to make request before him for her people.'),
(12774,17,'Esther','OT',4,9,'And Hatach came and told Esther the words of Mordecai.'),
(12775,17,'Esther','OT',4,10,'Again Esther spake unto Hatach, and gave him commandment unto Mordecai;'),
(12776,17,'Esther','OT',4,11,'All the king\'s servants, and the people of the king\'s provinces, do know, that whosoever, whether man or woman, shall come unto the king into the inner court, who is not called, {there is} one law of his to put {him} to death, except such to whom the king shall hold out the golden sceptre, that he may live: but I have not been called to come in unto the king these thirty days.'),
(12777,17,'Esther','OT',4,12,'And they told to Mordecai Esther\'s words.'),
(12778,17,'Esther','OT',4,13,'Then Mordecai commanded to answer Esther, Think not with thyself that thou shalt escape in the king\'s house, more than all the Jews.'),
(12779,17,'Esther','OT',4,14,'For if thou altogether holdest thy peace at this time, {then} shall there enlargement and deliverance arise to the Jews from another place; but thou and thy father\'s house shall be destroyed: and who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for {such} a time as this? {enlargement: Heb. respiration}'),
(12780,17,'Esther','OT',4,15,'Then Esther bade {them} return Mordecai {this answer},'),
(12781,17,'Esther','OT',4,16,'Go, gather together all the Jews that are present in Shushan, and fast ye for me, and neither eat nor drink three days, night or day: I also and my maidens will fast likewise; and so will I go in unto the king, which {is} not according to the law: and if I perish, I perish. {present: Heb. found}'),
(12782,17,'Esther','OT',4,17,'So Mordecai went his way, and did according to all that Esther had commanded him. {went...: Heb. passed}'),
(12783,17,'Esther','OT',5,1,'Now it came to pass on the third day, that Esther put on {her} royal {apparel}, and stood in the inner court of the king\'s house, over against the king\'s house: and the king sat upon his royal throne in the royal house, over against the gate of the house.'),
(12784,17,'Esther','OT',5,2,'And it was so, when the king saw Esther the queen standing in the court, {that} she obtained favour in his sight: and the king held out to Esther the golden sceptre that {was} in his hand. So Esther drew near, and touched the top of the sceptre.'),
(12785,17,'Esther','OT',5,3,'Then said the king unto her, What wilt thou, queen Esther? and what {is} thy request? it shall be even given thee to the half of the kingdom.'),
(12786,17,'Esther','OT',5,4,'And Esther answered, If {it seem} good unto the king, let the king and Haman come this day unto the banquet that I have prepared for him.'),
(12787,17,'Esther','OT',5,5,'Then the king said, Cause Haman to make haste, that he may do as Esther hath said. So the king and Haman came to the banquet that Esther had prepared.'),
(12788,17,'Esther','OT',5,6,'And the king said unto Esther at the banquet of wine, What {is} thy petition? and it shall be granted thee: and what {is} thy request? even to the half of the kingdom it shall be performed.'),
(12789,17,'Esther','OT',5,7,'Then answered Esther, and said, My petition and my request {is};'),
(12790,17,'Esther','OT',5,8,'If I have found favour in the sight of the king, and if it please the king to grant my petition, and to perform my request, let the king and Haman come to the banquet that I shall prepare for them, and I will do to morrow as the king hath said. {perform: Heb. do}'),
(12791,17,'Esther','OT',5,9,'Then went Haman forth that day joyful and with a glad heart: but when Haman saw Mordecai in the king\'s gate, that he stood not up, nor moved for him, he was full of indignation against Mordecai.'),
(12792,17,'Esther','OT',5,10,'Nevertheless Haman refrained himself: and when he came home, he sent and called for his friends, and Zeresh his wife. {called...: Heb. caused to come}'),
(12793,17,'Esther','OT',5,11,'And Haman told them of the glory of his riches, and the multitude of his children, and all {the things} wherein the king had promoted him, and how he had advanced him above the princes and servants of the king.'),
(12794,17,'Esther','OT',5,12,'Haman said moreover, Yea, Esther the queen did let no man come in with the king unto the banquet that she had prepared but myself; and to morrow am I invited unto her also with the king.'),
(12795,17,'Esther','OT',5,13,'Yet all this availeth me nothing, so long as I see Mordecai the Jew sitting at the king\'s gate.'),
(12796,17,'Esther','OT',5,14,'Then said Zeresh his wife and all his friends unto him, Let a gallows be made of fifty cubits high, and to morrow speak thou unto the king that Mordecai may be hanged thereon: then go thou in merrily with the king unto the banquet. And the thing pleased Haman; and he caused the gallows to be made. {gallows: Heb. tree}'),
(12797,17,'Esther','OT',6,1,'On that night could not the king sleep, and he commanded to bring the book of records of the chronicles; and they were read before the king. {could...: Heb. the king\'s sleep fled away}'),
(12798,17,'Esther','OT',6,2,'And it was found written, that Mordecai had told of Bigthana and Teresh, two of the king\'s chamberlains, the keepers of the door, who sought to lay hand on the king Ahasuerus. {Bigthana: also called, Bigthan} {door: Heb. threshold}'),
(12799,17,'Esther','OT',6,3,'And the king said, What honour and dignity hath been done to Mordecai for this? Then said the king\'s servants that ministered unto him, There is nothing done for him.'),
(12800,17,'Esther','OT',6,4,'And the king said, Who {is} in the court? Now Haman was come into the outward court of the king\'s house, to speak unto the king to hang Mordecai on the gallows that he had prepared for him.'),
(12801,17,'Esther','OT',6,5,'And the king\'s servants said unto him, Behold, Haman standeth in the court. And the king said, Let him come in.'),
(12802,17,'Esther','OT',6,6,'So Haman came in. And the king said unto him, What shall be done unto the man whom the king delighteth to honour? Now Haman thought in his heart, To whom would the king delight to do honour more than to myself? {whom the king...: Heb. in whose honour the king delighteth}'),
(12803,17,'Esther','OT',6,7,'And Haman answered the king, For the man whom the king delighteth to honour, {whom the king...: Heb. in whose honour the king delighteth}'),
(12804,17,'Esther','OT',6,8,'Let the royal apparel be brought which the king {useth} to wear, and the horse that the king rideth upon, and the crown royal which is set upon his head: {Let...: Heb. Let them bring the royal apparel} {which the king...: Heb. wherewith the king clotheth himself}'),
(12805,17,'Esther','OT',6,9,'And let this apparel and horse be delivered to the hand of one of the king\'s most noble princes, that they may array the man {withal} whom the king delighteth to honour, and bring him on horseback through the street of the city, and proclaim before him, Thus shall it be done to the man whom the king delighteth to honour. {bring...: Heb. cause him to ride}'),
(12806,17,'Esther','OT',6,10,'Then the king said to Haman, Make haste, {and} take the apparel and the horse, as thou hast said, and do even so to Mordecai the Jew, that sitteth at the king\'s gate: let nothing fail of all that thou hast spoken. {let...: Heb. suffer not a whit to fall}'),
(12807,17,'Esther','OT',6,11,'Then took Haman the apparel and the horse, and arrayed Mordecai, and brought him on horseback through the street of the city, and proclaimed before him, Thus shall it be done unto the man whom the king delighteth to honour.'),
(12808,17,'Esther','OT',6,12,'And Mordecai came again to the king\'s gate. But Haman hasted to his house mourning, and having his head covered.'),
(12809,17,'Esther','OT',6,13,'And Haman told Zeresh his wife and all his friends every {thing} that had befallen him. Then said his wise men and Zeresh his wife unto him, If Mordecai {be} of the seed of the Jews, before whom thou hast begun to fall, thou shalt not prevail against him, but shalt surely fall before him.'),
(12810,17,'Esther','OT',6,14,'And while they {were} yet talking with him, came the king\'s chamberlains, and hasted to bring Haman unto the banquet that Esther had prepared.'),
(12811,17,'Esther','OT',7,1,'So the king and Haman came to banquet with Esther the queen. {to banquet: Heb. to drink}'),
(12812,17,'Esther','OT',7,2,'And the king said again unto Esther on the second day at the banquet of wine, What {is} thy petition, queen Esther? and it shall be granted thee: and what {is} thy request? and it shall be performed, {even} to the half of the kingdom.'),
(12813,17,'Esther','OT',7,3,'Then Esther the queen answered and said, If I have found favour in thy sight, O king, and if it please the king, let my life be given me at my petition, and my people at my request:'),
(12814,17,'Esther','OT',7,4,'For we are sold, I and my people, to be destroyed, to be slain, and to perish. But if we had been sold for bondmen and bondwomen, I had held my tongue, although the enemy could not countervail the king\'s damage. {to be destroyed...: Heb. that they should destroy, and kill, and cause to perish}'),
(12815,17,'Esther','OT',7,5,'Then the king Ahasuerus answered and said unto Esther the queen, Who is he, and where is he, that durst presume in his heart to do so? {that...: Heb. whose heart hath filled him}'),
(12816,17,'Esther','OT',7,6,'And Esther said, The adversary and enemy {is} this wicked Haman. Then Haman was afraid before the king and the queen. {The adversary: Heb. The man adversary} {before: or, at the presence of}'),
(12817,17,'Esther','OT',7,7,'And the king arising from the banquet of wine in his wrath {went} into the palace garden: and Haman stood up to make request for his life to Esther the queen; for he saw that there was evil determined against him by the king.'),
(12818,17,'Esther','OT',7,8,'Then the king returned out of the palace garden into the place of the banquet of wine; and Haman was fallen upon the bed whereon Esther {was}. Then said the king, Will he force the queen also before me in the house? As the word went out of the king\'s mouth, they covered Haman\'s face. {before me: Heb. with me}'),
(12819,17,'Esther','OT',7,9,'And Harbonah, one of the chamberlains, said before the king, Behold also, the gallows fifty cubits high, which Haman had made for Mordecai, who had spoken good for the king, standeth in the house of Haman. Then the king said, Hang him thereon. {gallows: Heb. tree}'),
(12820,17,'Esther','OT',7,10,'So they hanged Haman on the gallows that he had prepared for Mordecai. Then was the king\'s wrath pacified.'),
(12821,17,'Esther','OT',8,1,'On that day did the king Ahasuerus give the house of Haman the Jews\' enemy unto Esther the queen. And Mordecai came before the king; for Esther had told what he {was} unto her.'),
(12822,17,'Esther','OT',8,2,'And the king took off his ring, which he had taken from Haman, and gave it unto Mordecai. And Esther set Mordecai over the house of Haman.'),
(12823,17,'Esther','OT',8,3,'And Esther spake yet again before the king, and fell down at his feet, and besought him with tears to put away the mischief of Haman the Agagite, and his device that he had devised against the Jews. {and besought...: Heb. and she wept, and besought him}'),
(12824,17,'Esther','OT',8,4,'Then the king held out the golden sceptre toward Esther. So Esther arose, and stood before the king,'),
(12825,17,'Esther','OT',8,5,'And said, If it please the king, and if I have found favour in his sight, and the thing {seem} right before the king, and I {be} pleasing in his eyes, let it be written to reverse the letters devised by Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, which he wrote to destroy the Jews which {are} in all the king\'s provinces: {devised: Heb. the device} {which he...: or, who wrote}'),
(12826,17,'Esther','OT',8,6,'For how can I endure to see the evil that shall come unto my people? or how can I endure to see the destruction of my kindred? {endure...: Heb. be able that I may see}'),
(12827,17,'Esther','OT',8,7,'Then the king Ahasuerus said unto Esther the queen and to Mordecai the Jew, Behold, I have given Esther the house of Haman, and him they have hanged upon the gallows, because he laid his hand upon the Jews.'),
(12828,17,'Esther','OT',8,8,'Write ye also for the Jews, as it liketh you, in the king\'s name, and seal {it} with the king\'s ring: for the writing which is written in the king\'s name, and sealed with the king\'s ring, may no man reverse.'),
(12829,17,'Esther','OT',8,9,'Then were the king\'s scribes called at that time in the third month, that {is}, the month Sivan, on the three and twentieth {day} thereof; and it was written according to all that Mordecai commanded unto the Jews, and to the lieutenants, and the deputies and rulers of the provinces which {are} from India unto Ethiopia, an hundred twenty and seven provinces, unto every province according to the writing thereof, and unto every people after their language, and to the Jews according to their writing, and according to their language.'),
(12830,17,'Esther','OT',8,10,'And he wrote in the king Ahasuerus\' name, and sealed {it} with the king\'s ring, and sent letters by posts on horseback, {and} riders on mules, camels, {and} young dromedaries:'),
(12831,17,'Esther','OT',8,11,'Wherein the king granted the Jews which {were} in every city to gather themselves together, and to stand for their life, to destroy, to slay, and to cause to perish, all the power of the people and province that would assault them, {both} little ones and women, and {to take} the spoil of them for a prey,'),
(12832,17,'Esther','OT',8,12,'Upon one day in all the provinces of king Ahasuerus, {namely}, upon the thirteenth {day} of the twelfth month, which {is} the month Adar.'),
(12833,17,'Esther','OT',8,13,'The copy of the writing for a commandment to be given in every province {was} published unto all people, and that the Jews should be ready against that day to avenge themselves on their enemies. {published: Heb. revealed}'),
(12834,17,'Esther','OT',8,14,'{So} the posts that rode upon mules {and} camels went out, being hastened and pressed on by the king\'s commandment. And the decree was given at Shushan the palace.'),
(12835,17,'Esther','OT',8,15,'And Mordecai went out from the presence of the king in royal apparel of blue and white, and with a great crown of gold, and with a garment of fine linen and purple: and the city of Shushan rejoiced and was glad. {blue: or, violet}'),
(12836,17,'Esther','OT',8,16,'The Jews had light, and gladness, and joy, and honour.'),
(12837,17,'Esther','OT',8,17,'And in every province, and in every city, whithersoever the king\'s commandment and his decree came, the Jews had joy and gladness, a feast and a good day. And many of the people of the land became Jews; for the fear of the Jews fell upon them.'),
(12838,17,'Esther','OT',9,1,'Now in the twelfth month, that {is}, the month Adar, on the thirteenth day of the same, when the king\'s commandment and his decree drew near to be put in execution, in the day that the enemies of the Jews hoped to have power over them, (though it was turned to the contrary, that the Jews had rule over them that hated them;)'),
(12839,17,'Esther','OT',9,2,'The Jews gathered themselves together in their cities throughout all the provinces of the king Ahasuerus, to lay hand on such as sought their hurt: and no man could withstand them; for the fear of them fell upon all people.'),
(12840,17,'Esther','OT',9,3,'And all the rulers of the provinces, and the lieutenants, and the deputies, and officers of the king, helped the Jews; because the fear of Mordecai fell upon them. {officers...: Heb. those which did the business that belonged to the king}'),
(12841,17,'Esther','OT',9,4,'For Mordecai {was} great in the king\'s house, and his fame went out throughout all the provinces: for this man Mordecai waxed greater and greater.'),
(12842,17,'Esther','OT',9,5,'Thus the Jews smote all their enemies with the stroke of the sword, and slaughter, and destruction, and did what they would unto those that hated them. {what...: Heb. according to their will}'),
(12843,17,'Esther','OT',9,6,'And in Shushan the palace the Jews slew and destroyed five hundred men.'),
(12844,17,'Esther','OT',9,7,'And Parshandatha, and Dalphon, and Aspatha,'),
(12845,17,'Esther','OT',9,8,'And Poratha, and Adalia, and Aridatha,'),
(12846,17,'Esther','OT',9,9,'And Parmashta, and Arisai, and Aridai, and Vajezatha,'),
(12847,17,'Esther','OT',9,10,'The ten sons of Haman the son of Hammedatha, the enemy of the Jews, slew they; but on the spoil laid they not their hand.'),
(12848,17,'Esther','OT',9,11,'On that day the number of those that were slain in Shushan the palace was brought before the king. {was...: Heb. came}'),
(12849,17,'Esther','OT',9,12,'And the king said unto Esther the queen, The Jews have slain and destroyed five hundred men in Shushan the palace, and the ten sons of Haman; what have they done in the rest of the king\'s provinces? now what {is} thy petition? and it shall be granted thee: or what {is} thy request further? and it shall be done.'),
(12850,17,'Esther','OT',9,13,'Then said Esther, If it please the king, let it be granted to the Jews which {are} in Shushan to do to morrow also according unto this day\'s decree, and let Haman\'s ten sons be hanged upon the gallows. {let Haman\'s...: Heb. let men hang, etc}'),
(12851,17,'Esther','OT',9,14,'And the king commanded it so to be done: and the decree was given at Shushan; and they hanged Haman\'s ten sons.'),
(12852,17,'Esther','OT',9,15,'For the Jews that {were} in Shushan gathered themselves together on the fourteenth day also of the month Adar, and slew three hundred men at Shushan; but on the prey they laid not their hand.'),
(12853,17,'Esther','OT',9,16,'But the other Jews that {were} in the king\'s provinces gathered themselves together, and stood for their lives, and had rest from their enemies, and slew of their foes seventy and five thousand, but they laid not their hands on the prey,'),
(12854,17,'Esther','OT',9,17,'On the thirteenth day of the month Adar; and on the fourteenth day of the same rested they, and made it a day of feasting and gladness. {of the same: Heb. in it}'),
(12855,17,'Esther','OT',9,18,'But the Jews that {were} at Shushan assembled together on the thirteenth {day} thereof, and on the fourteenth thereof; and on the fifteenth {day} of the same they rested, and made it a day of feasting and gladness.'),
(12856,17,'Esther','OT',9,19,'Therefore the Jews of the villages, that dwelt in the unwalled towns, made the fourteenth day of the month Adar {a day of} gladness and feasting, and a good day, and of sending portions one to another.'),
(12857,17,'Esther','OT',9,20,'And Mordecai wrote these things, and sent letters unto all the Jews that {were} in all the provinces of the king Ahasuerus, {both} nigh and far,'),
(12858,17,'Esther','OT',9,21,'To stablish {this} among them, that they should keep the fourteenth day of the month Adar, and the fifteenth day of the same, yearly,'),
(12859,17,'Esther','OT',9,22,'As the days wherein the Jews rested from their enemies, and the month which was turned unto them from sorrow to joy, and from mourning into a good day: that they should make them days of feasting and joy, and of sending portions one to another, and gifts to the poor.'),
(12860,17,'Esther','OT',9,23,'And the Jews undertook to do as they had begun, and as Mordecai had written unto them;'),
(12861,17,'Esther','OT',9,24,'Because Haman the son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of all the Jews, had devised against the Jews to destroy them, and had cast Pur, that {is}, the lot, to consume them, and to destroy them; {consume: Heb. crush}'),
(12862,17,'Esther','OT',9,25,'But when {Esther} came before the king, he commanded by letters that his wicked device, which he devised against the Jews, should return upon his own head, and that he and his sons should be hanged on the gallows. {when...: Heb. when she came}'),
(12863,17,'Esther','OT',9,26,'Wherefore they called these days Purim after the name of Pur. Therefore for all the words of this letter, and {of that} which they had seen concerning this matter, and which had come unto them, {Pur: that is, Lot}'),
(12864,17,'Esther','OT',9,27,'The Jews ordained, and took upon them, and upon their seed, and upon all such as joined themselves unto them, so as it should not fail, that they would keep these two days according to their writing, and according to their {appointed} time every year; {fail: Heb. pass}'),
(12865,17,'Esther','OT',9,28,'And {that} these days {should be} remembered and kept throughout every generation, every family, every province, and every city; and {that} these days of Purim should not fail from among the Jews, nor the memorial of them perish from their seed. {fail: Heb. pass} {perish: Heb. be ended}'),
(12866,17,'Esther','OT',9,29,'Then Esther the queen, the daughter of Abihail, and Mordecai the Jew, wrote with all authority, to confirm this second letter of Purim. {authority: Heb. strength}'),
(12867,17,'Esther','OT',9,30,'And he sent the letters unto all the Jews, to the hundred twenty and seven provinces of the kingdom of Ahasuerus, {with} words of peace and truth,'),
(12868,17,'Esther','OT',9,31,'To confirm these days of Purim in their times {appointed}, according as Mordecai the Jew and Esther the queen had enjoined them, and as they had decreed for themselves and for their seed, the matters of the fastings and their cry. {themselves: Heb. their souls}'),
(12869,17,'Esther','OT',9,32,'And the decree of Esther confirmed these matters of Purim; and it was written in the book.'),
(12870,17,'Esther','OT',10,1,'And the king Ahasuerus laid a tribute upon the land, and {upon} the isles of the sea.'),
(12871,17,'Esther','OT',10,2,'And all the acts of his power and of his might, and the declaration of the greatness of Mordecai, whereunto the king advanced him, {are} they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Media and Persia? {advanced...: Heb. made him great}'),
(12872,17,'Esther','OT',10,3,'For Mordecai the Jew {was} next unto king Ahasuerus, and great among the Jews, and accepted of the multitude of his brethren, seeking the wealth of his people, and speaking peace to all his seed.'),
(12873,18,'Job','OT',1,1,'There was a man in the land of Uz, whose name {was} Job; and that man was perfect and upright, and one that feared God, and eschewed evil.'),
(12874,18,'Job','OT',1,2,'And there were born unto him seven sons and three daughters.'),
(12875,18,'Job','OT',1,3,'His substance also was seven thousand sheep, and three thousand camels, and five hundred yoke of oxen, and five hundred she asses, and a very great household; so that this man was the greatest of all the men of the east. {substance: or, cattle} {household: or, husbandry} {men: Heb. sons}'),
(12876,18,'Job','OT',1,4,'And his sons went and feasted {in their} houses, every one his day; and sent and called for their three sisters to eat and to drink with them.'),
(12877,18,'Job','OT',1,5,'And it was so, when the days of {their} feasting were gone about, that Job sent and sanctified them, and rose up early in the morning, and offered burnt offerings {according} to the number of them all: for Job said, It may be that my sons have sinned, and cursed God in their hearts. Thus did Job continually. {continually: Heb. all the days}'),
(12878,18,'Job','OT',1,6,'Now there was a day when the sons of God came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan came also among them. {Satan: Heb. the adversary} {among: Heb. in the midst of}'),
(12879,18,'Job','OT',1,7,'And the LORD said unto Satan, Whence comest thou? Then Satan answered the LORD, and said, From going to and fro in the earth, and from walking up and down in it.'),
(12880,18,'Job','OT',1,8,'And the LORD said unto Satan, Hast thou considered my servant Job, that {there is} none like him in the earth, a perfect and an upright man, one that feareth God, and escheweth evil? {considered: Heb. set thy heart on}'),
(12881,18,'Job','OT',1,9,'Then Satan answered the LORD, and said, Doth Job fear God for nought?'),
(12882,18,'Job','OT',1,10,'Hast not thou made an hedge about him, and about his house, and about all that he hath on every side? thou hast blessed the work of his hands, and his substance is increased in the land. {substance: or, cattle}'),
(12883,18,'Job','OT',1,11,'But put forth thine hand now, and touch all that he hath, and he will curse thee to thy face. {and he...: Heb. if he curse thee not to thy face}'),
(12884,18,'Job','OT',1,12,'And the LORD said unto Satan, Behold, all that he hath {is} in thy power; only upon himself put not forth thine hand. So Satan went forth from the presence of the LORD. {power: Heb. hand}'),
(12885,18,'Job','OT',1,13,'And there was a day when his sons and his daughters {were} eating and drinking wine in their eldest brother\'s house:'),
(12886,18,'Job','OT',1,14,'And there came a messenger unto Job, and said, The oxen were plowing, and the asses feeding beside them:'),
(12887,18,'Job','OT',1,15,'And the Sabeans fell {upon them}, and took them away; yea, they have slain the servants with the edge of the sword; and I only am escaped alone to tell thee.'),
(12888,18,'Job','OT',1,16,'While he {was} yet speaking, there came also another, and said, The fire of God is fallen from heaven, and hath burned up the sheep, and the servants, and consumed them; and I only am escaped alone to tell thee. {The fire...: or, A great fire}'),
(12889,18,'Job','OT',1,17,'While he {was} yet speaking, there came also another, and said, The Chaldeans made out three bands, and fell upon the camels, and have carried them away, yea, and slain the servants with the edge of the sword; and I only am escaped alone to tell thee. {fell: Heb. rushed}'),
(12890,18,'Job','OT',1,18,'While he {was} yet speaking, there came also another, and said, Thy sons and thy daughters {were} eating and drinking wine in their eldest brother\'s house:'),
(12891,18,'Job','OT',1,19,'And, behold, there came a great wind from the wilderness, and smote the four corners of the house, and it fell upon the young men, and they are dead; and I only am escaped alone to tell thee. {from...: Heb. from aside, etc}'),
(12892,18,'Job','OT',1,20,'Then Job arose, and rent his mantle, and shaved his head, and fell down upon the ground, and worshipped, {mantle: or, robe}'),
(12893,18,'Job','OT',1,21,'And said, Naked came I out of my mother\'s womb, and naked shall I return thither: the LORD gave, and the LORD hath taken away; blessed be the name of the LORD.'),
(12894,18,'Job','OT',1,22,'In all this Job sinned not, nor charged God foolishly. {charged...: or, attributed folly to God}'),
(12895,18,'Job','OT',2,1,'Again there was a day when the sons of God came to present themselves before the LORD, and Satan came also among them to present himself before the LORD.'),
(12896,18,'Job','OT',2,2,'And the LORD said unto Satan, From whence comest thou? And Satan answered the LORD, and said, From going to and fro in the earth, and from walking up and down in it.'),
(12897,18,'Job','OT',2,3,'And the LORD said unto Satan, Hast thou considered my servant Job, that {there is} none like him in the earth, a perfect and an upright man, one that feareth God, and escheweth evil? and still he holdeth fast his integrity, although thou movedst me against him, to destroy him without cause. {to destroy...: Heb. to swallow him up}'),
(12898,18,'Job','OT',2,4,'And Satan answered the LORD, and said, Skin for skin, yea, all that a man hath will he give for his life.'),
(12899,18,'Job','OT',2,5,'But put forth thine hand now, and touch his bone and his flesh, and he will curse thee to thy face.'),
(12900,18,'Job','OT',2,6,'And the LORD said unto Satan, Behold, he {is} in thine hand; but save his life. {but: or, only}'),
(12901,18,'Job','OT',2,7,'So went Satan forth from the presence of the LORD, and smote Job with sore boils from the sole of his foot unto his crown.'),
(12902,18,'Job','OT',2,8,'And he took him a potsherd to scrape himself withal; and he sat down among the ashes.'),
(12903,18,'Job','OT',2,9,'Then said his wife unto him, Dost thou still retain thine integrity? curse God, and die.'),
(12904,18,'Job','OT',2,10,'But he said unto her, Thou speakest as one of the foolish women speaketh. What? shall we receive good at the hand of God, and shall we not receive evil? In all this did not Job sin with his lips.'),
(12905,18,'Job','OT',2,11,'Now when Job\'s three friends heard of all this evil that was come upon him, they came every one from his own place; Eliphaz the Temanite, and Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite: for they had made an appointment together to come to mourn with him and to comfort him.'),
(12906,18,'Job','OT',2,12,'And when they lifted up their eyes afar off, and knew him not, they lifted up their voice, and wept; and they rent every one his mantle, and sprinkled dust upon their heads toward heaven.'),
(12907,18,'Job','OT',2,13,'So they sat down with him upon the ground seven days and seven nights, and none spake a word unto him: for they saw that {his} grief was very great.'),
(12908,18,'Job','OT',3,1,'After this opened Job his mouth, and cursed his day.'),
(12909,18,'Job','OT',3,2,'And Job spake, and said, {spake: Heb. answered}'),
(12910,18,'Job','OT',3,3,'Let the day perish wherein I was born, and the night {in which} it was said, There is a man child conceived.'),
(12911,18,'Job','OT',3,4,'Let that day be darkness; let not God regard it from above, neither let the light shine upon it.'),
(12912,18,'Job','OT',3,5,'Let darkness and the shadow of death stain it; let a cloud dwell upon it; let the blackness of the day terrify it. {stain: or, challenge} {let the...: or, let them terrify it, as those who have a bitter day}'),
(12913,18,'Job','OT',3,6,'As {for} that night, let darkness seize upon it; let it not be joined unto the days of the year, let it not come into the number of the months. {let it not be...: or, let it not rejoice among the days}'),
(12914,18,'Job','OT',3,7,'Lo, let that night be solitary, let no joyful voice come therein.'),
(12915,18,'Job','OT',3,8,'Let them curse it that curse the day, who are ready to raise up their mourning. {their...: or, leviathan}'),
(12916,18,'Job','OT',3,9,'Let the stars of the twilight thereof be dark; let it look for light, but {have} none; neither let it see the dawning of the day: {the dawning...: Heb. the eyelids of the morning}'),
(12917,18,'Job','OT',3,10,'Because it shut not up the doors of my {mother\'s} womb, nor hid sorrow from mine eyes.'),
(12918,18,'Job','OT',3,11,'Why died I not from the womb? {why} did I {not} give up the ghost when I came out of the belly?'),
(12919,18,'Job','OT',3,12,'Why did the knees prevent me? or why the breasts that I should suck?'),
(12920,18,'Job','OT',3,13,'For now should I have lain still and been quiet, I should have slept: then had I been at rest,'),
(12921,18,'Job','OT',3,14,'With kings and counsellors of the earth, which built desolate places for themselves;'),
(12922,18,'Job','OT',3,15,'Or with princes that had gold, who filled their houses with silver:'),
(12923,18,'Job','OT',3,16,'Or as an hidden untimely birth I had not been; as infants {which} never saw light.'),
(12924,18,'Job','OT',3,17,'There the wicked cease {from} troubling; and there the weary be at rest. {weary: Heb. wearied in strength}'),
(12925,18,'Job','OT',3,18,'{There} the prisoners rest together; they hear not the voice of the oppressor.'),
(12926,18,'Job','OT',3,19,'The small and great are there; and the servant {is} free from his master.'),
(12927,18,'Job','OT',3,20,'Wherefore is light given to him that is in misery, and life unto the bitter {in} soul;'),
(12928,18,'Job','OT',3,21,'Which long for death, but it {cometh} not; and dig for it more than for hid treasures; {long: Heb. wait}'),
(12929,18,'Job','OT',3,22,'Which rejoice exceedingly, {and} are glad, when they can find the grave?'),
(12930,18,'Job','OT',3,23,'{Why is light given} to a man whose way is hid, and whom God hath hedged in?'),
(12931,18,'Job','OT',3,24,'For my sighing cometh before I eat, and my roarings are poured out like the waters. {I eat: Heb. my meat}'),
(12932,18,'Job','OT',3,25,'For the thing which I greatly feared is come upon me, and that which I was afraid of is come unto me. {the thing...: Heb. I feared a fear, and it came upon me}'),
(12933,18,'Job','OT',3,26,'I was not in safety, neither had I rest, neither was I quiet; yet trouble came.'),
(12934,18,'Job','OT',4,1,'Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered and said,'),
(12935,18,'Job','OT',4,2,'{If} we assay to commune with thee, wilt thou be grieved? but who can withhold himself from speaking? {to...: Heb. a word} {withhold...: Heb. refrain from words?}'),
(12936,18,'Job','OT',4,3,'Behold, thou hast instructed many, and thou hast strengthened the weak hands.'),
(12937,18,'Job','OT',4,4,'Thy words have upholden him that was falling, and thou hast strengthened the feeble knees.'),
(12938,18,'Job','OT',4,5,'But now it is come upon thee, and thou faintest; it toucheth thee, and thou art troubled.'),
(12939,18,'Job','OT',4,6,'{Is} not {this} thy fear, thy confidence, thy hope, and the uprightness of thy ways?'),
(12940,18,'Job','OT',4,7,'Remember, I pray thee, who {ever} perished, being innocent? or where were the righteous cut off?'),
(12941,18,'Job','OT',4,8,'Even as I have seen, they that plow iniquity, and sow wickedness, reap the same.'),
(12942,18,'Job','OT',4,9,'By the blast of God they perish, and by the breath of his nostrils are they consumed. {by the breath...: that is, by his anger}'),
(12943,18,'Job','OT',4,10,'The roaring of the lion, and the voice of the fierce lion, and the teeth of the young lions, are broken.'),
(12944,18,'Job','OT',4,11,'The old lion perisheth for lack of prey, and the stout lion\'s whelps are scattered abroad.'),
(12945,18,'Job','OT',4,12,'Now a thing was secretly brought to me, and mine ear received a little thereof. {secretly: Heb. by stealth}'),
(12946,18,'Job','OT',4,13,'In thoughts from the visions of the night, when deep sleep falleth on men,'),
(12947,18,'Job','OT',4,14,'Fear came upon me, and trembling, which made all my bones to shake. {came...: Heb. met} {all: Heb. the multitude of}'),
(12948,18,'Job','OT',4,15,'Then a spirit passed before my face; the hair of my flesh stood up:'),
(12949,18,'Job','OT',4,16,'It stood still, but I could not discern the form thereof: an image {was} before mine eyes, {there was} silence, and I heard a voice, {saying}, {there...: or, I heard a still voice}'),
(12950,18,'Job','OT',4,17,'Shall mortal man be more just than God? shall a man be more pure than his maker?'),
(12951,18,'Job','OT',4,18,'Behold, he put no trust in his servants; and his angels he charged with folly: {and his...: or, nor in his angels, in whom he put light}'),
(12952,18,'Job','OT',4,19,'How much less {in} them that dwell in houses of clay, whose foundation {is} in the dust, {which} are crushed before the moth?'),
(12953,18,'Job','OT',4,20,'They are destroyed from morning to evening: they perish for ever without any regarding {it}. {destroyed: Heb. beaten in pieces}'),
(12954,18,'Job','OT',4,21,'Doth not their excellency {which is} in them go away? they die, even without wisdom.'),
(12955,18,'Job','OT',5,1,'Call now, if there be any that will answer thee; and to which of the saints wilt thou turn? {turn: or, look?}'),
(12956,18,'Job','OT',5,2,'For wrath killeth the foolish man, and envy slayeth the silly one. {envy: or, indignation}'),
(12957,18,'Job','OT',5,3,'I have seen the foolish taking root: but suddenly I cursed his habitation.'),
(12958,18,'Job','OT',5,4,'His children are far from safety, and they are crushed in the gate, neither {is there} any to deliver {them}.'),
(12959,18,'Job','OT',5,5,'Whose harvest the hungry eateth up, and taketh it even out of the thorns, and the robber swalloweth up their substance.'),
(12960,18,'Job','OT',5,6,'Although affliction cometh not forth of the dust, neither doth trouble spring out of the ground; {affliction: or, iniquity}'),
(12961,18,'Job','OT',5,7,'Yet man is born unto trouble, as the sparks fly upward. {trouble: or, labour} {sparks...: Heb. the sons of the burning coal lift up to fly}'),
(12962,18,'Job','OT',5,8,'I would seek unto God, and unto God would I commit my cause:'),
(12963,18,'Job','OT',5,9,'Which doeth great things and unsearchable; marvellous things without number: {unsearchable: Heb. there is no search} {without...: Heb. till there be no number}'),
(12964,18,'Job','OT',5,10,'Who giveth rain upon the earth, and sendeth waters upon the fields: {fields: Heb. outplaces}'),
(12965,18,'Job','OT',5,11,'To set up on high those that be low; that those which mourn may be exalted to safety.'),
(12966,18,'Job','OT',5,12,'He disappointeth the devices of the crafty, so that their hands cannot perform {their} enterprise. {their enterprise: or, any thing}'),
(12967,18,'Job','OT',5,13,'He taketh the wise in their own craftiness: and the counsel of the froward is carried headlong.'),
(12968,18,'Job','OT',5,14,'They meet with darkness in the daytime, and grope in the noonday as in the night. {meet...: or, run into}'),
(12969,18,'Job','OT',5,15,'But he saveth the poor from the sword, from their mouth, and from the hand of the mighty.'),
(12970,18,'Job','OT',5,16,'So the poor hath hope, and iniquity stoppeth her mouth.'),
(12971,18,'Job','OT',5,17,'Behold, happy {is} the man whom God correcteth: therefore despise not thou the chastening of the Almighty:'),
(12972,18,'Job','OT',5,18,'For he maketh sore, and bindeth up: he woundeth, and his hands make whole.'),
(12973,18,'Job','OT',5,19,'He shall deliver thee in six troubles: yea, in seven there shall no evil touch thee.'),
