(13904,18,'Job','OT',41,13,'Who can discover the face of his garment? {or} who can come {to him} with his double bridle? {with: or, within}'),
(13905,18,'Job','OT',41,14,'Who can open the doors of his face? his teeth {are} terrible round about.'),
(13906,18,'Job','OT',41,15,'{His} scales {are his} pride, shut up together {as with} a close seal. {scales: Heb. strong pieces of shields}'),
(13907,18,'Job','OT',41,16,'One is so near to another, that no air can come between them.'),
(13908,18,'Job','OT',41,17,'They are joined one to another, they stick together, that they cannot be sundered.'),
(13909,18,'Job','OT',41,18,'By his neesings a light doth shine, and his eyes {are} like the eyelids of the morning.'),
(13910,18,'Job','OT',41,19,'Out of his mouth go burning lamps, {and} sparks of fire leap out.'),
(13911,18,'Job','OT',41,20,'Out of his nostrils goeth smoke, as {out} of a seething pot or caldron.'),
(13912,18,'Job','OT',41,21,'His breath kindleth coals, and a flame goeth out of his mouth.'),
(13913,18,'Job','OT',41,22,'In his neck remaineth strength, and sorrow is turned into joy before him. {is turned into joy: Heb. rejoiceth}'),
(13914,18,'Job','OT',41,23,'The flakes of his flesh are joined together: they are firm in themselves; they cannot be moved. {flakes: Heb. fallings}'),
(13915,18,'Job','OT',41,24,'His heart is as firm as a stone; yea, as hard as a piece of the nether {millstone}.'),
(13916,18,'Job','OT',41,25,'When he raiseth up himself, the mighty are afraid: by reason of breakings they purify themselves.'),
(13917,18,'Job','OT',41,26,'The sword of him that layeth at him cannot hold: the spear, the dart, nor the habergeon. {habergeon: or, breastplate}'),
(13918,18,'Job','OT',41,27,'He esteemeth iron as straw, {and} brass as rotten wood.'),
(13919,18,'Job','OT',41,28,'The arrow cannot make him flee: slingstones are turned with him into stubble.'),
(13920,18,'Job','OT',41,29,'Darts are counted as stubble: he laugheth at the shaking of a spear.'),
(13921,18,'Job','OT',41,30,'Sharp stones {are} under him: he spreadeth sharp pointed things upon the mire. {Sharp stones: Heb. Sharp pieces of potsherd}'),
(13922,18,'Job','OT',41,31,'He maketh the deep to boil like a pot: he maketh the sea like a pot of ointment.'),
(13923,18,'Job','OT',41,32,'He maketh a path to shine after him; {one} would think the deep {to be} hoary.'),
(13924,18,'Job','OT',41,33,'Upon earth there is not his like, who is made without fear. {is made without fear: or, behave themselves without fear}'),
(13925,18,'Job','OT',41,34,'He beholdeth all high {things}: he {is} a king over all the children of pride.'),
(13926,18,'Job','OT',42,1,'Then Job answered the LORD, and said,'),
(13927,18,'Job','OT',42,2,'I know that thou canst do every {thing}, and {that} no thought can be withholden from thee. {no thought can be...: or, no thought of thine can be hindered}'),
(13928,18,'Job','OT',42,3,'Who {is} he that hideth counsel without knowledge? therefore have I uttered that I understood not; things too wonderful for me, which I knew not.'),
(13929,18,'Job','OT',42,4,'Hear, I beseech thee, and I will speak: I will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.'),
(13930,18,'Job','OT',42,5,'I have heard of thee by the hearing of the ear: but now mine eye seeth thee.'),
(13931,18,'Job','OT',42,6,'Wherefore I abhor {myself}, and repent in dust and ashes.'),
(13932,18,'Job','OT',42,7,'And it was {so}, that after the LORD had spoken these words unto Job, the LORD said to Eliphaz the Temanite, My wrath is kindled against thee, and against thy two friends: for ye have not spoken of me {the thing that is} right, as my servant Job {hath}.'),
(13933,18,'Job','OT',42,8,'Therefore take unto you now seven bullocks and seven rams, and go to my servant Job, and offer up for yourselves a burnt offering; and my servant Job shall pray for you: for him will I accept: lest I deal with you {after your} folly, in that ye have not spoken of me {the thing which is} right, like my servant Job. {him: Heb. his face, or, person}'),
(13934,18,'Job','OT',42,9,'So Eliphaz the Temanite and Bildad the Shuhite {and} Zophar the Naamathite went, and did according as the LORD commanded them: the LORD also accepted Job. {Job: Heb. the face of Job}'),
(13935,18,'Job','OT',42,10,'And the LORD turned the captivity of Job, when he prayed for his friends: also the LORD gave Job twice as much as he had before. {gave...: Heb. added all that had been to Job unto the double}'),
(13936,18,'Job','OT',42,11,'Then came there unto him all his brethren, and all his sisters, and all they that had been of his acquaintance before, and did eat bread with him in his house: and they bemoaned him, and comforted him over all the evil that the LORD had brought upon him: every man also gave him a piece of money, and every one an earring of gold.'),
(13937,18,'Job','OT',42,12,'So the LORD blessed the latter end of Job more than his beginning: for he had fourteen thousand sheep, and six thousand camels, and a thousand yoke of oxen, and a thousand she asses.'),
(13938,18,'Job','OT',42,13,'He had also seven sons and three daughters.'),
(13939,18,'Job','OT',42,14,'And he called the name of the first, Jemima; and the name of the second, Kezia; and the name of the third, Kerenhappuch.'),
(13940,18,'Job','OT',42,15,'And in all the land were no women found {so} fair as the daughters of Job: and their father gave them inheritance among their brethren.'),
(13941,18,'Job','OT',42,16,'After this lived Job an hundred and forty years, and saw his sons, and his sons\' sons, {even} four generations.'),
(13942,18,'Job','OT',42,17,'So Job died, {being} old and full of days.'),
(13943,19,'Psalms','OT',1,1,'Blessed {is} the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful. {ungodly: or, wicked}'),
(13944,19,'Psalms','OT',1,2,'But his delight {is} in the law of the LORD; and in his law doth he meditate day and night.'),
(13945,19,'Psalms','OT',1,3,'And he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper. {wither: Heb. fade}'),
(13946,19,'Psalms','OT',1,4,'The ungodly {are} not so: but {are} like the chaff which the wind driveth away.'),
(13947,19,'Psalms','OT',1,5,'Therefore the ungodly shall not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous.'),
(13948,19,'Psalms','OT',1,6,'For the LORD knoweth the way of the righteous: but the way of the ungodly shall perish.'),
(13949,19,'Psalms','OT',2,1,'Why do the heathen rage, and the people imagine a vain thing? {rage: or, tumultuously assemble} {imagine: Heb. meditate}'),
(13950,19,'Psalms','OT',2,2,'The kings of the earth set themselves, and the rulers take counsel together, against the LORD, and against his anointed, {saying},'),
(13951,19,'Psalms','OT',2,3,'Let us break their bands asunder, and cast away their cords from us.'),
(13952,19,'Psalms','OT',2,4,'He that sitteth in the heavens shall laugh: the Lord shall have them in derision.'),
(13953,19,'Psalms','OT',2,5,'Then shall he speak unto them in his wrath, and vex them in his sore displeasure. {vex: or, trouble}'),
(13954,19,'Psalms','OT',2,6,'Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion. {set: Heb. anointed} {upon...: Heb. upon Zion, the hill of my holiness}'),
(13955,19,'Psalms','OT',2,7,'I will declare the decree: the LORD hath said unto me, Thou {art} my Son; this day have I begotten thee. {the decree: or, for a decree}'),
(13956,19,'Psalms','OT',2,8,'Ask of me, and I shall give {thee} the heathen {for} thine inheritance, and the uttermost parts of the earth {for} thy possession.'),
(13957,19,'Psalms','OT',2,9,'Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter\'s vessel.'),
(13958,19,'Psalms','OT',2,10,'Be wise now therefore, O ye kings: be instructed, ye judges of the earth.'),
(13959,19,'Psalms','OT',2,11,'Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with trembling.'),
(13960,19,'Psalms','OT',2,12,'Kiss the Son, lest he be angry, and ye perish {from} the way, when his wrath is kindled but a little. Blessed {are} all they that put their trust in him.'),
(13961,19,'Psalms','OT',3,1,'[A Psalm of David, when he fled from Absalom his son.] LORD, how are they increased that trouble me! many {are} they that rise up against me.'),
(13962,19,'Psalms','OT',3,2,'Many {there be} which say of my soul, {There is} no help for him in God. Selah.'),
(13963,19,'Psalms','OT',3,3,'But thou, O LORD, {art} a shield for me; my glory, and the lifter up of mine head. {for: or, about}'),
(13964,19,'Psalms','OT',3,4,'I cried unto the LORD with my voice, and he heard me out of his holy hill. Selah.'),
(13965,19,'Psalms','OT',3,5,'I laid me down and slept; I awaked; for the LORD sustained me.'),
(13966,19,'Psalms','OT',3,6,'I will not be afraid of ten thousands of people, that have set {themselves} against me round about.'),
(13967,19,'Psalms','OT',3,7,'Arise, O LORD; save me, O my God: for thou hast smitten all mine enemies {upon} the cheek bone; thou hast broken the teeth of the ungodly.'),
(13968,19,'Psalms','OT',3,8,'Salvation {belongeth} unto the LORD: thy blessing {is} upon thy people. Selah.'),
(13969,19,'Psalms','OT',4,1,'[To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm of David.] Hear me when I call, O God of my righteousness: thou hast enlarged me {when I was} in distress; have mercy upon me, and hear my prayer. {chief...: or, overseer} {have...: or, be gracious unto me}'),
(13970,19,'Psalms','OT',4,2,'O ye sons of men, how long {will ye turn} my glory into shame? {how long} will ye love vanity, {and} seek after leasing? Selah.'),
(13971,19,'Psalms','OT',4,3,'But know that the LORD hath set apart him that is godly for himself: the LORD will hear when I call unto him.'),
(13972,19,'Psalms','OT',4,4,'Stand in awe, and sin not: commune with your own heart upon your bed, and be still. Selah.'),
(13973,19,'Psalms','OT',4,5,'Offer the sacrifices of righteousness, and put your trust in the LORD.'),
(13974,19,'Psalms','OT',4,6,'{There be} many that say, Who will shew us {any} good? LORD, lift thou up the light of thy countenance upon us.'),
(13975,19,'Psalms','OT',4,7,'Thou hast put gladness in my heart, more than in the time {that} their corn and their wine increased.'),
(13976,19,'Psalms','OT',4,8,'I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, LORD, only makest me dwell in safety.'),
(13977,19,'Psalms','OT',5,1,'[To the chief Musician upon Nehiloth, A Psalm of David.] Give ear to my words, O LORD, consider my meditation.'),
(13978,19,'Psalms','OT',5,2,'Hearken unto the voice of my cry, my King, and my God: for unto thee will I pray.'),
(13979,19,'Psalms','OT',5,3,'My voice shalt thou hear in the morning, O LORD; in the morning will I direct {my prayer} unto thee, and will look up.'),
(13980,19,'Psalms','OT',5,4,'For thou {art} not a God that hath pleasure in wickedness: neither shall evil dwell with thee.'),
(13981,19,'Psalms','OT',5,5,'The foolish shall not stand in thy sight: thou hatest all workers of iniquity. {in...: Heb. before thine eyes}'),
(13982,19,'Psalms','OT',5,6,'Thou shalt destroy them that speak leasing: the LORD will abhor the bloody and deceitful man. {bloody...: Heb. man of bloods and deceit}'),
(13983,19,'Psalms','OT',5,7,'But as for me, I will come {into} thy house in the multitude of thy mercy: {and} in thy fear will I worship toward thy holy temple. {thy holy...: Heb. the temple of thy holiness}'),
(13984,19,'Psalms','OT',5,8,'Lead me, O LORD, in thy righteousness because of mine enemies; make thy way straight before my face. {mine...: Heb. those which observe me}'),
(13985,19,'Psalms','OT',5,9,'For {there is} no faithfulness in their mouth; their inward part {is} very wickedness; their throat {is} an open sepulchre; they flatter with their tongue. {faithfulness: or, stedfastness} {their mouth: Heb. his mouth, that is, the mouth of any of them} {very...: Heb. wickednesses}'),
(13986,19,'Psalms','OT',5,10,'Destroy thou them, O God; let them fall by their own counsels; cast them out in the multitude of their transgressions; for they have rebelled against thee. {Destroy...: or, Make them guilty} {by...: or, from their counsels}'),
(13987,19,'Psalms','OT',5,11,'But let all those that put their trust in thee rejoice: let them ever shout for joy, because thou defendest them: let them also that love thy name be joyful in thee. {defendest...: Heb. coverest over, or, protectest them}'),
(13988,19,'Psalms','OT',5,12,'For thou, LORD, wilt bless the righteous; with favour wilt thou compass him as {with} a shield. {compass: Heb. crown}'),
(13989,19,'Psalms','OT',6,1,'[To the chief Musician on Neginoth upon Sheminith, A Psalm of David.] O LORD, rebuke me not in thine anger, neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure. {chief...: or, overseer} {Sheminith: or, the eighth}'),
(13990,19,'Psalms','OT',6,2,'Have mercy upon me, O LORD; for I {am} weak: O LORD, heal me; for my bones are vexed.'),
(13991,19,'Psalms','OT',6,3,'My soul is also sore vexed: but thou, O LORD, how long?'),
(13992,19,'Psalms','OT',6,4,'Return, O LORD, deliver my soul: oh save me for thy mercies\' sake.'),
(13993,19,'Psalms','OT',6,5,'For in death {there is} no remembrance of thee: in the grave who shall give thee thanks?'),
(13994,19,'Psalms','OT',6,6,'I am weary with my groaning; all the night make I my bed to swim; I water my couch with my tears. {all...: or, every night}'),
(13995,19,'Psalms','OT',6,7,'Mine eye is consumed because of grief; it waxeth old because of all mine enemies.'),
(13996,19,'Psalms','OT',6,8,'Depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity; for the LORD hath heard the voice of my weeping.'),
(13997,19,'Psalms','OT',6,9,'The LORD hath heard my supplication; the LORD will receive my prayer.'),
(13998,19,'Psalms','OT',6,10,'Let all mine enemies be ashamed and sore vexed: let them return {and} be ashamed suddenly.'),
(13999,19,'Psalms','OT',7,1,'[Shiggaion of David, which he sang unto the LORD, concerning the words of Cush the Benjamite.] O LORD my God, in thee do I put my trust: save me from all them that persecute me, and deliver me: {words: or, business}'),
(14000,19,'Psalms','OT',7,2,'Lest he tear my soul like a lion, rending {it} in pieces, while {there is} none to deliver. {none...: Heb. not a deliverer}'),
(14001,19,'Psalms','OT',7,3,'O LORD my God, if I have done this; if there be iniquity in my hands;'),
(14002,19,'Psalms','OT',7,4,'If I have rewarded evil unto him that was at peace with me; (yea, I have delivered him that without cause is mine enemy:)'),
(14003,19,'Psalms','OT',7,5,'Let the enemy persecute my soul, and take {it}; yea, let him tread down my life upon the earth, and lay mine honour in the dust. Selah.'),
(14004,19,'Psalms','OT',7,6,'Arise, O LORD, in thine anger, lift up thyself because of the rage of mine enemies: and awake for me {to} the judgment {that} thou hast commanded.'),
(14005,19,'Psalms','OT',7,7,'So shall the congregation of the people compass thee about: for their sakes therefore return thou on high.'),
(14006,19,'Psalms','OT',7,8,'The LORD shall judge the people: judge me, O LORD, according to my righteousness, and according to mine integrity {that is} in me.'),
(14007,19,'Psalms','OT',7,9,'Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end; but establish the just: for the righteous God trieth the hearts and reins.'),
(14008,19,'Psalms','OT',7,10,'My defence {is} of God, which saveth the upright in heart. {My...: Heb. My buckler is upon God}'),
(14009,19,'Psalms','OT',7,11,'God judgeth the righteous, and God is angry {with the wicked} every day. {judgeth...: or, is a righteous judge}'),
(14010,19,'Psalms','OT',7,12,'If he turn not, he will whet his sword; he hath bent his bow, and made it ready.'),
(14011,19,'Psalms','OT',7,13,'He hath also prepared for him the instruments of death; he ordaineth his arrows against the persecutors.'),
(14012,19,'Psalms','OT',7,14,'Behold, he travaileth with iniquity, and hath conceived mischief, and brought forth falsehood.'),
(14013,19,'Psalms','OT',7,15,'He made a pit, and digged it, and is fallen into the ditch {which} he made. {He made a pit: Heb. He hath digged a pit}'),
(14014,19,'Psalms','OT',7,16,'His mischief shall return upon his own head, and his violent dealing shall come down upon his own pate.'),
(14015,19,'Psalms','OT',7,17,'I will praise the LORD according to his righteousness: and will sing praise to the name of the LORD most high.'),
(14016,19,'Psalms','OT',8,1,'[To the chief Musician upon Gittith, A Psalm of David.] O LORD our Lord, how excellent {is} thy name in all the earth! who hast set thy glory above the heavens.'),
(14017,19,'Psalms','OT',8,2,'Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings hast thou ordained strength because of thine enemies, that thou mightest still the enemy and the avenger. {ordained: Heb. founded}'),
(14018,19,'Psalms','OT',8,3,'When I consider thy heavens, the work of thy fingers, the moon and the stars, which thou hast ordained;'),
(14019,19,'Psalms','OT',8,4,'What is man, that thou art mindful of him? and the son of man, that thou visitest him?'),
(14020,19,'Psalms','OT',8,5,'For thou hast made him a little lower than the angels, and hast crowned him with glory and honour.'),
(14021,19,'Psalms','OT',8,6,'Thou madest him to have dominion over the works of thy hands; thou hast put all {things} under his feet:'),
(14022,19,'Psalms','OT',8,7,'All sheep and oxen, yea, and the beasts of the field; {All...: Heb. Flocks and oxen all of them}'),
(14023,19,'Psalms','OT',8,8,'The fowl of the air, and the fish of the sea, {and whatsoever} passeth through the paths of the seas.'),
(14024,19,'Psalms','OT',8,9,'O LORD our Lord, how excellent {is} thy name in all the earth!'),
(14025,19,'Psalms','OT',9,1,'[To the chief Musician upon Muthlabben, A Psalm of David.] I will praise {thee}, O LORD, with my whole heart; I will shew forth all thy marvellous works.'),
(14026,19,'Psalms','OT',9,2,'I will be glad and rejoice in thee: I will sing praise to thy name, O thou most High.'),
(14027,19,'Psalms','OT',9,3,'When mine enemies are turned back, they shall fall and perish at thy presence.'),
(14028,19,'Psalms','OT',9,4,'For thou hast maintained my right and my cause; thou satest in the throne judging right. {maintained...: Heb. made my judgment} {judging right: Heb. judging in righteousness}'),
(14029,19,'Psalms','OT',9,5,'Thou hast rebuked the heathen, thou hast destroyed the wicked, thou hast put out their name for ever and ever.'),
(14030,19,'Psalms','OT',9,6,'O thou enemy, destructions are come to a perpetual end: and thou hast destroyed cities; their memorial is perished with them. {O thou...: or, The destructions of the enemy are come to a perpetual end: and their cities hast thou destroyed, etc}'),
(14031,19,'Psalms','OT',9,7,'But the LORD shall endure for ever: he hath prepared his throne for judgment.'),
(14032,19,'Psalms','OT',9,8,'And he shall judge the world in righteousness, he shall minister judgment to the people in uprightness.'),
(14033,19,'Psalms','OT',9,9,'The LORD also will be a refuge for the oppressed, a refuge in times of trouble. {a refuge: Heb. an high place}'),
(14034,19,'Psalms','OT',9,10,'And they that know thy name will put their trust in thee: for thou, LORD, hast not forsaken them that seek thee.'),
(14035,19,'Psalms','OT',9,11,'Sing praises to the LORD, which dwelleth in Zion: declare among the people his doings.'),
(14036,19,'Psalms','OT',9,12,'When he maketh inquisition for blood, he remembereth them: he forgetteth not the cry of the humble. {humble: or, afflicted}'),
(14037,19,'Psalms','OT',9,13,'Have mercy upon me, O LORD; consider my trouble {which I suffer} of them that hate me, thou that liftest me up from the gates of death:'),
(14038,19,'Psalms','OT',9,14,'That I may shew forth all thy praise in the gates of the daughter of Zion: I will rejoice in thy salvation.'),
(14039,19,'Psalms','OT',9,15,'The heathen are sunk down in the pit {that} they made: in the net which they hid is their own foot taken.'),
(14040,19,'Psalms','OT',9,16,'The LORD is known {by} the judgment {which} he executeth: the wicked is snared in the work of his own hands. Higgaion. Selah. {Higgaion: that is, Meditation}'),
(14041,19,'Psalms','OT',9,17,'The wicked shall be turned into hell, {and} all the nations that forget God.'),
(14042,19,'Psalms','OT',9,18,'For the needy shall not alway be forgotten: the expectation of the poor shall {not} perish for ever.'),
(14043,19,'Psalms','OT',9,19,'Arise, O LORD; let not man prevail: let the heathen be judged in thy sight.'),
(14044,19,'Psalms','OT',9,20,'Put them in fear, O LORD: {that} the nations may know themselves {to be but} men. Selah.'),
(14045,19,'Psalms','OT',10,1,'Why standest thou afar off, O LORD? {why} hidest thou {thyself} in times of trouble?'),
(14046,19,'Psalms','OT',10,2,'The wicked in {his} pride doth persecute the poor: let them be taken in the devices that they have imagined. {The wicked...: Heb. In the pride of the wicked he doth persecute}'),
(14047,19,'Psalms','OT',10,3,'For the wicked boasteth of his heart\'s desire, and blesseth the covetous, {whom} the LORD abhorreth. {heart\'s: Heb. soul\'s} {blesseth...: or, the covetous blesseth himself, he abhorreth the LORD}'),
(14048,19,'Psalms','OT',10,4,'The wicked, through the pride of his countenance, will not seek {after God}: God {is} not in all his thoughts. {God is...: or, all his thoughts are, There is no God}'),
(14049,19,'Psalms','OT',10,5,'His ways are always grievous; thy judgments {are} far above out of his sight: {as for} all his enemies, he puffeth at them.'),
(14050,19,'Psalms','OT',10,6,'He hath said in his heart, I shall not be moved: for {I shall} never {be} in adversity. {never: Heb. unto generation and generation}'),
(14051,19,'Psalms','OT',10,7,'His mouth is full of cursing and deceit and fraud: under his tongue {is} mischief and vanity. {deceit: Heb. deceits} {vanity: or, iniquity}'),
(14052,19,'Psalms','OT',10,8,'He sitteth in the lurking places of the villages: in the secret places doth he murder the innocent: his eyes are privily set against the poor. {are...: Heb. hide themselves}'),
(14053,19,'Psalms','OT',10,9,'He lieth in wait secretly as a lion in his den: he lieth in wait to catch the poor: he doth catch the poor, when he draweth him into his net. {secretly: Heb. in the secret places}'),
(14054,19,'Psalms','OT',10,10,'He croucheth, {and} humbleth himself, that the poor may fall by his strong ones. {He...: Heb. He breaketh himself} {by...: or, into his strong parts}'),
(14055,19,'Psalms','OT',10,11,'He hath said in his heart, God hath forgotten: he hideth his face; he will never see {it}.'),
(14056,19,'Psalms','OT',10,12,'Arise, O LORD; O God, lift up thine hand: forget not the humble. {humble: or, afflicted}'),
(14057,19,'Psalms','OT',10,13,'Wherefore doth the wicked contemn God? he hath said in his heart, Thou wilt not require {it}.'),
(14058,19,'Psalms','OT',10,14,'Thou hast seen {it}; for thou beholdest mischief and spite, to requite {it} with thy hand: the poor committeth himself unto thee; thou art the helper of the fatherless. {committeth: Heb. leaveth}'),
(14059,19,'Psalms','OT',10,15,'Break thou the arm of the wicked and the evil {man}: seek out his wickedness {till} thou find none.'),
(14060,19,'Psalms','OT',10,16,'The LORD {is} King for ever and ever: the heathen are perished out of his land.'),
(14061,19,'Psalms','OT',10,17,'LORD, thou hast heard the desire of the humble: thou wilt prepare their heart, thou wilt cause thine ear to hear: {prepare: or, establish}'),
(14062,19,'Psalms','OT',10,18,'To judge the fatherless and the oppressed, that the man of the earth may no more oppress. {oppress: or, terrify}'),
(14063,19,'Psalms','OT',11,1,'[To the chief Musician, {A Psalm} of David.] In the LORD put I my trust: how say ye to my soul, Flee {as} a bird to your mountain?'),
(14064,19,'Psalms','OT',11,2,'For, lo, the wicked bend {their} bow, they make ready their arrow upon the string, that they may privily shoot at the upright in heart. {privily: Heb. in darkness}'),
(14065,19,'Psalms','OT',11,3,'If the foundations be destroyed, what can the righteous do?'),
(14066,19,'Psalms','OT',11,4,'The LORD {is} in his holy temple, the LORD\'S throne {is} in heaven: his eyes behold, his eyelids try, the children of men.'),
(14067,19,'Psalms','OT',11,5,'The LORD trieth the righteous: but the wicked and him that loveth violence his soul hateth.'),
(14068,19,'Psalms','OT',11,6,'Upon the wicked he shall rain snares, fire and brimstone, and an horrible tempest: {this shall be} the portion of their cup. {an horrible...: or, a burning tempest}'),
(14069,19,'Psalms','OT',11,7,'For the righteous LORD loveth righteousness; his countenance doth behold the upright.'),
(14070,19,'Psalms','OT',12,1,'[To the chief Musician upon Sheminith, A Psalm of David.] Help, LORD; for the godly man ceaseth; for the faithful fail from among the children of men. {upon...: or, upon the eighth} {Help: or, Save}'),
(14071,19,'Psalms','OT',12,2,'They speak vanity every one with his neighbour: {with} flattering lips {and} with a double heart do they speak. {a double...: Heb. an heart and an heart}'),
(14072,19,'Psalms','OT',12,3,'The LORD shall cut off all flattering lips, {and} the tongue that speaketh proud things: {proud: Heb. great}'),
(14073,19,'Psalms','OT',12,4,'Who have said, With our tongue will we prevail; our lips {are} our own: who {is} lord over us? {are...: Heb. are with us}'),
(14074,19,'Psalms','OT',12,5,'For the oppression of the poor, for the sighing of the needy, now will I arise, saith the LORD; I will set {him} in safety {from him that} puffeth at him. {puffeth...: or, would ensnare him}'),
(14075,19,'Psalms','OT',12,6,'The words of the LORD {are} pure words: {as} silver tried in a furnace of earth, purified seven times.'),
(14076,19,'Psalms','OT',12,7,'Thou shalt keep them, O LORD, thou shalt preserve them from this generation for ever. {them from: Heb. him, etc: that is, every one of them, etc}'),
(14077,19,'Psalms','OT',12,8,'The wicked walk on every side, when the vilest men are exalted. {men: Heb. of the sons of the men}'),
(14078,19,'Psalms','OT',13,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.] How long wilt thou forget me, O LORD? for ever? how long wilt thou hide thy face from me? {chief...: or, overseer}'),
(14079,19,'Psalms','OT',13,2,'How long shall I take counsel in my soul, {having} sorrow in my heart daily? how long shall mine enemy be exalted over me?'),
(14080,19,'Psalms','OT',13,3,'Consider {and} hear me, O LORD my God: lighten mine eyes, lest I sleep the {sleep of} death;'),
(14081,19,'Psalms','OT',13,4,'Lest mine enemy say, I have prevailed against him; {and} those that trouble me rejoice when I am moved.'),
(14082,19,'Psalms','OT',13,5,'But I have trusted in thy mercy; my heart shall rejoice in thy salvation.'),
(14083,19,'Psalms','OT',13,6,'I will sing unto the LORD, because he hath dealt bountifully with me.'),
(14084,19,'Psalms','OT',14,1,'[To the chief Musician, {A Psalm} of David.] The fool hath said in his heart, {There is} no God. They are corrupt, they have done abominable works, {there is} none that doeth good.'),
(14085,19,'Psalms','OT',14,2,'The LORD looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were any that did understand, {and} seek God.'),
(14086,19,'Psalms','OT',14,3,'They are all gone aside, they are {all} together become filthy: {there is} none that doeth good, no, not one. {filthy: Heb. stinking}'),
(14087,19,'Psalms','OT',14,4,'Have all the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people {as} they eat bread, and call not upon the LORD.'),
(14088,19,'Psalms','OT',14,5,'There were they in great fear: for God {is} in the generation of the righteous. {were...: Heb. they feared a fear}'),
(14089,19,'Psalms','OT',14,6,'Ye have shamed the counsel of the poor, because the LORD {is} his refuge.'),
(14090,19,'Psalms','OT',14,7,'Oh that the salvation of Israel {were come} out of Zion! when the LORD bringeth back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, {and} Israel shall be glad. {Oh...: Heb. Who will give}'),
(14091,19,'Psalms','OT',15,1,'[A Psalm of David.] LORD, who shall abide in thy tabernacle? who shall dwell in thy holy hill? {abide: Heb. sojourn}'),
(14092,19,'Psalms','OT',15,2,'He that walketh uprightly, and worketh righteousness, and speaketh the truth in his heart.'),
(14093,19,'Psalms','OT',15,3,'{He that} backbiteth not with his tongue, nor doeth evil to his neighbour, nor taketh up a reproach against his neighbour. {taketh...: or, receiveth, or, endureth}'),
(14094,19,'Psalms','OT',15,4,'In whose eyes a vile person is contemned; but he honoureth them that fear the LORD. {He that} sweareth to {his own} hurt, and changeth not.'),
(14095,19,'Psalms','OT',15,5,'{He that} putteth not out his money to usury, nor taketh reward against the innocent. He that doeth these {things} shall never be moved.'),
(14096,19,'Psalms','OT',16,1,'[Michtam of David.] Preserve me, O God: for in thee do I put my trust. {Michtam: or, A golden Psalm}'),
(14097,19,'Psalms','OT',16,2,'{O my soul}, thou hast said unto the LORD, Thou {art} my Lord: my goodness {extendeth} not to thee;'),
(14098,19,'Psalms','OT',16,3,'{But} to the saints that {are} in the earth, and {to} the excellent, in whom {is} all my delight.'),
(14099,19,'Psalms','OT',16,4,'Their sorrows shall be multiplied {that} hasten {after} another {god}: their drink offerings of blood will I not offer, nor take up their names into my lips. {hasten...: or, give gifts to another}'),
(14100,19,'Psalms','OT',16,5,'The LORD {is} the portion of mine inheritance and of my cup: thou maintainest my lot. {of mine...: Heb. of my part}'),
(14101,19,'Psalms','OT',16,6,'The lines are fallen unto me in pleasant {places}; yea, I have a goodly heritage.'),
(14102,19,'Psalms','OT',16,7,'I will bless the LORD, who hath given me counsel: my reins also instruct me in the night seasons.'),
(14103,19,'Psalms','OT',16,8,'I have set the LORD always before me: because {he is} at my right hand, I shall not be moved.'),
(14104,19,'Psalms','OT',16,9,'Therefore my heart is glad, and my glory rejoiceth: my flesh also shall rest in hope. {rest...: Heb. dwell confidently}'),
(14105,19,'Psalms','OT',16,10,'For thou wilt not leave my soul in hell; neither wilt thou suffer thine Holy One to see corruption.'),
(14106,19,'Psalms','OT',16,11,'Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence {is} fulness of joy; at thy right hand {there are} pleasures for evermore.'),
(14107,19,'Psalms','OT',17,1,'[A Prayer of David.] Hear the right, O LORD, attend unto my cry, give ear unto my prayer, {that goeth} not out of feigned lips. {the right: Heb. justice} {not...: Heb. without lips of deceit}'),
(14108,19,'Psalms','OT',17,2,'Let my sentence come forth from thy presence; let thine eyes behold the things that are equal.'),
(14109,19,'Psalms','OT',17,3,'Thou hast proved mine heart; thou hast visited {me} in the night; thou hast tried me, {and} shalt find nothing; I am purposed {that} my mouth shall not transgress.'),
(14110,19,'Psalms','OT',17,4,'Concerning the works of men, by the word of thy lips I have kept {me from} the paths of the destroyer.'),
(14111,19,'Psalms','OT',17,5,'Hold up my goings in thy paths, {that} my footsteps slip not. {slip...: Heb. be not moved}'),
(14112,19,'Psalms','OT',17,6,'I have called upon thee, for thou wilt hear me, O God: incline thine ear unto me, {and hear} my speech.'),
(14113,19,'Psalms','OT',17,7,'Shew thy marvellous lovingkindness, O thou that savest by thy right hand them which put their trust {in thee} from those that rise up {against them}. {by thy...: or, them which trust in thee from those that rise up against thy right hand}'),
(14114,19,'Psalms','OT',17,8,'Keep me as the apple of the eye, hide me under the shadow of thy wings,'),
(14115,19,'Psalms','OT',17,9,'From the wicked that oppress me, {from} my deadly enemies, {who} compass me about. {oppress: Heb. waste} {my...: Heb. my enemies against the soul}'),
(14116,19,'Psalms','OT',17,10,'They are inclosed in their own fat: with their mouth they speak proudly.'),
(14117,19,'Psalms','OT',17,11,'They have now compassed us in our steps: they have set their eyes bowing down to the earth;'),
(14118,19,'Psalms','OT',17,12,'Like as a lion {that} is greedy of his prey, and as it were a young lion lurking in secret places. {Like...: Heb. The likeness of him (that is, of every one of them) is as a lion that desireth to ravin} {lurking: Heb. sitting}'),
(14119,19,'Psalms','OT',17,13,'Arise, O LORD, disappoint him, cast him down: deliver my soul from the wicked, {which is} thy sword: {disappoint...: Heb. prevent his face} {which is: or, by}'),
(14120,19,'Psalms','OT',17,14,'From men {which are} thy hand, O LORD, from men of the world, {which have} their portion in {this} life, and whose belly thou fillest with thy hid {treasure}: they are full of children, and leave the rest of their {substance} to their babes. {which are: or, by} {they...: or, their children are full}'),
(14121,19,'Psalms','OT',17,15,'As for me, I will behold thy face in righteousness: I shall be satisfied, when I awake, with thy likeness.'),
(14122,19,'Psalms','OT',18,1,'[To the chief Musician, {A Psalm} of David, the servant of the LORD, who spake unto the LORD the words of this song in the day {that} the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul: And he said,] I will love thee, O LORD, my strength.'),
(14123,19,'Psalms','OT',18,2,'The LORD {is} my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, {and} my high tower. {my strength: Heb. my rock}'),
(14124,19,'Psalms','OT',18,3,'I will call upon the LORD, {who is worthy} to be praised: so shall I be saved from mine enemies.'),
(14125,19,'Psalms','OT',18,4,'The sorrows of death compassed me, and the floods of ungodly men made me afraid. {ungodly men: Heb. Belial}'),
(14126,19,'Psalms','OT',18,5,'The sorrows of hell compassed me about: the snares of death prevented me. {sorrows: or, cords}'),
(14127,19,'Psalms','OT',18,6,'In my distress I called upon the LORD, and cried unto my God: he heard my voice out of his temple, and my cry came before him, {even} into his ears.'),
(14128,19,'Psalms','OT',18,7,'Then the earth shook and trembled; the foundations also of the hills moved and were shaken, because he was wroth.'),
(14129,19,'Psalms','OT',18,8,'There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it. {out of his nostrils: Heb. by his, etc}'),
(14130,19,'Psalms','OT',18,9,'He bowed the heavens also, and came down: and darkness {was} under his feet.'),
(14131,19,'Psalms','OT',18,10,'And he rode upon a cherub, and did fly: yea, he did fly upon the wings of the wind.'),
(14132,19,'Psalms','OT',18,11,'He made darkness his secret place; his pavilion round about him {were} dark waters {and} thick clouds of the skies.'),
(14133,19,'Psalms','OT',18,12,'At the brightness {that was} before him his thick clouds passed, hail {stones} and coals of fire.'),
(14134,19,'Psalms','OT',18,13,'The LORD also thundered in the heavens, and the Highest gave his voice; hail {stones} and coals of fire.'),
(14135,19,'Psalms','OT',18,14,'Yea, he sent out his arrows, and scattered them; and he shot out lightnings, and discomfited them.'),
(14136,19,'Psalms','OT',18,15,'Then the channels of waters were seen, and the foundations of the world were discovered at thy rebuke, O LORD, at the blast of the breath of thy nostrils.'),
(14137,19,'Psalms','OT',18,16,'He sent from above, he took me, he drew me out of many waters. {many: or, great}'),
(14138,19,'Psalms','OT',18,17,'He delivered me from my strong enemy, and from them which hated me: for they were too strong for me.'),
(14139,19,'Psalms','OT',18,18,'They prevented me in the day of my calamity: but the LORD was my stay.'),
(14140,19,'Psalms','OT',18,19,'He brought me forth also into a large place; he delivered me, because he delighted in me.'),
(14141,19,'Psalms','OT',18,20,'The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness; according to the cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me.'),
(14142,19,'Psalms','OT',18,21,'For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and have not wickedly departed from my God.'),
(14143,19,'Psalms','OT',18,22,'For all his judgments {were} before me, and I did not put away his statutes from me.'),
(14144,19,'Psalms','OT',18,23,'I was also upright before him, and I kept myself from mine iniquity. {before: Heb. with}'),
(14145,19,'Psalms','OT',18,24,'Therefore hath the LORD recompensed me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in his eyesight. {in...: Heb. before his eyes}'),
(14146,19,'Psalms','OT',18,25,'With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful; with an upright man thou wilt shew thyself upright;'),
(14147,19,'Psalms','OT',18,26,'With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure; and with the froward thou wilt shew thyself froward. {shew thyself froward: or, wrestle}'),
(14148,19,'Psalms','OT',18,27,'For thou wilt save the afflicted people; but wilt bring down high looks.'),
(14149,19,'Psalms','OT',18,28,'For thou wilt light my candle: the LORD my God will enlighten my darkness. {candle: or, lamp}'),
(14150,19,'Psalms','OT',18,29,'For by thee I have run through a troop; and by my God have I leaped over a wall. {run...: or, broken}'),
(14151,19,'Psalms','OT',18,30,'{As for} God, his way {is} perfect: the word of the LORD is tried: he {is} a buckler to all those that trust in him. {tried: or, refined}'),
(14152,19,'Psalms','OT',18,31,'For who {is} God save the LORD? or who {is} a rock save our God?'),
(14153,19,'Psalms','OT',18,32,'{It is} God that girdeth me with strength, and maketh my way perfect.'),
(14154,19,'Psalms','OT',18,33,'He maketh my feet like hinds\' {feet}, and setteth me upon my high places.'),
(14155,19,'Psalms','OT',18,34,'He teacheth my hands to war, so that a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.'),
(14156,19,'Psalms','OT',18,35,'Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation: and thy right hand hath holden me up, and thy gentleness hath made me great. {thy gentleness...: or, with thy meekness thou hast multiplied me}'),
(14157,19,'Psalms','OT',18,36,'Thou hast enlarged my steps under me, that my feet did not slip. {my feet: Heb. mine ankles}'),
(14158,19,'Psalms','OT',18,37,'I have pursued mine enemies, and overtaken them: neither did I turn again till they were consumed.'),
(14159,19,'Psalms','OT',18,38,'I have wounded them that they were not able to rise: they are fallen under my feet.'),
(14160,19,'Psalms','OT',18,39,'For thou hast girded me with strength unto the battle: thou hast subdued under me those that rose up against me. {subdued: Heb. caused to bow}'),
(14161,19,'Psalms','OT',18,40,'Thou hast also given me the necks of mine enemies; that I might destroy them that hate me.'),
(14162,19,'Psalms','OT',18,41,'They cried, but {there was} none to save {them: even} unto the LORD, but he answered them not.'),
(14163,19,'Psalms','OT',18,42,'Then did I beat them small as the dust before the wind: I did cast them out as the dirt in the streets.'),
(14164,19,'Psalms','OT',18,43,'Thou hast delivered me from the strivings of the people; {and} thou hast made me the head of the heathen: a people {whom} I have not known shall serve me.'),
(14165,19,'Psalms','OT',18,44,'As soon as they hear of me, they shall obey me: the strangers shall submit themselves unto me. {As soon...: Heb. At the hearing of the ear} {submit...: or, yield feigned obedience} {strangers: Heb. sons of the stranger}'),
(14166,19,'Psalms','OT',18,45,'The strangers shall fade away, and be afraid out of their close places. {strangers: Heb. sons of the stranger}'),
(14167,19,'Psalms','OT',18,46,'The LORD liveth; and blessed {be} my rock; and let the God of my salvation be exalted.'),
(14168,19,'Psalms','OT',18,47,'{It is} God that avengeth me, and subdueth the people under me. {avengeth: Heb. giveth avengements for} {subdueth: or, destroyeth}'),
(14169,19,'Psalms','OT',18,48,'He delivereth me from mine enemies: yea, thou liftest me up above those that rise up against me: thou hast delivered me from the violent man. {violent...: Heb. man of violence}'),
(14170,19,'Psalms','OT',18,49,'Therefore will I give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the heathen, and sing praises unto thy name. {give...: or, confess}'),
(14171,19,'Psalms','OT',18,50,'Great deliverance giveth he to his king; and sheweth mercy to his anointed, to David, and to his seed for evermore.'),
(14172,19,'Psalms','OT',19,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.] The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth his handywork.'),
(14173,19,'Psalms','OT',19,2,'Day unto day uttereth speech, and night unto night sheweth knowledge.'),
(14174,19,'Psalms','OT',19,3,'{There is} no speech nor language, {where} their voice is not heard. {where...: or, without these their voice is heard: Heb. without their voice heard}'),
(14175,19,'Psalms','OT',19,4,'Their line is gone out through all the earth, and their words to the end of the world. In them hath he set a tabernacle for the sun, {line: or, rule, or, direction}'),
(14176,19,'Psalms','OT',19,5,'Which {is} as a bridegroom coming out of his chamber, {and} rejoiceth as a strong man to run a race.'),
(14177,19,'Psalms','OT',19,6,'His going forth {is} from the end of the heaven, and his circuit unto the ends of it: and there is nothing hid from the heat thereof.'),
(14178,19,'Psalms','OT',19,7,'The law of the LORD {is} perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of the LORD {is} sure, making wise the simple. {law: or, doctrine} {converting: or, restoring}'),
(14179,19,'Psalms','OT',19,8,'The statutes of the LORD {are} right, rejoicing the heart: the commandment of the LORD {is} pure, enlightening the eyes.'),
(14180,19,'Psalms','OT',19,9,'The fear of the LORD {is} clean, enduring for ever: the judgments of the LORD {are} true {and} righteous altogether. {true: Heb. truth}'),
(14181,19,'Psalms','OT',19,10,'More to be desired {are they} than gold, yea, than much fine gold: sweeter also than honey and the honeycomb. {the honeycomb: Heb. the dropping of honeycombs}'),
(14182,19,'Psalms','OT',19,11,'Moreover by them is thy servant warned: {and} in keeping of them {there is} great reward.'),
(14183,19,'Psalms','OT',19,12,'Who can understand {his} errors? cleanse thou me from secret {faults}.'),
(14184,19,'Psalms','OT',19,13,'Keep back thy servant also from presumptuous {sins}; let them not have dominion over me: then shall I be upright, and I shall be innocent from the great transgression. {the great: or, much}'),
(14185,19,'Psalms','OT',19,14,'Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my strength, and my redeemer. {strength: Heb. rock}'),
(14186,19,'Psalms','OT',20,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.] The LORD hear thee in the day of trouble; the name of the God of Jacob defend thee; {defend...: Heb. set thee on an high place}'),
(14187,19,'Psalms','OT',20,2,'Send thee help from the sanctuary, and strengthen thee out of Zion; {thee help: Heb. thy help} {strengthen: Heb. support}'),
(14188,19,'Psalms','OT',20,3,'Remember all thy offerings, and accept thy burnt sacrifice; Selah. {accept: Heb. turn to ashes: or, make fat}'),
(14189,19,'Psalms','OT',20,4,'Grant thee according to thine own heart, and fulfil all thy counsel.'),
(14190,19,'Psalms','OT',20,5,'We will rejoice in thy salvation, and in the name of our God we will set up {our} banners: the LORD fulfil all thy petitions.'),
(14191,19,'Psalms','OT',20,6,'Now know I that the LORD saveth his anointed; he will hear him from his holy heaven with the saving strength of his right hand. {his holy...: Heb. the heaven of his holiness} {with...: Heb. by the strength of the salvation of}'),
(14192,19,'Psalms','OT',20,7,'Some {trust} in chariots, and some in horses: but we will remember the name of the LORD our God.'),
(14193,19,'Psalms','OT',20,8,'They are brought down and fallen: but we are risen, and stand upright.'),
(14194,19,'Psalms','OT',20,9,'Save, LORD: let the king hear us when we call.'),
(14195,19,'Psalms','OT',21,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.] The king shall joy in thy strength, O LORD; and in thy salvation how greatly shall he rejoice!'),
(14196,19,'Psalms','OT',21,2,'Thou hast given him his heart\'s desire, and hast not withholden the request of his lips. Selah.'),
(14197,19,'Psalms','OT',21,3,'For thou preventest him with the blessings of goodness: thou settest a crown of pure gold on his head.'),
(14198,19,'Psalms','OT',21,4,'He asked life of thee, {and} thou gavest {it} him, {even} length of days for ever and ever.'),
(14199,19,'Psalms','OT',21,5,'His glory {is} great in thy salvation: honour and majesty hast thou laid upon him.'),
(14200,19,'Psalms','OT',21,6,'For thou hast made him most blessed for ever: thou hast made him exceeding glad with thy countenance. {made him most...: Heb. set him to be blessings} {made him exceeding...: Heb. make him glad with joy}'),
(14201,19,'Psalms','OT',21,7,'For the king trusteth in the LORD, and through the mercy of the most High he shall not be moved.'),
(14202,19,'Psalms','OT',21,8,'Thine hand shall find out all thine enemies: thy right hand shall find out those that hate thee.'),
(14203,19,'Psalms','OT',21,9,'Thou shalt make them as a fiery oven in the time of thine anger: the LORD shall swallow them up in his wrath, and the fire shall devour them.'),
(14204,19,'Psalms','OT',21,10,'Their fruit shalt thou destroy from the earth, and their seed from among the children of men.'),
(14205,19,'Psalms','OT',21,11,'For they intended evil against thee: they imagined a mischievous device, {which} they are not able {to perform}.'),
(14206,19,'Psalms','OT',21,12,'Therefore shalt thou make them turn their back, {when} thou shalt make ready {thine arrows} upon thy strings against the face of them. {shalt thou...: or, thou shalt set them as a butt} {back: Heb. shoulder}'),
(14207,19,'Psalms','OT',21,13,'Be thou exalted, LORD, in thine own strength: {so} will we sing and praise thy power.'),
(14208,19,'Psalms','OT',22,1,'[To the chief Musician upon Aijeleth Shahar, A Psalm of David.] My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me? {why art thou so} far from helping me, {and from} the words of my roaring? {Aijeleth...: or, the hind of the morning} {helping...: Heb. my salvation}'),
(14209,19,'Psalms','OT',22,2,'O my God, I cry in the daytime, but thou hearest not; and in the night season, and am not silent. {am...: Heb. there is no silence to me}'),
(14210,19,'Psalms','OT',22,3,'But thou {art} holy, {O thou} that inhabitest the praises of Israel.'),
(14211,19,'Psalms','OT',22,4,'Our fathers trusted in thee: they trusted, and thou didst deliver them.'),
(14212,19,'Psalms','OT',22,5,'They cried unto thee, and were delivered: they trusted in thee, and were not confounded.'),
(14213,19,'Psalms','OT',22,6,'But I {am} a worm, and no man; a reproach of men, and despised of the people.'),
(14214,19,'Psalms','OT',22,7,'All they that see me laugh me to scorn: they shoot out the lip, they shake the head, {saying}, {shoot...: Heb. open}'),
(14215,19,'Psalms','OT',22,8,'He trusted on the LORD {that} he would deliver him: let him deliver him, seeing he delighted in him. {He trusted...: Heb. He rolled himself on} {seeing...: or, if he delight in}'),
(14216,19,'Psalms','OT',22,9,'But thou {art} he that took me out of the womb: thou didst make me hope {when I was} upon my mother\'s breasts. {didst...: or, kept me in safety}'),
(14217,19,'Psalms','OT',22,10,'I was cast upon thee from the womb: thou {art} my God from my mother\'s belly.'),
(14218,19,'Psalms','OT',22,11,'Be not far from me; for trouble {is} near; for {there is} none to help. {none...: Heb. not a helper}'),
(14219,19,'Psalms','OT',22,12,'Many bulls have compassed me: strong {bulls} of Bashan have beset me round.'),
(14220,19,'Psalms','OT',22,13,'They gaped upon me {with} their mouths, {as} a ravening and a roaring lion. {gaped...: Heb. opened their mouths against me}'),
(14221,19,'Psalms','OT',22,14,'I am poured out like water, and all my bones are out of joint: my heart is like wax; it is melted in the midst of my bowels. {out of...: or, sundered}'),
(14222,19,'Psalms','OT',22,15,'My strength is dried up like a potsherd; and my tongue cleaveth to my jaws; and thou hast brought me into the dust of death.'),
(14223,19,'Psalms','OT',22,16,'For dogs have compassed me: the assembly of the wicked have inclosed me: they pierced my hands and my feet.'),
(14224,19,'Psalms','OT',22,17,'I may tell all my bones: they look {and} stare upon me.'),
(14225,19,'Psalms','OT',22,18,'They part my garments among them, and cast lots upon my vesture.'),
(14226,19,'Psalms','OT',22,19,'But be not thou far from me, O LORD: O my strength, haste thee to help me.'),
(14227,19,'Psalms','OT',22,20,'Deliver my soul from the sword; my darling from the power of the dog. {my darling: Heb. my only one} {power: Heb. hand}'),
(14228,19,'Psalms','OT',22,21,'Save me from the lion\'s mouth: for thou hast heard me from the horns of the unicorns.'),
(14229,19,'Psalms','OT',22,22,'I will declare thy name unto my brethren: in the midst of the congregation will I praise thee.'),
(14230,19,'Psalms','OT',22,23,'Ye that fear the LORD, praise him; all ye the seed of Jacob, glorify him; and fear him, all ye the seed of Israel.'),
(14231,19,'Psalms','OT',22,24,'For he hath not despised nor abhorred the affliction of the afflicted; neither hath he hid his face from him; but when he cried unto him, he heard.'),
(14232,19,'Psalms','OT',22,25,'My praise {shall be} of thee in the great congregation: I will pay my vows before them that fear him.'),
(14233,19,'Psalms','OT',22,26,'The meek shall eat and be satisfied: they shall praise the LORD that seek him: your heart shall live for ever.'),
(14234,19,'Psalms','OT',22,27,'All the ends of the world shall remember and turn unto the LORD: and all the kindreds of the nations shall worship before thee.'),
(14235,19,'Psalms','OT',22,28,'For the kingdom {is} the LORD\'S: and he {is} the governor among the nations.'),
(14236,19,'Psalms','OT',22,29,'All {they that be} fat upon earth shall eat and worship: all they that go down to the dust shall bow before him: and none can keep alive his own soul.'),
(14237,19,'Psalms','OT',22,30,'A seed shall serve him; it shall be accounted to the Lord for a generation.'),
(14238,19,'Psalms','OT',22,31,'They shall come, and shall declare his righteousness unto a people that shall be born, that he hath done {this}.'),
(14239,19,'Psalms','OT',23,1,'[A Psalm of David.] The LORD {is} my shepherd; I shall not want.'),
(14240,19,'Psalms','OT',23,2,'He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters. {green...: Heb. pastures of tender grass} {still...: Heb. waters of quietness}'),
(14241,19,'Psalms','OT',23,3,'He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name\'s sake.'),
(14242,19,'Psalms','OT',23,4,'Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou {art} with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.'),
(14243,19,'Psalms','OT',23,5,'Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over. {anointest: Heb. makest fat}'),
(14244,19,'Psalms','OT',23,6,'Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the LORD for ever. {for ever: Heb. to length of days}'),
(14245,19,'Psalms','OT',24,1,'[A Psalm of David.] The earth {is} the LORD\'S, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein.'),
(14246,19,'Psalms','OT',24,2,'For he hath founded it upon the seas, and established it upon the floods.'),
(14247,19,'Psalms','OT',24,3,'Who shall ascend into the hill of the LORD? or who shall stand in his holy place?'),
(14248,19,'Psalms','OT',24,4,'He that hath clean hands, and a pure heart; who hath not lifted up his soul unto vanity, nor sworn deceitfully. {He...: Heb. The clean of hands}'),
(14249,19,'Psalms','OT',24,5,'He shall receive the blessing from the LORD, and righteousness from the God of his salvation.'),
(14250,19,'Psalms','OT',24,6,'This {is} the generation of them that seek him, that seek thy face, O Jacob. Selah. {O Jacob: or, O God of Jacob}'),
(14251,19,'Psalms','OT',24,7,'Lift up your heads, O ye gates; and be ye lift up, ye everlasting doors; and the King of glory shall come in.'),
(14252,19,'Psalms','OT',24,8,'Who {is} this King of glory? The LORD strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in battle.'),
(14253,19,'Psalms','OT',24,9,'Lift up your heads, O ye gates; even lift {them} up, ye everlasting doors; and the King of glory shall come in.'),
(14254,19,'Psalms','OT',24,10,'Who is this King of glory? The LORD of hosts, he {is} the King of glory. Selah.'),
(14255,19,'Psalms','OT',25,1,'[{A Psalm} of David.] Unto thee, O LORD, do I lift up my soul.'),
(14256,19,'Psalms','OT',25,2,'O my God, I trust in thee: let me not be ashamed, let not mine enemies triumph over me.'),
(14257,19,'Psalms','OT',25,3,'Yea, let none that wait on thee be ashamed: let them be ashamed which transgress without cause.'),
(14258,19,'Psalms','OT',25,4,'Shew me thy ways, O LORD; teach me thy paths.'),
(14259,19,'Psalms','OT',25,5,'Lead me in thy truth, and teach me: for thou {art} the God of my salvation; on thee do I wait all the day.'),
(14260,19,'Psalms','OT',25,6,'Remember, O LORD, thy tender mercies and thy lovingkindnesses; for they {have been} ever of old. {tender...: Heb. bowels}'),
(14261,19,'Psalms','OT',25,7,'Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions: according to thy mercy remember thou me for thy goodness\' sake, O LORD.'),
(14262,19,'Psalms','OT',25,8,'Good and upright {is} the LORD: therefore will he teach sinners in the way.'),
(14263,19,'Psalms','OT',25,9,'The meek will he guide in judgment: and the meek will he teach his way.'),
(14264,19,'Psalms','OT',25,10,'All the paths of the LORD {are} mercy and truth unto such as keep his covenant and his testimonies.'),
(14265,19,'Psalms','OT',25,11,'For thy name\'s sake, O LORD, pardon mine iniquity; for it {is} great.'),
(14266,19,'Psalms','OT',25,12,'What man {is} he that feareth the LORD? him shall he teach in the way {that} he shall choose.'),
(14267,19,'Psalms','OT',25,13,'His soul shall dwell at ease; and his seed shall inherit the earth. {dwell...: Heb. lodge in goodness}'),
(14268,19,'Psalms','OT',25,14,'The secret of the LORD {is} with them that fear him; and he will shew them his covenant. {and...: or, and his covenant to make them know it}'),
(14269,19,'Psalms','OT',25,15,'Mine eyes {are} ever toward the LORD; for he shall pluck my feet out of the net. {pluck: Heb. bring forth}'),
(14270,19,'Psalms','OT',25,16,'Turn thee unto me, and have mercy upon me; for I {am} desolate and afflicted.'),
(14271,19,'Psalms','OT',25,17,'The troubles of my heart are enlarged: {O} bring thou me out of my distresses.'),
(14272,19,'Psalms','OT',25,18,'Look upon mine affliction and my pain; and forgive all my sins.'),
(14273,19,'Psalms','OT',25,19,'Consider mine enemies; for they are many; and they hate me with cruel hatred. {cruel...: Heb. hatred of violence}'),
(14274,19,'Psalms','OT',25,20,'O keep my soul, and deliver me: let me not be ashamed; for I put my trust in thee.'),
(14275,19,'Psalms','OT',25,21,'Let integrity and uprightness preserve me; for I wait on thee.'),
(14276,19,'Psalms','OT',25,22,'Redeem Israel, O God, out of all his troubles.'),
(14277,19,'Psalms','OT',26,1,'[{A Psalm} of David.] Judge me, O LORD; for I have walked in mine integrity: I have trusted also in the LORD; {therefore} I shall not slide.'),
(14278,19,'Psalms','OT',26,2,'Examine me, O LORD, and prove me; try my reins and my heart.'),
(14279,19,'Psalms','OT',26,3,'For thy lovingkindness {is} before mine eyes: and I have walked in thy truth.'),
(14280,19,'Psalms','OT',26,4,'I have not sat with vain persons, neither will I go in with dissemblers.'),
(14281,19,'Psalms','OT',26,5,'I have hated the congregation of evil doers; and will not sit with the wicked.'),
(14282,19,'Psalms','OT',26,6,'I will wash mine hands in innocency: so will I compass thine altar, O LORD:'),
(14283,19,'Psalms','OT',26,7,'That I may publish with the voice of thanksgiving, and tell of all thy wondrous works.'),
(14284,19,'Psalms','OT',26,8,'LORD, I have loved the habitation of thy house, and the place where thine honour dwelleth. {where...: Heb. of the tabernacle of thy honour}'),
(14285,19,'Psalms','OT',26,9,'Gather not my soul with sinners, nor my life with bloody men: {Gather...: or, Take not away} {bloody...: Heb. men of blood}'),
(14286,19,'Psalms','OT',26,10,'In whose hands {is} mischief, and their right hand is full of bribes. {full...: Heb. filled with}'),
(14287,19,'Psalms','OT',26,11,'But as for me, I will walk in mine integrity: redeem me, and be merciful unto me.'),
(14288,19,'Psalms','OT',26,12,'My foot standeth in an even place: in the congregations will I bless the LORD.'),
(14289,19,'Psalms','OT',27,1,'[{A Psalm} of David.] The LORD {is} my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the LORD {is} the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?'),
(14290,19,'Psalms','OT',27,2,'When the wicked, {even} mine enemies and my foes, came upon me to eat up my flesh, they stumbled and fell. {came...: Heb. approached against me}'),
(14291,19,'Psalms','OT',27,3,'Though an host should encamp against me, my heart shall not fear: though war should rise against me, in this {will} I {be} confident.'),
(14292,19,'Psalms','OT',27,4,'One {thing} have I desired of the LORD, that will I seek after; that I may dwell in the house of the LORD all the days of my life, to behold the beauty of the LORD, and to enquire in his temple. {the beauty: or, the delight}'),
(14293,19,'Psalms','OT',27,5,'For in the time of trouble he shall hide me in his pavilion: in the secret of his tabernacle shall he hide me; he shall set me up upon a rock.'),
(14294,19,'Psalms','OT',27,6,'And now shall mine head be lifted up above mine enemies round about me: therefore will I offer in his tabernacle sacrifices of joy; I will sing, yea, I will sing praises unto the LORD. {joy: Heb. shouting}'),
(14295,19,'Psalms','OT',27,7,'Hear, O LORD, {when} I cry with my voice: have mercy also upon me, and answer me.'),
(14296,19,'Psalms','OT',27,8,'{When thou saidst}, Seek ye my face; my heart said unto thee, Thy face, LORD, will I seek. {When...: or, My heart said unto thee, Let my face seek thy face, etc}'),
(14297,19,'Psalms','OT',27,9,'Hide not thy face {far} from me; put not thy servant away in anger: thou hast been my help; leave me not, neither forsake me, O God of my salvation.'),
(14298,19,'Psalms','OT',27,10,'When my father and my mother forsake me, then the LORD will take me up. {take...: Heb. gather me}'),
(14299,19,'Psalms','OT',27,11,'Teach me thy way, O LORD, and lead me in a plain path, because of mine enemies. {a plain...: Heb. a way of plainness} {mine...: Heb. those which observe me}'),
(14300,19,'Psalms','OT',27,12,'Deliver me not over unto the will of mine enemies: for false witnesses are risen up against me, and such as breathe out cruelty.'),
(14301,19,'Psalms','OT',27,13,'{I had fainted}, unless I had believed to see the goodness of the LORD in the land of the living.'),
(14302,19,'Psalms','OT',27,14,'Wait on the LORD: be of good courage, and he shall strengthen thine heart: wait, I say, on the LORD.'),
(14303,19,'Psalms','OT',28,1,'[{A Psalm} of David.] Unto thee will I cry, O LORD my rock; be not silent to me: lest, {if} thou be silent to me, I become like them that go down into the pit. {to me: Heb. from me}'),
(14304,19,'Psalms','OT',28,2,'Hear the voice of my supplications, when I cry unto thee, when I lift up my hands toward thy holy oracle. {thy...: or, the oracle of thy sanctuary}'),
(14305,19,'Psalms','OT',28,3,'Draw me not away with the wicked, and with the workers of iniquity, which speak peace to their neighbours, but mischief {is} in their hearts.'),
(14306,19,'Psalms','OT',28,4,'Give them according to their deeds, and according to the wickedness of their endeavours: give them after the work of their hands; render to them their desert.'),
(14307,19,'Psalms','OT',28,5,'Because they regard not the works of the LORD, nor the operation of his hands, he shall destroy them, and not build them up.'),
(14308,19,'Psalms','OT',28,6,'Blessed {be} the LORD, because he hath heard the voice of my supplications.'),
(14309,19,'Psalms','OT',28,7,'The LORD {is} my strength and my shield; my heart trusted in him, and I am helped: therefore my heart greatly rejoiceth; and with my song will I praise him.'),
(14310,19,'Psalms','OT',28,8,'The LORD {is} their strength, and he {is} the saving strength of his anointed. {their: or, his} {saving...: Heb. strength of salvations}'),
(14311,19,'Psalms','OT',28,9,'Save thy people, and bless thine inheritance: feed them also, and lift them up for ever. {feed: or, rule}'),
(14312,19,'Psalms','OT',29,1,'[A Psalm of David.] Give unto the LORD, O ye mighty, give unto the LORD glory and strength. {ye mighty: Heb. ye sons of the mighty}'),
(14313,19,'Psalms','OT',29,2,'Give unto the LORD the glory due unto his name; worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness. {the glory...: Heb. the honour of his name} {in...: or, in his glorious sanctuary}'),
(14314,19,'Psalms','OT',29,3,'The voice of the LORD {is} upon the waters: the God of glory thundereth: the LORD {is} upon many waters. {many: or, great}'),
(14315,19,'Psalms','OT',29,4,'The voice of the LORD {is} powerful; the voice of the LORD {is} full of majesty. {powerful: Heb. in power} {full...: Heb. in majesty}'),
(14316,19,'Psalms','OT',29,5,'The voice of the LORD breaketh the cedars; yea, the LORD breaketh the cedars of Lebanon.'),
(14317,19,'Psalms','OT',29,6,'He maketh them also to skip like a calf; Lebanon and Sirion like a young unicorn.'),
(14318,19,'Psalms','OT',29,7,'The voice of the LORD divideth the flames of fire. {divideth: Heb. cutteth out}'),
(14319,19,'Psalms','OT',29,8,'The voice of the LORD shaketh the wilderness; the LORD shaketh the wilderness of Kadesh.'),
(14320,19,'Psalms','OT',29,9,'The voice of the LORD maketh the hinds to calve, and discovereth the forests: and in his temple doth every one speak of {his} glory. {to calve: or, to be in pain} {doth...: or, every whit of it uttereth, etc}'),
(14321,19,'Psalms','OT',29,10,'The LORD sitteth upon the flood; yea, the LORD sitteth King for ever.'),
(14322,19,'Psalms','OT',29,11,'The LORD will give strength unto his people; the LORD will bless his people with peace.'),
(14323,19,'Psalms','OT',30,1,'[A Psalm {and} Song {at} the dedication of the house of David.] I will extol thee, O LORD; for thou hast lifted me up, and hast not made my foes to rejoice over me.'),
(14324,19,'Psalms','OT',30,2,'O LORD my God, I cried unto thee, and thou hast healed me.'),
(14325,19,'Psalms','OT',30,3,'O LORD, thou hast brought up my soul from the grave: thou hast kept me alive, that I should not go down to the pit.'),
(14326,19,'Psalms','OT',30,4,'Sing unto the LORD, O ye saints of his, and give thanks at the remembrance of his holiness. {at...: or, to the memorial}'),
(14327,19,'Psalms','OT',30,5,'For his anger {endureth but} a moment; in his favour {is} life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy {cometh} in the morning. {his anger...: Heb. there is but a moment in his anger} {for a night: Heb. in the evening} {joy: Heb. singing}'),
(14328,19,'Psalms','OT',30,6,'And in my prosperity I said, I shall never be moved.'),
(14329,19,'Psalms','OT',30,7,'LORD, by thy favour thou hast made my mountain to stand strong: thou didst hide thy face, {and} I was troubled. {made...: Heb. settled strength for my mountain}'),
(14330,19,'Psalms','OT',30,8,'I cried to thee, O LORD; and unto the LORD I made supplication.'),
(14331,19,'Psalms','OT',30,9,'What profit {is there} in my blood, when I go down to the pit? Shall the dust praise thee? shall it declare thy truth?'),
(14332,19,'Psalms','OT',30,10,'Hear, O LORD, and have mercy upon me: LORD, be thou my helper.'),
(14333,19,'Psalms','OT',30,11,'Thou hast turned for me my mourning into dancing: thou hast put off my sackcloth, and girded me with gladness;'),
(14334,19,'Psalms','OT',30,12,'To the end that {my} glory may sing praise to thee, and not be silent. O LORD my God, I will give thanks unto thee for ever. {my glory: that is, my tongue, or, my soul}'),
(14335,19,'Psalms','OT',31,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.] In thee, O LORD, do I put my trust; let me never be ashamed: deliver me in thy righteousness.'),
(14336,19,'Psalms','OT',31,2,'Bow down thine ear to me; deliver me speedily: be thou my strong rock, for an house of defence to save me. {my...: Heb. to me for a rock of strength}'),
(14337,19,'Psalms','OT',31,3,'For thou {art} my rock and my fortress; therefore for thy name\'s sake lead me, and guide me.'),
(14338,19,'Psalms','OT',31,4,'Pull me out of the net that they have laid privily for me: for thou {art} my strength.'),
(14339,19,'Psalms','OT',31,5,'Into thine hand I commit my spirit: thou hast redeemed me, O LORD God of truth.'),
(14340,19,'Psalms','OT',31,6,'I have hated them that regard lying vanities: but I trust in the LORD.'),
(14341,19,'Psalms','OT',31,7,'I will be glad and rejoice in thy mercy: for thou hast considered my trouble; thou hast known my soul in adversities;'),
(14342,19,'Psalms','OT',31,8,'And hast not shut me up into the hand of the enemy: thou hast set my feet in a large room.'),
(14343,19,'Psalms','OT',31,9,'Have mercy upon me, O LORD, for I am in trouble: mine eye is consumed with grief, {yea}, my soul and my belly.'),
(14344,19,'Psalms','OT',31,10,'For my life is spent with grief, and my years with sighing: my strength faileth because of mine iniquity, and my bones are consumed.'),
(14345,19,'Psalms','OT',31,11,'I was a reproach among all mine enemies, but especially among my neighbours, and a fear to mine acquaintance: they that did see me without fled from me.'),
(14346,19,'Psalms','OT',31,12,'I am forgotten as a dead man out of mind: I am like a broken vessel. {a broken...: Heb. a vessel that perisheth}'),
(14347,19,'Psalms','OT',31,13,'For I have heard the slander of many: fear {was} on every side: while they took counsel together against me, they devised to take away my life.'),
(14348,19,'Psalms','OT',31,14,'But I trusted in thee, O LORD: I said, Thou {art} my God.'),
(14349,19,'Psalms','OT',31,15,'My times {are} in thy hand: deliver me from the hand of mine enemies, and from them that persecute me.'),
(14350,19,'Psalms','OT',31,16,'Make thy face to shine upon thy servant: save me for thy mercies\' sake.'),
(14351,19,'Psalms','OT',31,17,'Let me not be ashamed, O LORD; for I have called upon thee: let the wicked be ashamed, {and} let them be silent in the grave. {silent...: or, cut off for}'),
(14352,19,'Psalms','OT',31,18,'Let the lying lips be put to silence; which speak grievous things proudly and contemptuously against the righteous. {grievous...: Heb. a hard thing}'),
(14353,19,'Psalms','OT',31,19,'{Oh} how great {is} thy goodness, which thou hast laid up for them that fear thee; {which} thou hast wrought for them that trust in thee before the sons of men!'),
(14354,19,'Psalms','OT',31,20,'Thou shalt hide them in the secret of thy presence from the pride of man: thou shalt keep them secretly in a pavilion from the strife of tongues.'),
(14355,19,'Psalms','OT',31,21,'Blessed {be} the LORD: for he hath shewed me his marvellous kindness in a strong city. {strong: or, fenced}'),
(14356,19,'Psalms','OT',31,22,'For I said in my haste, I am cut off from before thine eyes: nevertheless thou heardest the voice of my supplications when I cried unto thee.'),
(14357,19,'Psalms','OT',31,23,'O love the LORD, all ye his saints: {for} the LORD preserveth the faithful, and plentifully rewardeth the proud doer.'),
(14358,19,'Psalms','OT',31,24,'Be of good courage, and he shall strengthen your heart, all ye that hope in the LORD.'),
(14359,19,'Psalms','OT',32,1,'[{A Psalm} of David, Maschil.] Blessed {is he whose} transgression {is} forgiven, {whose} sin {is} covered. {A Psalm...: or, A Psalm of David giving instruction}'),
(14360,19,'Psalms','OT',32,2,'Blessed {is} the man unto whom the LORD imputeth not iniquity, and in whose spirit {there is} no guile.'),
(14361,19,'Psalms','OT',32,3,'When I kept silence, my bones waxed old through my roaring all the day long.'),
(14362,19,'Psalms','OT',32,4,'For day and night thy hand was heavy upon me: my moisture is turned into the drought of summer. Selah.'),
(14363,19,'Psalms','OT',32,5,'I acknowledged my sin unto thee, and mine iniquity have I not hid. I said, I will confess my transgressions unto the LORD; and thou forgavest the iniquity of my sin. Selah.'),
(14364,19,'Psalms','OT',32,6,'For this shall every one that is godly pray unto thee in a time when thou mayest be found: surely in the floods of great waters they shall not come nigh unto him. {when...: Heb. of finding}'),
(14365,19,'Psalms','OT',32,7,'Thou {art} my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble; thou shalt compass me about with songs of deliverance. Selah.'),
(14366,19,'Psalms','OT',32,8,'I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye. {guide...: Heb. counsel thee, mine eye shall be upon thee}'),
(14367,19,'Psalms','OT',32,9,'Be ye not as the horse, {or} as the mule, {which} have no understanding: whose mouth must be held in with bit and bridle, lest they come near unto thee.'),
(14368,19,'Psalms','OT',32,10,'Many sorrows {shall be} to the wicked: but he that trusteth in the LORD, mercy shall compass him about.'),
(14369,19,'Psalms','OT',32,11,'Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, ye righteous: and shout for joy, all {ye that are} upright in heart.'),
(14370,19,'Psalms','OT',33,1,'Rejoice in the LORD, O ye righteous: {for} praise is comely for the upright.'),
(14371,19,'Psalms','OT',33,2,'Praise the LORD with harp: sing unto him with the psaltery {and} an instrument of ten strings.'),
(14372,19,'Psalms','OT',33,3,'Sing unto him a new song; play skilfully with a loud noise.'),
(14373,19,'Psalms','OT',33,4,'For the word of the LORD {is} right; and all his works {are done} in truth.'),
(14374,19,'Psalms','OT',33,5,'He loveth righteousness and judgment: the earth is full of the goodness of the LORD. {goodness: or, mercy}'),
(14375,19,'Psalms','OT',33,6,'By the word of the LORD were the heavens made; and all the host of them by the breath of his mouth.'),
(14376,19,'Psalms','OT',33,7,'He gathereth the waters of the sea together as an heap: he layeth up the depth in storehouses.'),
(14377,19,'Psalms','OT',33,8,'Let all the earth fear the LORD: let all the inhabitants of the world stand in awe of him.'),
(14378,19,'Psalms','OT',33,9,'For he spake, and it was {done}; he commanded, and it stood fast.'),
(14379,19,'Psalms','OT',33,10,'The LORD bringeth the counsel of the heathen to nought: he maketh the devices of the people of none effect. {bringeth: Heb. maketh frustrate}'),
(14380,19,'Psalms','OT',33,11,'The counsel of the LORD standeth for ever, the thoughts of his heart to all generations. {to all...: Heb. to generation and generation}'),
(14381,19,'Psalms','OT',33,12,'Blessed {is} the nation whose God {is} the LORD; {and} the people {whom} he hath chosen for his own inheritance.'),
(14382,19,'Psalms','OT',33,13,'The LORD looketh from heaven; he beholdeth all the sons of men.'),
(14383,19,'Psalms','OT',33,14,'From the place of his habitation he looketh upon all the inhabitants of the earth.'),
(14384,19,'Psalms','OT',33,15,'He fashioneth their hearts alike; he considereth all their works.'),
(14385,19,'Psalms','OT',33,16,'There is no king saved by the multitude of an host: a mighty man is not delivered by much strength.'),
(14386,19,'Psalms','OT',33,17,'An horse {is} a vain thing for safety: neither shall he deliver {any} by his great strength.'),
(14387,19,'Psalms','OT',33,18,'Behold, the eye of the LORD {is} upon them that fear him, upon them that hope in his mercy;'),
(14388,19,'Psalms','OT',33,19,'To deliver their soul from death, and to keep them alive in famine.'),
(14389,19,'Psalms','OT',33,20,'Our soul waiteth for the LORD: he {is} our help and our shield.'),
(14390,19,'Psalms','OT',33,21,'For our heart shall rejoice in him, because we have trusted in his holy name.'),
(14391,19,'Psalms','OT',33,22,'Let thy mercy, O LORD, be upon us, according as we hope in thee.'),
(14392,19,'Psalms','OT',34,1,'[{A Psalm} of David, when he changed his behaviour before Abimelech; who drove him away, and he departed.] I will bless the LORD at all times: his praise {shall} continually {be} in my mouth. {Abimelech: or, Achish}'),
(14393,19,'Psalms','OT',34,2,'My soul shall make her boast in the LORD: the humble shall hear {thereof}, and be glad.'),
(14394,19,'Psalms','OT',34,3,'O magnify the LORD with me, and let us exalt his name together.'),
(14395,19,'Psalms','OT',34,4,'I sought the LORD, and he heard me, and delivered me from all my fears.'),
(14396,19,'Psalms','OT',34,5,'They looked unto him, and were lightened: and their faces were not ashamed. {were lightened: or, they flowed unto him}'),
(14397,19,'Psalms','OT',34,6,'This poor man cried, and the LORD heard {him}, and saved him out of all his troubles.'),
(14398,19,'Psalms','OT',34,7,'The angel of the LORD encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.'),
(14399,19,'Psalms','OT',34,8,'O taste and see that the LORD {is} good: blessed {is} the man {that} trusteth in him.'),
(14400,19,'Psalms','OT',34,9,'O fear the LORD, ye his saints: for {there is} no want to them that fear him.'),
(14401,19,'Psalms','OT',34,10,'The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger: but they that seek the LORD shall not want any good {thing}.'),
(14402,19,'Psalms','OT',34,11,'Come, ye children, hearken unto me: I will teach you the fear of the LORD.'),
(14403,19,'Psalms','OT',34,12,'What man {is he that} desireth life, {and} loveth {many} days, that he may see good?'),
(14404,19,'Psalms','OT',34,13,'Keep thy tongue from evil, and thy lips from speaking guile.'),
(14405,19,'Psalms','OT',34,14,'Depart from evil, and do good; seek peace, and pursue it.'),
(14406,19,'Psalms','OT',34,15,'The eyes of the LORD {are} upon the righteous, and his ears {are open} unto their cry.'),
(14407,19,'Psalms','OT',34,16,'The face of the LORD {is} against them that do evil, to cut off the remembrance of them from the earth.'),
(14408,19,'Psalms','OT',34,17,'{The righteous} cry, and the LORD heareth, and delivereth them out of all their troubles.'),
(14409,19,'Psalms','OT',34,18,'The LORD {is} nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit. {unto...: Heb. to the broken of heart} {of a contrite...: Heb. contrite of spirit}'),
(14410,19,'Psalms','OT',34,19,'Many {are} the afflictions of the righteous: but the LORD delivereth him out of them all.'),
(14411,19,'Psalms','OT',34,20,'He keepeth all his bones: not one of them is broken.'),
(14412,19,'Psalms','OT',34,21,'Evil shall slay the wicked: and they that hate the righteous shall be desolate. {desolate: or, guilty}'),
(14413,19,'Psalms','OT',34,22,'The LORD redeemeth the soul of his servants: and none of them that trust in him shall be desolate. {desolate: or, guilty}'),
(14414,19,'Psalms','OT',35,1,'[{A Psalm} of David.] Plead {my cause}, O LORD, with them that strive with me: fight against them that fight against me.'),
(14415,19,'Psalms','OT',35,2,'Take hold of shield and buckler, and stand up for mine help.'),
(14416,19,'Psalms','OT',35,3,'Draw out also the spear, and stop {the way} against them that persecute me: say unto my soul, I {am} thy salvation.'),
(14417,19,'Psalms','OT',35,4,'Let them be confounded and put to shame that seek after my soul: let them be turned back and brought to confusion that devise my hurt.'),
(14418,19,'Psalms','OT',35,5,'Let them be as chaff before the wind: and let the angel of the LORD chase {them}.'),
(14419,19,'Psalms','OT',35,6,'Let their way be dark and slippery: and let the angel of the LORD persecute them. {dark...: Heb. darkness and slipperiness}'),
(14420,19,'Psalms','OT',35,7,'For without cause have they hid for me their net {in} a pit, {which} without cause they have digged for my soul.'),
(14421,19,'Psalms','OT',35,8,'Let destruction come upon him at unawares; and let his net that he hath hid catch himself: into that very destruction let him fall. {at...: Heb. which he knoweth not of}'),
(14422,19,'Psalms','OT',35,9,'And my soul shall be joyful in the LORD: it shall rejoice in his salvation.'),
(14423,19,'Psalms','OT',35,10,'All my bones shall say, LORD, who {is} like unto thee, which deliverest the poor from him that is too strong for him, yea, the poor and the needy from him that spoileth him?'),
(14424,19,'Psalms','OT',35,11,'False witnesses did rise up; they laid to my charge {things} that I knew not. {False...: Heb. Witnesses of wrong} {they...: Heb. they asked me}'),
(14425,19,'Psalms','OT',35,12,'They rewarded me evil for good {to} the spoiling of my soul. {spoiling: Heb. depriving}'),
(14426,19,'Psalms','OT',35,13,'But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing {was} sackcloth: I humbled my soul with fasting; and my prayer returned into mine own bosom. {humbled: or, afflicted}'),
(14427,19,'Psalms','OT',35,14,'I behaved myself as though {he had been} my friend {or} brother: I bowed down heavily, as one that mourneth {for his} mother. {behaved myself: Heb. walked} {as though...: Heb. as a friend, as a brother to me}'),
(14428,19,'Psalms','OT',35,15,'But in mine adversity they rejoiced, and gathered themselves together: {yea}, the abjects gathered themselves together against me, and I knew {it} not; they did tear {me}, and ceased not: {adversity: Heb. halting}'),
(14429,19,'Psalms','OT',35,16,'With hypocritical mockers in feasts, they gnashed upon me with their teeth.'),
(14430,19,'Psalms','OT',35,17,'Lord, how long wilt thou look on? rescue my soul from their destructions, my darling from the lions. {darling: Heb. only one}'),
(14431,19,'Psalms','OT',35,18,'I will give thee thanks in the great congregation: I will praise thee among much people. {much: Heb. strong}'),
(14432,19,'Psalms','OT',35,19,'Let not them that are mine enemies wrongfully rejoice over me: {neither} let them wink with the eye that hate me without a cause. {wrongfully: Heb. falsely}'),
(14433,19,'Psalms','OT',35,20,'For they speak not peace: but they devise deceitful matters against {them that are} quiet in the land.'),
(14434,19,'Psalms','OT',35,21,'Yea, they opened their mouth wide against me, {and} said, Aha, aha, our eye hath seen {it}.'),
(14435,19,'Psalms','OT',35,22,'{This} thou hast seen, O LORD: keep not silence: O Lord, be not far from me.'),
(14436,19,'Psalms','OT',35,23,'Stir up thyself, and awake to my judgment, {even} unto my cause, my God and my Lord.'),
(14437,19,'Psalms','OT',35,24,'Judge me, O LORD my God, according to thy righteousness; and let them not rejoice over me.'),
(14438,19,'Psalms','OT',35,25,'Let them not say in their hearts, Ah, so would we have it: let them not say, We have swallowed him up. {Ah...: Heb. Ah, ah, our soul}'),
(14439,19,'Psalms','OT',35,26,'Let them be ashamed and brought to confusion together that rejoice at mine hurt: let them be clothed with shame and dishonour that magnify {themselves} against me.'),
(14440,19,'Psalms','OT',35,27,'Let them shout for joy, and be glad, that favour my righteous cause: yea, let them say continually, Let the LORD be magnified, which hath pleasure in the prosperity of his servant. {righteous...: Heb. righteousness}'),
(14441,19,'Psalms','OT',35,28,'And my tongue shall speak of thy righteousness {and} of thy praise all the day long.'),
(14442,19,'Psalms','OT',36,1,'[To the chief Musician, {A Psalm} of David the servant of the LORD.] The transgression of the wicked saith within my heart, {that there is} no fear of God before his eyes.'),
(14443,19,'Psalms','OT',36,2,'For he flattereth himself in his own eyes, until his iniquity be found to be hateful. {until...: Heb. to find his iniquity to hate}'),
(14444,19,'Psalms','OT',36,3,'The words of his mouth {are} iniquity and deceit: he hath left off to be wise, {and} to do good.'),
(14445,19,'Psalms','OT',36,4,'He deviseth mischief upon his bed; he setteth himself in a way {that is} not good; he abhorreth not evil. {mischief: or, vanity}'),
(14446,19,'Psalms','OT',36,5,'Thy mercy, O LORD, {is} in the heavens; {and} thy faithfulness {reacheth} unto the clouds.'),
(14447,19,'Psalms','OT',36,6,'Thy righteousness {is} like the great mountains; thy judgments {are} a great deep: O LORD, thou preservest man and beast. {the...: Heb. the mountains of God}'),
(14448,19,'Psalms','OT',36,7,'How excellent {is} thy lovingkindness, O God! therefore the children of men put their trust under the shadow of thy wings. {excellent: Heb. precious}'),
(14449,19,'Psalms','OT',36,8,'They shall be abundantly satisfied with the fatness of thy house; and thou shalt make them drink of the river of thy pleasures. {abundantly...: Heb. watered}'),
(14450,19,'Psalms','OT',36,9,'For with thee {is} the fountain of life: in thy light shall we see light.'),
(14451,19,'Psalms','OT',36,10,'O continue thy lovingkindness unto them that know thee; and thy righteousness to the upright in heart. {continue: Heb. draw out at length}'),
(14452,19,'Psalms','OT',36,11,'Let not the foot of pride come against me, and let not the hand of the wicked remove me.'),
(14453,19,'Psalms','OT',36,12,'There are the workers of iniquity fallen: they are cast down, and shall not be able to rise.'),
(14454,19,'Psalms','OT',37,1,'[{A Psalm} of David.] Fret not thyself because of evildoers, neither be thou envious against the workers of iniquity.'),
(14455,19,'Psalms','OT',37,2,'For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither as the green herb.'),
(14456,19,'Psalms','OT',37,3,'Trust in the LORD, and do good; {so} shalt thou dwell in the land, and verily thou shalt be fed. {verily: Heb. in truth, or, stableness}'),
(14457,19,'Psalms','OT',37,4,'Delight thyself also in the LORD; and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart.'),
(14458,19,'Psalms','OT',37,5,'Commit thy way unto the LORD; trust also in him; and he shall bring {it} to pass. {Commit...: Heb. Roll thy way upon}'),
(14459,19,'Psalms','OT',37,6,'And he shall bring forth thy righteousness as the light, and thy judgment as the noonday.'),
(14460,19,'Psalms','OT',37,7,'Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him: fret not thyself because of him who prospereth in his way, because of the man who bringeth wicked devices to pass. {Rest in: Heb. Be silent to}'),
(14461,19,'Psalms','OT',37,8,'Cease from anger, and forsake wrath: fret not thyself in any wise to do evil.'),
(14462,19,'Psalms','OT',37,9,'For evildoers shall be cut off: but those that wait upon the LORD, they shall inherit the earth.'),
(14463,19,'Psalms','OT',37,10,'For yet a little while, and the wicked {shall} not {be}: yea, thou shalt diligently consider his place, and it {shall} not {be}.'),
(14464,19,'Psalms','OT',37,11,'But the meek shall inherit the earth; and shall delight themselves in the abundance of peace.'),
(14465,19,'Psalms','OT',37,12,'The wicked plotteth against the just, and gnasheth upon him with his teeth. {plotteth: or, practiseth}'),
(14466,19,'Psalms','OT',37,13,'The Lord shall laugh at him: for he seeth that his day is coming.'),
(14467,19,'Psalms','OT',37,14,'The wicked have drawn out the sword, and have bent their bow, to cast down the poor and needy, {and} to slay such as be of upright conversation. {such...: Heb. the upright of way}'),
(14468,19,'Psalms','OT',37,15,'Their sword shall enter into their own heart, and their bows shall be broken.'),
(14469,19,'Psalms','OT',37,16,'A little that a righteous man hath {is} better than the riches of many wicked.'),
(14470,19,'Psalms','OT',37,17,'For the arms of the wicked shall be broken: but the LORD upholdeth the righteous.'),
(14471,19,'Psalms','OT',37,18,'The LORD knoweth the days of the upright: and their inheritance shall be for ever.'),
(14472,19,'Psalms','OT',37,19,'They shall not be ashamed in the evil time: and in the days of famine they shall be satisfied.'),
(14473,19,'Psalms','OT',37,20,'But the wicked shall perish, and the enemies of the LORD {shall be} as the fat of lambs: they shall consume; into smoke shall they consume away. {the fat: Heb. the preciousness}'),
(14474,19,'Psalms','OT',37,21,'The wicked borroweth, and payeth not again: but the righteous sheweth mercy, and giveth.'),
(14475,19,'Psalms','OT',37,22,'For {such as be} blessed of him shall inherit the earth; and {they that be} cursed of him shall be cut off.'),
(14476,19,'Psalms','OT',37,23,'The steps of a {good} man are ordered by the LORD: and he delighteth in his way. {ordered: or, established}'),
(14477,19,'Psalms','OT',37,24,'Though he fall, he shall not be utterly cast down: for the LORD upholdeth {him with} his hand.'),
(14478,19,'Psalms','OT',37,25,'I have been young, and {now} am old; yet have I not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed begging bread.'),
(14479,19,'Psalms','OT',37,26,'{He is} ever merciful, and lendeth; and his seed {is} blessed. {ever: Heb. all the day}'),
(14480,19,'Psalms','OT',37,27,'Depart from evil, and do good; and dwell for evermore.'),
(14481,19,'Psalms','OT',37,28,'For the LORD loveth judgment, and forsaketh not his saints; they are preserved for ever: but the seed of the wicked shall be cut off.'),
(14482,19,'Psalms','OT',37,29,'The righteous shall inherit the land, and dwell therein for ever.'),
(14483,19,'Psalms','OT',37,30,'The mouth of the righteous speaketh wisdom, and his tongue talketh of judgment.'),
(14484,19,'Psalms','OT',37,31,'The law of his God {is} in his heart; none of his steps shall slide. {steps: or, goings}'),
(14485,19,'Psalms','OT',37,32,'The wicked watcheth the righteous, and seeketh to slay him.'),
(14486,19,'Psalms','OT',37,33,'The LORD will not leave him in his hand, nor condemn him when he is judged.'),
(14487,19,'Psalms','OT',37,34,'Wait on the LORD, and keep his way, and he shall exalt thee to inherit the land: when the wicked are cut off, thou shalt see {it}.'),
(14488,19,'Psalms','OT',37,35,'I have seen the wicked in great power, and spreading himself like a green bay tree. {a green...: or, a green tree that groweth in his own soil}'),
(14489,19,'Psalms','OT',37,36,'Yet he passed away, and, lo, he {was} not: yea, I sought him, but he could not be found.'),
(14490,19,'Psalms','OT',37,37,'Mark the perfect {man}, and behold the upright: for the end of {that} man {is} peace.'),
(14491,19,'Psalms','OT',37,38,'But the transgressors shall be destroyed together: the end of the wicked shall be cut off.'),
(14492,19,'Psalms','OT',37,39,'But the salvation of the righteous {is} of the LORD: {he is} their strength in the time of trouble.'),
(14493,19,'Psalms','OT',37,40,'And the LORD shall help them, and deliver them: he shall deliver them from the wicked, and save them, because they trust in him.'),
(14494,19,'Psalms','OT',38,1,'[A Psalm of David, to bring to remembrance.] O LORD, rebuke me not in thy wrath: neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure.'),
(14495,19,'Psalms','OT',38,2,'For thine arrows stick fast in me, and thy hand presseth me sore.'),
(14496,19,'Psalms','OT',38,3,'{There is} no soundness in my flesh because of thine anger; neither {is there any} rest in my bones because of my sin. {rest: Heb. peace, or, health}'),
(14497,19,'Psalms','OT',38,4,'For mine iniquities are gone over mine head: as an heavy burden they are too heavy for me.'),
(14498,19,'Psalms','OT',38,5,'My wounds stink {and} are corrupt because of my foolishness.'),
(14499,19,'Psalms','OT',38,6,'I am troubled; I am bowed down greatly; I go mourning all the day long. {troubled: Heb. wried}'),
(14500,19,'Psalms','OT',38,7,'For my loins are filled with a loathsome {disease}: and {there is} no soundness in my flesh.'),
(14501,19,'Psalms','OT',38,8,'I am feeble and sore broken: I have roared by reason of the disquietness of my heart.'),
(14502,19,'Psalms','OT',38,9,'Lord, all my desire {is} before thee; and my groaning is not hid from thee.'),
(14503,19,'Psalms','OT',38,10,'My heart panteth, my strength faileth me: as for the light of mine eyes, it also is gone from me. {is gone...: Heb. is not with me}'),
(14504,19,'Psalms','OT',38,11,'My lovers and my friends stand aloof from my sore; and my kinsmen stand afar off. {sore: Heb. stroke} {my kinsmen: or, my neighbours}'),
(14505,19,'Psalms','OT',38,12,'They also that seek after my life lay snares {for me}: and they that seek my hurt speak mischievous things, and imagine deceits all the day long.'),
(14506,19,'Psalms','OT',38,13,'But I, as a deaf {man}, heard not; and {I was} as a dumb man {that} openeth not his mouth.'),
(14507,19,'Psalms','OT',38,14,'Thus I was as a man that heareth not, and in whose mouth {are} no reproofs.'),
(14508,19,'Psalms','OT',38,15,'For in thee, O LORD, do I hope: thou wilt hear, O Lord my God. {in...: or, thee do I wait for} {hear: or, answer}'),
(14509,19,'Psalms','OT',38,16,'For I said, {Hear me}, lest {otherwise} they should rejoice over me: when my foot slippeth, they magnify {themselves} against me.'),
(14510,19,'Psalms','OT',38,17,'For I {am} ready to halt, and my sorrow {is} continually before me. {to halt: Heb. for halting}'),
(14511,19,'Psalms','OT',38,18,'For I will declare mine iniquity; I will be sorry for my sin.'),
(14512,19,'Psalms','OT',38,19,'But mine enemies {are} lively, {and} they are strong: and they that hate me wrongfully are multiplied. {are lively...: Heb. being living, are strong}'),
(14513,19,'Psalms','OT',38,20,'They also that render evil for good are mine adversaries; because I follow {the thing that} good {is}.'),
(14514,19,'Psalms','OT',38,21,'Forsake me not, O LORD: O my God, be not far from me.'),
(14515,19,'Psalms','OT',38,22,'Make haste to help me, O Lord my salvation. {to...: Heb. for my help}'),
(14516,19,'Psalms','OT',39,1,'[To the chief Musician, {even} to Jeduthun, A Psalm of David.] I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I will keep my mouth with a bridle, while the wicked is before me. {my mouth...: Heb. a bridle, or, muzzle for my mouth}'),
(14517,19,'Psalms','OT',39,2,'I was dumb with silence, I held my peace, {even} from good; and my sorrow was stirred. {stirred: Heb. troubled}'),
(14518,19,'Psalms','OT',39,3,'My heart was hot within me, while I was musing the fire burned: {then} spake I with my tongue,'),
(14519,19,'Psalms','OT',39,4,'LORD, make me to know mine end, and the measure of my days, what it {is; that} I may know how frail I {am}. {how...: or, what time I have here}'),
(14520,19,'Psalms','OT',39,5,'Behold, thou hast made my days {as} an handbreadth; and mine age {is} as nothing before thee: verily every man at his best state {is} altogether vanity. Selah. {at...: Heb. settled}'),
(14521,19,'Psalms','OT',39,6,'Surely every man walketh in a vain shew: surely they are disquieted in vain: he heapeth up {riches}, and knoweth not who shall gather them. {a vain...: Heb. an image}'),
(14522,19,'Psalms','OT',39,7,'And now, Lord, what wait I for? my hope {is} in thee.'),
(14523,19,'Psalms','OT',39,8,'Deliver me from all my transgressions: make me not the reproach of the foolish.'),
(14524,19,'Psalms','OT',39,9,'I was dumb, I opened not my mouth; because thou didst {it}.'),
(14525,19,'Psalms','OT',39,10,'Remove thy stroke away from me: I am consumed by the blow of thine hand. {blow: Heb. conflict}'),
(14526,19,'Psalms','OT',39,11,'When thou with rebukes dost correct man for iniquity, thou makest his beauty to consume away like a moth: surely every man {is} vanity. Selah. {his...: Heb. that which is to be desired in him to melt away}'),
(14527,19,'Psalms','OT',39,12,'Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear unto my cry; hold not thy peace at my tears: for I {am} a stranger with thee, {and} a sojourner, as all my fathers {were}.'),
(14528,19,'Psalms','OT',39,13,'O spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go hence, and be no more.'),
(14529,19,'Psalms','OT',40,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.] I waited patiently for the LORD; and he inclined unto me, and heard my cry. {I waited...: Heb. In waiting I waited}'),
(14530,19,'Psalms','OT',40,2,'He brought me up also out of an horrible pit, out of the miry clay, and set my feet upon a rock, {and} established my goings. {an...: Heb. a pit of noise}'),
(14531,19,'Psalms','OT',40,3,'And he hath put a new song in my mouth, {even} praise unto our God: many shall see {it}, and fear, and shall trust in the LORD.'),
(14532,19,'Psalms','OT',40,4,'Blessed {is} that man that maketh the LORD his trust, and respecteth not the proud, nor such as turn aside to lies.'),
(14533,19,'Psalms','OT',40,5,'Many, O LORD my God, {are} thy wonderful works {which} thou hast done, and thy thoughts {which are} to us-ward: they cannot be reckoned up in order unto thee: {if} I would declare and speak {of them}, they are more than can be numbered. {they cannot...: or, none can order them unto thee}'),
(14534,19,'Psalms','OT',40,6,'Sacrifice and offering thou didst not desire; mine ears hast thou opened: burnt offering and sin offering hast thou not required. {opened: Heb. digged}'),
(14535,19,'Psalms','OT',40,7,'Then said I, Lo, I come: in the volume of the book {it is} written of me,'),
(14536,19,'Psalms','OT',40,8,'I delight to do thy will, O my God: yea, thy law {is} within my heart. {within...: Heb. in the midst of my bowels}'),
(14537,19,'Psalms','OT',40,9,'I have preached righteousness in the great congregation: lo, I have not refrained my lips, O LORD, thou knowest.'),
(14538,19,'Psalms','OT',40,10,'I have not hid thy righteousness within my heart; I have declared thy faithfulness and thy salvation: I have not concealed thy lovingkindness and thy truth from the great congregation.'),
(14539,19,'Psalms','OT',40,11,'Withhold not thou thy tender mercies from me, O LORD: let thy lovingkindness and thy truth continually preserve me.'),
(14540,19,'Psalms','OT',40,12,'For innumerable evils have compassed me about: mine iniquities have taken hold upon me, so that I am not able to look up; they are more than the hairs of mine head: therefore my heart faileth me. {falleth: Heb. forsaketh}'),
(14541,19,'Psalms','OT',40,13,'Be pleased, O LORD, to deliver me: O LORD, make haste to help me.'),
(14542,19,'Psalms','OT',40,14,'Let them be ashamed and confounded together that seek after my soul to destroy it; let them be driven backward and put to shame that wish me evil.'),
(14543,19,'Psalms','OT',40,15,'Let them be desolate for a reward of their shame that say unto me, Aha, aha.'),
(14544,19,'Psalms','OT',40,16,'Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: let such as love thy salvation say continually, The LORD be magnified.'),
(14545,19,'Psalms','OT',40,17,'But I {am} poor and needy; {yet} the Lord thinketh upon me: thou {art} my help and my deliverer; make no tarrying, O my God.'),
(14546,19,'Psalms','OT',41,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.] Blessed {is} he that considereth the poor: the LORD will deliver him in time of trouble. {the poor: or, the weak, or, sick} {in time...: Heb. in the day of evil}'),
(14547,19,'Psalms','OT',41,2,'The LORD will preserve him, and keep him alive; {and} he shall be blessed upon the earth: and thou wilt not deliver him unto the will of his enemies. {thou...: or, do not thou deliver}'),
(14548,19,'Psalms','OT',41,3,'The LORD will strengthen him upon the bed of languishing: thou wilt make all his bed in his sickness. {make: Heb. turn}'),
(14549,19,'Psalms','OT',41,4,'I said, LORD, be merciful unto me: heal my soul; for I have sinned against thee.'),
(14550,19,'Psalms','OT',41,5,'Mine enemies speak evil of me, When shall he die, and his name perish?'),
(14551,19,'Psalms','OT',41,6,'And if he come to see {me}, he speaketh vanity: his heart gathereth iniquity to itself; {when} he goeth abroad, he telleth {it}.'),
(14552,19,'Psalms','OT',41,7,'All that hate me whisper together against me: against me do they devise my hurt. {my...: Heb. evil to me}'),
(14553,19,'Psalms','OT',41,8,'An evil disease, {say they}, cleaveth fast unto him: and {now} that he lieth he shall rise up no more. {An...: Heb. A thing of Belial}'),
(14554,19,'Psalms','OT',41,9,'Yea, mine own familiar friend, in whom I trusted, which did eat of my bread, hath lifted up {his} heel against me. {mine...: Heb. the man of my peace} {lifted...: Heb. magnified}'),
(14555,19,'Psalms','OT',41,10,'But thou, O LORD, be merciful unto me, and raise me up, that I may requite them.'),
(14556,19,'Psalms','OT',41,11,'By this I know that thou favourest me, because mine enemy doth not triumph over me.'),
(14557,19,'Psalms','OT',41,12,'And as for me, thou upholdest me in mine integrity, and settest me before thy face for ever.'),
(14558,19,'Psalms','OT',41,13,'Blessed {be} the LORD God of Israel from everlasting, and to everlasting. Amen, and Amen.'),
(14559,19,'Psalms','OT',42,1,'[To the chief Musician, Maschil, for the sons of Korah.] As the hart panteth after the water brooks, so panteth my soul after thee, O God. {Maschil...: or, A Psalm giving instruction of the sons, etc} {panteth: Heb. brayeth}'),
(14560,19,'Psalms','OT',42,2,'My soul thirsteth for God, for the living God: when shall I come and appear before God?'),
(14561,19,'Psalms','OT',42,3,'My tears have been my meat day and night, while they continually say unto me, Where {is} thy God?'),
(14562,19,'Psalms','OT',42,4,'When I remember these {things}, I pour out my soul in me: for I had gone with the multitude, I went with them to the house of God, with the voice of joy and praise, with a multitude that kept holyday.'),
(14563,19,'Psalms','OT',42,5,'Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and {why} art thou disquieted in me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him {for} the help of his countenance. {cast: Heb. bowed} {praise: or, give thanks} {for the...: or, his presence is salvation}'),
(14564,19,'Psalms','OT',42,6,'O my God, my soul is cast down within me: therefore will I remember thee from the land of Jordan, and of the Hermonites, from the hill Mizar. {the hill...: or, the little hill}'),
(14565,19,'Psalms','OT',42,7,'Deep calleth unto deep at the noise of thy waterspouts: all thy waves and thy billows are gone over me.'),
(14566,19,'Psalms','OT',42,8,'{Yet} the LORD will command his lovingkindness in the daytime, and in the night his song {shall be} with me, {and} my prayer unto the God of my life.'),
(14567,19,'Psalms','OT',42,9,'I will say unto God my rock, Why hast thou forgotten me? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?'),
(14568,19,'Psalms','OT',42,10,'{As} with a sword in my bones, mine enemies reproach me; while they say daily unto me, Where {is} thy God? {sword: or, killing}'),
(14569,19,'Psalms','OT',42,11,'Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him, {who is} the health of my countenance, and my God.'),
(14570,19,'Psalms','OT',43,1,'Judge me, O God, and plead my cause against an ungodly nation: O deliver me from the deceitful and unjust man. {ungodly: or, unmerciful} {the deceitful...: Heb. a man of deceit and iniquity}'),
(14571,19,'Psalms','OT',43,2,'For thou {art} the God of my strength: why dost thou cast me off? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?'),
(14572,19,'Psalms','OT',43,3,'O send out thy light and thy truth: let them lead me; let them bring me unto thy holy hill, and to thy tabernacles.'),
(14573,19,'Psalms','OT',43,4,'Then will I go unto the altar of God, unto God my exceeding joy: yea, upon the harp will I praise thee, O God my God. {my exceeding...: Heb. the gladness of my joy}'),
(14574,19,'Psalms','OT',43,5,'Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope in God: for I shall yet praise him, {who is} the health of my countenance, and my God.'),
(14575,19,'Psalms','OT',44,1,'[To the chief Musician for the sons of Korah, Maschil.] We have heard with our ears, O God, our fathers have told us, {what} work thou didst in their days, in the times of old. {Maschil: or, of instruction}'),
(14576,19,'Psalms','OT',44,2,'{How} thou didst drive out the heathen with thy hand, and plantedst them; {how} thou didst afflict the people, and cast them out.'),
(14577,19,'Psalms','OT',44,3,'For they got not the land in possession by their own sword, neither did their own arm save them: but thy right hand, and thine arm, and the light of thy countenance, because thou hadst a favour unto them.'),
(14578,19,'Psalms','OT',44,4,'Thou art my King, O God: command deliverances for Jacob.'),
(14579,19,'Psalms','OT',44,5,'Through thee will we push down our enemies: through thy name will we tread them under that rise up against us.'),
(14580,19,'Psalms','OT',44,6,'For I will not trust in my bow, neither shall my sword save me.'),
(14581,19,'Psalms','OT',44,7,'But thou hast saved us from our enemies, and hast put them to shame that hated us.'),
(14582,19,'Psalms','OT',44,8,'In God we boast all the day long, and praise thy name for ever. Selah.'),
(14583,19,'Psalms','OT',44,9,'But thou hast cast off, and put us to shame; and goest not forth with our armies.'),
(14584,19,'Psalms','OT',44,10,'Thou makest us to turn back from the enemy: and they which hate us spoil for themselves.'),
(14585,19,'Psalms','OT',44,11,'Thou hast given us like sheep {appointed} for meat; and hast scattered us among the heathen. {like...: Heb. as sheep of meat}'),
(14586,19,'Psalms','OT',44,12,'Thou sellest thy people for nought, and dost not increase {thy wealth} by their price. {for...: Heb. without riches}'),
(14587,19,'Psalms','OT',44,13,'Thou makest us a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and a derision to them that are round about us.'),
(14588,19,'Psalms','OT',44,14,'Thou makest us a byword among the heathen, a shaking of the head among the people.'),
(14589,19,'Psalms','OT',44,15,'My confusion {is} continually before me, and the shame of my face hath covered me,'),
(14590,19,'Psalms','OT',44,16,'For the voice of him that reproacheth and blasphemeth; by reason of the enemy and avenger.'),
(14591,19,'Psalms','OT',44,17,'All this is come upon us; yet have we not forgotten thee, neither have we dealt falsely in thy covenant.'),
(14592,19,'Psalms','OT',44,18,'Our heart is not turned back, neither have our steps declined from thy way; {steps: or, goings}'),
(14593,19,'Psalms','OT',44,19,'Though thou hast sore broken us in the place of dragons, and covered us with the shadow of death.'),
(14594,19,'Psalms','OT',44,20,'If we have forgotten the name of our God, or stretched out our hands to a strange god;'),
(14595,19,'Psalms','OT',44,21,'Shall not God search this out? for he knoweth the secrets of the heart.'),
(14596,19,'Psalms','OT',44,22,'Yea, for thy sake are we killed all the day long; we are counted as sheep for the slaughter.'),
(14597,19,'Psalms','OT',44,23,'Awake, why sleepest thou, O Lord? arise, cast {us} not off for ever.'),
(14598,19,'Psalms','OT',44,24,'Wherefore hidest thou thy face, {and} forgettest our affliction and our oppression?'),
(14599,19,'Psalms','OT',44,25,'For our soul is bowed down to the dust: our belly cleaveth unto the earth.'),
(14600,19,'Psalms','OT',44,26,'Arise for our help, and redeem us for thy mercies\' sake. {for our...: Heb. a help for us}'),
(14601,19,'Psalms','OT',45,1,'[To the chief Musician upon Shoshannim, for the sons of Korah, Maschil, A Song of loves.] My heart is inditing a good matter: I speak of the things which I have made touching the king: my tongue {is} the pen of a ready writer. {Maschil: or, of instruction} {is inditing: Heb. boileth, or, bubbleth up}'),
(14602,19,'Psalms','OT',45,2,'Thou art fairer than the children of men: grace is poured into thy lips: therefore God hath blessed thee for ever.'),
(14603,19,'Psalms','OT',45,3,'Gird thy sword upon {thy} thigh, O {most} mighty, with thy glory and thy majesty.'),
(14604,19,'Psalms','OT',45,4,'And in thy majesty ride prosperously because of truth and meekness {and} righteousness; and thy right hand shall teach thee terrible things. {ride...: Heb. prosper thou, ride thou}'),
(14605,19,'Psalms','OT',45,5,'Thine arrows {are} sharp in the heart of the king\'s enemies; {whereby} the people fall under thee.'),
(14606,19,'Psalms','OT',45,6,'Thy throne, O God, {is} for ever and ever: the sceptre of thy kingdom {is} a right sceptre.'),
(14607,19,'Psalms','OT',45,7,'Thou lovest righteousness, and hatest wickedness: therefore God, thy God, hath anointed thee with the oil of gladness above thy fellows.'),
(14608,19,'Psalms','OT',45,8,'All thy garments {smell} of myrrh, and aloes, {and} cassia, out of the ivory palaces, whereby they have made thee glad.'),
(14609,19,'Psalms','OT',45,9,'Kings\' daughters {were} among thy honourable women: upon thy right hand did stand the queen in gold of Ophir.'),
(14610,19,'Psalms','OT',45,10,'Hearken, O daughter, and consider, and incline thine ear; forget also thine own people, and thy father\'s house;'),
(14611,19,'Psalms','OT',45,11,'So shall the king greatly desire thy beauty: for he {is} thy Lord; and worship thou him.'),
(14612,19,'Psalms','OT',45,12,'And the daughter of Tyre {shall be there} with a gift; {even} the rich among the people shall intreat thy favour. {favour: Heb. face}'),
(14613,19,'Psalms','OT',45,13,'The king\'s daughter {is} all glorious within: her clothing {is} of wrought gold.'),
(14614,19,'Psalms','OT',45,14,'She shall be brought unto the king in raiment of needlework: the virgins her companions that follow her shall be brought unto thee.'),
(14615,19,'Psalms','OT',45,15,'With gladness and rejoicing shall they be brought: they shall enter into the king\'s palace.'),
(14616,19,'Psalms','OT',45,16,'Instead of thy fathers shall be thy children, whom thou mayest make princes in all the earth.'),
(14617,19,'Psalms','OT',45,17,'I will make thy name to be remembered in all generations: therefore shall the people praise thee for ever and ever.'),
(14618,19,'Psalms','OT',46,1,'[To the chief Musician for the sons of Korah, A Song upon Alamoth.] God {is} our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble. {for: or, of}'),
(14619,19,'Psalms','OT',46,2,'Therefore will not we fear, though the earth be removed, and though the mountains be carried into the midst of the sea; {midst...: Heb. heart of the seas}'),
(14620,19,'Psalms','OT',46,3,'{Though} the waters thereof roar {and} be troubled, {though} the mountains shake with the swelling thereof. Selah.'),
(14621,19,'Psalms','OT',46,4,'{There is} a river, the streams whereof shall make glad the city of God, the holy {place} of the tabernacles of the most High.'),
(14622,19,'Psalms','OT',46,5,'God {is} in the midst of her; she shall not be moved: God shall help her, {and that} right early. {and...: Heb. when the morning appeareth}'),
(14623,19,'Psalms','OT',46,6,'The heathen raged, the kingdoms were moved: he uttered his voice, the earth melted.'),
(14624,19,'Psalms','OT',46,7,'The LORD of hosts {is} with us; the God of Jacob {is} our refuge. Selah. {our...: Heb. an high place for us}'),
(14625,19,'Psalms','OT',46,8,'Come, behold the works of the LORD, what desolations he hath made in the earth.'),
(14626,19,'Psalms','OT',46,9,'He maketh wars to cease unto the end of the earth; he breaketh the bow, and cutteth the spear in sunder; he burneth the chariot in the fire.'),
(14627,19,'Psalms','OT',46,10,'Be still, and know that I {am} God: I will be exalted among the heathen, I will be exalted in the earth.'),
(14628,19,'Psalms','OT',46,11,'The LORD of hosts {is} with us; the God of Jacob {is} our refuge. Selah.'),
(14629,19,'Psalms','OT',47,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.] O clap your hands, all ye people; shout unto God with the voice of triumph. {for: or, of}'),
(14630,19,'Psalms','OT',47,2,'For the LORD most high {is} terrible; {he is} a great King over all the earth.'),
(14631,19,'Psalms','OT',47,3,'He shall subdue the people under us, and the nations under our feet.'),
(14632,19,'Psalms','OT',47,4,'He shall choose our inheritance for us, the excellency of Jacob whom he loved. Selah.'),
(14633,19,'Psalms','OT',47,5,'God is gone up with a shout, the LORD with the sound of a trumpet.'),
(14634,19,'Psalms','OT',47,6,'Sing praises to God, sing praises: sing praises unto our King, sing praises.'),
(14635,19,'Psalms','OT',47,7,'For God {is} the King of all the earth: sing ye praises with understanding. {with: or, every one that hath}'),
(14636,19,'Psalms','OT',47,8,'God reigneth over the heathen: God sitteth upon the throne of his holiness.'),
(14637,19,'Psalms','OT',47,9,'The princes of the people are gathered together, {even} the people of the God of Abraham: for the shields of the earth {belong} unto God: he is greatly exalted. {princes...: or, voluntary of the people are gathered unto the people of the God of Abraham}'),
(14638,19,'Psalms','OT',48,1,'[A Song {and} Psalm for the sons of Korah.] Great {is} the LORD, and greatly to be praised in the city of our God, {in} the mountain of his holiness. {for: or, of}'),
(14639,19,'Psalms','OT',48,2,'Beautiful for situation, the joy of the whole earth, {is} mount Zion, {on} the sides of the north, the city of the great King.'),
(14640,19,'Psalms','OT',48,3,'God is known in her palaces for a refuge.'),
(14641,19,'Psalms','OT',48,4,'For, lo, the kings were assembled, they passed by together.'),
(14642,19,'Psalms','OT',48,5,'They saw {it, and} so they marvelled; they were troubled, {and} hasted away.'),
(14643,19,'Psalms','OT',48,6,'Fear took hold upon them there, {and} pain, as of a woman in travail.'),
(14644,19,'Psalms','OT',48,7,'Thou breakest the ships of Tarshish with an east wind.'),
(14645,19,'Psalms','OT',48,8,'As we have heard, so have we seen in the city of the LORD of hosts, in the city of our God: God will establish it for ever. Selah.'),
(14646,19,'Psalms','OT',48,9,'We have thought of thy lovingkindness, O God, in the midst of thy temple.'),
(14647,19,'Psalms','OT',48,10,'According to thy name, O God, so {is} thy praise unto the ends of the earth: thy right hand is full of righteousness.'),
(14648,19,'Psalms','OT',48,11,'Let mount Zion rejoice, let the daughters of Judah be glad, because of thy judgments.'),
(14649,19,'Psalms','OT',48,12,'Walk about Zion, and go round about her: tell the towers thereof.'),
(14650,19,'Psalms','OT',48,13,'Mark ye well her bulwarks, consider her palaces; that ye may tell {it} to the generation following. {Mark...: Heb. Set your heart to} {consider: or, raise up}'),
(14651,19,'Psalms','OT',48,14,'For this God {is} our God for ever and ever: he will be our guide {even} unto death.'),
(14652,19,'Psalms','OT',49,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.] Hear this, all {ye} people; give ear, all {ye} inhabitants of the world: {for: or, of}'),
(14653,19,'Psalms','OT',49,2,'Both low and high, rich and poor, together.'),
(14654,19,'Psalms','OT',49,3,'My mouth shall speak of wisdom; and the meditation of my heart {shall be} of understanding.'),
(14655,19,'Psalms','OT',49,4,'I will incline mine ear to a parable: I will open my dark saying upon the harp.'),
(14656,19,'Psalms','OT',49,5,'Wherefore should I fear in the days of evil, {when} the iniquity of my heels shall compass me about?'),
(14657,19,'Psalms','OT',49,6,'They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;'),
(14658,19,'Psalms','OT',49,7,'None {of them} can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to God a ransom for him:'),
(14659,19,'Psalms','OT',49,8,'(For the redemption of their soul {is} precious, and it ceaseth for ever:)'),
(14660,19,'Psalms','OT',49,9,'That he should still live for ever, {and} not see corruption.'),
(14661,19,'Psalms','OT',49,10,'For he seeth {that} wise men die, likewise the fool and the brutish person perish, and leave their wealth to others.'),
(14662,19,'Psalms','OT',49,11,'Their inward thought {is, that} their houses {shall continue} for ever, {and} their dwelling places to all generations; they call {their} lands after their own names. {all...: Heb. generation and generation}'),
(14663,19,'Psalms','OT',49,12,'Nevertheless man {being} in honour abideth not: he is like the beasts {that} perish.'),
(14664,19,'Psalms','OT',49,13,'This their way {is} their folly: yet their posterity approve their sayings. Selah. {approve...: Heb. delight in their mouth}'),
(14665,19,'Psalms','OT',49,14,'Like sheep they are laid in the grave; death shall feed on them; and the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning; and their beauty shall consume in the grave from their dwelling. {beauty: or, strength} {in the grave from...: or, the grave being an habitation to every one of them}'),
(14666,19,'Psalms','OT',49,15,'But God will redeem my soul from the power of the grave: for he shall receive me. Selah. {power: Heb. hand} {the grave: or, hell}'),
(14667,19,'Psalms','OT',49,16,'Be not thou afraid when one is made rich, when the glory of his house is increased;'),
(14668,19,'Psalms','OT',49,17,'For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away: his glory shall not descend after him.'),
(14669,19,'Psalms','OT',49,18,'Though while he lived he blessed his soul: and {men} will praise thee, when thou doest well to thyself. {while...: Heb. in his life}'),
(14670,19,'Psalms','OT',49,19,'He shall go to the generation of his fathers; they shall never see light. {He...: Heb. The soul shall}'),
(14671,19,'Psalms','OT',49,20,'Man {that is} in honour, and understandeth not, is like the beasts {that} perish.'),
(14672,19,'Psalms','OT',50,1,'[A Psalm of Asaph.] The mighty God, {even} the LORD, hath spoken, and called the earth from the rising of the sun unto the going down thereof. {of...: or, for Asaph}'),
(14673,19,'Psalms','OT',50,2,'Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God hath shined.'),
(14674,19,'Psalms','OT',50,3,'Our God shall come, and shall not keep silence: a fire shall devour before him, and it shall be very tempestuous round about him.'),
(14675,19,'Psalms','OT',50,4,'He shall call to the heavens from above, and to the earth, that he may judge his people.'),
(14676,19,'Psalms','OT',50,5,'Gather my saints together unto me; those that have made a covenant with me by sacrifice.'),
(14677,19,'Psalms','OT',50,6,'And the heavens shall declare his righteousness: for God {is} judge himself. Selah.'),
(14678,19,'Psalms','OT',50,7,'Hear, O my people, and I will speak; O Israel, and I will testify against thee: I {am} God, {even} thy God.'),
(14679,19,'Psalms','OT',50,8,'I will not reprove thee for thy sacrifices or thy burnt offerings, {to have been} continually before me.'),
(14680,19,'Psalms','OT',50,9,'I will take no bullock out of thy house, {nor} he goats out of thy folds.'),
(14681,19,'Psalms','OT',50,10,'For every beast of the forest {is} mine, {and} the cattle upon a thousand hills.'),
(14682,19,'Psalms','OT',50,11,'I know all the fowls of the mountains: and the wild beasts of the field {are} mine. {mine: Heb. with me}'),
(14683,19,'Psalms','OT',50,12,'If I were hungry, I would not tell thee: for the world {is} mine, and the fulness thereof.'),
(14684,19,'Psalms','OT',50,13,'Will I eat the flesh of bulls, or drink the blood of goats?'),
(14685,19,'Psalms','OT',50,14,'Offer unto God thanksgiving; and pay thy vows unto the most High:'),
(14686,19,'Psalms','OT',50,15,'And call upon me in the day of trouble: I will deliver thee, and thou shalt glorify me.'),
(14687,19,'Psalms','OT',50,16,'But unto the wicked God saith, What hast thou to do to declare my statutes, or {that} thou shouldest take my covenant in thy mouth?'),
(14688,19,'Psalms','OT',50,17,'Seeing thou hatest instruction, and castest my words behind thee.'),
(14689,19,'Psalms','OT',50,18,'When thou sawest a thief, then thou consentedst with him, and hast been partaker with adulterers. {hast...: Heb. thy portion was with}'),
(14690,19,'Psalms','OT',50,19,'Thou givest thy mouth to evil, and thy tongue frameth deceit. {givest: Heb. sendest}'),
(14691,19,'Psalms','OT',50,20,'Thou sittest {and} speakest against thy brother; thou slanderest thine own mother\'s son.'),
(14692,19,'Psalms','OT',50,21,'These {things} hast thou done, and I kept silence; thou thoughtest that I was altogether {such an one} as thyself: {but} I will reprove thee, and set {them} in order before thine eyes.'),
(14693,19,'Psalms','OT',50,22,'Now consider this, ye that forget God, lest I tear {you} in pieces, and {there be} none to deliver.'),
(14694,19,'Psalms','OT',50,23,'Whoso offereth praise glorifieth me: and to him that ordereth {his} conversation {aright} will I shew the salvation of God. {that...: Heb. that disposeth his way}'),
(14695,19,'Psalms','OT',51,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David, when Nathan the prophet came unto him, after he had gone in to Bathsheba.] Have mercy upon me, O God, according to thy lovingkindness: according unto the multitude of thy tender mercies blot out my transgressions.'),
(14696,19,'Psalms','OT',51,2,'Wash me throughly from mine iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin.'),
(14697,19,'Psalms','OT',51,3,'For I acknowledge my transgressions: and my sin {is} ever before me.'),
(14698,19,'Psalms','OT',51,4,'Against thee, thee only, have I sinned, and done {this} evil in thy sight: that thou mightest be justified when thou speakest, {and} be clear when thou judgest.'),
(14699,19,'Psalms','OT',51,5,'Behold, I was shapen in iniquity; and in sin did my mother conceive me. {conceive...: Heb. warm me}'),
(14700,19,'Psalms','OT',51,6,'Behold, thou desirest truth in the inward parts: and in the hidden {part} thou shalt make me to know wisdom.'),
(14701,19,'Psalms','OT',51,7,'Purge me with hyssop, and I shall be clean: wash me, and I shall be whiter than snow.'),
(14702,19,'Psalms','OT',51,8,'Make me to hear joy and gladness; {that} the bones {which} thou hast broken may rejoice.'),
(14703,19,'Psalms','OT',51,9,'Hide thy face from my sins, and blot out all mine iniquities.'),
(14704,19,'Psalms','OT',51,10,'Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me. {right: or, constant}'),
(14705,19,'Psalms','OT',51,11,'Cast me not away from thy presence; and take not thy holy spirit from me.'),
(14706,19,'Psalms','OT',51,12,'Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation; and uphold me {with thy} free spirit.'),
(14707,19,'Psalms','OT',51,13,'{Then} will I teach transgressors thy ways; and sinners shall be converted unto thee.'),
(14708,19,'Psalms','OT',51,14,'Deliver me from bloodguiltiness, O God, thou God of my salvation: {and} my tongue shall sing aloud of thy righteousness. {bloodguiltiness: Heb. bloods}'),
(14709,19,'Psalms','OT',51,15,'O Lord, open thou my lips; and my mouth shall shew forth thy praise.'),
(14710,19,'Psalms','OT',51,16,'For thou desirest not sacrifice; else would I give {it}: thou delightest not in burnt offering. {else...: or, that I should}'),
(14711,19,'Psalms','OT',51,17,'The sacrifices of God {are} a broken spirit: a broken and a contrite heart, O God, thou wilt not despise.'),
(14712,19,'Psalms','OT',51,18,'Do good in thy good pleasure unto Zion: build thou the walls of Jerusalem.'),
(14713,19,'Psalms','OT',51,19,'Then shalt thou be pleased with the sacrifices of righteousness, with burnt offering and whole burnt offering: then shall they offer bullocks upon thine altar.'),
(14714,19,'Psalms','OT',52,1,'[To the chief Musician, Maschil, {A Psalm} of David, when Doeg the Edomite came and told Saul, and said unto him, David is come to the house of Ahimelech.] Why boastest thou thyself in mischief, O mighty man? the goodness of God {endureth} continually. {Maschil: or, of instruction}'),
(14715,19,'Psalms','OT',52,2,'Thy tongue deviseth mischiefs; like a sharp razor, working deceitfully.'),
(14716,19,'Psalms','OT',52,3,'Thou lovest evil more than good; {and} lying rather than to speak righteousness. Selah.'),
(14717,19,'Psalms','OT',52,4,'Thou lovest all devouring words, O {thou} deceitful tongue. {O thou...: or, and the deceitful tongue}'),
(14718,19,'Psalms','OT',52,5,'God shall likewise destroy thee for ever, he shall take thee away, and pluck thee out of {thy} dwelling place, and root thee out of the land of the living. Selah. {destroy...: Heb. beat thee down}'),
(14719,19,'Psalms','OT',52,6,'The righteous also shall see, and fear, and shall laugh at him:'),
