(14876,19,'Psalms','OT',65,13,'The pastures are clothed with flocks; the valleys also are covered over with corn; they shout for joy, they also sing.'),
(14877,19,'Psalms','OT',66,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Song {or} Psalm.] Make a joyful noise unto God, all ye lands: {all...: Heb. all the earth}'),
(14878,19,'Psalms','OT',66,2,'Sing forth the honour of his name: make his praise glorious.'),
(14879,19,'Psalms','OT',66,3,'Say unto God, How terrible {art thou in} thy works! through the greatness of thy power shall thine enemies submit themselves unto thee. {submit...: or, yield feigned obedience: Heb. lie}'),
(14880,19,'Psalms','OT',66,4,'All the earth shall worship thee, and shall sing unto thee; they shall sing {to} thy name. Selah.'),
(14881,19,'Psalms','OT',66,5,'Come and see the works of God: {he is} terrible {in his} doing toward the children of men.'),
(14882,19,'Psalms','OT',66,6,'He turned the sea into dry {land}: they went through the flood on foot: there did we rejoice in him.'),
(14883,19,'Psalms','OT',66,7,'He ruleth by his power for ever; his eyes behold the nations: let not the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah.'),
