(14901,19,'Psalms','OT',67,5,'Let the people praise thee, O God; let all the people praise thee.'),
(14902,19,'Psalms','OT',67,6,'{Then} shall the earth yield her increase; {and} God, {even} our own God, shall bless us.'),
(14903,19,'Psalms','OT',67,7,'God shall bless us; and all the ends of the earth shall fear him.'),
(14904,19,'Psalms','OT',68,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm {or} Song of David.] Let God arise, let his enemies be scattered: let them also that hate him flee before him. {before...: Heb. from his face}'),
(14905,19,'Psalms','OT',68,2,'As smoke is driven away, {so} drive {them} away: as wax melteth before the fire, {so} let the wicked perish at the presence of God.'),
(14906,19,'Psalms','OT',68,3,'But let the righteous be glad; let them rejoice before God: yea, let them exceedingly rejoice. {exceedingly...: Heb. rejoice with gladness}'),
(14907,19,'Psalms','OT',68,4,'Sing unto God, sing praises to his name: extol him that rideth upon the heavens by his name JAH, and rejoice before him.'),
