(14909,19,'Psalms','OT',68,6,'God setteth the solitary in families: he bringeth out those which are bound with chains: but the rebellious dwell in a dry {land}. {in families: Heb. in a house}'),
(14910,19,'Psalms','OT',68,7,'O God, when thou wentest forth before thy people, when thou didst march through the wilderness; Selah:'),
(14911,19,'Psalms','OT',68,8,'The earth shook, the heavens also dropped at the presence of God: {even} Sinai itself {was moved} at the presence of God, the God of Israel.'),
(14912,19,'Psalms','OT',68,9,'Thou, O God, didst send a plentiful rain, whereby thou didst confirm thine inheritance, when it was weary. {send: Heb. shake out} {confirm: Heb. confirm it}'),
(14913,19,'Psalms','OT',68,10,'Thy congregation hath dwelt therein: thou, O God, hast prepared of thy goodness for the poor.'),
(14914,19,'Psalms','OT',68,11,'The Lord gave the word: great {was} the company of those that published {it}. {company: Heb. army}'),
(14915,19,'Psalms','OT',68,12,'Kings of armies did flee apace: and she that tarried at home divided the spoil. {did...: Heb. did flee, did flee}'),
(14916,19,'Psalms','OT',68,13,'Though ye have lien among the pots, {yet shall ye be as} the wings of a dove covered with silver, and her feathers with yellow gold.'),
(14917,19,'Psalms','OT',68,14,'When the Almighty scattered kings in it, it was {white} as snow in Salmon. {in it...: or, for her, she}'),
(14918,19,'Psalms','OT',68,15,'The hill of God {is as} the hill of Bashan; an high hill {as} the hill of Bashan.'),
(14919,19,'Psalms','OT',68,16,'Why leap ye, ye high hills? {this is} the hill {which} God desireth to dwell in; yea, the LORD will dwell {in it} for ever.'),
(14920,19,'Psalms','OT',68,17,'The chariots of God {are} twenty thousand, {even} thousands of angels: the Lord {is} among them, {as in} Sinai, in the holy {place}. {even...: or, even many thousands}'),
(14921,19,'Psalms','OT',68,18,'Thou hast ascended on high, thou hast led captivity captive: thou hast received gifts for men; yea, {for} the rebellious also, that the LORD God might dwell {among them}. {for men: Heb. in the man}'),
(14922,19,'Psalms','OT',68,19,'Blessed {be} the Lord, {who} daily loadeth us {with benefits, even} the God of our salvation. Selah.'),
(14923,19,'Psalms','OT',68,20,'{He that is} our God {is} the God of salvation; and unto GOD the Lord {belong} the issues from death.'),
(14924,19,'Psalms','OT',68,21,'But God shall wound the head of his enemies, {and} the hairy scalp of such an one as goeth on still in his trespasses.'),
(14925,19,'Psalms','OT',68,22,'The Lord said, I will bring again from Bashan, I will bring {my people} again from the depths of the sea:'),
(14926,19,'Psalms','OT',68,23,'That thy foot may be dipped in the blood of {thine} enemies, {and} the tongue of thy dogs in the same. {dipped: or, red}'),
(14927,19,'Psalms','OT',68,24,'They have seen thy goings, O God; {even} the goings of my God, my King, in the sanctuary.'),
(14928,19,'Psalms','OT',68,25,'The singers went before, the players on instruments {followed} after; among {them were} the damsels playing with timbrels.'),
(14929,19,'Psalms','OT',68,26,'Bless ye God in the congregations, {even} the Lord, from the fountain of Israel. {from...: or, ye that are of the fountain of Israel}'),
(14930,19,'Psalms','OT',68,27,'There {is} little Benjamin {with} their ruler, the princes of Judah {and} their council, the princes of Zebulun, {and} the princes of Naphtali. {and their...: or, with their company}'),
(14931,19,'Psalms','OT',68,28,'Thy God hath commanded thy strength: strengthen, O God, that which thou hast wrought for us.'),
(14932,19,'Psalms','OT',68,29,'Because of thy temple at Jerusalem shall kings bring presents unto thee.'),
(14933,19,'Psalms','OT',68,30,'Rebuke the company of spearmen, the multitude of the bulls, with the calves of the people, {till every one} submit himself with pieces of silver: scatter thou the people {that} delight in war. {the company...: or, the beasts of the reeds} {scatter...: or, he scattereth}'),
(14934,19,'Psalms','OT',68,31,'Princes shall come out of Egypt; Ethiopia shall soon stretch out her hands unto God.'),
(14935,19,'Psalms','OT',68,32,'Sing unto God, ye kingdoms of the earth; O sing praises unto the Lord; Selah:'),
(14936,19,'Psalms','OT',68,33,'To him that rideth upon the heavens of heavens, {which were} of old; lo, he doth send out his voice, {and that} a mighty voice. {send...: Heb. give}'),
