(15017,19,'Psalms','OT',72,14,'He shall redeem their soul from deceit and violence: and precious shall their blood be in his sight.'),
(15018,19,'Psalms','OT',72,15,'And he shall live, and to him shall be given of the gold of Sheba: prayer also shall be made for him continually; {and} daily shall he be praised. {shall be given: Heb. one shall give}'),
(15019,19,'Psalms','OT',72,16,'There shall be an handful of corn in the earth upon the top of the mountains; the fruit thereof shall shake like Lebanon: and {they} of the city shall flourish like grass of the earth.'),
(15020,19,'Psalms','OT',72,17,'His name shall endure for ever: his name shall be continued as long as the sun: and {men} shall be blessed in him: all nations shall call him blessed. {endure: Heb. be} {his name shall be...: Heb. shall be as a son to continue his father\'s name for ever}'),
(15021,19,'Psalms','OT',72,18,'Blessed {be} the LORD God, the God of Israel, who only doeth wondrous things.'),
(15022,19,'Psalms','OT',72,19,'And blessed {be} his glorious name for ever: and let the whole earth be filled {with} his glory; Amen, and Amen.'),
(15023,19,'Psalms','OT',72,20,'The prayers of David the son of Jesse are ended.'),
(15024,19,'Psalms','OT',73,1,'[A Psalm of Asaph.] Truly God {is} good to Israel, {even} to such as are of a clean heart. {of: or, for} {Truly: or, Yet} {of...: Heb. clean of heart}'),
(15025,19,'Psalms','OT',73,2,'But as for me, my feet were almost gone; my steps had well nigh slipped.'),
(15026,19,'Psalms','OT',73,3,'For I was envious at the foolish, {when} I saw the prosperity of the wicked.'),
(15027,19,'Psalms','OT',73,4,'For {there are} no bands in their death: but their strength {is} firm. {firm: Heb. fat}'),
(15028,19,'Psalms','OT',73,5,'They {are} not in trouble {as other} men; neither are they plagued like {other} men. {in...: Heb. in the trouble of other men} {like: Heb. with}'),
(15029,19,'Psalms','OT',73,6,'Therefore pride compasseth them about as a chain; violence covereth them {as} a garment.'),
(15030,19,'Psalms','OT',73,7,'Their eyes stand out with fatness: they have more than heart could wish. {have...: Heb. pass the thoughts of the heart}'),
(15031,19,'Psalms','OT',73,8,'They are corrupt, and speak wickedly {concerning} oppression: they speak loftily.'),
(15032,19,'Psalms','OT',73,9,'They set their mouth against the heavens, and their tongue walketh through the earth.'),
(15033,19,'Psalms','OT',73,10,'Therefore his people return hither: and waters of a full {cup} are wrung out to them.'),
(15034,19,'Psalms','OT',73,11,'And they say, How doth God know? and is there knowledge in the most High?'),
(15035,19,'Psalms','OT',73,12,'Behold, these {are} the ungodly, who prosper in the world; they increase {in} riches.'),
(15036,19,'Psalms','OT',73,13,'Verily I have cleansed my heart {in} vain, and washed my hands in innocency.'),
