(15197,19,'Psalms','OT',79,9,'Help us, O God of our salvation, for the glory of thy name: and deliver us, and purge away our sins, for thy name\'s sake.'),
(15198,19,'Psalms','OT',79,10,'Wherefore should the heathen say, Where {is} their God? let him be known among the heathen in our sight {by} the revenging of the blood of thy servants {which is} shed. {revenging: Heb. vengeance}'),
(15199,19,'Psalms','OT',79,11,'Let the sighing of the prisoner come before thee; according to the greatness of thy power preserve thou those that are appointed to die; {thy...: Heb. thine arm} {preserve...: Heb. reserve the children of death}'),
