(15211,19,'Psalms','OT',80,10,'The hills were covered with the shadow of it, and the boughs thereof {were like} the goodly cedars. {goodly...: Heb. cedars of God}'),
(15212,19,'Psalms','OT',80,11,'She sent out her boughs unto the sea, and her branches unto the river.'),
(15213,19,'Psalms','OT',80,12,'Why hast thou {then} broken down her hedges, so that all they which pass by the way do pluck her?'),
(15214,19,'Psalms','OT',80,13,'The boar out of the wood doth waste it, and the wild beast of the field doth devour it.'),
(15215,19,'Psalms','OT',80,14,'Return, we beseech thee, O God of hosts: look down from heaven, and behold, and visit this vine;'),
(15216,19,'Psalms','OT',80,15,'And the vineyard which thy right hand hath planted, and the branch {that} thou madest strong for thyself.'),
(15217,19,'Psalms','OT',80,16,'{It is} burned with fire, {it is} cut down: they perish at the rebuke of thy countenance.'),
(15218,19,'Psalms','OT',80,17,'Let thy hand be upon the man of thy right hand, upon the son of man {whom} thou madest strong for thyself.'),
(15219,19,'Psalms','OT',80,18,'So will not we go back from thee: quicken us, and we will call upon thy name.'),
(15220,19,'Psalms','OT',80,19,'Turn us again, O LORD God of hosts, cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.'),
(15221,19,'Psalms','OT',81,1,'[To the chief Musician upon Gittith, {A Psalm} of Asaph.] Sing aloud unto God our strength: make a joyful noise unto the God of Jacob. {of Asaph: or, for Asaph}'),
(15222,19,'Psalms','OT',81,2,'Take a psalm, and bring hither the timbrel, the pleasant harp with the psaltery.'),
(15223,19,'Psalms','OT',81,3,'Blow up the trumpet in the new moon, in the time appointed, on our solemn feast day.'),
(15224,19,'Psalms','OT',81,4,'For this {was} a statute for Israel, {and} a law of the God of Jacob.'),
(15225,19,'Psalms','OT',81,5,'This he ordained in Joseph {for} a testimony, when he went out through the land of Egypt: {where} I heard a language {that} I understood not. {through: or, against}'),
(15226,19,'Psalms','OT',81,6,'I removed his shoulder from the burden: his hands were delivered from the pots. {were...: Heb. passed away}'),
(15227,19,'Psalms','OT',81,7,'Thou calledst in trouble, and I delivered thee; I answered thee in the secret place of thunder: I proved thee at the waters of Meribah. Selah. {Meribah: or, Strife}'),
(15228,19,'Psalms','OT',81,8,'Hear, O my people, and I will testify unto thee: O Israel, if thou wilt hearken unto me;'),
(15229,19,'Psalms','OT',81,9,'There shall no strange god be in thee; neither shalt thou worship any strange god.'),
(15230,19,'Psalms','OT',81,10,'I {am} the LORD thy God, which brought thee out of the land of Egypt: open thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.'),
(15231,19,'Psalms','OT',81,11,'But my people would not hearken to my voice; and Israel would none of me.'),
(15232,19,'Psalms','OT',81,12,'So I gave them up unto their own hearts\' lust: {and} they walked in their own counsels. {unto...: or, to the hardness of their hearts, or, imagination}'),
(15233,19,'Psalms','OT',81,13,'Oh that my people had hearkened unto me, {and} Israel had walked in my ways!'),
(15234,19,'Psalms','OT',81,14,'I should soon have subdued their enemies, and turned my hand against their adversaries.'),
(15235,19,'Psalms','OT',81,15,'The haters of the LORD should have submitted themselves unto him: but their time should have endured for ever. {submitted...: or, yielded feigned obedience: Heb. lied}'),
(15236,19,'Psalms','OT',81,16,'He should have fed them also with the finest of the wheat: and with honey out of the rock should I have satisfied thee. {finest...: Heb. fat of wheat}'),
(15237,19,'Psalms','OT',82,1,'[A Psalm of Asaph.] God standeth in the congregation of the mighty; he judgeth among the gods. {of Asaph: or, for Asaph}'),
(15238,19,'Psalms','OT',82,2,'How long will ye judge unjustly, and accept the persons of the wicked? Selah.'),
(15239,19,'Psalms','OT',82,3,'Defend the poor and fatherless: do justice to the afflicted and needy. {Defend: Heb. Judge}'),
(15240,19,'Psalms','OT',82,4,'Deliver the poor and needy: rid {them} out of the hand of the wicked.'),
(15241,19,'Psalms','OT',82,5,'They know not, neither will they understand; they walk on in darkness: all the foundations of the earth are out of course. {out...: Heb. moved}'),
(15242,19,'Psalms','OT',82,6,'I have said, Ye {are} gods; and all of you {are} children of the most High.'),
(15243,19,'Psalms','OT',82,7,'But ye shall die like men, and fall like one of the princes.'),
(15244,19,'Psalms','OT',82,8,'Arise, O God, judge the earth: for thou shalt inherit all nations.'),
(15245,19,'Psalms','OT',83,1,'[A Song {or} Psalm of Asaph.] Keep not thou silence, O God: hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God. {of Asaph: or, for Asaph}'),
(15246,19,'Psalms','OT',83,2,'For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head.'),
(15247,19,'Psalms','OT',83,3,'They have taken crafty counsel against thy people, and consulted against thy hidden ones.'),
(15248,19,'Psalms','OT',83,4,'They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from {being} a nation; that the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance.'),
(15249,19,'Psalms','OT',83,5,'For they have consulted together with one consent: they are confederate against thee: {consent: Heb. heart}'),
(15250,19,'Psalms','OT',83,6,'The tabernacles of Edom, and the Ishmaelites; of Moab, and the Hagarenes;'),
(15251,19,'Psalms','OT',83,7,'Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; the Philistines with the inhabitants of Tyre;'),
(15252,19,'Psalms','OT',83,8,'Assur also is joined with them: they have holpen the children of Lot. Selah. {holpen: Heb. been an arm to}'),
(15253,19,'Psalms','OT',83,9,'Do unto them as {unto} the Midianites; as {to} Sisera, as {to} Jabin, at the brook of Kison:'),
(15254,19,'Psalms','OT',83,10,'{Which} perished at Endor: they became {as} dung for the earth.'),
(15255,19,'Psalms','OT',83,11,'Make their nobles like Oreb, and like Zeeb: yea, all their princes as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:'),
(15256,19,'Psalms','OT',83,12,'Who said, Let us take to ourselves the houses of God in possession.'),
(15257,19,'Psalms','OT',83,13,'O my God, make them like a wheel; as the stubble before the wind.'),
(15258,19,'Psalms','OT',83,14,'As the fire burneth a wood, and as the flame setteth the mountains on fire;'),
(15259,19,'Psalms','OT',83,15,'So persecute them with thy tempest, and make them afraid with thy storm.'),
(15260,19,'Psalms','OT',83,16,'Fill their faces with shame; that they may seek thy name, O LORD.'),
(15261,19,'Psalms','OT',83,17,'Let them be confounded and troubled for ever; yea, let them be put to shame, and perish:'),
(15262,19,'Psalms','OT',83,18,'That {men} may know that thou, whose name alone {is} JEHOVAH, {art} the most high over all the earth.'),
(15263,19,'Psalms','OT',84,1,'[To the chief Musician upon Gittith, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.] How amiable {are} thy tabernacles, O LORD of hosts! {for the sons: or, of the sons}'),
(15264,19,'Psalms','OT',84,2,'My soul longeth, yea, even fainteth for the courts of the LORD: my heart and my flesh crieth out for the living God.'),
(15265,19,'Psalms','OT',84,3,'Yea, the sparrow hath found an house, and the swallow a nest for herself, where she may lay her young, {even} thine altars, O LORD of hosts, my King, and my God.'),
(15266,19,'Psalms','OT',84,4,'Blessed {are} they that dwell in thy house: they will be still praising thee. Selah.'),
(15267,19,'Psalms','OT',84,5,'Blessed {is} the man whose strength {is} in thee; in whose heart {are} the ways {of them}.'),
(15268,19,'Psalms','OT',84,6,'{Who} passing through the valley of Baca make it a well; the rain also filleth the pools. {Baca...: or, mulberry trees make him a well, etc} {filleth: Heb. covereth}'),
(15269,19,'Psalms','OT',84,7,'They go from strength to strength, {every one of them} in Zion appeareth before God. {strength to...: or, company to company}'),
(15270,19,'Psalms','OT',84,8,'O LORD God of hosts, hear my prayer: give ear, O God of Jacob. Selah.'),
(15271,19,'Psalms','OT',84,9,'Behold, O God our shield, and look upon the face of thine anointed.'),
(15272,19,'Psalms','OT',84,10,'For a day in thy courts {is} better than a thousand. I had rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God, than to dwell in the tents of wickedness. {I had...: Heb. I would choose rather to sit at the threshold}'),
(15273,19,'Psalms','OT',84,11,'For the LORD God {is} a sun and shield: the LORD will give grace and glory: no good {thing} will he withhold from them that walk uprightly.'),
(15274,19,'Psalms','OT',84,12,'O LORD of hosts, blessed {is} the man that trusteth in thee.'),
(15275,19,'Psalms','OT',85,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm for the sons of Korah.] LORD, thou hast been favourable unto thy land: thou hast brought back the captivity of Jacob. {for the sons: or, of the sons} {favourable: or, well pleased}'),
(15276,19,'Psalms','OT',85,2,'Thou hast forgiven the iniquity of thy people, thou hast covered all their sin. Selah.'),
(15277,19,'Psalms','OT',85,3,'Thou hast taken away all thy wrath: thou hast turned {thyself} from the fierceness of thine anger. {thyself...: or, thine anger from waxing hot}'),
(15278,19,'Psalms','OT',85,4,'Turn us, O God of our salvation, and cause thine anger toward us to cease.'),
(15279,19,'Psalms','OT',85,5,'Wilt thou be angry with us for ever? wilt thou draw out thine anger to all generations?'),
(15280,19,'Psalms','OT',85,6,'Wilt thou not revive us again: that thy people may rejoice in thee?'),
(15281,19,'Psalms','OT',85,7,'Shew us thy mercy, O LORD, and grant us thy salvation.'),
(15282,19,'Psalms','OT',85,8,'I will hear what God the LORD will speak: for he will speak peace unto his people, and to his saints: but let them not turn again to folly.'),
(15283,19,'Psalms','OT',85,9,'Surely his salvation {is} nigh them that fear him; that glory may dwell in our land.'),
(15284,19,'Psalms','OT',85,10,'Mercy and truth are met together; righteousness and peace have kissed {each other}.'),
(15285,19,'Psalms','OT',85,11,'Truth shall spring out of the earth; and righteousness shall look down from heaven.'),
(15286,19,'Psalms','OT',85,12,'Yea, the LORD shall give {that which is} good; and our land shall yield her increase.'),
(15287,19,'Psalms','OT',85,13,'Righteousness shall go before him; and shall set {us} in the way of his steps.'),
(15288,19,'Psalms','OT',86,1,'[A Prayer of David.] Bow down thine ear, O LORD, hear me: for I {am} poor and needy. {A Prayer...: or, A Prayer, being a Psalm of David}'),
(15289,19,'Psalms','OT',86,2,'Preserve my soul; for I {am} holy: O thou my God, save thy servant that trusteth in thee. {holy: or, one whom thou favourest}'),
(15290,19,'Psalms','OT',86,3,'Be merciful unto me, O Lord: for I cry unto thee daily. {daily: or, all the day}'),
(15291,19,'Psalms','OT',86,4,'Rejoice the soul of thy servant: for unto thee, O Lord, do I lift up my soul.'),
(15292,19,'Psalms','OT',86,5,'For thou, Lord, {art} good, and ready to forgive; and plenteous in mercy unto all them that call upon thee.'),
(15293,19,'Psalms','OT',86,6,'Give ear, O LORD, unto my prayer; and attend to the voice of my supplications.'),
(15294,19,'Psalms','OT',86,7,'In the day of my trouble I will call upon thee: for thou wilt answer me.'),
(15295,19,'Psalms','OT',86,8,'Among the gods {there is} none like unto thee, O Lord; neither {are there any works} like unto thy works.'),
(15296,19,'Psalms','OT',86,9,'All nations whom thou hast made shall come and worship before thee, O Lord; and shall glorify thy name.'),
(15297,19,'Psalms','OT',86,10,'For thou {art} great, and doest wondrous things: thou {art} God alone.'),
(15298,19,'Psalms','OT',86,11,'Teach me thy way, O LORD; I will walk in thy truth: unite my heart to fear thy name.'),
(15299,19,'Psalms','OT',86,12,'I will praise thee, O Lord my God, with all my heart: and I will glorify thy name for evermore.'),
(15300,19,'Psalms','OT',86,13,'For great {is} thy mercy toward me: and thou hast delivered my soul from the lowest hell. {hell: or, grave}'),
(15301,19,'Psalms','OT',86,14,'O God, the proud are risen against me, and the assemblies of violent {men} have sought after my soul; and have not set thee before them. {violent: Heb. terrible}'),
(15302,19,'Psalms','OT',86,15,'But thou, O Lord, {art} a God full of compassion, and gracious, longsuffering, and plenteous in mercy and truth.'),
(15303,19,'Psalms','OT',86,16,'O turn unto me, and have mercy upon me; give thy strength unto thy servant, and save the son of thine handmaid.'),
(15304,19,'Psalms','OT',86,17,'Shew me a token for good; that they which hate me may see {it}, and be ashamed: because thou, LORD, hast holpen me, and comforted me.'),
(15305,19,'Psalms','OT',87,1,'[A Psalm {or} Song for the sons of Korah.] His foundation {is} in the holy mountains. {for the sons: or, of the sons}'),
(15306,19,'Psalms','OT',87,2,'The LORD loveth the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob.'),
(15307,19,'Psalms','OT',87,3,'Glorious things are spoken of thee, O city of God. Selah.'),
(15308,19,'Psalms','OT',87,4,'I will make mention of Rahab and Babylon to them that know me: behold Philistia, and Tyre, with Ethiopia; this {man} was born there.'),
(15309,19,'Psalms','OT',87,5,'And of Zion it shall be said, This and that man was born in her: and the highest himself shall establish her.'),
(15310,19,'Psalms','OT',87,6,'The LORD shall count, when he writeth up the people, {that} this {man} was born there. Selah.'),
(15311,19,'Psalms','OT',87,7,'As well the singers as the players on instruments {shall be there}: all my springs {are} in thee.'),
(15312,19,'Psalms','OT',88,1,'[A Song {or} Psalm for the sons of Korah, to the chief Musician upon Mahalath Leannoth, Maschil of Heman the Ezrahite.] O LORD God of my salvation, I have cried day {and} night before thee: {for the sons: or, of the sons} {Maschil...: or, A Psalm of Heman the Ezrahite, giving instruction}'),
(15313,19,'Psalms','OT',88,2,'Let my prayer come before thee: incline thine ear unto my cry;'),
(15314,19,'Psalms','OT',88,3,'For my soul is full of troubles: and my life draweth nigh unto the grave.'),
(15315,19,'Psalms','OT',88,4,'I am counted with them that go down into the pit: I am as a man {that hath} no strength:'),
(15316,19,'Psalms','OT',88,5,'Free among the dead, like the slain that lie in the grave, whom thou rememberest no more: and they are cut off from thy hand. {from: or, by}'),
(15317,19,'Psalms','OT',88,6,'Thou hast laid me in the lowest pit, in darkness, in the deeps.'),
(15318,19,'Psalms','OT',88,7,'Thy wrath lieth hard upon me, and thou hast afflicted {me} with all thy waves. Selah.'),
(15319,19,'Psalms','OT',88,8,'Thou hast put away mine acquaintance far from me; thou hast made me an abomination unto them: {I am} shut up, and I cannot come forth.'),
(15320,19,'Psalms','OT',88,9,'Mine eye mourneth by reason of affliction: LORD, I have called daily upon thee, I have stretched out my hands unto thee.'),
(15321,19,'Psalms','OT',88,10,'Wilt thou shew wonders to the dead? shall the dead arise {and} praise thee? Selah.'),
(15322,19,'Psalms','OT',88,11,'Shall thy lovingkindness be declared in the grave? {or} thy faithfulness in destruction?'),
(15323,19,'Psalms','OT',88,12,'Shall thy wonders be known in the dark? and thy righteousness in the land of forgetfulness?'),
(15324,19,'Psalms','OT',88,13,'But unto thee have I cried, O LORD; and in the morning shall my prayer prevent thee.'),
(15325,19,'Psalms','OT',88,14,'LORD, why castest thou off my soul? {why} hidest thou thy face from me?'),
(15326,19,'Psalms','OT',88,15,'I {am} afflicted and ready to die from {my} youth up: {while} I suffer thy terrors I am distracted.'),
(15327,19,'Psalms','OT',88,16,'Thy fierce wrath goeth over me; thy terrors have cut me off.'),
(15328,19,'Psalms','OT',88,17,'They came round about me daily like water; they compassed me about together. {daily: or, all the day}'),
(15329,19,'Psalms','OT',88,18,'Lover and friend hast thou put far from me, {and} mine acquaintance into darkness.'),
(15330,19,'Psalms','OT',89,1,'[Maschil of Ethan the Ezrahite.] I will sing of the mercies of the LORD for ever: with my mouth will I make known thy faithfulness to all generations. {Maschil...: or, A Psalm for Ethan the Ezrahite, to give instruction} {to all...: Heb. to generation and generation}'),
(15331,19,'Psalms','OT',89,2,'For I have said, Mercy shall be built up for ever: thy faithfulness shalt thou establish in the very heavens.'),
(15332,19,'Psalms','OT',89,3,'I have made a covenant with my chosen, I have sworn unto David my servant,'),
(15333,19,'Psalms','OT',89,4,'Thy seed will I establish for ever, and build up thy throne to all generations. Selah.'),
(15334,19,'Psalms','OT',89,5,'And the heavens shall praise thy wonders, O LORD: thy faithfulness also in the congregation of the saints.'),
(15335,19,'Psalms','OT',89,6,'For who in the heaven can be compared unto the LORD? {who} among the sons of the mighty can be likened unto the LORD?'),
(15336,19,'Psalms','OT',89,7,'God is greatly to be feared in the assembly of the saints, and to be had in reverence of all {them that are} about him.'),
(15337,19,'Psalms','OT',89,8,'O LORD God of hosts, who {is} a strong LORD like unto thee? or to thy faithfulness round about thee?'),
(15338,19,'Psalms','OT',89,9,'Thou rulest the raging of the sea: when the waves thereof arise, thou stillest them.'),
(15339,19,'Psalms','OT',89,10,'Thou hast broken Rahab in pieces, as one that is slain; thou hast scattered thine enemies with thy strong arm. {Rahab: or, Egypt} {thy...: Heb. the arm of thy strength}'),
(15340,19,'Psalms','OT',89,11,'The heavens {are} thine, the earth also {is} thine: {as for} the world and the fulness thereof, thou hast founded them. {the fulness...: or, all it containeth}'),
(15341,19,'Psalms','OT',89,12,'The north and the south thou hast created them: Tabor and Hermon shall rejoice in thy name.'),
(15342,19,'Psalms','OT',89,13,'Thou hast a mighty arm: strong is thy hand, {and} high is thy right hand. {a...: Heb. an arm with might}'),
(15343,19,'Psalms','OT',89,14,'Justice and judgment {are} the habitation of thy throne: mercy and truth shall go before thy face. {habitation: or, establishment}'),
(15344,19,'Psalms','OT',89,15,'Blessed {is} the people that know the joyful sound: they shall walk, O LORD, in the light of thy countenance.'),
(15345,19,'Psalms','OT',89,16,'In thy name shall they rejoice all the day: and in thy righteousness shall they be exalted.'),
(15346,19,'Psalms','OT',89,17,'For thou {art} the glory of their strength: and in thy favour our horn shall be exalted.'),
(15347,19,'Psalms','OT',89,18,'For the LORD {is} our defence; and the Holy One of Israel {is} our king. {the LORD...: or, our shield is of the LORD, and our king is of the Holy One of Israel}'),
(15348,19,'Psalms','OT',89,19,'Then thou spakest in vision to thy holy one, and saidst, I have laid help upon {one that is} mighty; I have exalted {one} chosen out of the people.'),
(15349,19,'Psalms','OT',89,20,'I have found David my servant; with my holy oil have I anointed him:'),
(15350,19,'Psalms','OT',89,21,'With whom my hand shall be established: mine arm also shall strengthen him.'),
(15351,19,'Psalms','OT',89,22,'The enemy shall not exact upon him; nor the son of wickedness afflict him.'),
(15352,19,'Psalms','OT',89,23,'And I will beat down his foes before his face, and plague them that hate him.'),
(15353,19,'Psalms','OT',89,24,'But my faithfulness and my mercy {shall be} with him: and in my name shall his horn be exalted.'),
(15354,19,'Psalms','OT',89,25,'I will set his hand also in the sea, and his right hand in the rivers.'),
(15355,19,'Psalms','OT',89,26,'He shall cry unto me, Thou {art} my father, my God, and the rock of my salvation.'),
(15356,19,'Psalms','OT',89,27,'Also I will make him {my} firstborn, higher than the kings of the earth.'),
(15357,19,'Psalms','OT',89,28,'My mercy will I keep for him for evermore, and my covenant shall stand fast with him.'),
(15358,19,'Psalms','OT',89,29,'His seed also will I make {to endure} for ever, and his throne as the days of heaven.'),
(15359,19,'Psalms','OT',89,30,'If his children forsake my law, and walk not in my judgments;'),
(15360,19,'Psalms','OT',89,31,'If they break my statutes, and keep not my commandments; {break: Heb. profane}'),
(15361,19,'Psalms','OT',89,32,'Then will I visit their transgression with the rod, and their iniquity with stripes.'),
(15362,19,'Psalms','OT',89,33,'Nevertheless my lovingkindness will I not utterly take from him, nor suffer my faithfulness to fail. {will...: Heb. I will not make void from him} {to fall: Heb. to lie}'),
(15363,19,'Psalms','OT',89,34,'My covenant will I not break, nor alter the thing that is gone out of my lips.'),
(15364,19,'Psalms','OT',89,35,'Once have I sworn by my holiness that I will not lie unto David. {that...: Heb. if I lie}'),
(15365,19,'Psalms','OT',89,36,'His seed shall endure for ever, and his throne as the sun before me.'),
(15366,19,'Psalms','OT',89,37,'It shall be established for ever as the moon, and {as} a faithful witness in heaven. Selah.'),
(15367,19,'Psalms','OT',89,38,'But thou hast cast off and abhorred, thou hast been wroth with thine anointed.'),
(15368,19,'Psalms','OT',89,39,'Thou hast made void the covenant of thy servant: thou hast profaned his crown {by casting it} to the ground.'),
(15369,19,'Psalms','OT',89,40,'Thou hast broken down all his hedges; thou hast brought his strong holds to ruin.'),
(15370,19,'Psalms','OT',89,41,'All that pass by the way spoil him: he is a reproach to his neighbours.'),
(15371,19,'Psalms','OT',89,42,'Thou hast set up the right hand of his adversaries; thou hast made all his enemies to rejoice.'),
(15372,19,'Psalms','OT',89,43,'Thou hast also turned the edge of his sword, and hast not made him to stand in the battle.'),
(15373,19,'Psalms','OT',89,44,'Thou hast made his glory to cease, and cast his throne down to the ground. {glory: Heb. brightness}'),
(15374,19,'Psalms','OT',89,45,'The days of his youth hast thou shortened: thou hast covered him with shame. Selah.'),
(15375,19,'Psalms','OT',89,46,'How long, LORD? wilt thou hide thyself for ever? shall thy wrath burn like fire?'),
(15376,19,'Psalms','OT',89,47,'Remember how short my time is: wherefore hast thou made all men in vain?'),
(15377,19,'Psalms','OT',89,48,'What man {is he that} liveth, and shall not see death? shall he deliver his soul from the hand of the grave? Selah.'),
(15378,19,'Psalms','OT',89,49,'Lord, where {are} thy former lovingkindnesses, {which} thou swarest unto David in thy truth?'),
(15379,19,'Psalms','OT',89,50,'Remember, Lord, the reproach of thy servants; {how} I do bear in my bosom {the reproach of} all the mighty people;'),
(15380,19,'Psalms','OT',89,51,'Wherewith thine enemies have reproached, O LORD; wherewith they have reproached the footsteps of thine anointed.'),
(15381,19,'Psalms','OT',89,52,'Blessed {be} the LORD for evermore. Amen, and Amen.'),
(15382,19,'Psalms','OT',90,1,'[A Prayer of Moses the man of God.] Lord, thou hast been our dwelling place in all generations. {A Prayer...: or, A Prayer, being a Psalm of Moses} {in...: Heb. in generation and generation}'),
(15383,19,'Psalms','OT',90,2,'Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, thou {art} God.'),
(15384,19,'Psalms','OT',90,3,'Thou turnest man to destruction; and sayest, Return, ye children of men.'),
(15385,19,'Psalms','OT',90,4,'For a thousand years in thy sight {are but} as yesterday when it is past, and {as} a watch in the night. {when...: or, when he hath passed them}'),
(15386,19,'Psalms','OT',90,5,'Thou carriest them away as with a flood; they are {as} a sleep: in the morning {they are} like grass {which} groweth up. {groweth...: or, is changed}'),
(15387,19,'Psalms','OT',90,6,'In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth up; in the evening it is cut down, and withereth.'),
(15388,19,'Psalms','OT',90,7,'For we are consumed by thine anger, and by thy wrath are we troubled.'),
(15389,19,'Psalms','OT',90,8,'Thou hast set our iniquities before thee, our secret {sins} in the light of thy countenance.'),
(15390,19,'Psalms','OT',90,9,'For all our days are passed away in thy wrath: we spend our years as a tale {that is told}. {passed...: Heb. turned away} {as a...: or, as a meditation}'),
(15391,19,'Psalms','OT',90,10,'The days of our years {are} threescore years and ten; and if by reason of strength {they be} fourscore years, yet {is} their strength labour and sorrow; for it is soon cut off, and we fly away. {The days...: Heb. As for the days of our years, in them are seventy years}'),
(15392,19,'Psalms','OT',90,11,'Who knoweth the power of thine anger? even according to thy fear, {so is} thy wrath.'),
(15393,19,'Psalms','OT',90,12,'So teach {us} to number our days, that we may apply {our} hearts unto wisdom. {apply: Heb. cause to come}'),
(15394,19,'Psalms','OT',90,13,'Return, O LORD, how long? and let it repent thee concerning thy servants.'),
(15395,19,'Psalms','OT',90,14,'O satisfy us early with thy mercy; that we may rejoice and be glad all our days.'),
(15396,19,'Psalms','OT',90,15,'Make us glad according to the days {wherein} thou hast afflicted us, {and} the years {wherein} we have seen evil.'),
(15397,19,'Psalms','OT',90,16,'Let thy work appear unto thy servants, and thy glory unto their children.'),
(15398,19,'Psalms','OT',90,17,'And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it.'),
(15399,19,'Psalms','OT',91,1,'He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty. {abide: Heb. lodge}'),
(15400,19,'Psalms','OT',91,2,'I will say of the LORD, {He is} my refuge and my fortress: my God; in him will I trust.'),
(15401,19,'Psalms','OT',91,3,'Surely he shall deliver thee from the snare of the fowler, {and} from the noisome pestilence.'),
(15402,19,'Psalms','OT',91,4,'He shall cover thee with his feathers, and under his wings shalt thou trust: his truth {shall be thy} shield and buckler.'),
(15403,19,'Psalms','OT',91,5,'Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night; {nor} for the arrow {that} flieth by day;'),
(15404,19,'Psalms','OT',91,6,'{Nor} for the pestilence {that} walketh in darkness; {nor} for the destruction {that} wasteth at noonday.'),
(15405,19,'Psalms','OT',91,7,'A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand; {but} it shall not come nigh thee.'),
(15406,19,'Psalms','OT',91,8,'Only with thine eyes shalt thou behold and see the reward of the wicked.'),
(15407,19,'Psalms','OT',91,9,'Because thou hast made the LORD, {which is} my refuge, {even} the most High, thy habitation;'),
(15408,19,'Psalms','OT',91,10,'There shall no evil befall thee, neither shall any plague come nigh thy dwelling.'),
(15409,19,'Psalms','OT',91,11,'For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.'),
(15410,19,'Psalms','OT',91,12,'They shall bear thee up in {their} hands, lest thou dash thy foot against a stone.'),
(15411,19,'Psalms','OT',91,13,'Thou shalt tread upon the lion and adder: the young lion and the dragon shalt thou trample under feet. {adder: or, asp}'),
(15412,19,'Psalms','OT',91,14,'Because he hath set his love upon me, therefore will I deliver him: I will set him on high, because he hath known my name.'),
(15413,19,'Psalms','OT',91,15,'He shall call upon me, and I will answer him: I {will be} with him in trouble; I will deliver him, and honour him.'),
(15414,19,'Psalms','OT',91,16,'With long life will I satisfy him, and shew him my salvation. {long...: Heb. length of days}'),
(15415,19,'Psalms','OT',92,1,'[A Psalm {or} Song for the sabbath day.] {It is a} good {thing} to give thanks unto the LORD, and to sing praises unto thy name, O most High:'),
(15416,19,'Psalms','OT',92,2,'To shew forth thy lovingkindness in the morning, and thy faithfulness every night, {every...: Heb. in the nights}'),
(15417,19,'Psalms','OT',92,3,'Upon an instrument of ten strings, and upon the psaltery; upon the harp with a solemn sound. {the harp...: or, the solemn sound with the harp} {a solemn...: Heb. Higgaion}'),
(15418,19,'Psalms','OT',92,4,'For thou, LORD, hast made me glad through thy work: I will triumph in the works of thy hands.'),
(15419,19,'Psalms','OT',92,5,'O LORD, how great are thy works! {and} thy thoughts are very deep.'),
(15420,19,'Psalms','OT',92,6,'A brutish man knoweth not; neither doth a fool understand this.'),
(15421,19,'Psalms','OT',92,7,'When the wicked spring as the grass, and when all the workers of iniquity do flourish; {it is} that they shall be destroyed for ever:'),
(15422,19,'Psalms','OT',92,8,'But thou, LORD, {art most} high for evermore.'),
(15423,19,'Psalms','OT',92,9,'For, lo, thine enemies, O LORD, for, lo, thine enemies shall perish; all the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.'),
(15424,19,'Psalms','OT',92,10,'But my horn shalt thou exalt like {the horn of} an unicorn: I shall be anointed with fresh oil.'),
(15425,19,'Psalms','OT',92,11,'Mine eye also shall see {my desire} on mine enemies, {and} mine ears shall hear {my desire} of the wicked that rise up against me.'),
(15426,19,'Psalms','OT',92,12,'The righteous shall flourish like the palm tree: he shall grow like a cedar in Lebanon.'),
(15427,19,'Psalms','OT',92,13,'Those that be planted in the house of the LORD shall flourish in the courts of our God.'),
(15428,19,'Psalms','OT',92,14,'They shall still bring forth fruit in old age; they shall be fat and flourishing; {flourishing: Heb. green}'),
(15429,19,'Psalms','OT',92,15,'To shew that the LORD {is} upright: {he is} my rock, and {there is} no unrighteousness in him.'),
(15430,19,'Psalms','OT',93,1,'The LORD reigneth, he is clothed with majesty; the LORD is clothed with strength, {wherewith} he hath girded himself: the world also is stablished, that it cannot be moved.'),
(15431,19,'Psalms','OT',93,2,'Thy throne {is} established of old: thou {art} from everlasting. {of old: Heb. from then}'),
(15432,19,'Psalms','OT',93,3,'The floods have lifted up, O LORD, the floods have lifted up their voice; the floods lift up their waves.'),
(15433,19,'Psalms','OT',93,4,'The LORD on high {is} mightier than the noise of many waters, {yea, than} the mighty waves of the sea.'),
(15434,19,'Psalms','OT',93,5,'Thy testimonies are very sure: holiness becometh thine house, O LORD, for ever. {for ever: Heb. to length of days}'),
(15435,19,'Psalms','OT',94,1,'O LORD God, to whom vengeance belongeth; O God, to whom vengeance belongeth, shew thyself. {God...: Heb. God of revenges} {shew...: Heb. shine forth}'),
(15436,19,'Psalms','OT',94,2,'Lift up thyself, thou judge of the earth: render a reward to the proud.'),
(15437,19,'Psalms','OT',94,3,'LORD, how long shall the wicked, how long shall the wicked triumph?'),
(15438,19,'Psalms','OT',94,4,'{How long} shall they utter {and} speak hard things? {and} all the workers of iniquity boast themselves?'),
(15439,19,'Psalms','OT',94,5,'They break in pieces thy people, O LORD, and afflict thine heritage.'),
(15440,19,'Psalms','OT',94,6,'They slay the widow and the stranger, and murder the fatherless.'),
(15441,19,'Psalms','OT',94,7,'Yet they say, The LORD shall not see, neither shall the God of Jacob regard {it}.'),
(15442,19,'Psalms','OT',94,8,'Understand, ye brutish among the people: and {ye} fools, when will ye be wise?'),
(15443,19,'Psalms','OT',94,9,'He that planted the ear, shall he not hear? he that formed the eye, shall he not see?'),
(15444,19,'Psalms','OT',94,10,'He that chastiseth the heathen, shall not he correct? he that teacheth man knowledge, {shall not he know}?'),
(15445,19,'Psalms','OT',94,11,'The LORD knoweth the thoughts of man, that they {are} vanity.'),
(15446,19,'Psalms','OT',94,12,'Blessed {is} the man whom thou chastenest, O LORD, and teachest him out of thy law;'),
(15447,19,'Psalms','OT',94,13,'That thou mayest give him rest from the days of adversity, until the pit be digged for the wicked.'),
(15448,19,'Psalms','OT',94,14,'For the LORD will not cast off his people, neither will he forsake his inheritance.'),
(15449,19,'Psalms','OT',94,15,'But judgment shall return unto righteousness: and all the upright in heart shall follow it. {shall follow...: Heb. shall be after it}'),
(15450,19,'Psalms','OT',94,16,'Who will rise up for me against the evildoers? {or} who will stand up for me against the workers of iniquity?'),
(15451,19,'Psalms','OT',94,17,'Unless the LORD {had been} my help, my soul had almost dwelt in silence. {almost: or, quickly}'),
(15452,19,'Psalms','OT',94,18,'When I said, My foot slippeth; thy mercy, O LORD, held me up.'),
(15453,19,'Psalms','OT',94,19,'In the multitude of my thoughts within me thy comforts delight my soul.'),
(15454,19,'Psalms','OT',94,20,'Shall the throne of iniquity have fellowship with thee, which frameth mischief by a law?'),
(15455,19,'Psalms','OT',94,21,'They gather themselves together against the soul of the righteous, and condemn the innocent blood.'),
(15456,19,'Psalms','OT',94,22,'But the LORD is my defence; and my God {is} the rock of my refuge.'),
(15457,19,'Psalms','OT',94,23,'And he shall bring upon them their own iniquity, and shall cut them off in their own wickedness; {yea}, the LORD our God shall cut them off.'),
(15458,19,'Psalms','OT',95,1,'O come, let us sing unto the LORD: let us make a joyful noise to the rock of our salvation.'),
(15459,19,'Psalms','OT',95,2,'Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving, and make a joyful noise unto him with psalms. {come...: Heb. prevent his face}'),
(15460,19,'Psalms','OT',95,3,'For the LORD {is} a great God, and a great King above all gods.'),
(15461,19,'Psalms','OT',95,4,'In his hand {are} the deep places of the earth: the strength of the hills {is} his also. {In...: Heb. In whose} {the strength...: or, the heights of the hills are his}'),
(15462,19,'Psalms','OT',95,5,'The sea {is} his, and he made it: and his hands formed the dry {land}. {The sea...: Heb. Whose the sea is}'),
(15463,19,'Psalms','OT',95,6,'O come, let us worship and bow down: let us kneel before the LORD our maker.'),
(15464,19,'Psalms','OT',95,7,'For he {is} our God; and we {are} the people of his pasture, and the sheep of his hand. To day if ye will hear his voice,'),
(15465,19,'Psalms','OT',95,8,'Harden not your heart, as in the provocation, {and} as {in} the day of temptation in the wilderness: {provocation: Heb. contention}'),
(15466,19,'Psalms','OT',95,9,'When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my work.'),
(15467,19,'Psalms','OT',95,10,'Forty years long was I grieved with {this} generation, and said, It {is} a people that do err in their heart, and they have not known my ways:'),
(15468,19,'Psalms','OT',95,11,'Unto whom I sware in my wrath that they should not enter into my rest. {that...: Heb. if they enter into my rest}'),
(15469,19,'Psalms','OT',96,1,'O sing unto the LORD a new song: sing unto the LORD, all the earth.'),
(15470,19,'Psalms','OT',96,2,'Sing unto the LORD, bless his name; shew forth his salvation from day to day.'),
(15471,19,'Psalms','OT',96,3,'Declare his glory among the heathen, his wonders among all people.'),
(15472,19,'Psalms','OT',96,4,'For the LORD {is} great, and greatly to be praised: he {is} to be feared above all gods.'),
(15473,19,'Psalms','OT',96,5,'For all the gods of the nations {are} idols: but the LORD made the heavens.'),
(15474,19,'Psalms','OT',96,6,'Honour and majesty {are} before him: strength and beauty {are} in his sanctuary.'),
(15475,19,'Psalms','OT',96,7,'Give unto the LORD, O ye kindreds of the people, give unto the LORD glory and strength.'),
(15476,19,'Psalms','OT',96,8,'Give unto the LORD the glory {due unto} his name: bring an offering, and come into his courts. {due...: Heb. of his name}'),
(15477,19,'Psalms','OT',96,9,'O worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness: fear before him, all the earth. {in the...: or, in the glorious sanctuary}'),
(15478,19,'Psalms','OT',96,10,'Say among the heathen {that} the LORD reigneth: the world also shall be established that it shall not be moved: he shall judge the people righteously.'),
(15479,19,'Psalms','OT',96,11,'Let the heavens rejoice, and let the earth be glad; let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof. {the fulness...: or, all it containeth}'),
(15480,19,'Psalms','OT',96,12,'Let the field be joyful, and all that {is} therein: then shall all the trees of the wood rejoice'),
(15481,19,'Psalms','OT',96,13,'Before the LORD: for he cometh, for he cometh to judge the earth: he shall judge the world with righteousness, and the people with his truth.'),
(15482,19,'Psalms','OT',97,1,'The LORD reigneth; let the earth rejoice; let the multitude of isles be glad {thereof}. {multitude...: Heb. many, or, great isles}'),
(15483,19,'Psalms','OT',97,2,'Clouds and darkness {are} round about him: righteousness and judgment {are} the habitation of his throne. {habitation: or, establishment}'),
(15484,19,'Psalms','OT',97,3,'A fire goeth before him, and burneth up his enemies round about.'),
(15485,19,'Psalms','OT',97,4,'His lightnings enlightened the world: the earth saw, and trembled.'),
(15486,19,'Psalms','OT',97,5,'The hills melted like wax at the presence of the LORD, at the presence of the Lord of the whole earth.'),
(15487,19,'Psalms','OT',97,6,'The heavens declare his righteousness, and all the people see his glory.'),
(15488,19,'Psalms','OT',97,7,'Confounded be all they that serve graven images, that boast themselves of idols: worship him, all {ye} gods.'),
(15489,19,'Psalms','OT',97,8,'Zion heard, and was glad; and the daughters of Judah rejoiced because of thy judgments, O LORD.'),
(15490,19,'Psalms','OT',97,9,'For thou, LORD, {art} high above all the earth: thou art exalted far above all gods.'),
(15491,19,'Psalms','OT',97,10,'Ye that love the LORD, hate evil: he preserveth the souls of his saints; he delivereth them out of the hand of the wicked.'),
(15492,19,'Psalms','OT',97,11,'Light is sown for the righteous, and gladness for the upright in heart.'),
(15493,19,'Psalms','OT',97,12,'Rejoice in the LORD, ye righteous; and give thanks at the remembrance of his holiness. {at...: or, to the memorial}'),
(15494,19,'Psalms','OT',98,1,'[A Psalm.] O sing unto the LORD a new song; for he hath done marvellous things: his right hand, and his holy arm, hath gotten him the victory.'),
(15495,19,'Psalms','OT',98,2,'The LORD hath made known his salvation: his righteousness hath he openly shewed in the sight of the heathen. {openly...: or, revealed}'),
(15496,19,'Psalms','OT',98,3,'He hath remembered his mercy and his truth toward the house of Israel: all the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.'),
(15497,19,'Psalms','OT',98,4,'Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all the earth: make a loud noise, and rejoice, and sing praise.'),
(15498,19,'Psalms','OT',98,5,'Sing unto the LORD with the harp; with the harp, and the voice of a psalm.'),
(15499,19,'Psalms','OT',98,6,'With trumpets and sound of cornet make a joyful noise before the LORD, the King.'),
(15500,19,'Psalms','OT',98,7,'Let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein. {the fulness...: or, all it containeth}'),
(15501,19,'Psalms','OT',98,8,'Let the floods clap {their} hands: let the hills be joyful together'),
(15502,19,'Psalms','OT',98,9,'Before the LORD; for he cometh to judge the earth: with righteousness shall he judge the world, and the people with equity.'),
(15503,19,'Psalms','OT',99,1,'The LORD reigneth; let the people tremble: he sitteth {between} the cherubims; let the earth be moved. {be moved: Heb. stagger}'),
(15504,19,'Psalms','OT',99,2,'The LORD {is} great in Zion; and he {is} high above all the people.'),
(15505,19,'Psalms','OT',99,3,'Let them praise thy great and terrible name; {for} it {is} holy.'),
(15506,19,'Psalms','OT',99,4,'The king\'s strength also loveth judgment; thou dost establish equity, thou executest judgment and righteousness in Jacob.'),
(15507,19,'Psalms','OT',99,5,'Exalt ye the LORD our God, and worship at his footstool; {for} he {is} holy. {he is...: or, it is holy}'),
(15508,19,'Psalms','OT',99,6,'Moses and Aaron among his priests, and Samuel among them that call upon his name; they called upon the LORD, and he answered them.'),
(15509,19,'Psalms','OT',99,7,'He spake unto them in the cloudy pillar: they kept his testimonies, and the ordinance {that} he gave them.'),
(15510,19,'Psalms','OT',99,8,'Thou answeredst them, O LORD our God: thou wast a God that forgavest them, though thou tookest vengeance of their inventions.'),
(15511,19,'Psalms','OT',99,9,'Exalt the LORD our God, and worship at his holy hill; for the LORD our God {is} holy.'),
(15512,19,'Psalms','OT',100,1,'[A Psalm of praise.] Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all ye lands. {praise: or, thanksgiving} {all...: Heb. all the earth}'),
(15513,19,'Psalms','OT',100,2,'Serve the LORD with gladness: come before his presence with singing.'),
(15514,19,'Psalms','OT',100,3,'Know ye that the LORD he {is} God: {it is} he {that} hath made us, and not we ourselves; {we are} his people, and the sheep of his pasture. {and not...: or, and his we are}'),
(15515,19,'Psalms','OT',100,4,'Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, {and} into his courts with praise: be thankful unto him, {and} bless his name.'),
(15516,19,'Psalms','OT',100,5,'For the LORD {is} good; his mercy {is} everlasting; and his truth {endureth} to all generations. {to all...: Heb. to generation and generation}'),
(15517,19,'Psalms','OT',101,1,'[A Psalm of David.] I will sing of mercy and judgment: unto thee, O LORD, will I sing.'),
(15518,19,'Psalms','OT',101,2,'I will behave myself wisely in a perfect way. O when wilt thou come unto me? I will walk within my house with a perfect heart.'),
(15519,19,'Psalms','OT',101,3,'I will set no wicked thing before mine eyes: I hate the work of them that turn aside; {it} shall not cleave to me. {wicked...: Heb. thing of Belial}'),
(15520,19,'Psalms','OT',101,4,'A froward heart shall depart from me: I will not know a wicked {person}.'),
(15521,19,'Psalms','OT',101,5,'Whoso privily slandereth his neighbour, him will I cut off: him that hath an high look and a proud heart will not I suffer.'),
(15522,19,'Psalms','OT',101,6,'Mine eyes {shall be} upon the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me: he that walketh in a perfect way, he shall serve me. {in a...: or, perfect in the way}'),
(15523,19,'Psalms','OT',101,7,'He that worketh deceit shall not dwell within my house: he that telleth lies shall not tarry in my sight. {shall not tarry: Heb. shall not be established}'),
(15524,19,'Psalms','OT',101,8,'I will early destroy all the wicked of the land; that I may cut off all wicked doers from the city of the LORD.'),
(15525,19,'Psalms','OT',102,1,'[A Prayer of the afflicted, when he is overwhelmed, and poureth out his complaint before the LORD.] Hear my prayer, O LORD, and let my cry come unto thee. {of: or, for}'),
(15526,19,'Psalms','OT',102,2,'Hide not thy face from me in the day {when} I am in trouble; incline thine ear unto me: in the day {when} I call answer me speedily.'),
(15527,19,'Psalms','OT',102,3,'For my days are consumed like smoke, and my bones are burned as an hearth. {like...: or, (as some read) into smoke}'),
(15528,19,'Psalms','OT',102,4,'My heart is smitten, and withered like grass; so that I forget to eat my bread.'),
(15529,19,'Psalms','OT',102,5,'By reason of the voice of my groaning my bones cleave to my skin. {skin: or, flesh}'),
(15530,19,'Psalms','OT',102,6,'I am like a pelican of the wilderness: I am like an owl of the desert.'),
(15531,19,'Psalms','OT',102,7,'I watch, and am as a sparrow alone upon the house top.'),
(15532,19,'Psalms','OT',102,8,'Mine enemies reproach me all the day; {and} they that are mad against me are sworn against me.'),
(15533,19,'Psalms','OT',102,9,'For I have eaten ashes like bread, and mingled my drink with weeping,'),
(15534,19,'Psalms','OT',102,10,'Because of thine indignation and thy wrath: for thou hast lifted me up, and cast me down.'),
(15535,19,'Psalms','OT',102,11,'My days {are} like a shadow that declineth; and I am withered like grass.'),
(15536,19,'Psalms','OT',102,12,'But thou, O LORD, shalt endure for ever; and thy remembrance unto all generations.'),
(15537,19,'Psalms','OT',102,13,'Thou shalt arise, {and} have mercy upon Zion: for the time to favour her, yea, the set time, is come.'),
(15538,19,'Psalms','OT',102,14,'For thy servants take pleasure in her stones, and favour the dust thereof.'),
(15539,19,'Psalms','OT',102,15,'So the heathen shall fear the name of the LORD, and all the kings of the earth thy glory.'),
(15540,19,'Psalms','OT',102,16,'When the LORD shall build up Zion, he shall appear in his glory.'),
(15541,19,'Psalms','OT',102,17,'He will regard the prayer of the destitute, and not despise their prayer.'),
(15542,19,'Psalms','OT',102,18,'This shall be written for the generation to come: and the people which shall be created shall praise the LORD.'),
(15543,19,'Psalms','OT',102,19,'For he hath looked down from the height of his sanctuary; from heaven did the LORD behold the earth;'),
(15544,19,'Psalms','OT',102,20,'To hear the groaning of the prisoner; to loose those that are appointed to death; {those...: Heb. the children of death}'),
(15545,19,'Psalms','OT',102,21,'To declare the name of the LORD in Zion, and his praise in Jerusalem;'),
(15546,19,'Psalms','OT',102,22,'When the people are gathered together, and the kingdoms, to serve the LORD.'),
(15547,19,'Psalms','OT',102,23,'He weakened my strength in the way; he shortened my days. {weakened: Heb. afflicted}'),
(15548,19,'Psalms','OT',102,24,'I said, O my God, take me not away in the midst of my days: thy years {are} throughout all generations.'),
(15549,19,'Psalms','OT',102,25,'Of old hast thou laid the foundation of the earth: and the heavens {are} the work of thy hands.'),
(15550,19,'Psalms','OT',102,26,'They shall perish, but thou shalt endure: yea, all of them shall wax old like a garment; as a vesture shalt thou change them, and they shall be changed: {endure: Heb. stand}'),
(15551,19,'Psalms','OT',102,27,'But thou {art} the same, and thy years shall have no end.'),
(15552,19,'Psalms','OT',102,28,'The children of thy servants shall continue, and their seed shall be established before thee.'),
(15553,19,'Psalms','OT',103,1,'[{A Psalm} of David.] Bless the LORD, O my soul: and all that is within me, {bless} his holy name.'),
(15554,19,'Psalms','OT',103,2,'Bless the LORD, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits:'),
(15555,19,'Psalms','OT',103,3,'Who forgiveth all thine iniquities; who healeth all thy diseases;'),
(15556,19,'Psalms','OT',103,4,'Who redeemeth thy life from destruction; who crowneth thee with lovingkindness and tender mercies;'),
(15557,19,'Psalms','OT',103,5,'Who satisfieth thy mouth with good {things; so that} thy youth is renewed like the eagle\'s.'),
(15558,19,'Psalms','OT',103,6,'The LORD executeth righteousness and judgment for all that are oppressed.'),
(15559,19,'Psalms','OT',103,7,'He made known his ways unto Moses, his acts unto the children of Israel.'),
(15560,19,'Psalms','OT',103,8,'The LORD {is} merciful and gracious, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy. {plentious...: Heb. great in mercy}'),
(15561,19,'Psalms','OT',103,9,'He will not always chide: neither will he keep {his anger} for ever.'),
(15562,19,'Psalms','OT',103,10,'He hath not dealt with us after our sins; nor rewarded us according to our iniquities.'),
(15563,19,'Psalms','OT',103,11,'For as the heaven is high above the earth, {so} great is his mercy toward them that fear him. {as...: Heb. according to the height of the heaven}'),
(15564,19,'Psalms','OT',103,12,'As far as the east is from the west, {so} far hath he removed our transgressions from us.'),
(15565,19,'Psalms','OT',103,13,'Like as a father pitieth {his} children, {so} the LORD pitieth them that fear him.'),
(15566,19,'Psalms','OT',103,14,'For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we {are} dust.'),
(15567,19,'Psalms','OT',103,15,'{As for} man, his days {are} as grass: as a flower of the field, so he flourisheth.'),
(15568,19,'Psalms','OT',103,16,'For the wind passeth over it, and it is gone; and the place thereof shall know it no more. {it is...: Heb. it is not}'),
(15569,19,'Psalms','OT',103,17,'But the mercy of the LORD {is} from everlasting to everlasting upon them that fear him, and his righteousness unto children\'s children;'),
(15570,19,'Psalms','OT',103,18,'To such as keep his covenant, and to those that remember his commandments to do them.'),
(15571,19,'Psalms','OT',103,19,'The LORD hath prepared his throne in the heavens; and his kingdom ruleth over all.'),
(15572,19,'Psalms','OT',103,20,'Bless the LORD, ye his angels, that excel in strength, that do his commandments, hearkening unto the voice of his word. {that excel...: Heb. mighty in strength}'),
(15573,19,'Psalms','OT',103,21,'Bless ye the LORD, all {ye} his hosts; {ye} ministers of his, that do his pleasure.'),
(15574,19,'Psalms','OT',103,22,'Bless the LORD, all his works in all places of his dominion: bless the LORD, O my soul.'),
(15575,19,'Psalms','OT',104,1,'Bless the LORD, O my soul. O LORD my God, thou art very great; thou art clothed with honour and majesty.'),
(15576,19,'Psalms','OT',104,2,'Who coverest {thyself} with light as {with} a garment: who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:'),
(15577,19,'Psalms','OT',104,3,'Who layeth the beams of his chambers in the waters: who maketh the clouds his chariot: who walketh upon the wings of the wind:'),
(15578,19,'Psalms','OT',104,4,'Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:'),
(15579,19,'Psalms','OT',104,5,'{Who} laid the foundations of the earth, {that} it should not be removed for ever. {Who...: Heb. He hath founded the earth upon her bases}'),
(15580,19,'Psalms','OT',104,6,'Thou coveredst it with the deep as {with} a garment: the waters stood above the mountains.'),
(15581,19,'Psalms','OT',104,7,'At thy rebuke they fled; at the voice of thy thunder they hasted away.'),
(15582,19,'Psalms','OT',104,8,'They go up by the mountains; they go down by the valleys unto the place which thou hast founded for them. {They go up...: or, The mountains ascend, the valleys descend}'),
(15583,19,'Psalms','OT',104,9,'Thou hast set a bound that they may not pass over; that they turn not again to cover the earth.'),
(15584,19,'Psalms','OT',104,10,'He sendeth the springs into the valleys, {which} run among the hills. {He: Heb. Who} {run: Heb. walk}'),
(15585,19,'Psalms','OT',104,11,'They give drink to every beast of the field: the wild asses quench their thirst. {quench: Heb. break}'),
(15586,19,'Psalms','OT',104,12,'By them shall the fowls of the heaven have their habitation, {which} sing among the branches. {sing: Heb. give a voice}'),
(15587,19,'Psalms','OT',104,13,'He watereth the hills from his chambers: the earth is satisfied with the fruit of thy works.'),
(15588,19,'Psalms','OT',104,14,'He causeth the grass to grow for the cattle, and herb for the service of man: that he may bring forth food out of the earth;'),
(15589,19,'Psalms','OT',104,15,'And wine {that} maketh glad the heart of man, {and} oil to make {his} face to shine, and bread {which} strengtheneth man\'s heart. {oil...: Heb. to make his face shine with oil, or, more than oil}'),
(15590,19,'Psalms','OT',104,16,'The trees of the LORD are full {of sap}; the cedars of Lebanon, which he hath planted;'),
(15591,19,'Psalms','OT',104,17,'Where the birds make their nests: {as for} the stork, the fir trees {are} her house.'),
(15592,19,'Psalms','OT',104,18,'The high hills {are} a refuge for the wild goats; {and} the rocks for the conies.'),
(15593,19,'Psalms','OT',104,19,'He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.'),
(15594,19,'Psalms','OT',104,20,'Thou makest darkness, and it is night: wherein all the beasts of the forest do creep {forth}. {beasts...: Heb. beasts thereof do trample on the forest}'),
(15595,19,'Psalms','OT',104,21,'The young lions roar after their prey, and seek their meat from God.'),
(15596,19,'Psalms','OT',104,22,'The sun ariseth, they gather themselves together, and lay them down in their dens.'),
(15597,19,'Psalms','OT',104,23,'Man goeth forth unto his work and to his labour until the evening.'),
(15598,19,'Psalms','OT',104,24,'O LORD, how manifold are thy works! in wisdom hast thou made them all: the earth is full of thy riches.'),
(15599,19,'Psalms','OT',104,25,'{So is} this great and wide sea, wherein {are} things creeping innumerable, both small and great beasts.'),
(15600,19,'Psalms','OT',104,26,'There go the ships: {there is} that leviathan, {whom} thou hast made to play therein. {made: Heb. formed}'),
(15601,19,'Psalms','OT',104,27,'These wait all upon thee; that thou mayest give {them} their meat in due season.'),
(15602,19,'Psalms','OT',104,28,'{That} thou givest them they gather: thou openest thine hand, they are filled with good.'),
(15603,19,'Psalms','OT',104,29,'Thou hidest thy face, they are troubled: thou takest away their breath, they die, and return to their dust.'),
(15604,19,'Psalms','OT',104,30,'Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they are created: and thou renewest the face of the earth.'),
(15605,19,'Psalms','OT',104,31,'The glory of the LORD shall endure for ever: the LORD shall rejoice in his works. {endure: Heb. be}'),
(15606,19,'Psalms','OT',104,32,'He looketh on the earth, and it trembleth: he toucheth the hills, and they smoke.'),
(15607,19,'Psalms','OT',104,33,'I will sing unto the LORD as long as I live: I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.'),
(15608,19,'Psalms','OT',104,34,'My meditation of him shall be sweet: I will be glad in the LORD.'),
(15609,19,'Psalms','OT',104,35,'Let the sinners be consumed out of the earth, and let the wicked be no more. Bless thou the LORD, O my soul. Praise ye the LORD.'),
(15610,19,'Psalms','OT',105,1,'O give thanks unto the LORD; call upon his name: make known his deeds among the people.'),
(15611,19,'Psalms','OT',105,2,'Sing unto him, sing psalms unto him: talk ye of all his wondrous works.'),
(15612,19,'Psalms','OT',105,3,'Glory ye in his holy name: let the heart of them rejoice that seek the LORD.'),
(15613,19,'Psalms','OT',105,4,'Seek the LORD, and his strength: seek his face evermore.'),
(15614,19,'Psalms','OT',105,5,'Remember his marvellous works that he hath done; his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth;'),
(15615,19,'Psalms','OT',105,6,'O ye seed of Abraham his servant, ye children of Jacob his chosen.'),
(15616,19,'Psalms','OT',105,7,'He {is} the LORD our God: his judgments {are} in all the earth.'),
(15617,19,'Psalms','OT',105,8,'He hath remembered his covenant for ever, the word {which} he commanded to a thousand generations.'),
(15618,19,'Psalms','OT',105,9,'Which {covenant} he made with Abraham, and his oath unto Isaac;'),
(15619,19,'Psalms','OT',105,10,'And confirmed the same unto Jacob for a law, {and} to Israel {for} an everlasting covenant:'),
(15620,19,'Psalms','OT',105,11,'Saying, Unto thee will I give the land of Canaan, the lot of your inheritance: {lot: Heb. cord}'),
(15621,19,'Psalms','OT',105,12,'When they were {but} a few men in number; yea, very few, and strangers in it.'),
(15622,19,'Psalms','OT',105,13,'When they went from one nation to another, from {one} kingdom to another people;'),
(15623,19,'Psalms','OT',105,14,'He suffered no man to do them wrong: yea, he reproved kings for their sakes;'),
(15624,19,'Psalms','OT',105,15,'{Saying}, Touch not mine anointed, and do my prophets no harm.'),
(15625,19,'Psalms','OT',105,16,'Moreover he called for a famine upon the land: he brake the whole staff of bread.'),
(15626,19,'Psalms','OT',105,17,'He sent a man before them, {even} Joseph, {who} was sold for a servant:'),
(15627,19,'Psalms','OT',105,18,'Whose feet they hurt with fetters: he was laid in iron: {he...: Heb. his soul came into iron}'),
(15628,19,'Psalms','OT',105,19,'Until the time that his word came: the word of the LORD tried him.'),
(15629,19,'Psalms','OT',105,20,'The king sent and loosed him; {even} the ruler of the people, and let him go free.'),
(15630,19,'Psalms','OT',105,21,'He made him lord of his house, and ruler of all his substance: {substance: Heb. possession}'),
(15631,19,'Psalms','OT',105,22,'To bind his princes at his pleasure; and teach his senators wisdom.'),
(15632,19,'Psalms','OT',105,23,'Israel also came into Egypt; and Jacob sojourned in the land of Ham.'),
(15633,19,'Psalms','OT',105,24,'And he increased his people greatly; and made them stronger than their enemies.'),
(15634,19,'Psalms','OT',105,25,'He turned their heart to hate his people, to deal subtilly with his servants.'),
(15635,19,'Psalms','OT',105,26,'He sent Moses his servant; {and} Aaron whom he had chosen.'),
(15636,19,'Psalms','OT',105,27,'They shewed his signs among them, and wonders in the land of Ham. {his...: Heb. words of his signs}'),
(15637,19,'Psalms','OT',105,28,'He sent darkness, and made it dark; and they rebelled not against his word.'),
(15638,19,'Psalms','OT',105,29,'He turned their waters into blood, and slew their fish.'),
(15639,19,'Psalms','OT',105,30,'Their land brought forth frogs in abundance, in the chambers of their kings.'),
(15640,19,'Psalms','OT',105,31,'He spake, and there came divers sorts of flies, {and} lice in all their coasts.'),
(15641,19,'Psalms','OT',105,32,'He gave them hail for rain, {and} flaming fire in their land. {them...: Heb. their rain hail}'),
(15642,19,'Psalms','OT',105,33,'He smote their vines also and their fig trees; and brake the trees of their coasts.'),
(15643,19,'Psalms','OT',105,34,'He spake, and the locusts came, and caterpillers, and that without number,'),
(15644,19,'Psalms','OT',105,35,'And did eat up all the herbs in their land, and devoured the fruit of their ground.'),
(15645,19,'Psalms','OT',105,36,'He smote also all the firstborn in their land, the chief of all their strength.'),
(15646,19,'Psalms','OT',105,37,'He brought them forth also with silver and gold: and {there was} not one feeble {person} among their tribes.'),
(15647,19,'Psalms','OT',105,38,'Egypt was glad when they departed: for the fear of them fell upon them.'),
(15648,19,'Psalms','OT',105,39,'He spread a cloud for a covering; and fire to give light in the night.'),
(15649,19,'Psalms','OT',105,40,'{The people} asked, and he brought quails, and satisfied them with the bread of heaven.'),
(15650,19,'Psalms','OT',105,41,'He opened the rock, and the waters gushed out; they ran in the dry places {like} a river.'),
(15651,19,'Psalms','OT',105,42,'For he remembered his holy promise, {and} Abraham his servant.'),
(15652,19,'Psalms','OT',105,43,'And he brought forth his people with joy, {and} his chosen with gladness: {gladness: Heb. singing}'),
(15653,19,'Psalms','OT',105,44,'And gave them the lands of the heathen: and they inherited the labour of the people;'),
(15654,19,'Psalms','OT',105,45,'That they might observe his statutes, and keep his laws. Praise ye the LORD. {Praise...: Heb. Hallelujah}'),
(15655,19,'Psalms','OT',106,1,'Praise ye the LORD. O give thanks unto the LORD; for {he is} good: for his mercy {endureth} for ever. {Praise...: Heb. Hallelujah}'),
(15656,19,'Psalms','OT',106,2,'Who can utter the mighty acts of the LORD? {who} can shew forth all his praise?'),
(15657,19,'Psalms','OT',106,3,'Blessed {are} they that keep judgment, {and} he that doeth righteousness at all times.'),
(15658,19,'Psalms','OT',106,4,'Remember me, O LORD, with the favour {that thou bearest unto} thy people: O visit me with thy salvation;'),
(15659,19,'Psalms','OT',106,5,'That I may see the good of thy chosen, that I may rejoice in the gladness of thy nation, that I may glory with thine inheritance.'),
(15660,19,'Psalms','OT',106,6,'We have sinned with our fathers, we have committed iniquity, we have done wickedly.'),
(15661,19,'Psalms','OT',106,7,'Our fathers understood not thy wonders in Egypt; they remembered not the multitude of thy mercies; but provoked {him} at the sea, {even} at the Red sea.'),
(15662,19,'Psalms','OT',106,8,'Nevertheless he saved them for his name\'s sake, that he might make his mighty power to be known.'),
(15663,19,'Psalms','OT',106,9,'He rebuked the Red sea also, and it was dried up: so he led them through the depths, as through the wilderness.'),
(15664,19,'Psalms','OT',106,10,'And he saved them from the hand of him that hated {them}, and redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.'),
(15665,19,'Psalms','OT',106,11,'And the waters covered their enemies: there was not one of them left.'),
(15666,19,'Psalms','OT',106,12,'Then believed they his words; they sang his praise.'),
(15667,19,'Psalms','OT',106,13,'They soon forgat his works; they waited not for his counsel: {They soon...: Heb. They made haste, they forgat}'),
(15668,19,'Psalms','OT',106,14,'But lusted exceedingly in the wilderness, and tempted God in the desert. {lusted...: Heb. lusted a lust}'),
(15669,19,'Psalms','OT',106,15,'And he gave them their request; but sent leanness into their soul.'),
(15670,19,'Psalms','OT',106,16,'They envied Moses also in the camp, {and} Aaron the saint of the LORD.'),
(15671,19,'Psalms','OT',106,17,'The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan, and covered the company of Abiram.'),
(15672,19,'Psalms','OT',106,18,'And a fire was kindled in their company; the flame burned up the wicked.'),
(15673,19,'Psalms','OT',106,19,'They made a calf in Horeb, and worshipped the molten image.'),
(15674,19,'Psalms','OT',106,20,'Thus they changed their glory into the similitude of an ox that eateth grass.'),
(15675,19,'Psalms','OT',106,21,'They forgat God their saviour, which had done great things in Egypt;'),
(15676,19,'Psalms','OT',106,22,'Wondrous works in the land of Ham, {and} terrible things by the Red sea.'),
(15677,19,'Psalms','OT',106,23,'Therefore he said that he would destroy them, had not Moses his chosen stood before him in the breach, to turn away his wrath, lest he should destroy {them}.'),
(15678,19,'Psalms','OT',106,24,'Yea, they despised the pleasant land, they believed not his word: {the pleasant...: Heb. a land of desire}'),
(15679,19,'Psalms','OT',106,25,'But murmured in their tents, {and} hearkened not unto the voice of the LORD.'),
(15680,19,'Psalms','OT',106,26,'Therefore he lifted up his hand against them, to overthrow them in the wilderness: {to overthrow: Heb. to make them fall}'),
(15681,19,'Psalms','OT',106,27,'To overthrow their seed also among the nations, and to scatter them in the lands. {to overthrow: Heb. to make them fall}'),
(15682,19,'Psalms','OT',106,28,'They joined themselves also unto Baalpeor, and ate the sacrifices of the dead.'),
(15683,19,'Psalms','OT',106,29,'Thus they provoked {him} to anger with their inventions: and the plague brake in upon them.'),
(15684,19,'Psalms','OT',106,30,'Then stood up Phinehas, and executed judgment: and {so} the plague was stayed.'),
(15685,19,'Psalms','OT',106,31,'And that was counted unto him for righteousness unto all generations for evermore.'),
(15686,19,'Psalms','OT',106,32,'They angered {him} also at the waters of strife, so that it went ill with Moses for their sakes:'),
(15687,19,'Psalms','OT',106,33,'Because they provoked his spirit, so that he spake unadvisedly with his lips.'),
(15688,19,'Psalms','OT',106,34,'They did not destroy the nations, concerning whom the LORD commanded them:'),
(15689,19,'Psalms','OT',106,35,'But were mingled among the heathen, and learned their works.'),
(15690,19,'Psalms','OT',106,36,'And they served their idols: which were a snare unto them.'),
(15691,19,'Psalms','OT',106,37,'Yea, they sacrificed their sons and their daughters unto devils,'),
(15692,19,'Psalms','OT',106,38,'And shed innocent blood, {even} the blood of their sons and of their daughters, whom they sacrificed unto the idols of Canaan: and the land was polluted with blood.'),
(15693,19,'Psalms','OT',106,39,'Thus were they defiled with their own works, and went a whoring with their own inventions.'),
(15694,19,'Psalms','OT',106,40,'Therefore was the wrath of the LORD kindled against his people, insomuch that he abhorred his own inheritance.'),
(15695,19,'Psalms','OT',106,41,'And he gave them into the hand of the heathen; and they that hated them ruled over them.'),
(15696,19,'Psalms','OT',106,42,'Their enemies also oppressed them, and they were brought into subjection under their hand.'),
(15697,19,'Psalms','OT',106,43,'Many times did he deliver them; but they provoked {him} with their counsel, and were brought low for their iniquity. {brought...: or, impoverished, or, weakened}'),
(15698,19,'Psalms','OT',106,44,'Nevertheless he regarded their affliction, when he heard their cry:'),
(15699,19,'Psalms','OT',106,45,'And he remembered for them his covenant, and repented according to the multitude of his mercies.'),
(15700,19,'Psalms','OT',106,46,'He made them also to be pitied of all those that carried them captives.'),
(15701,19,'Psalms','OT',106,47,'Save us, O LORD our God, and gather us from among the heathen, to give thanks unto thy holy name, {and} to triumph in thy praise.'),
(15702,19,'Psalms','OT',106,48,'Blessed {be} the LORD God of Israel from everlasting to everlasting: and let all the people say, Amen. Praise ye the LORD. {Praise...: Heb. Hallelujah}'),
(15703,19,'Psalms','OT',107,1,'O give thanks unto the LORD, for {he is} good: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(15704,19,'Psalms','OT',107,2,'Let the redeemed of the LORD say {so}, whom he hath redeemed from the hand of the enemy;'),
(15705,19,'Psalms','OT',107,3,'And gathered them out of the lands, from the east, and from the west, from the north, and from the south. {south: Heb. sea}'),
(15706,19,'Psalms','OT',107,4,'They wandered in the wilderness in a solitary way; they found no city to dwell in.'),
(15707,19,'Psalms','OT',107,5,'Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in them.'),
(15708,19,'Psalms','OT',107,6,'Then they cried unto the LORD in their trouble, {and} he delivered them out of their distresses.'),
(15709,19,'Psalms','OT',107,7,'And he led them forth by the right way, that they might go to a city of habitation.'),
(15710,19,'Psalms','OT',107,8,'Oh that {men} would praise the LORD {for} his goodness, and {for} his wonderful works to the children of men!'),
(15711,19,'Psalms','OT',107,9,'For he satisfieth the longing soul, and filleth the hungry soul with goodness.'),
(15712,19,'Psalms','OT',107,10,'Such as sit in darkness and in the shadow of death, {being} bound in affliction and iron;'),
(15713,19,'Psalms','OT',107,11,'Because they rebelled against the words of God, and contemned the counsel of the most High:'),
(15714,19,'Psalms','OT',107,12,'Therefore he brought down their heart with labour; they fell down, and {there was} none to help.'),
(15715,19,'Psalms','OT',107,13,'Then they cried unto the LORD in their trouble, {and} he saved them out of their distresses.'),
(15716,19,'Psalms','OT',107,14,'He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and brake their bands in sunder.'),
(15717,19,'Psalms','OT',107,15,'Oh that {men} would praise the LORD {for} his goodness, and {for} his wonderful works to the children of men!'),
(15718,19,'Psalms','OT',107,16,'For he hath broken the gates of brass, and cut the bars of iron in sunder.'),
(15719,19,'Psalms','OT',107,17,'Fools because of their transgression, and because of their iniquities, are afflicted.'),
(15720,19,'Psalms','OT',107,18,'Their soul abhorreth all manner of meat; and they draw near unto the gates of death.'),
(15721,19,'Psalms','OT',107,19,'Then they cry unto the LORD in their trouble, {and} he saveth them out of their distresses.'),
(15722,19,'Psalms','OT',107,20,'He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered {them} from their destructions.'),
(15723,19,'Psalms','OT',107,21,'Oh that {men} would praise the LORD {for} his goodness, and {for} his wonderful works to the children of men!'),
(15724,19,'Psalms','OT',107,22,'And let them sacrifice the sacrifices of thanksgiving, and declare his works with rejoicing. {rejoicing: Heb. singing}'),
(15725,19,'Psalms','OT',107,23,'They that go down to the sea in ships, that do business in great waters;'),
(15726,19,'Psalms','OT',107,24,'These see the works of the LORD, and his wonders in the deep.'),
(15727,19,'Psalms','OT',107,25,'For he commandeth, and raiseth the stormy wind, which lifteth up the waves thereof. {raiseth: Heb. maketh to stand}'),
(15728,19,'Psalms','OT',107,26,'They mount up to the heaven, they go down again to the depths: their soul is melted because of trouble.'),
(15729,19,'Psalms','OT',107,27,'They reel to and fro, and stagger like a drunken man, and are at their wits\' end. {are...: Heb. all their wisdom is swallowed up}'),
(15730,19,'Psalms','OT',107,28,'Then they cry unto the LORD in their trouble, and he bringeth them out of their distresses.'),
(15731,19,'Psalms','OT',107,29,'He maketh the storm a calm, so that the waves thereof are still.'),
(15732,19,'Psalms','OT',107,30,'Then are they glad because they be quiet; so he bringeth them unto their desired haven.'),
(15733,19,'Psalms','OT',107,31,'Oh that {men} would praise the LORD {for} his goodness, and {for} his wonderful works to the children of men!'),
(15734,19,'Psalms','OT',107,32,'Let them exalt him also in the congregation of the people, and praise him in the assembly of the elders.'),
(15735,19,'Psalms','OT',107,33,'He turneth rivers into a wilderness, and the watersprings into dry ground;'),
(15736,19,'Psalms','OT',107,34,'A fruitful land into barrenness, for the wickedness of them that dwell therein. {barrenness: Heb. saltiness}'),
(15737,19,'Psalms','OT',107,35,'He turneth the wilderness into a standing water, and dry ground into watersprings.'),
(15738,19,'Psalms','OT',107,36,'And there he maketh the hungry to dwell, that they may prepare a city for habitation;'),
(15739,19,'Psalms','OT',107,37,'And sow the fields, and plant vineyards, which may yield fruits of increase.'),
(15740,19,'Psalms','OT',107,38,'He blesseth them also, so that they are multiplied greatly; and suffereth not their cattle to decrease.'),
(15741,19,'Psalms','OT',107,39,'Again, they are minished and brought low through oppression, affliction, and sorrow.'),
(15742,19,'Psalms','OT',107,40,'He poureth contempt upon princes, and causeth them to wander in the wilderness, {where there is} no way. {wilderness: or, void place}'),
(15743,19,'Psalms','OT',107,41,'Yet setteth he the poor on high from affliction, and maketh {him} families like a flock. {from: or, after}'),
(15744,19,'Psalms','OT',107,42,'The righteous shall see {it}, and rejoice: and all iniquity shall stop her mouth.'),
(15745,19,'Psalms','OT',107,43,'Whoso {is} wise, and will observe these {things}, even they shall understand the lovingkindness of the LORD.'),
(15746,19,'Psalms','OT',108,1,'[A Song {or} Psalm of David.] O God, my heart is fixed; I will sing and give praise, even with my glory.'),
(15747,19,'Psalms','OT',108,2,'Awake, psaltery and harp: I {myself} will awake early.'),
(15748,19,'Psalms','OT',108,3,'I will praise thee, O LORD, among the people: and I will sing praises unto thee among the nations.'),
(15749,19,'Psalms','OT',108,4,'For thy mercy {is} great above the heavens: and thy truth {reacheth} unto the clouds. {clouds: or, skies}'),
(15750,19,'Psalms','OT',108,5,'Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens: and thy glory above all the earth;'),
(15751,19,'Psalms','OT',108,6,'That thy beloved may be delivered: save {with} thy right hand, and answer me.'),
(15752,19,'Psalms','OT',108,7,'God hath spoken in his holiness; I will rejoice, I will divide Shechem, and mete out the valley of Succoth.'),
(15753,19,'Psalms','OT',108,8,'Gilead {is} mine; Manasseh {is} mine; Ephraim also {is} the strength of mine head; Judah {is} my lawgiver;'),
(15754,19,'Psalms','OT',108,9,'Moab {is} my washpot; over Edom will I cast out my shoe; over Philistia will I triumph.'),
