(15944,19,'Psalms','OT',119,43,'And take not the word of truth utterly out of my mouth; for I have hoped in thy judgments.'),
(15945,19,'Psalms','OT',119,44,'So shall I keep thy law continually for ever and ever.'),
(15946,19,'Psalms','OT',119,45,'And I will walk at liberty: for I seek thy precepts. {at liberty: Heb. at large}'),
(15947,19,'Psalms','OT',119,46,'I will speak of thy testimonies also before kings, and will not be ashamed.'),
(15948,19,'Psalms','OT',119,47,'And I will delight myself in thy commandments, which I have loved.'),
(15949,19,'Psalms','OT',119,48,'My hands also will I lift up unto thy commandments, which I have loved; and I will meditate in thy statutes.'),
(15950,19,'Psalms','OT',119,49,'ZAIN. Remember the word unto thy servant, upon which thou hast caused me to hope.'),
(15951,19,'Psalms','OT',119,50,'This {is} my comfort in my affliction: for thy word hath quickened me.'),
(15952,19,'Psalms','OT',119,51,'The proud have had me greatly in derision: {yet} have I not declined from thy law.'),
(15953,19,'Psalms','OT',119,52,'I remembered thy judgments of old, O LORD; and have comforted myself.'),
(15954,19,'Psalms','OT',119,53,'Horror hath taken hold upon me because of the wicked that forsake thy law.'),
(15955,19,'Psalms','OT',119,54,'Thy statutes have been my songs in the house of my pilgrimage.'),
(15956,19,'Psalms','OT',119,55,'I have remembered thy name, O LORD, in the night, and have kept thy law.'),
(15957,19,'Psalms','OT',119,56,'This I had, because I kept thy precepts.'),
(15958,19,'Psalms','OT',119,57,'CHETH. {Thou art} my portion, O LORD: I have said that I would keep thy words.'),
(15959,19,'Psalms','OT',119,58,'I intreated thy favour with {my} whole heart: be merciful unto me according to thy word. {favour: Heb. face}'),
(15960,19,'Psalms','OT',119,59,'I thought on my ways, and turned my feet unto thy testimonies.'),
(15961,19,'Psalms','OT',119,60,'I made haste, and delayed not to keep thy commandments.'),
(15962,19,'Psalms','OT',119,61,'The bands of the wicked have robbed me: {but} I have not forgotten thy law. {bands: or, companies}'),
(15963,19,'Psalms','OT',119,62,'At midnight I will rise to give thanks unto thee because of thy righteous judgments.'),
(15964,19,'Psalms','OT',119,63,'I {am} a companion of all {them} that fear thee, and of them that keep thy precepts.'),
(15965,19,'Psalms','OT',119,64,'The earth, O LORD, is full of thy mercy: teach me thy statutes.'),
(15966,19,'Psalms','OT',119,65,'TETH. Thou hast dealt well with thy servant, O LORD, according unto thy word.'),
(15967,19,'Psalms','OT',119,66,'Teach me good judgment and knowledge: for I have believed thy commandments.'),
(15968,19,'Psalms','OT',119,67,'Before I was afflicted I went astray: but now have I kept thy word.'),
(15969,19,'Psalms','OT',119,68,'Thou {art} good, and doest good; teach me thy statutes.'),
(15970,19,'Psalms','OT',119,69,'The proud have forged a lie against me: {but} I will keep thy precepts with {my} whole heart.'),
(15971,19,'Psalms','OT',119,70,'Their heart is as fat as grease; {but} I delight in thy law.'),
(15972,19,'Psalms','OT',119,71,'{It is} good for me that I have been afflicted; that I might learn thy statutes.'),
(15973,19,'Psalms','OT',119,72,'The law of thy mouth {is} better unto me than thousands of gold and silver.'),
(15974,19,'Psalms','OT',119,73,'JOD. Thy hands have made me and fashioned me: give me understanding, that I may learn thy commandments.'),
(15975,19,'Psalms','OT',119,74,'They that fear thee will be glad when they see me; because I have hoped in thy word.'),
(15976,19,'Psalms','OT',119,75,'I know, O LORD, that thy judgments {are} right, and {that} thou in faithfulness hast afflicted me. {right: Heb. righteousness}'),
(15977,19,'Psalms','OT',119,76,'Let, I pray thee, thy merciful kindness be for my comfort, according to thy word unto thy servant. {for...: Heb. to comfort me}'),
(15978,19,'Psalms','OT',119,77,'Let thy tender mercies come unto me, that I may live: for thy law {is} my delight.'),
(15979,19,'Psalms','OT',119,78,'Let the proud be ashamed; for they dealt perversely with me without a cause: {but} I will meditate in thy precepts.'),
(15980,19,'Psalms','OT',119,79,'Let those that fear thee turn unto me, and those that have known thy testimonies.'),
(15981,19,'Psalms','OT',119,80,'Let my heart be sound in thy statutes; that I be not ashamed.'),
(15982,19,'Psalms','OT',119,81,'CAPH. My soul fainteth for thy salvation: {but} I hope in thy word.'),
(15983,19,'Psalms','OT',119,82,'Mine eyes fail for thy word, saying, When wilt thou comfort me?'),
(15984,19,'Psalms','OT',119,83,'For I am become like a bottle in the smoke; {yet} do I not forget thy statutes.'),
(15985,19,'Psalms','OT',119,84,'How many {are} the days of thy servant? when wilt thou execute judgment on them that persecute me?'),
(15986,19,'Psalms','OT',119,85,'The proud have digged pits for me, which {are} not after thy law.'),
(15987,19,'Psalms','OT',119,86,'All thy commandments {are} faithful: they persecute me wrongfully; help thou me. {faithful: Heb. faithfulness}'),
(15988,19,'Psalms','OT',119,87,'They had almost consumed me upon earth; but I forsook not thy precepts.'),
(15989,19,'Psalms','OT',119,88,'Quicken me after thy lovingkindness; so shall I keep the testimony of thy mouth.'),
(15990,19,'Psalms','OT',119,89,'LAMED. For ever, O LORD, thy word is settled in heaven.'),
(15991,19,'Psalms','OT',119,90,'Thy faithfulness {is} unto all generations: thou hast established the earth, and it abideth. {unto...: Heb. to generation and generation} {abideth: Heb. standeth}'),
(15992,19,'Psalms','OT',119,91,'They continue this day according to thine ordinances: for all {are} thy servants.'),
(15993,19,'Psalms','OT',119,92,'Unless thy law {had been} my delights, I should then have perished in mine affliction.'),
(15994,19,'Psalms','OT',119,93,'I will never forget thy precepts: for with them thou hast quickened me.'),
(15995,19,'Psalms','OT',119,94,'I {am} thine, save me; for I have sought thy precepts.'),
(15996,19,'Psalms','OT',119,95,'The wicked have waited for me to destroy me: {but} I will consider thy testimonies.'),
(15997,19,'Psalms','OT',119,96,'I have seen an end of all perfection: {but} thy commandment {is} exceeding broad.'),
(15998,19,'Psalms','OT',119,97,'MEM. O how love I thy law! it {is} my meditation all the day.'),
(15999,19,'Psalms','OT',119,98,'Thou through thy commandments hast made me wiser than mine enemies: for they {are} ever with me. {they...: Heb. it is ever with me}'),
(16000,19,'Psalms','OT',119,99,'I have more understanding than all my teachers: for thy testimonies {are} my meditation.'),
(16001,19,'Psalms','OT',119,100,'I understand more than the ancients, because I keep thy precepts.'),
(16002,19,'Psalms','OT',119,101,'I have refrained my feet from every evil way, that I might keep thy word.'),
(16003,19,'Psalms','OT',119,102,'I have not departed from thy judgments: for thou hast taught me.'),
(16004,19,'Psalms','OT',119,103,'How sweet are thy words unto my taste! {yea, sweeter} than honey to my mouth! {taste: Heb. palate}'),
(16005,19,'Psalms','OT',119,104,'Through thy precepts I get understanding: therefore I hate every false way.'),
(16006,19,'Psalms','OT',119,105,'NUN. Thy word {is} a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path. {lamp: or, candle}'),
(16007,19,'Psalms','OT',119,106,'I have sworn, and I will perform {it}, that I will keep thy righteous judgments.'),
(16008,19,'Psalms','OT',119,107,'I am afflicted very much: quicken me, O LORD, according unto thy word.'),
(16009,19,'Psalms','OT',119,108,'Accept, I beseech thee, the freewill offerings of my mouth, O LORD, and teach me thy judgments.'),
(16010,19,'Psalms','OT',119,109,'My soul {is} continually in my hand: yet do I not forget thy law.'),
(16011,19,'Psalms','OT',119,110,'The wicked have laid a snare for me: yet I erred not from thy precepts.'),
(16012,19,'Psalms','OT',119,111,'Thy testimonies have I taken as an heritage for ever: for they {are} the rejoicing of my heart.'),
(16013,19,'Psalms','OT',119,112,'I have inclined mine heart to perform thy statutes alway, {even unto} the end. {to perform: Heb. to do}'),
(16014,19,'Psalms','OT',119,113,'SAMECH. I hate {vain} thoughts: but thy law do I love.'),
(16015,19,'Psalms','OT',119,114,'Thou {art} my hiding place and my shield: I hope in thy word.'),
(16016,19,'Psalms','OT',119,115,'Depart from me, ye evildoers: for I will keep the commandments of my God.'),
(16017,19,'Psalms','OT',119,116,'Uphold me according unto thy word, that I may live: and let me not be ashamed of my hope.'),
(16018,19,'Psalms','OT',119,117,'Hold thou me up, and I shall be safe: and I will have respect unto thy statutes continually.'),
(16019,19,'Psalms','OT',119,118,'Thou hast trodden down all them that err from thy statutes: for their deceit {is} falsehood.'),
(16020,19,'Psalms','OT',119,119,'Thou puttest away all the wicked of the earth {like} dross: therefore I love thy testimonies. {puttest...: Heb. causest to cease}'),
(16021,19,'Psalms','OT',119,120,'My flesh trembleth for fear of thee; and I am afraid of thy judgments.'),
(16022,19,'Psalms','OT',119,121,'AIN. I have done judgment and justice: leave me not to mine oppressors.'),
(16023,19,'Psalms','OT',119,122,'Be surety for thy servant for good: let not the proud oppress me.'),
(16024,19,'Psalms','OT',119,123,'Mine eyes fail for thy salvation, and for the word of thy righteousness.'),
(16025,19,'Psalms','OT',119,124,'Deal with thy servant according unto thy mercy, and teach me thy statutes.'),
(16026,19,'Psalms','OT',119,125,'I {am} thy servant; give me understanding, that I may know thy testimonies.'),
(16027,19,'Psalms','OT',119,126,'{It is} time for {thee}, LORD, to work: {for} they have made void thy law.'),
(16028,19,'Psalms','OT',119,127,'Therefore I love thy commandments above gold; yea, above fine gold.'),
(16029,19,'Psalms','OT',119,128,'Therefore I esteem all {thy} precepts {concerning} all {things to be} right; {and} I hate every false way.'),
(16030,19,'Psalms','OT',119,129,'PE. Thy testimonies {are} wonderful: therefore doth my soul keep them.'),
(16031,19,'Psalms','OT',119,130,'The entrance of thy words giveth light; it giveth understanding unto the simple.'),
(16032,19,'Psalms','OT',119,131,'I opened my mouth, and panted: for I longed for thy commandments.'),
(16033,19,'Psalms','OT',119,132,'Look thou upon me, and be merciful unto me, as thou usest to do unto those that love thy name. {as thou...: Heb. according to the custom toward those, etc}'),
(16034,19,'Psalms','OT',119,133,'Order my steps in thy word: and let not any iniquity have dominion over me.'),
(16035,19,'Psalms','OT',119,134,'Deliver me from the oppression of man: so will I keep thy precepts.'),
(16036,19,'Psalms','OT',119,135,'Make thy face to shine upon thy servant; and teach me thy statutes.'),
(16037,19,'Psalms','OT',119,136,'Rivers of waters run down mine eyes, because they keep not thy law.'),
(16038,19,'Psalms','OT',119,137,'TZADDI. Righteous {art} thou, O LORD, and upright {are} thy judgments.'),
(16039,19,'Psalms','OT',119,138,'Thy testimonies {that} thou hast commanded {are} righteous and very faithful. {righteous: Heb. righteousness} {faithful: Heb. faithfulness}'),
(16040,19,'Psalms','OT',119,139,'My zeal hath consumed me, because mine enemies have forgotten thy words. {consumed...: Heb. cut me off}'),
(16041,19,'Psalms','OT',119,140,'Thy word {is} very pure: therefore thy servant loveth it. {pure: Heb. tried, or, refined}'),
(16042,19,'Psalms','OT',119,141,'I {am} small and despised: {yet} do not I forget thy precepts.'),
(16043,19,'Psalms','OT',119,142,'Thy righteousness {is} an everlasting righteousness, and thy law {is} the truth.'),
(16044,19,'Psalms','OT',119,143,'Trouble and anguish have taken hold on me: {yet} thy commandments {are} my delights. {taken...: Heb. found me}'),
(16045,19,'Psalms','OT',119,144,'The righteousness of thy testimonies {is} everlasting: give me understanding, and I shall live.'),
(16046,19,'Psalms','OT',119,145,'KOPH. I cried with {my} whole heart; hear me, O LORD: I will keep thy statutes.'),
(16047,19,'Psalms','OT',119,146,'I cried unto thee; save me, and I shall keep thy testimonies. {and I...: or, that I may keep}'),
(16048,19,'Psalms','OT',119,147,'I prevented the dawning of the morning, and cried: I hoped in thy word.'),
(16049,19,'Psalms','OT',119,148,'Mine eyes prevent the {night} watches, that I might meditate in thy word.'),
(16050,19,'Psalms','OT',119,149,'Hear my voice according unto thy lovingkindness: O LORD, quicken me according to thy judgment.'),
(16051,19,'Psalms','OT',119,150,'They draw nigh that follow after mischief: they are far from thy law.'),
(16052,19,'Psalms','OT',119,151,'Thou {art} near, O LORD; and all thy commandments {are} truth.'),
(16053,19,'Psalms','OT',119,152,'Concerning thy testimonies, I have known of old that thou hast founded them for ever.'),
(16054,19,'Psalms','OT',119,153,'RESH. Consider mine affliction, and deliver me: for I do not forget thy law.'),
(16055,19,'Psalms','OT',119,154,'Plead my cause, and deliver me: quicken me according to thy word.'),
(16056,19,'Psalms','OT',119,155,'Salvation {is} far from the wicked: for they seek not thy statutes.'),
(16057,19,'Psalms','OT',119,156,'Great {are} thy tender mercies, O LORD: quicken me according to thy judgments. {Great: or, Many}'),
(16058,19,'Psalms','OT',119,157,'Many {are} my persecutors and mine enemies; {yet} do I not decline from thy testimonies.'),
(16059,19,'Psalms','OT',119,158,'I beheld the transgressors, and was grieved; because they kept not thy word.'),
(16060,19,'Psalms','OT',119,159,'Consider how I love thy precepts: quicken me, O LORD, according to thy lovingkindness.'),
(16061,19,'Psalms','OT',119,160,'Thy word {is} true {from} the beginning: and every one of thy righteous judgments {endureth} for ever. {Thy word...: Heb. The beginning of thy word is true}'),
(16062,19,'Psalms','OT',119,161,'SCHIN. Princes have persecuted me without a cause: but my heart standeth in awe of thy word.'),
(16063,19,'Psalms','OT',119,162,'I rejoice at thy word, as one that findeth great spoil.'),
(16064,19,'Psalms','OT',119,163,'I hate and abhor lying: {but} thy law do I love.'),
(16065,19,'Psalms','OT',119,164,'Seven times a day do I praise thee because of thy righteous judgments.'),
(16066,19,'Psalms','OT',119,165,'Great peace have they which love thy law: and nothing shall offend them. {nothing...: Heb. they shall have no stumblingblock}'),
(16067,19,'Psalms','OT',119,166,'LORD, I have hoped for thy salvation, and done thy commandments.'),
(16068,19,'Psalms','OT',119,167,'My soul hath kept thy testimonies; and I love them exceedingly.'),
(16069,19,'Psalms','OT',119,168,'I have kept thy precepts and thy testimonies: for all my ways {are} before thee.'),
(16070,19,'Psalms','OT',119,169,'TAU. Let my cry come near before thee, O LORD: give me understanding according to thy word.'),
(16071,19,'Psalms','OT',119,170,'Let my supplication come before thee: deliver me according to thy word.'),
(16072,19,'Psalms','OT',119,171,'My lips shall utter praise, when thou hast taught me thy statutes.'),
(16073,19,'Psalms','OT',119,172,'My tongue shall speak of thy word: for all thy commandments {are} righteousness.'),
(16074,19,'Psalms','OT',119,173,'Let thine hand help me; for I have chosen thy precepts.'),
(16075,19,'Psalms','OT',119,174,'I have longed for thy salvation, O LORD; and thy law {is} my delight.'),
(16076,19,'Psalms','OT',119,175,'Let my soul live, and it shall praise thee; and let thy judgments help me.'),
(16077,19,'Psalms','OT',119,176,'I have gone astray like a lost sheep; seek thy servant; for I do not forget thy commandments.'),
(16078,19,'Psalms','OT',120,1,'[A Song of degrees.] In my distress I cried unto the LORD, and he heard me.'),
(16079,19,'Psalms','OT',120,2,'Deliver my soul, O LORD, from lying lips, {and} from a deceitful tongue.'),
(16080,19,'Psalms','OT',120,3,'What shall be given unto thee? or what shall be done unto thee, thou false tongue? {What shall be given...: or, What shall the deceitful tongue give unto thee? or, what shall it profit thee?} {done: Heb. added}'),
(16081,19,'Psalms','OT',120,4,'Sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals of juniper. {Sharp...: or, It is as the sharp arrows of the mighty man, with coals of juniper}'),
(16082,19,'Psalms','OT',120,5,'Woe is me, that I sojourn in Mesech, {that} I dwell in the tents of Kedar!'),
(16083,19,'Psalms','OT',120,6,'My soul hath long dwelt with him that hateth peace.'),
(16084,19,'Psalms','OT',120,7,'I {am for} peace: but when I speak, they {are} for war. {for peace: or, a man of peace}'),
(16085,19,'Psalms','OT',121,1,'[A Song of degrees.] I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help. {I will...: or, Shall I lift up mine eyes to the hills? whence should my help come?}'),
(16086,19,'Psalms','OT',121,2,'My help {cometh} from the LORD, which made heaven and earth.'),
(16087,19,'Psalms','OT',121,3,'He will not suffer thy foot to be moved: he that keepeth thee will not slumber.'),
(16088,19,'Psalms','OT',121,4,'Behold, he that keepeth Israel shall neither slumber nor sleep.'),
(16089,19,'Psalms','OT',121,5,'The LORD {is} thy keeper: the LORD {is} thy shade upon thy right hand.'),
(16090,19,'Psalms','OT',121,6,'The sun shall not smite thee by day, nor the moon by night.'),
(16091,19,'Psalms','OT',121,7,'The LORD shall preserve thee from all evil: he shall preserve thy soul.'),
(16092,19,'Psalms','OT',121,8,'The LORD shall preserve thy going out and thy coming in from this time forth, and even for evermore.'),
(16093,19,'Psalms','OT',122,1,'[A Song of degrees of David.] I was glad when they said unto me, Let us go into the house of the LORD.'),
(16094,19,'Psalms','OT',122,2,'Our feet shall stand within thy gates, O Jerusalem.'),
(16095,19,'Psalms','OT',122,3,'Jerusalem is builded as a city that is compact together:'),
(16096,19,'Psalms','OT',122,4,'Whither the tribes go up, the tribes of the LORD, unto the testimony of Israel, to give thanks unto the name of the LORD.'),
(16097,19,'Psalms','OT',122,5,'For there are set thrones of judgment, the thrones of the house of David. {are...: Heb. do sit}'),
(16098,19,'Psalms','OT',122,6,'Pray for the peace of Jerusalem: they shall prosper that love thee.'),
(16099,19,'Psalms','OT',122,7,'Peace be within thy walls, {and} prosperity within thy palaces.'),
(16100,19,'Psalms','OT',122,8,'For my brethren and companions\' sakes, I will now say, Peace {be} within thee.'),
(16101,19,'Psalms','OT',122,9,'Because of the house of the LORD our God I will seek thy good.'),
(16102,19,'Psalms','OT',123,1,'[A Song of degrees.] Unto thee lift I up mine eyes, O thou that dwellest in the heavens.'),
(16103,19,'Psalms','OT',123,2,'Behold, as the eyes of servants {look} unto the hand of their masters, {and} as the eyes of a maiden unto the hand of her mistress; so our eyes {wait} upon the LORD our God, until that he have mercy upon us.'),
(16104,19,'Psalms','OT',123,3,'Have mercy upon us, O LORD, have mercy upon us: for we are exceedingly filled with contempt.'),
(16105,19,'Psalms','OT',123,4,'Our soul is exceedingly filled with the scorning of those that are at ease, {and} with the contempt of the proud.'),
(16106,19,'Psalms','OT',124,1,'[A Song of degrees of David.] If {it had not been} the LORD who was on our side, now may Israel say;'),
(16107,19,'Psalms','OT',124,2,'If {it had not been} the LORD who was on our side, when men rose up against us:'),
(16108,19,'Psalms','OT',124,3,'Then they had swallowed us up quick, when their wrath was kindled against us:'),
(16109,19,'Psalms','OT',124,4,'Then the waters had overwhelmed us, the stream had gone over our soul:'),
(16110,19,'Psalms','OT',124,5,'Then the proud waters had gone over our soul.'),
(16111,19,'Psalms','OT',124,6,'Blessed {be} the LORD, who hath not given us {as} a prey to their teeth.'),
(16112,19,'Psalms','OT',124,7,'Our soul is escaped as a bird out of the snare of the fowlers: the snare is broken, and we are escaped.'),
(16113,19,'Psalms','OT',124,8,'Our help {is} in the name of the LORD, who made heaven and earth.'),
(16114,19,'Psalms','OT',125,1,'[A Song of degrees.] They that trust in the LORD {shall be} as mount Zion, {which} cannot be removed, {but} abideth for ever.'),
(16115,19,'Psalms','OT',125,2,'As the mountains {are} round about Jerusalem, so the LORD {is} round about his people from henceforth even for ever.'),
(16116,19,'Psalms','OT',125,3,'For the rod of the wicked shall not rest upon the lot of the righteous; lest the righteous put forth their hands unto iniquity. {the wicked: Heb. wickedness}'),
(16117,19,'Psalms','OT',125,4,'Do good, O LORD, unto {those that be} good, and {to them that are} upright in their hearts.'),
(16118,19,'Psalms','OT',125,5,'As for such as turn aside unto their crooked ways, the LORD shall lead them forth with the workers of iniquity: {but} peace {shall be} upon Israel.'),
(16119,19,'Psalms','OT',126,1,'[A Song of degrees.] When the LORD turned again the captivity of Zion, we were like them that dream. {turned...: Heb. returned the returning}'),
(16120,19,'Psalms','OT',126,2,'Then was our mouth filled with laughter, and our tongue with singing: then said they among the heathen, The LORD hath done great things for them. {hath...: Heb. hath magnified to do with them}'),
(16121,19,'Psalms','OT',126,3,'The LORD hath done great things for us; {whereof} we are glad.'),
(16122,19,'Psalms','OT',126,4,'Turn again our captivity, O LORD, as the streams in the south.'),
(16123,19,'Psalms','OT',126,5,'They that sow in tears shall reap in joy. {joy: or, singing}'),
(16124,19,'Psalms','OT',126,6,'He that goeth forth and weepeth, bearing precious seed, shall doubtless come again with rejoicing, bringing his sheaves {with him}. {precious...: or, seed basket}'),
(16125,19,'Psalms','OT',127,1,'[A Song of degrees for Solomon.] Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it: except the LORD keep the city, the watchman waketh {but} in vain. {for...: or, of Solomon} {that...: Heb. that are builders of it in it}'),
(16126,19,'Psalms','OT',127,2,'{It is} vain for you to rise up early, to sit up late, to eat the bread of sorrows: {for} so he giveth his beloved sleep.'),
(16127,19,'Psalms','OT',127,3,'Lo, children {are} an heritage of the LORD: {and} the fruit of the womb {is his} reward.'),
(16128,19,'Psalms','OT',127,4,'As arrows {are} in the hand of a mighty man; so {are} children of the youth.'),
(16129,19,'Psalms','OT',127,5,'Happy {is} the man that hath his quiver full of them: they shall not be ashamed, but they shall speak with the enemies in the gate. {his...: Heb. filled his quiver with them} {speak...: or, subdue, or, destroy}'),
(16130,19,'Psalms','OT',128,1,'[A Song of degrees.] Blessed {is} every one that feareth the LORD; that walketh in his ways.'),
(16131,19,'Psalms','OT',128,2,'For thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands: happy {shalt} thou {be}, and {it shall be} well with thee.'),
(16132,19,'Psalms','OT',128,3,'Thy wife {shall be} as a fruitful vine by the sides of thine house: thy children like olive plants round about thy table.'),
(16133,19,'Psalms','OT',128,4,'Behold, that thus shall the man be blessed that feareth the LORD.'),
(16134,19,'Psalms','OT',128,5,'The LORD shall bless thee out of Zion: and thou shalt see the good of Jerusalem all the days of thy life.'),
(16135,19,'Psalms','OT',128,6,'Yea, thou shalt see thy children\'s children, {and} peace upon Israel.'),
(16136,19,'Psalms','OT',129,1,'[A Song of degrees.] Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth, may Israel now say: {Many...: or, Much}'),
(16137,19,'Psalms','OT',129,2,'Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth: yet they have not prevailed against me. {Many...: or, Much}'),
(16138,19,'Psalms','OT',129,3,'The plowers plowed upon my back: they made long their furrows.'),
(16139,19,'Psalms','OT',129,4,'The LORD {is} righteous: he hath cut asunder the cords of the wicked.'),
(16140,19,'Psalms','OT',129,5,'Let them all be confounded and turned back that hate Zion.'),
(16141,19,'Psalms','OT',129,6,'Let them be as the grass {upon} the housetops, which withereth afore it groweth up:'),
(16142,19,'Psalms','OT',129,7,'Wherewith the mower filleth not his hand; nor he that bindeth sheaves his bosom.'),
(16143,19,'Psalms','OT',129,8,'Neither do they which go by say, The blessing of the LORD {be} upon you: we bless you in the name of the LORD.'),
(16144,19,'Psalms','OT',130,1,'[A Song of degrees.] Out of the depths have I cried unto thee, O LORD.'),
(16145,19,'Psalms','OT',130,2,'Lord, hear my voice: let thine ears be attentive to the voice of my supplications.'),
(16146,19,'Psalms','OT',130,3,'If thou, LORD, shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, who shall stand?'),
(16147,19,'Psalms','OT',130,4,'But {there is} forgiveness with thee, that thou mayest be feared.'),
(16148,19,'Psalms','OT',130,5,'I wait for the LORD, my soul doth wait, and in his word do I hope.'),
(16149,19,'Psalms','OT',130,6,'My soul {waiteth} for the Lord more than they that watch for the morning: {I say, more than} they that watch for the morning. {I say...: or, which watch unto}'),
(16150,19,'Psalms','OT',130,7,'Let Israel hope in the LORD: for with the LORD {there is} mercy, and with him {is} plenteous redemption.'),
(16151,19,'Psalms','OT',130,8,'And he shall redeem Israel from all his iniquities.'),
(16152,19,'Psalms','OT',131,1,'[A Song of degrees of David.] LORD, my heart is not haughty, nor mine eyes lofty: neither do I exercise myself in great matters, or in things too high for me. {exercise...: Heb. walk} {high: Heb. wonderful}'),
(16153,19,'Psalms','OT',131,2,'Surely I have behaved and quieted myself, as a child that is weaned of his mother: my soul {is} even as a weaned child. {myself: Heb. my soul}'),
(16154,19,'Psalms','OT',131,3,'Let Israel hope in the LORD from henceforth and for ever. {henceforth: Heb. now}'),
(16155,19,'Psalms','OT',132,1,'A Song of degrees. LORD, remember David, {and} all his afflictions:'),
(16156,19,'Psalms','OT',132,2,'How he sware unto the LORD, {and} vowed unto the mighty {God} of Jacob;'),
(16157,19,'Psalms','OT',132,3,'Surely I will not come into the tabernacle of my house, nor go up into my bed;'),
(16158,19,'Psalms','OT',132,4,'I will not give sleep to mine eyes, {or} slumber to mine eyelids,'),
(16159,19,'Psalms','OT',132,5,'Until I find out a place for the LORD, an habitation for the mighty {God} of Jacob. {an habitation: Heb. habitations}'),
(16160,19,'Psalms','OT',132,6,'Lo, we heard of it at Ephratah: we found it in the fields of the wood.'),
(16161,19,'Psalms','OT',132,7,'We will go into his tabernacles: we will worship at his footstool.'),
(16162,19,'Psalms','OT',132,8,'Arise, O LORD, into thy rest; thou, and the ark of thy strength.'),
(16163,19,'Psalms','OT',132,9,'Let thy priests be clothed with righteousness; and let thy saints shout for joy.'),
(16164,19,'Psalms','OT',132,10,'For thy servant David\'s sake turn not away the face of thine anointed.'),
(16165,19,'Psalms','OT',132,11,'The LORD hath sworn {in} truth unto David; he will not turn from it; Of the fruit of thy body will I set upon thy throne. {body: Heb. belly}'),
(16166,19,'Psalms','OT',132,12,'If thy children will keep my covenant and my testimony that I shall teach them, their children shall also sit upon thy throne for evermore.'),
(16167,19,'Psalms','OT',132,13,'For the LORD hath chosen Zion; he hath desired {it} for his habitation.'),
(16168,19,'Psalms','OT',132,14,'This {is} my rest for ever: here will I dwell; for I have desired it.'),
(16169,19,'Psalms','OT',132,15,'I will abundantly bless her provision: I will satisfy her poor with bread. {abundantly: or, surely}'),
(16170,19,'Psalms','OT',132,16,'I will also clothe her priests with salvation: and her saints shall shout aloud for joy.'),
(16171,19,'Psalms','OT',132,17,'There will I make the horn of David to bud: I have ordained a lamp for mine anointed. {lamp: or, candle}'),
(16172,19,'Psalms','OT',132,18,'His enemies will I clothe with shame: but upon himself shall his crown flourish.'),
(16173,19,'Psalms','OT',133,1,'[A Song of degrees of David.] Behold, how good and how pleasant {it is} for brethren to dwell together in unity! {together...: Heb. even together}'),
(16174,19,'Psalms','OT',133,2,'{It is} like the precious ointment upon the head, that ran down upon the beard, {even} Aaron\'s beard: that went down to the skirts of his garments;'),
(16175,19,'Psalms','OT',133,3,'As the dew of Hermon, {and as the dew} that descended upon the mountains of Zion: for there the LORD commanded the blessing, {even} life for evermore.'),
(16176,19,'Psalms','OT',134,1,'[A Song of degrees.] Behold, bless ye the LORD, all {ye} servants of the LORD, which by night stand in the house of the LORD.'),
(16177,19,'Psalms','OT',134,2,'Lift up your hands {in} the sanctuary, and bless the LORD. {the sanctuary: or, holiness}'),
(16178,19,'Psalms','OT',134,3,'The LORD that made heaven and earth bless thee out of Zion.'),
(16179,19,'Psalms','OT',135,1,'Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the name of the LORD; praise {him}, O ye servants of the LORD.'),
(16180,19,'Psalms','OT',135,2,'Ye that stand in the house of the LORD, in the courts of the house of our God,'),
(16181,19,'Psalms','OT',135,3,'Praise the LORD; for the LORD {is} good: sing praises unto his name; for {it is} pleasant.'),
(16182,19,'Psalms','OT',135,4,'For the LORD hath chosen Jacob unto himself, {and} Israel for his peculiar treasure.'),
(16183,19,'Psalms','OT',135,5,'For I know that the LORD {is} great, and {that} our Lord {is} above all gods.'),
(16184,19,'Psalms','OT',135,6,'Whatsoever the LORD pleased, {that} did he in heaven, and in earth, in the seas, and all deep places.'),
(16185,19,'Psalms','OT',135,7,'He causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings for the rain; he bringeth the wind out of his treasuries.'),
(16186,19,'Psalms','OT',135,8,'Who smote the firstborn of Egypt, both of man and beast. {both...: Heb. from man unto beast}'),
(16187,19,'Psalms','OT',135,9,'{Who} sent tokens and wonders into the midst of thee, O Egypt, upon Pharaoh, and upon all his servants.'),
(16188,19,'Psalms','OT',135,10,'Who smote great nations, and slew mighty kings;'),
(16189,19,'Psalms','OT',135,11,'Sihon king of the Amorites, and Og king of Bashan, and all the kingdoms of Canaan:'),
(16190,19,'Psalms','OT',135,12,'And gave their land {for} an heritage, an heritage unto Israel his people.'),
(16191,19,'Psalms','OT',135,13,'Thy name, O LORD, {endureth} for ever; {and} thy memorial, O LORD, throughout all generations. {throughout...: Heb. to generation and generation}'),
(16192,19,'Psalms','OT',135,14,'For the LORD will judge his people, and he will repent himself concerning his servants.'),
(16193,19,'Psalms','OT',135,15,'The idols of the heathen {are} silver and gold, the work of men\'s hands.'),
(16194,19,'Psalms','OT',135,16,'They have mouths, but they speak not; eyes have they, but they see not;'),
(16195,19,'Psalms','OT',135,17,'They have ears, but they hear not; neither is there {any} breath in their mouths.'),
(16196,19,'Psalms','OT',135,18,'They that make them are like unto them: {so is} every one that trusteth in them.'),
(16197,19,'Psalms','OT',135,19,'Bless the LORD, O house of Israel: bless the LORD, O house of Aaron:'),
(16198,19,'Psalms','OT',135,20,'Bless the LORD, O house of Levi: ye that fear the LORD, bless the LORD.'),
(16199,19,'Psalms','OT',135,21,'Blessed be the LORD out of Zion, which dwelleth at Jerusalem. Praise ye the LORD.'),
(16200,19,'Psalms','OT',136,1,'O give thanks unto the LORD; for {he is} good: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16201,19,'Psalms','OT',136,2,'O give thanks unto the God of gods: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16202,19,'Psalms','OT',136,3,'O give thanks to the Lord of lords: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16203,19,'Psalms','OT',136,4,'To him who alone doeth great wonders: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16204,19,'Psalms','OT',136,5,'To him that by wisdom made the heavens: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16205,19,'Psalms','OT',136,6,'To him that stretched out the earth above the waters: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16206,19,'Psalms','OT',136,7,'To him that made great lights: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16207,19,'Psalms','OT',136,8,'The sun to rule by day: for his mercy {endureth} for ever: {to rule...: Heb. for the rulings by day}'),
(16208,19,'Psalms','OT',136,9,'The moon and stars to rule by night: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16209,19,'Psalms','OT',136,10,'To him that smote Egypt in their firstborn: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16210,19,'Psalms','OT',136,11,'And brought out Israel from among them: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16211,19,'Psalms','OT',136,12,'With a strong hand, and with a stretched out arm: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16212,19,'Psalms','OT',136,13,'To him which divided the Red sea into parts: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16213,19,'Psalms','OT',136,14,'And made Israel to pass through the midst of it: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16214,19,'Psalms','OT',136,15,'But overthrew Pharaoh and his host in the Red sea: for his mercy {endureth} for ever. {overthrew: Heb. shaked off}'),
(16215,19,'Psalms','OT',136,16,'To him which led his people through the wilderness: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16216,19,'Psalms','OT',136,17,'To him which smote great kings: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16217,19,'Psalms','OT',136,18,'And slew famous kings: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16218,19,'Psalms','OT',136,19,'Sihon king of the Amorites: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16219,19,'Psalms','OT',136,20,'And Og the king of Bashan: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16220,19,'Psalms','OT',136,21,'And gave their land for an heritage: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16221,19,'Psalms','OT',136,22,'{Even} an heritage unto Israel his servant: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16222,19,'Psalms','OT',136,23,'Who remembered us in our low estate: for his mercy {endureth} for ever:'),
(16223,19,'Psalms','OT',136,24,'And hath redeemed us from our enemies: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16224,19,'Psalms','OT',136,25,'Who giveth food to all flesh: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16225,19,'Psalms','OT',136,26,'O give thanks unto the God of heaven: for his mercy {endureth} for ever.'),
(16226,19,'Psalms','OT',137,1,'By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion.'),
(16227,19,'Psalms','OT',137,2,'We hanged our harps upon the willows in the midst thereof.'),
(16228,19,'Psalms','OT',137,3,'For there they that carried us away captive required of us a song; and they that wasted us {required of us} mirth, {saying}, Sing us {one} of the songs of Zion. {a song: Heb. the words of a song} {wasted...: Heb. laid us on heaps}'),
(16229,19,'Psalms','OT',137,4,'How shall we sing the LORD\'S song in a strange land? {strange...: Heb. land of a stranger?}'),
(16230,19,'Psalms','OT',137,5,'If I forget thee, O Jerusalem, let my right hand forget {her cunning}.'),
(16231,19,'Psalms','OT',137,6,'If I do not remember thee, let my tongue cleave to the roof of my mouth; if I prefer not Jerusalem above my chief joy. {my chief...: Heb. the head of my joy}'),
(16232,19,'Psalms','OT',137,7,'Remember, O LORD, the children of Edom in the day of Jerusalem; who said, Rase {it}, rase {it, even} to the foundation thereof. {Rase it: Heb. Make bare}'),
(16233,19,'Psalms','OT',137,8,'O daughter of Babylon, who art to be destroyed; happy {shall he be}, that rewardeth thee as thou hast served us. {destroyed: Heb. wasted} {rewardeth...: Heb. recompenseth unto thee thy deed which thou didst to us}'),
(16234,19,'Psalms','OT',137,9,'Happy {shall he be}, that taketh and dasheth thy little ones against the stones. {the stones: Heb. the rock}'),
(16235,19,'Psalms','OT',138,1,'[{A Psalm} of David.] I will praise thee with my whole heart: before the gods will I sing praise unto thee.'),
(16236,19,'Psalms','OT',138,2,'I will worship toward thy holy temple, and praise thy name for thy lovingkindness and for thy truth: for thou hast magnified thy word above all thy name.'),
(16237,19,'Psalms','OT',138,3,'In the day when I cried thou answeredst me, {and} strengthenedst me {with} strength in my soul.'),
(16238,19,'Psalms','OT',138,4,'All the kings of the earth shall praise thee, O LORD, when they hear the words of thy mouth.'),
(16239,19,'Psalms','OT',138,5,'Yea, they shall sing in the ways of the LORD: for great {is} the glory of the LORD.'),
(16240,19,'Psalms','OT',138,6,'Though the LORD {be} high, yet hath he respect unto the lowly: but the proud he knoweth afar off.'),
(16241,19,'Psalms','OT',138,7,'Though I walk in the midst of trouble, thou wilt revive me: thou shalt stretch forth thine hand against the wrath of mine enemies, and thy right hand shall save me.'),
(16242,19,'Psalms','OT',138,8,'The LORD will perfect {that which} concerneth me: thy mercy, O LORD, {endureth} for ever: forsake not the works of thine own hands.'),
(16243,19,'Psalms','OT',139,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.] O LORD, thou hast searched me, and known {me}.'),
(16244,19,'Psalms','OT',139,2,'Thou knowest my downsitting and mine uprising, thou understandest my thought afar off.'),
(16245,19,'Psalms','OT',139,3,'Thou compassest my path and my lying down, and art acquainted {with} all my ways. {compassest: or, winnowest}'),
(16246,19,'Psalms','OT',139,4,'For {there is} not a word in my tongue, {but}, lo, O LORD, thou knowest it altogether.'),
(16247,19,'Psalms','OT',139,5,'Thou hast beset me behind and before, and laid thine hand upon me.'),
(16248,19,'Psalms','OT',139,6,'{Such} knowledge {is} too wonderful for me; it is high, I cannot {attain} unto it.'),
(16249,19,'Psalms','OT',139,7,'Whither shall I go from thy spirit? or whither shall I flee from thy presence?'),
(16250,19,'Psalms','OT',139,8,'If I ascend up into heaven, thou {art} there: if I make my bed in hell, behold, thou {art there}.'),
(16251,19,'Psalms','OT',139,9,'{If} I take the wings of the morning, {and} dwell in the uttermost parts of the sea;'),
(16252,19,'Psalms','OT',139,10,'Even there shall thy hand lead me, and thy right hand shall hold me.'),
(16253,19,'Psalms','OT',139,11,'If I say, Surely the darkness shall cover me; even the night shall be light about me.'),
(16254,19,'Psalms','OT',139,12,'Yea, the darkness hideth not from thee; but the night shineth as the day: the darkness and the light {are} both alike {to thee}. {hideth...: Heb. darkeneth not} {the darkness and...: Heb. as is the darkness, so is the light}'),
(16255,19,'Psalms','OT',139,13,'For thou hast possessed my reins: thou hast covered me in my mother\'s womb.'),
(16256,19,'Psalms','OT',139,14,'I will praise thee; for I am fearfully {and} wonderfully made: marvellous {are} thy works; and {that} my soul knoweth right well. {right...: Heb. greatly}'),
(16257,19,'Psalms','OT',139,15,'My substance was not hid from thee, when I was made in secret, {and} curiously wrought in the lowest parts of the earth. {substance: or, strength, or, body}'),
(16258,19,'Psalms','OT',139,16,'Thine eyes did see my substance, yet being unperfect; and in thy book all {my members} were written, {which} in continuance were fashioned, when {as yet there was} none of them. {all...: Heb. all of them} {which...: or, what days they should be fashioned}'),
(16259,19,'Psalms','OT',139,17,'How precious also are thy thoughts unto me, O God! how great is the sum of them!'),
(16260,19,'Psalms','OT',139,18,'{If} I should count them, they are more in number than the sand: when I awake, I am still with thee.'),
(16261,19,'Psalms','OT',139,19,'Surely thou wilt slay the wicked, O God: depart from me therefore, ye bloody men.'),
(16262,19,'Psalms','OT',139,20,'For they speak against thee wickedly, {and} thine enemies take {thy name} in vain.'),
(16263,19,'Psalms','OT',139,21,'Do not I hate them, O LORD, that hate thee? and am not I grieved with those that rise up against thee?'),
(16264,19,'Psalms','OT',139,22,'I hate them with perfect hatred: I count them mine enemies.'),
(16265,19,'Psalms','OT',139,23,'Search me, O God, and know my heart: try me, and know my thoughts:'),
(16266,19,'Psalms','OT',139,24,'And see if {there be any} wicked way in me, and lead me in the way everlasting. {wicked...: Heb. way of pain, or, grief}'),
(16267,19,'Psalms','OT',140,1,'[To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David.] Deliver me, O LORD, from the evil man: preserve me from the violent man; {violent...: Heb. man of violences}'),
(16268,19,'Psalms','OT',140,2,'Which imagine mischiefs in {their} heart; continually are they gathered together {for} war.'),
(16269,19,'Psalms','OT',140,3,'They have sharpened their tongues like a serpent; adders\' poison {is} under their lips. Selah.'),
(16270,19,'Psalms','OT',140,4,'Keep me, O LORD, from the hands of the wicked; preserve me from the violent man; who have purposed to overthrow my goings.'),
(16271,19,'Psalms','OT',140,5,'The proud have hid a snare for me, and cords; they have spread a net by the wayside; they have set gins for me. Selah.'),
(16272,19,'Psalms','OT',140,6,'I said unto the LORD, Thou {art} my God: hear the voice of my supplications, O LORD.'),
(16273,19,'Psalms','OT',140,7,'O GOD the Lord, the strength of my salvation, thou hast covered my head in the day of battle.'),
(16274,19,'Psalms','OT',140,8,'Grant not, O LORD, the desires of the wicked: further not his wicked device; {lest} they exalt themselves. Selah. {lest...: or, let them not be exalted}'),
(16275,19,'Psalms','OT',140,9,'{As for} the head of those that compass me about, let the mischief of their own lips cover them.'),
(16276,19,'Psalms','OT',140,10,'Let burning coals fall upon them: let them be cast into the fire; into deep pits, that they rise not up again.'),
(16277,19,'Psalms','OT',140,11,'Let not an evil speaker be established in the earth: evil shall hunt the violent man to overthrow {him}. {an...: or, an evil speaker (Heb. a man of tongue), a wicked man of violence, be established in the earth: let him be hunted to his overthrow}'),
(16278,19,'Psalms','OT',140,12,'I know that the LORD will maintain the cause of the afflicted, {and} the right of the poor.'),
(16279,19,'Psalms','OT',140,13,'Surely the righteous shall give thanks unto thy name: the upright shall dwell in thy presence.'),
(16280,19,'Psalms','OT',141,1,'[A Psalm of David.] LORD, I cry unto thee: make haste unto me; give ear unto my voice, when I cry unto thee.'),
(16281,19,'Psalms','OT',141,2,'Let my prayer be set forth before thee {as} incense; {and} the lifting up of my hands {as} the evening sacrifice. {set...: Heb. directed}'),
(16282,19,'Psalms','OT',141,3,'Set a watch, O LORD, before my mouth; keep the door of my lips.'),
(16283,19,'Psalms','OT',141,4,'Incline not my heart to {any} evil thing, to practise wicked works with men that work iniquity: and let me not eat of their dainties.'),
(16284,19,'Psalms','OT',141,5,'Let the righteous smite me; {it shall be} a kindness: and let him reprove me; {it shall be} an excellent oil, {which} shall not break my head: for yet my prayer also {shall be} in their calamities. {me; it shall be a...: or, me kindly, and reprove me; let not their precious oil break, etc}'),
(16285,19,'Psalms','OT',141,6,'When their judges are overthrown in stony places, they shall hear my words; for they are sweet.'),
(16286,19,'Psalms','OT',141,7,'Our bones are scattered at the grave\'s mouth, as when one cutteth and cleaveth {wood} upon the earth.'),
(16287,19,'Psalms','OT',141,8,'But mine eyes {are} unto thee, O GOD the Lord: in thee is my trust; leave not my soul destitute. {leave...: Heb. make not my soul bare}'),
(16288,19,'Psalms','OT',141,9,'Keep me from the snares {which} they have laid for me, and the gins of the workers of iniquity.'),
(16289,19,'Psalms','OT',141,10,'Let the wicked fall into their own nets, whilst that I withal escape. {escape: Heb. pass over}'),
(16290,19,'Psalms','OT',142,1,'[Maschil of David; A Prayer when he was in the cave.] I cried unto the LORD with my voice; with my voice unto the LORD did I make my supplication. {Maschil...: or, A Psalm of David, giving instruction}'),
(16291,19,'Psalms','OT',142,2,'I poured out my complaint before him; I shewed before him my trouble.'),
(16292,19,'Psalms','OT',142,3,'When my spirit was overwhelmed within me, then thou knewest my path. In the way wherein I walked have they privily laid a snare for me.'),
(16293,19,'Psalms','OT',142,4,'I looked on {my} right hand, and beheld, but {there was} no man that would know me: refuge failed me; no man cared for my soul. {I looked...: or, Look on the right hand, and see} {failed...: Heb. perished from me} {cared...: Heb. sought after}'),
(16294,19,'Psalms','OT',142,5,'I cried unto thee, O LORD: I said, Thou {art} my refuge {and} my portion in the land of the living.'),
(16295,19,'Psalms','OT',142,6,'Attend unto my cry; for I am brought very low: deliver me from my persecutors; for they are stronger than I.'),
(16296,19,'Psalms','OT',142,7,'Bring my soul out of prison, that I may praise thy name: the righteous shall compass me about; for thou shalt deal bountifully with me.'),
(16297,19,'Psalms','OT',143,1,'[A Psalm of David.] Hear my prayer, O LORD, give ear to my supplications: in thy faithfulness answer me, {and} in thy righteousness.'),
(16298,19,'Psalms','OT',143,2,'And enter not into judgment with thy servant: for in thy sight shall no man living be justified.'),
(16299,19,'Psalms','OT',143,3,'For the enemy hath persecuted my soul; he hath smitten my life down to the ground; he hath made me to dwell in darkness, as those that have been long dead.'),
(16300,19,'Psalms','OT',143,4,'Therefore is my spirit overwhelmed within me; my heart within me is desolate.'),
(16301,19,'Psalms','OT',143,5,'I remember the days of old; I meditate on all thy works; I muse on the work of thy hands.'),
(16302,19,'Psalms','OT',143,6,'I stretch forth my hands unto thee: my soul {thirsteth} after thee, as a thirsty land. Selah.'),
(16303,19,'Psalms','OT',143,7,'Hear me speedily, O LORD: my spirit faileth: hide not thy face from me, lest I be like unto them that go down into the pit. {lest...: or, for I am become like, etc}'),
(16304,19,'Psalms','OT',143,8,'Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk; for I lift up my soul unto thee.'),
(16305,19,'Psalms','OT',143,9,'Deliver me, O LORD, from mine enemies: I flee unto thee to hide me. {flee...: Heb. hide me with thee}'),
(16306,19,'Psalms','OT',143,10,'Teach me to do thy will; for thou {art} my God: thy spirit {is} good; lead me into the land of uprightness.'),
(16307,19,'Psalms','OT',143,11,'Quicken me, O LORD, for thy name\'s sake: for thy righteousness\' sake bring my soul out of trouble.'),
(16308,19,'Psalms','OT',143,12,'And of thy mercy cut off mine enemies, and destroy all them that afflict my soul: for I {am} thy servant.'),
(16309,19,'Psalms','OT',144,1,'[{A Psalm} of David.] Blessed {be} the LORD my strength, which teacheth my hands to war, {and} my fingers to fight: {strength: Heb. rock} {to war...: Heb. to the war, etc}'),
(16310,19,'Psalms','OT',144,2,'My goodness, and my fortress; my high tower, and my deliverer; my shield, and {he} in whom I trust; who subdueth my people under me. {My goodness: or, My mercy}'),
(16311,19,'Psalms','OT',144,3,'LORD, what {is} man, that thou takest knowledge of him! {or} the son of man, that thou makest account of him!'),
(16312,19,'Psalms','OT',144,4,'Man is like to vanity: his days {are} as a shadow that passeth away.'),
(16313,19,'Psalms','OT',144,5,'Bow thy heavens, O LORD, and come down: touch the mountains, and they shall smoke.'),
(16314,19,'Psalms','OT',144,6,'Cast forth lightning, and scatter them: shoot out thine arrows, and destroy them.'),
(16315,19,'Psalms','OT',144,7,'Send thine hand from above; rid me, and deliver me out of great waters, from the hand of strange children; {hand from: Heb. hands from}'),
(16316,19,'Psalms','OT',144,8,'Whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand {is} a right hand of falsehood.'),
(16317,19,'Psalms','OT',144,9,'I will sing a new song unto thee, O God: upon a psaltery {and} an instrument of ten strings will I sing praises unto thee.'),
(16318,19,'Psalms','OT',144,10,'{It is he} that giveth salvation unto kings: who delivereth David his servant from the hurtful sword. {salvation: or, victory}'),
(16319,19,'Psalms','OT',144,11,'Rid me, and deliver me from the hand of strange children, whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand {is} a right hand of falsehood:'),
(16320,19,'Psalms','OT',144,12,'That our sons {may be} as plants grown up in their youth; {that} our daughters {may be} as corner stones, polished {after} the similitude of a palace: {polished: Heb. cut}'),
(16321,19,'Psalms','OT',144,13,'{That} our garners {may be} full, affording all manner of store: {that} our sheep may bring forth thousands and ten thousands in our streets: {all...: Heb. from kind to kind}'),
(16322,19,'Psalms','OT',144,14,'{That} our oxen {may be} strong to labour; {that there be} no breaking in, nor going out; that {there be} no complaining in our streets. {strong...: Heb. able to bear burdens, or, loaden with flesh}'),
(16323,19,'Psalms','OT',144,15,'Happy {is that} people, that is in such a case: {yea}, happy {is that} people, whose God {is} the LORD.'),
(16324,19,'Psalms','OT',145,1,'[David\'s {Psalm} of praise.] I will extol thee, my God, O king; and I will bless thy name for ever and ever.'),
(16325,19,'Psalms','OT',145,2,'Every day will I bless thee; and I will praise thy name for ever and ever.'),
(16326,19,'Psalms','OT',145,3,'Great {is} the LORD, and greatly to be praised; and his greatness {is} unsearchable. {and his...: Heb. and of his greatness there is no search}'),
(16327,19,'Psalms','OT',145,4,'One generation shall praise thy works to another, and shall declare thy mighty acts.'),
(16328,19,'Psalms','OT',145,5,'I will speak of the glorious honour of thy majesty, and of thy wondrous works. {works: Heb. things, or, words}'),
(16329,19,'Psalms','OT',145,6,'And {men} shall speak of the might of thy terrible acts: and I will declare thy greatness. {declare: Heb. declare it}'),
(16330,19,'Psalms','OT',145,7,'They shall abundantly utter the memory of thy great goodness, and shall sing of thy righteousness.'),
(16331,19,'Psalms','OT',145,8,'The LORD {is} gracious, and full of compassion; slow to anger, and of great mercy. {of great...: Heb. great in mercy}'),
(16332,19,'Psalms','OT',145,9,'The LORD {is} good to all: and his tender mercies {are} over all his works.'),
(16333,19,'Psalms','OT',145,10,'All thy works shall praise thee, O LORD; and thy saints shall bless thee.'),
(16334,19,'Psalms','OT',145,11,'They shall speak of the glory of thy kingdom, and talk of thy power;'),
(16335,19,'Psalms','OT',145,12,'To make known to the sons of men his mighty acts, and the glorious majesty of his kingdom.'),
(16336,19,'Psalms','OT',145,13,'Thy kingdom {is} an everlasting kingdom, and thy dominion {endureth} throughout all generations. {an...: Heb. a kingdom of all ages}'),
(16337,19,'Psalms','OT',145,14,'The LORD upholdeth all that fall, and raiseth up all {those that be} bowed down.'),
(16338,19,'Psalms','OT',145,15,'The eyes of all wait upon thee; and thou givest them their meat in due season. {wait...: or, look unto}'),
(16339,19,'Psalms','OT',145,16,'Thou openest thine hand, and satisfiest the desire of every living thing.'),
(16340,19,'Psalms','OT',145,17,'The LORD {is} righteous in all his ways, and holy in all his works. {holy: or, merciful, or, bountiful}'),
(16341,19,'Psalms','OT',145,18,'The LORD {is} nigh unto all them that call upon him, to all that call upon him in truth.'),
(16342,19,'Psalms','OT',145,19,'He will fulfil the desire of them that fear him: he also will hear their cry, and will save them.'),
(16343,19,'Psalms','OT',145,20,'The LORD preserveth all them that love him: but all the wicked will he destroy.'),
(16344,19,'Psalms','OT',145,21,'My mouth shall speak the praise of the LORD: and let all flesh bless his holy name for ever and ever.'),
(16345,19,'Psalms','OT',146,1,'Praise ye the LORD. Praise the LORD, O my soul. {Praise ye...: Heb. Hallelujah}'),
(16346,19,'Psalms','OT',146,2,'While I live will I praise the LORD: I will sing praises unto my God while I have any being.'),
(16347,19,'Psalms','OT',146,3,'Put not your trust in princes, {nor} in the son of man, in whom {there is} no help. {help: or, salvation}'),
(16348,19,'Psalms','OT',146,4,'His breath goeth forth, he returneth to his earth; in that very day his thoughts perish.'),
(16349,19,'Psalms','OT',146,5,'Happy {is he} that {hath} the God of Jacob for his help, whose hope {is} in the LORD his God:'),
(16350,19,'Psalms','OT',146,6,'Which made heaven, and earth, the sea, and all that therein {is}: which keepeth truth for ever:'),
(16351,19,'Psalms','OT',146,7,'Which executeth judgment for the oppressed: which giveth food to the hungry. The LORD looseth the prisoners:'),
(16352,19,'Psalms','OT',146,8,'The LORD openeth {the eyes of} the blind: the LORD raiseth them that are bowed down: the LORD loveth the righteous:'),
(16353,19,'Psalms','OT',146,9,'The LORD preserveth the strangers; he relieveth the fatherless and widow: but the way of the wicked he turneth upside down.'),
(16354,19,'Psalms','OT',146,10,'The LORD shall reign for ever, {even} thy God, O Zion, unto all generations. Praise ye the LORD.'),
(16355,19,'Psalms','OT',147,1,'Praise ye the LORD: for {it is} good to sing praises unto our God; for {it is} pleasant; {and} praise is comely.'),
(16356,19,'Psalms','OT',147,2,'The LORD doth build up Jerusalem: he gathereth together the outcasts of Israel.'),
(16357,19,'Psalms','OT',147,3,'He healeth the broken in heart, and bindeth up their wounds. {wounds: Heb. griefs}'),
(16358,19,'Psalms','OT',147,4,'He telleth the number of the stars; he calleth them all by {their} names.'),
(16359,19,'Psalms','OT',147,5,'Great {is} our Lord, and of great power: his understanding {is} infinite. {his...: Heb. of his understanding there is no number}'),
(16360,19,'Psalms','OT',147,6,'The LORD lifteth up the meek: he casteth the wicked down to the ground.'),
(16361,19,'Psalms','OT',147,7,'Sing unto the LORD with thanksgiving; sing praise upon the harp unto our God:'),
(16362,19,'Psalms','OT',147,8,'Who covereth the heaven with clouds, who prepareth rain for the earth, who maketh grass to grow upon the mountains.'),
(16363,19,'Psalms','OT',147,9,'He giveth to the beast his food, {and} to the young ravens which cry.'),
(16364,19,'Psalms','OT',147,10,'He delighteth not in the strength of the horse: he taketh not pleasure in the legs of a man.'),
(16365,19,'Psalms','OT',147,11,'The LORD taketh pleasure in them that fear him, in those that hope in his mercy.'),
(16366,19,'Psalms','OT',147,12,'Praise the LORD, O Jerusalem; praise thy God, O Zion.'),
(16367,19,'Psalms','OT',147,13,'For he hath strengthened the bars of thy gates; he hath blessed thy children within thee.'),
(16368,19,'Psalms','OT',147,14,'He maketh peace {in} thy borders, {and} filleth thee with the finest of the wheat. {He...: Heb. Who maketh thy border peace} {finest...: Heb. fat of wheat}'),
(16369,19,'Psalms','OT',147,15,'He sendeth forth his commandment {upon} earth: his word runneth very swiftly.'),
(16370,19,'Psalms','OT',147,16,'He giveth snow like wool: he scattereth the hoarfrost like ashes.'),
(16371,19,'Psalms','OT',147,17,'He casteth forth his ice like morsels: who can stand before his cold?'),
(16372,19,'Psalms','OT',147,18,'He sendeth out his word, and melteth them: he causeth his wind to blow, {and} the waters flow.'),
(16373,19,'Psalms','OT',147,19,'He sheweth his word unto Jacob, his statutes and his judgments unto Israel. {his word: Heb. his words}'),
(16374,19,'Psalms','OT',147,20,'He hath not dealt so with any nation: and {as for his} judgments, they have not known them. Praise ye the LORD.'),
(16375,19,'Psalms','OT',148,1,'Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the LORD from the heavens: praise him in the heights. {Praise ye the LORD. Praise: Heb. Hallelujah, etc}'),
(16376,19,'Psalms','OT',148,2,'Praise ye him, all his angels: praise ye him, all his hosts.'),
(16377,19,'Psalms','OT',148,3,'Praise ye him, sun and moon: praise him, all ye stars of light.'),
(16378,19,'Psalms','OT',148,4,'Praise him, ye heavens of heavens, and ye waters that {be} above the heavens.'),
(16379,19,'Psalms','OT',148,5,'Let them praise the name of the LORD: for he commanded, and they were created.'),
(16380,19,'Psalms','OT',148,6,'He hath also stablished them for ever and ever: he hath made a decree which shall not pass.'),
(16381,19,'Psalms','OT',148,7,'Praise the LORD from the earth, ye dragons, and all deeps:'),
(16382,19,'Psalms','OT',148,8,'Fire, and hail; snow, and vapour; stormy wind fulfilling his word:'),
(16383,19,'Psalms','OT',148,9,'Mountains, and all hills; fruitful trees, and all cedars:'),
(16384,19,'Psalms','OT',148,10,'Beasts, and all cattle; creeping things, and flying fowl: {flying...: Heb. birds of wing}'),
(16385,19,'Psalms','OT',148,11,'Kings of the earth, and all people; princes, and all judges of the earth:'),
(16386,19,'Psalms','OT',148,12,'Both young men, and maidens; old men, and children:'),
(16387,19,'Psalms','OT',148,13,'Let them praise the name of the LORD: for his name alone is excellent; his glory {is} above the earth and heaven. {excellent: Heb. exalted}'),
(16388,19,'Psalms','OT',148,14,'He also exalteth the horn of his people, the praise of all his saints; {even} of the children of Israel, a people near unto him. Praise ye the LORD.'),
(16389,19,'Psalms','OT',149,1,'Praise ye the LORD. Sing unto the LORD a new song, {and} his praise in the congregation of saints. {Praise...: Heb. Hallelujah}'),
(16390,19,'Psalms','OT',149,2,'Let Israel rejoice in him that made him: let the children of Zion be joyful in their King. {in him...: Heb. in his Makers}'),
(16391,19,'Psalms','OT',149,3,'Let them praise his name in the dance: let them sing praises unto him with the timbrel and harp. {in...: or, with the pipe}'),
(16392,19,'Psalms','OT',149,4,'For the LORD taketh pleasure in his people: he will beautify the meek with salvation.'),
(16393,19,'Psalms','OT',149,5,'Let the saints be joyful in glory: let them sing aloud upon their beds.'),
(16394,19,'Psalms','OT',149,6,'{Let} the high {praises} of God {be} in their mouth, and a twoedged sword in their hand; {mouth: Heb. throat}'),
(16395,19,'Psalms','OT',149,7,'To execute vengeance upon the heathen, {and} punishments upon the people;'),
(16396,19,'Psalms','OT',149,8,'To bind their kings with chains, and their nobles with fetters of iron;'),
(16397,19,'Psalms','OT',149,9,'To execute upon them the judgment written: this honour have all his saints. Praise ye the LORD.'),
(16398,19,'Psalms','OT',150,1,'Praise ye the LORD. Praise God in his sanctuary: praise him in the firmament of his power. {Praise ye...: Heb. Hallelujah}'),
(16399,19,'Psalms','OT',150,2,'Praise him for his mighty acts: praise him according to his excellent greatness.'),
(16400,19,'Psalms','OT',150,3,'Praise him with the sound of the trumpet: praise him with the psaltery and harp. {trumpet: or, cornet}'),
(16401,19,'Psalms','OT',150,4,'Praise him with the timbrel and dance: praise him with stringed instruments and organs. {dance: or, pipe}'),
(16402,19,'Psalms','OT',150,5,'Praise him upon the loud cymbals: praise him upon the high sounding cymbals.'),
(16403,19,'Psalms','OT',150,6,'Let every thing that hath breath praise the LORD. Praise ye the LORD.'),
(16404,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,1,'The proverbs of Solomon the son of David, king of Israel;'),
(16405,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,2,'To know wisdom and instruction; to perceive the words of understanding;'),
(16406,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,3,'To receive the instruction of wisdom, justice, and judgment, and equity; {equity: Heb. equities}'),
(16407,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,4,'To give subtilty to the simple, to the young man knowledge and discretion. {discretion: or, advisement}'),
(16408,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,5,'A wise {man} will hear, and will increase learning; and a man of understanding shall attain unto wise counsels:'),
(16409,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,6,'To understand a proverb, and the interpretation; the words of the wise, and their dark sayings. {the interpretation: or, an eloquent speech}'),
(16410,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,7,'The fear of the LORD {is} the beginning of knowledge: {but} fools despise wisdom and instruction. {the beginning: or, the principal part}'),
(16411,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,8,'My son, hear the instruction of thy father, and forsake not the law of thy mother:'),
(16412,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,9,'For they {shall be} an ornament of grace unto thy head, and chains about thy neck. {an...: Heb. an adding}'),
(16413,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,10,'My son, if sinners entice thee, consent thou not.'),
(16414,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,11,'If they say, Come with us, let us lay wait for blood, let us lurk privily for the innocent without cause:'),
(16415,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,12,'Let us swallow them up alive as the grave; and whole, as those that go down into the pit:'),
(16416,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,13,'We shall find all precious substance, we shall fill our houses with spoil:'),
(16417,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,14,'Cast in thy lot among us; let us all have one purse:'),
(16418,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,15,'My son, walk not thou in the way with them; refrain thy foot from their path:'),
(16419,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,16,'For their feet run to evil, and make haste to shed blood.'),
(16420,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,17,'Surely in vain the net is spread in the sight of any bird. {in the...: Heb. in the eyes of every thing that hath a wing}'),
(16421,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,18,'And they lay wait for their {own} blood; they lurk privily for their {own} lives.'),
(16422,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,19,'So {are} the ways of every one that is greedy of gain; {which} taketh away the life of the owners thereof.'),
(16423,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,20,'Wisdom crieth without; she uttereth her voice in the streets: {Wisdom: Heb. Wisdoms, that is, Excellent wisdom}'),
(16424,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,21,'She crieth in the chief place of concourse, in the openings of the gates: in the city she uttereth her words, {saying},'),
(16425,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,22,'How long, ye simple ones, will ye love simplicity? and the scorners delight in their scorning, and fools hate knowledge?'),
(16426,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,23,'Turn you at my reproof: behold, I will pour out my spirit unto you, I will make known my words unto you.'),
(16427,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,24,'Because I have called, and ye refused; I have stretched out my hand, and no man regarded;'),
(16428,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,25,'But ye have set at nought all my counsel, and would none of my reproof:'),
(16429,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,26,'I also will laugh at your calamity; I will mock when your fear cometh;'),
(16430,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,27,'When your fear cometh as desolation, and your destruction cometh as a whirlwind; when distress and anguish cometh upon you.'),
(16431,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,28,'Then shall they call upon me, but I will not answer; they shall seek me early, but they shall not find me:'),
(16432,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,29,'For that they hated knowledge, and did not choose the fear of the LORD:'),
(16433,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,30,'They would none of my counsel: they despised all my reproof.'),
(16434,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,31,'Therefore shall they eat of the fruit of their own way, and be filled with their own devices.'),
(16435,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,32,'For the turning away of the simple shall slay them, and the prosperity of fools shall destroy them. {turning...: or, ease of the simple}'),
(16436,20,'Proverbs','OT',1,33,'But whoso hearkeneth unto me shall dwell safely, and shall be quiet from fear of evil.'),
(16437,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,1,'My son, if thou wilt receive my words, and hide my commandments with thee;'),
(16438,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,2,'So that thou incline thine ear unto wisdom, {and} apply thine heart to understanding;'),
(16439,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,3,'Yea, if thou criest after knowledge, {and} liftest up thy voice for understanding; {liftest...: Heb. givest thy voice}'),
(16440,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,4,'If thou seekest her as silver, and searchest for her as {for} hid treasures;'),
(16441,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,5,'Then shalt thou understand the fear of the LORD, and find the knowledge of God.'),
(16442,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,6,'For the LORD giveth wisdom: out of his mouth {cometh} knowledge and understanding.'),
(16443,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,7,'He layeth up sound wisdom for the righteous: {he is} a buckler to them that walk uprightly.'),
(16444,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,8,'He keepeth the paths of judgment, and preserveth the way of his saints.'),
(16445,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,9,'Then shalt thou understand righteousness, and judgment, and equity; {yea}, every good path.'),
(16446,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,10,'When wisdom entereth into thine heart, and knowledge is pleasant unto thy soul;'),
(16447,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,11,'Discretion shall preserve thee, understanding shall keep thee:'),
(16448,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,12,'To deliver thee from the way of the evil {man}, from the man that speaketh froward things;'),
(16449,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,13,'Who leave the paths of uprightness, to walk in the ways of darkness;'),
(16450,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,14,'Who rejoice to do evil, {and} delight in the frowardness of the wicked;'),
(16451,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,15,'Whose ways {are} crooked, and {they} froward in their paths:'),
(16452,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,16,'To deliver thee from the strange woman, {even} from the stranger {which} flattereth with her words;'),
(16453,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,17,'Which forsaketh the guide of her youth, and forgetteth the covenant of her God.'),
(16454,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,18,'For her house inclineth unto death, and her paths unto the dead.'),
(16455,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,19,'None that go unto her return again, neither take they hold of the paths of life.'),
(16456,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,20,'That thou mayest walk in the way of good {men}, and keep the paths of the righteous.'),
(16457,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,21,'For the upright shall dwell in the land, and the perfect shall remain in it.'),
(16458,20,'Proverbs','OT',2,22,'But the wicked shall be cut off from the earth, and the transgressors shall be rooted out of it. {rooted: or, plucked up}'),
(16459,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,1,'My son, forget not my law; but let thine heart keep my commandments:'),
(16460,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,2,'For length of days, and long life, and peace, shall they add to thee. {long...: Heb. years of life}'),
(16461,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,3,'Let not mercy and truth forsake thee: bind them about thy neck; write them upon the table of thine heart:'),
(16462,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,4,'So shalt thou find favour and good understanding in the sight of God and man. {good...: or, good success}'),
(16463,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,5,'Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding.'),
(16464,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,6,'In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.'),
(16465,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,7,'Be not wise in thine own eyes: fear the LORD, and depart from evil.'),
(16466,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,8,'It shall be health to thy navel, and marrow to thy bones. {health: Heb. medicine} {marrow: Heb. watering, or, moistening}'),
(16467,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,9,'Honour the LORD with thy substance, and with the firstfruits of all thine increase:'),
(16468,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,10,'So shall thy barns be filled with plenty, and thy presses shall burst out with new wine.'),
(16469,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,11,'My son, despise not the chastening of the LORD; neither be weary of his correction:'),
(16470,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,12,'For whom the LORD loveth he correcteth; even as a father the son {in whom} he delighteth.'),
(16471,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,13,'Happy {is} the man {that} findeth wisdom, and the man {that} getteth understanding. {that getteth...: Heb. that draweth out understanding}'),
(16472,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,14,'For the merchandise of it {is} better than the merchandise of silver, and the gain thereof than fine gold.'),
(16473,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,15,'She {is} more precious than rubies: and all the things thou canst desire are not to be compared unto her.'),
(16474,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,16,'Length of days {is} in her right hand; {and} in her left hand riches and honour.'),
(16475,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,17,'Her ways {are} ways of pleasantness, and all her paths {are} peace.'),
(16476,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,18,'She {is} a tree of life to them that lay hold upon her: and happy {is every one} that retaineth her.'),
(16477,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,19,'The LORD by wisdom hath founded the earth; by understanding hath he established the heavens. {established: or, prepared}'),
(16478,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,20,'By his knowledge the depths are broken up, and the clouds drop down the dew.'),
(16479,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,21,'My son, let not them depart from thine eyes: keep sound wisdom and discretion:'),
(16480,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,22,'So shall they be life unto thy soul, and grace to thy neck.'),
(16481,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,23,'Then shalt thou walk in thy way safely, and thy foot shall not stumble.'),
(16482,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,24,'When thou liest down, thou shalt not be afraid: yea, thou shalt lie down, and thy sleep shall be sweet.'),
(16483,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,25,'Be not afraid of sudden fear, neither of the desolation of the wicked, when it cometh.'),
(16484,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,26,'For the LORD shall be thy confidence, and shall keep thy foot from being taken.'),
(16485,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,27,'Withhold not good from them to whom it is due, when it is in the power of thine hand to do {it}. {them...: Heb. the owners thereof}'),
(16486,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,28,'Say not unto thy neighbour, Go, and come again, and to morrow I will give; when thou hast it by thee.'),
(16487,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,29,'Devise not evil against thy neighbour, seeing he dwelleth securely by thee. {Devise...: or, Practise no evil}'),
(16488,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,30,'Strive not with a man without cause, if he have done thee no harm.'),
(16489,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,31,'Envy thou not the oppressor, and choose none of his ways. {the oppressor: Heb. a man of violence}'),
(16490,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,32,'For the froward {is} abomination to the LORD: but his secret {is} with the righteous.'),
(16491,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,33,'The curse of the LORD {is} in the house of the wicked: but he blesseth the habitation of the just.'),
(16492,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,34,'Surely he scorneth the scorners: but he giveth grace unto the lowly.'),
(16493,20,'Proverbs','OT',3,35,'The wise shall inherit glory: but shame shall be the promotion of fools. {shall be...: Heb. exalteth the fools}'),
(16494,20,'Proverbs','OT',4,1,'Hear, ye children, the instruction of a father, and attend to know understanding.'),
(16495,20,'Proverbs','OT',4,2,'For I give you good doctrine, forsake ye not my law.'),
(16496,20,'Proverbs','OT',4,3,'For I was my father\'s son, tender and only {beloved} in the sight of my mother.'),
(16497,20,'Proverbs','OT',4,4,'He taught me also, and said unto me, Let thine heart retain my words: keep my commandments, and live.'),
(16498,20,'Proverbs','OT',4,5,'Get wisdom, get understanding: forget {it} not; neither decline from the words of my mouth.'),
(16499,20,'Proverbs','OT',4,6,'Forsake her not, and she shall preserve thee: love her, and she shall keep thee.'),
(16500,20,'Proverbs','OT',4,7,'Wisdom {is} the principal thing; {therefore} get wisdom: and with all thy getting get understanding.'),
(16501,20,'Proverbs','OT',4,8,'Exalt her, and she shall promote thee: she shall bring thee to honour, when thou dost embrace her.'),
