(16530,20,'Proverbs','OT',5,10,'Lest strangers be filled with thy wealth; and thy labours {be} in the house of a stranger; {thy wealth: Heb. thy strength}'),
(16531,20,'Proverbs','OT',5,11,'And thou mourn at the last, when thy flesh and thy body are consumed,'),
(16532,20,'Proverbs','OT',5,12,'And say, How have I hated instruction, and my heart despised reproof;'),
(16533,20,'Proverbs','OT',5,13,'And have not obeyed the voice of my teachers, nor inclined mine ear to them that instructed me!'),
