(16555,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,12,'A naughty person, a wicked man, walketh with a froward mouth.'),
(16556,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,13,'He winketh with his eyes, he speaketh with his feet, he teacheth with his fingers;'),
(16557,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,14,'Frowardness {is} in his heart, he deviseth mischief continually; he soweth discord. {soweth: Heb. casteth forth}'),
(16558,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,15,'Therefore shall his calamity come suddenly; suddenly shall he be broken without remedy.'),
(16559,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,16,'These six {things} doth the LORD hate: yea, seven {are} an abomination unto him: {unto...: Heb. of his soul}'),
(16560,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,17,'A proud look, a lying tongue, and hands that shed innocent blood, {A proud...: Heb. Haughty eyes}'),
(16561,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,18,'An heart that deviseth wicked imaginations, feet that be swift in running to mischief,'),
(16562,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,19,'A false witness {that} speaketh lies, and he that soweth discord among brethren.'),
(16563,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,20,'My son, keep thy father\'s commandment, and forsake not the law of thy mother:'),
(16564,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,21,'Bind them continually upon thine heart, {and} tie them about thy neck.'),
(16565,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,22,'When thou goest, it shall lead thee; when thou sleepest, it shall keep thee; and {when} thou awakest, it shall talk with thee.'),
(16566,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,23,'For the commandment {is} a lamp; and the law {is} light; and reproofs of instruction {are} the way of life: {lamp: or, candle}'),
(16567,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,24,'To keep thee from the evil woman, from the flattery of the tongue of a strange woman. {of the...: or, of the strange tongue}'),
(16568,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,25,'Lust not after her beauty in thine heart; neither let her take thee with her eyelids.'),
