(16576,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,33,'A wound and dishonour shall he get; and his reproach shall not be wiped away.'),
(16577,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,34,'For jealousy {is} the rage of a man: therefore he will not spare in the day of vengeance.'),
(16578,20,'Proverbs','OT',6,35,'He will not regard any ransom; neither will he rest content, though thou givest many gifts. {He will...: Heb. He will not accept the face of any ransom}'),
(16579,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,1,'My son, keep my words, and lay up my commandments with thee.'),
(16580,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,2,'Keep my commandments, and live; and my law as the apple of thine eye.'),
(16581,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,3,'Bind them upon thy fingers, write them upon the table of thine heart.'),
(16582,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,4,'Say unto wisdom, Thou {art} my sister; and call understanding {thy} kinswoman:'),
(16583,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,5,'That they may keep thee from the strange woman, from the stranger {which} flattereth with her words.'),
(16584,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,6,'For at the window of my house I looked through my casement,'),
(16585,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,7,'And beheld among the simple ones, I discerned among the youths, a young man void of understanding, {the youths: Heb. the sons}'),
(16586,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,8,'Passing through the street near her corner; and he went the way to her house,'),
