(16588,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,10,'And, behold, there met him a woman {with} the attire of an harlot, and subtil of heart.'),
(16589,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,11,'(She {is} loud and stubborn; her feet abide not in her house:'),
(16590,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,12,'Now {is she} without, now in the streets, and lieth in wait at every corner.)'),
(16591,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,13,'So she caught him, and kissed him, {and} with an impudent face said unto him, {with...: Heb. she strengthened her face and said}'),
(16592,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,14,'{I have} peace offerings with me; this day have I payed my vows. {I have...: Heb. Peace offerings are upon me}'),
(16593,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,15,'Therefore came I forth to meet thee, diligently to seek thy face, and I have found thee.'),
(16594,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,16,'I have decked my bed with coverings of tapestry, with carved {works}, with fine linen of Egypt.'),
(16595,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,17,'I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.'),
(16596,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,18,'Come, let us take our fill of love until the morning: let us solace ourselves with loves.'),
(16597,20,'Proverbs','OT',7,19,'For the goodman {is} not at home, he is gone a long journey:'),
