(16615,20,'Proverbs','OT',8,10,'Receive my instruction, and not silver; and knowledge rather than choice gold.'),
(16616,20,'Proverbs','OT',8,11,'For wisdom {is} better than rubies; and all the things that may be desired are not to be compared to it.'),
(16617,20,'Proverbs','OT',8,12,'I wisdom dwell with prudence, and find out knowledge of witty inventions. {prudence: or, subtilty}'),
