(18065,23,'Isaiah','OT',22,10,'And ye have numbered the houses of Jerusalem, and the houses have ye broken down to fortify the wall.'),
(18066,23,'Isaiah','OT',22,11,'Ye made also a ditch between the two walls for the water of the old pool: but ye have not looked unto the maker thereof, neither had respect unto him that fashioned it long ago.'),
(18067,23,'Isaiah','OT',22,12,'And in that day did the Lord GOD of hosts call to weeping, and to mourning, and to baldness, and to girding with sackcloth:'),
(18068,23,'Isaiah','OT',22,13,'And behold joy and gladness, slaying oxen, and killing sheep, eating flesh, and drinking wine: let us eat and drink; for to morrow we shall die.'),
