(18098,23,'Isaiah','OT',23,18,'And her merchandise and her hire shall be holiness to the LORD: it shall not be treasured nor laid up; for her merchandise shall be for them that dwell before the LORD, to eat sufficiently, and for durable clothing. {durable: Heb. old}'),
(18099,23,'Isaiah','OT',24,1,'Behold, the LORD maketh the earth empty, and maketh it waste, and turneth it upside down, and scattereth abroad the inhabitants thereof. {turneth...: Heb. perverteth the face thereof}'),
(18100,23,'Isaiah','OT',24,2,'And it shall be, as with the people, so with the priest; as with the servant, so with his master; as with the maid, so with her mistress; as with the buyer, so with the seller; as with the lender, so with the borrower; as with the taker of usury, so with the giver of usury to him. {priest: or, prince}'),
(18101,23,'Isaiah','OT',24,3,'The land shall be utterly emptied, and utterly spoiled: for the LORD hath spoken this word.'),
