(19137,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,15,'And I will cast you out of my sight, as I have cast out all your brethren, {even} the whole seed of Ephraim.'),
(19138,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,16,'Therefore pray not thou for this people, neither lift up cry nor prayer for them, neither make intercession to me: for I will not hear thee.'),
(19139,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,17,'Seest thou not what they do in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem?'),
(19140,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,18,'The children gather wood, and the fathers kindle the fire, and the women knead {their} dough, to make cakes to the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto other gods, that they may provoke me to anger. {queen...: or, frame, or, workmanship of heaven}'),
(19141,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,19,'Do they provoke me to anger? saith the LORD: {do they} not {provoke} themselves to the confusion of their own faces?'),
(19142,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,20,'Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, mine anger and my fury shall be poured out upon this place, upon man, and upon beast, and upon the trees of the field, and upon the fruit of the ground; and it shall burn, and shall not be quenched.'),
(19143,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,21,'Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Put your burnt offerings unto your sacrifices, and eat flesh.'),
(19144,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,22,'For I spake not unto your fathers, nor commanded them in the day that I brought them out of the land of Egypt, concerning burnt offerings or sacrifices: {concerning: Heb. concerning the matter of}'),
(19145,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,23,'But this thing commanded I them, saying, Obey my voice, and I will be your God, and ye shall be my people: and walk ye in all the ways that I have commanded you, that it may be well unto you.'),
(19146,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,24,'But they hearkened not, nor inclined their ear, but walked in the counsels {and} in the imagination of their evil heart, and went backward, and not forward. {imagination: or, stubbornness} {went: Heb. were}'),
(19147,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,25,'Since the day that your fathers came forth out of the land of Egypt unto this day I have even sent unto you all my servants the prophets, daily rising up early and sending {them}:'),
(19148,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,26,'Yet they hearkened not unto me, nor inclined their ear, but hardened their neck: they did worse than their fathers.'),
(19149,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,27,'Therefore thou shalt speak all these words unto them; but they will not hearken to thee: thou shalt also call unto them; but they will not answer thee.'),
(19150,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,28,'But thou shalt say unto them, This {is} a nation that obeyeth not the voice of the LORD their God, nor receiveth correction: truth is perished, and is cut off from their mouth. {correction: or, instruction}'),
(19151,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,29,'Cut off thine hair, {O Jerusalem}, and cast {it} away, and take up a lamentation on high places; for the LORD hath rejected and forsaken the generation of his wrath.'),
(19152,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,30,'For the children of Judah have done evil in my sight, saith the LORD: they have set their abominations in the house which is called by my name, to pollute it.'),
(19153,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,31,'And they have built the high places of Tophet, which {is} in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to burn their sons and their daughters in the fire; which I commanded {them} not, neither came it into my heart. {came...: Heb. came it upon my heart}'),
(19154,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,32,'Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that it shall no more be called Tophet, nor the valley of the son of Hinnom, but the valley of slaughter: for they shall bury in Tophet, till there be no place.'),
(19155,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,33,'And the carcases of this people shall be meat for the fowls of the heaven, and for the beasts of the earth; and none shall fray {them} away.'),
(19156,24,'Jeremiah','OT',7,34,'Then will I cause to cease from the cities of Judah, and from the streets of Jerusalem, the voice of mirth, and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom, and the voice of the bride: for the land shall be desolate.'),
(19157,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,1,'At that time, saith the LORD, they shall bring out the bones of the kings of Judah, and the bones of his princes, and the bones of the priests, and the bones of the prophets, and the bones of the inhabitants of Jerusalem, out of their graves:'),
(19158,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,2,'And they shall spread them before the sun, and the moon, and all the host of heaven, whom they have loved, and whom they have served, and after whom they have walked, and whom they have sought, and whom they have worshipped: they shall not be gathered, nor be buried; they shall be for dung upon the face of the earth.'),
(19159,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,3,'And death shall be chosen rather than life by all the residue of them that remain of this evil family, which remain in all the places whither I have driven them, saith the LORD of hosts.'),
(19160,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,4,'Moreover thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the LORD; Shall they fall, and not arise? shall he turn away, and not return?'),
(19161,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,5,'Why {then} is this people of Jerusalem slidden back by a perpetual backsliding? they hold fast deceit, they refuse to return.'),
(19162,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,6,'I hearkened and heard, {but} they spake not aright: no man repented him of his wickedness, saying, What have I done? every one turned to his course, as the horse rusheth into the battle.'),
(19163,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,7,'Yea, the stork in the heaven knoweth her appointed times; and the turtle and the crane and the swallow observe the time of their coming; but my people know not the judgment of the LORD.'),
(19164,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,8,'How do ye say, We {are} wise, and the law of the LORD {is} with us? Lo, certainly in vain made he {it}; the pen of the scribes {is} in vain. {in vain made...: or, the false pen of the scribes worketh for falsehood}'),
(19165,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,9,'The wise {men} are ashamed, they are dismayed and taken: lo, they have rejected the word of the LORD; and what wisdom {is} in them? {The wise...: or, Have they been ashamed, etc} {what...: Heb. the wisdom of what thing}'),
(19166,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,10,'Therefore will I give their wives unto others, {and} their fields to them that shall inherit {them}: for every one from the least even unto the greatest is given to covetousness, from the prophet even unto the priest every one dealeth falsely.'),
(19167,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,11,'For they have healed the hurt of the daughter of my people slightly, saying, Peace, peace; when {there is} no peace.'),
(19168,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,12,'Were they ashamed when they had committed abomination? nay, they were not at all ashamed, neither could they blush: therefore shall they fall among them that fall: in the time of their visitation they shall be cast down, saith the LORD. {I will...: or, In gathering I will consume}'),
(19169,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,13,'I will surely consume them, saith the LORD: {there shall be} no grapes on the vine, nor figs on the fig tree, and the leaf shall fade; and {the things that} I have given them shall pass away from them.'),
(19170,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,14,'Why do we sit still? assemble yourselves, and let us enter into the defenced cities, and let us be silent there: for the LORD our God hath put us to silence, and given us water of gall to drink, because we have sinned against the LORD. {gall: or, poison}'),
(19171,24,'Jeremiah','OT',8,15,'We looked for peace, but no good {came; and} for a time of health, and behold trouble!'),
