(19197,24,'Jeremiah','OT',9,19,'For a voice of wailing is heard out of Zion, How are we spoiled! we are greatly confounded, because we have forsaken the land, because our dwellings have cast {us} out.'),
(19198,24,'Jeremiah','OT',9,20,'Yet hear the word of the LORD, O ye women, and let your ear receive the word of his mouth, and teach your daughters wailing, and every one her neighbour lamentation.'),
(19199,24,'Jeremiah','OT',9,21,'For death is come up into our windows, {and} is entered into our palaces, to cut off the children from without, {and} the young men from the streets.'),
