(19207,24,'Jeremiah','OT',10,3,'For the customs of the people {are} vain: for {one} cutteth a tree out of the forest, the work of the hands of the workman, with the axe. {customs...: Heb. statutes, or, ordinances are vanity}'),
(19208,24,'Jeremiah','OT',10,4,'They deck it with silver and with gold; they fasten it with nails and with hammers, that it move not.'),
(19209,24,'Jeremiah','OT',10,5,'They {are} upright as the palm tree, but speak not: they must needs be borne, because they cannot go. Be not afraid of them; for they cannot do evil, neither also {is it} in them to do good.'),
