(23506,40,'Matthew','NT',12,15,'But when Jesus knew {it}, he withdrew himself from thence: and great multitudes followed him, and he healed them all;'),
(23507,40,'Matthew','NT',12,16,'And charged them that they should not make him known:'),
(23508,40,'Matthew','NT',12,17,'That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying,'),
(23509,40,'Matthew','NT',12,18,'Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him, and he shall shew judgment to the Gentiles.'),
(23510,40,'Matthew','NT',12,19,'He shall not strive, nor cry; neither shall any man hear his voice in the streets.'),
(23511,40,'Matthew','NT',12,20,'A bruised reed shall he not break, and smoking flax shall he not quench, till he send forth judgment unto victory.'),
(23512,40,'Matthew','NT',12,21,'And in his name shall the Gentiles trust.'),
(23513,40,'Matthew','NT',12,22,'Then was brought unto him one possessed with a devil, blind, and dumb: and he healed him, insomuch that the blind and dumb both spake and saw.'),
(23514,40,'Matthew','NT',12,23,'And all the people were amazed, and said, Is not this the son of David?'),
(23515,40,'Matthew','NT',12,24,'But when the Pharisees heard {it}, they said, This {fellow} doth not cast out devils, but by Beelzebub the prince of the devils. {Beelzebub: Gr. Beelzebul}'),
(23516,40,'Matthew','NT',12,25,'And Jesus knew their thoughts, and said unto them, Every kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation; and every city or house divided against itself shall not stand:'),
(23517,40,'Matthew','NT',12,26,'And if Satan cast out Satan, he is divided against himself; how shall then his kingdom stand?'),
(23518,40,'Matthew','NT',12,27,'And if I by Beelzebub cast out devils, by whom do your children cast {them} out? therefore they shall be your judges.'),
(23519,40,'Matthew','NT',12,28,'But if I cast out devils by the Spirit of God, then the kingdom of God is come unto you.'),
(23520,40,'Matthew','NT',12,29,'Or else how can one enter into a strong man\'s house, and spoil his goods, except he first bind the strong man? and then he will spoil his house.'),
(23521,40,'Matthew','NT',12,30,'He that is not with me is against me; and he that gathereth not with me scattereth abroad.'),
(23522,40,'Matthew','NT',12,31,'Wherefore I say unto you, All manner of sin and blasphemy shall be forgiven unto men: but the blasphemy {against} the {Holy} Ghost shall not be forgiven unto men.'),
(23523,40,'Matthew','NT',12,32,'And whosoever speaketh a word against the Son of man, it shall be forgiven him: but whosoever speaketh against the Holy Ghost, it shall not be forgiven him, neither in this world, neither in the {world} to come.'),
(23524,40,'Matthew','NT',12,33,'Either make the tree good, and his fruit good; or else make the tree corrupt, and his fruit corrupt: for the tree is known by {his} fruit.'),
(23525,40,'Matthew','NT',12,34,'O generation of vipers, how can ye, being evil, speak good things? for out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh.'),
(23526,40,'Matthew','NT',12,35,'A good man out of the good treasure of the heart bringeth forth good things: and an evil man out of the evil treasure bringeth forth evil things.'),
(23527,40,'Matthew','NT',12,36,'But I say unto you, That every idle word that men shall speak, they shall give account thereof in the day of judgment.'),
(23528,40,'Matthew','NT',12,37,'For by thy words thou shalt be justified, and by thy words thou shalt be condemned.'),
(23529,40,'Matthew','NT',12,38,'Then certain of the scribes and of the Pharisees answered, saying, Master, we would see a sign from thee.'),
(23530,40,'Matthew','NT',12,39,'But he answered and said unto them, An evil and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be given to it, but the sign of the prophet Jonas:'),
(23531,40,'Matthew','NT',12,40,'For as Jonas was three days and three nights in the whale\'s belly; so shall the Son of man be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth.'),
(23532,40,'Matthew','NT',12,41,'The men of Nineveh shall rise in judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: because they repented at the preaching of Jonas; and, behold, a greater than Jonas {is} here.'),
(23533,40,'Matthew','NT',12,42,'The queen of the south shall rise up in the judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: for she came from the uttermost parts of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and, behold, a greater than Solomon {is} here.'),
(23534,40,'Matthew','NT',12,43,'When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through dry places, seeking rest, and findeth none.'),
(23535,40,'Matthew','NT',12,44,'Then he saith, I will return into my house from whence I came out; and when he is come, he findeth {it} empty, swept, and garnished.'),
(23536,40,'Matthew','NT',12,45,'Then goeth he, and taketh with himself seven other spirits more wicked than himself, and they enter in and dwell there: and the last {state} of that man is worse than the first. Even so shall it be also unto this wicked generation.'),
(23537,40,'Matthew','NT',12,46,'While he yet talked to the people, behold, {his} mother and his brethren stood without, desiring to speak with him.'),
(23538,40,'Matthew','NT',12,47,'Then one said unto him, Behold, thy mother and thy brethren stand without, desiring to speak with thee.'),
(23539,40,'Matthew','NT',12,48,'But he answered and said unto him that told him, Who is my mother? and who are my brethren?'),
(23540,40,'Matthew','NT',12,49,'And he stretched forth his hand toward his disciples, and said, Behold my mother and my brethren!'),
(23541,40,'Matthew','NT',12,50,'For whosoever shall do the will of my Father which is in heaven, the same is my brother, and sister, and mother.'),
(23542,40,'Matthew','NT',13,1,'The same day went Jesus out of the house, and sat by the sea side.'),
(23543,40,'Matthew','NT',13,2,'And great multitudes were gathered together unto him, so that he went into a ship, and sat; and the whole multitude stood on the shore.'),
(23544,40,'Matthew','NT',13,3,'And he spake many things unto them in parables, saying, Behold, a sower went forth to sow;'),
(23545,40,'Matthew','NT',13,4,'And when he sowed, some {seeds} fell by the way side, and the fowls came and devoured them up:'),
(23546,40,'Matthew','NT',13,5,'Some fell upon stony places, where they had not much earth: and forthwith they sprung up, because they had no deepness of earth:'),
(23547,40,'Matthew','NT',13,6,'And when the sun was up, they were scorched; and because they had no root, they withered away.'),
(23548,40,'Matthew','NT',13,7,'And some fell among thorns; and the thorns sprung up, and choked them:'),
(23549,40,'Matthew','NT',13,8,'But other fell into good ground, and brought forth fruit, some an hundredfold, some sixtyfold, some thirtyfold.'),
(23550,40,'Matthew','NT',13,9,'Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.'),
(23551,40,'Matthew','NT',13,10,'And the disciples came, and said unto him, Why speakest thou unto them in parables?'),
(23552,40,'Matthew','NT',13,11,'He answered and said unto them, Because it is given unto you to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven, but to them it is not given.'),
(23553,40,'Matthew','NT',13,12,'For whosoever hath, to him shall be given, and he shall have more abundance: but whosoever hath not, from him shall be taken away even that he hath.'),
(23554,40,'Matthew','NT',13,13,'Therefore speak I to them in parables: because they seeing see not; and hearing they hear not, neither do they understand.'),
(23555,40,'Matthew','NT',13,14,'And in them is fulfilled the prophecy of Esaias, which saith, By hearing ye shall hear, and shall not understand; and seeing ye shall see, and shall not perceive:'),
(23556,40,'Matthew','NT',13,15,'For this people\'s heart is waxed gross, and {their} ears are dull of hearing, and their eyes they have closed; lest at any time they should see with {their} eyes, and hear with {their} ears, and should understand with {their} heart, and should be converted, and I should heal them.'),
(23557,40,'Matthew','NT',13,16,'But blessed {are} your eyes, for they see: and your ears, for they hear.'),
(23558,40,'Matthew','NT',13,17,'For verily I say unto you, That many prophets and righteous {men} have desired to see {those things} which ye see, and have not seen {them}; and to hear {those things} which ye hear, and have not heard {them}.'),
(23559,40,'Matthew','NT',13,18,'Hear ye therefore the parable of the sower.'),
(23560,40,'Matthew','NT',13,19,'When any one heareth the word of the kingdom, and understandeth {it} not, then cometh the wicked {one}, and catcheth away that which was sown in his heart. This is he which received seed by the way side.'),
(23561,40,'Matthew','NT',13,20,'But he that received the seed into stony places, the same is he that heareth the word, and anon with joy receiveth it;'),
(23562,40,'Matthew','NT',13,21,'Yet hath he not root in himself, but dureth for a while: for when tribulation or persecution ariseth because of the word, by and by he is offended. {offended: he relapseth, or, falleth into sin}'),
(23563,40,'Matthew','NT',13,22,'He also that received seed among the thorns is he that heareth the word; and the care of this world, and the deceitfulness of riches, choke the word, and he becometh unfruitful.'),
(23564,40,'Matthew','NT',13,23,'But he that received seed into the good ground is he that heareth the word, and understandeth {it}; which also beareth fruit, and bringeth forth, some an hundredfold, some sixty, some thirty.'),
(23565,40,'Matthew','NT',13,24,'Another parable put he forth unto them, saying, The kingdom of heaven is likened unto a man which sowed good seed in his field:'),
(23566,40,'Matthew','NT',13,25,'But while men slept, his enemy came and sowed tares among the wheat, and went his way.'),
(23567,40,'Matthew','NT',13,26,'But when the blade was sprung up, and brought forth fruit, then appeared the tares also.'),
(23568,40,'Matthew','NT',13,27,'So the servants of the householder came and said unto him, Sir, didst not thou sow good seed in thy field? from whence then hath it tares?'),
(23569,40,'Matthew','NT',13,28,'He said unto them, An enemy hath done this. The servants said unto him, Wilt thou then that we go and gather them up?'),
(23570,40,'Matthew','NT',13,29,'But he said, Nay; lest while ye gather up the tares, ye root up also the wheat with them.'),
(23571,40,'Matthew','NT',13,30,'Let both grow together until the harvest: and in the time of harvest I will say to the reapers, Gather ye together first the tares, and bind them in bundles to burn them: but gather the wheat into my barn.'),
(23572,40,'Matthew','NT',13,31,'Another parable put he forth unto them, saying, The kingdom of heaven is like to a grain of mustard seed, which a man took, and sowed in his field:'),
(23573,40,'Matthew','NT',13,32,'Which indeed is the least of all seeds: but when it is grown, it is the greatest among herbs, and becometh a tree, so that the birds of the air come and lodge in the branches thereof.'),
(23574,40,'Matthew','NT',13,33,'Another parable spake he unto them; The kingdom of heaven is like unto leaven, which a woman took, and hid in three measures of meal, till the whole was leavened. {measures: the word in the Greek is a measure containing about a peck and a half, wanting a little more than a pint}'),
(23575,40,'Matthew','NT',13,34,'All these things spake Jesus unto the multitude in parables; and without a parable spake he not unto them:'),
(23576,40,'Matthew','NT',13,35,'That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying, I will open my mouth in parables; I will utter things which have been kept secret from the foundation of the world.'),
(23577,40,'Matthew','NT',13,36,'Then Jesus sent the multitude away, and went into the house: and his disciples came unto him, saying, Declare unto us the parable of the tares of the field.'),
(23578,40,'Matthew','NT',13,37,'He answered and said unto them, He that soweth the good seed is the Son of man;'),
(23579,40,'Matthew','NT',13,38,'The field is the world; the good seed are the children of the kingdom; but the tares are the children of the wicked {one};'),
(23580,40,'Matthew','NT',13,39,'The enemy that sowed them is the devil; the harvest is the end of the world; and the reapers are the angels.'),
(23581,40,'Matthew','NT',13,40,'As therefore the tares are gathered and burned in the fire; so shall it be in the end of this world.'),
(23582,40,'Matthew','NT',13,41,'The Son of man shall send forth his angels, and they shall gather out of his kingdom all things that offend, and them which do iniquity; {things...: or, scandals}'),
(23583,40,'Matthew','NT',13,42,'And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.'),
(23584,40,'Matthew','NT',13,43,'Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.'),
(23585,40,'Matthew','NT',13,44,'Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto treasure hid in a field; the which when a man hath found, he hideth, and for joy thereof goeth and selleth all that he hath, and buyeth that field.'),
(23586,40,'Matthew','NT',13,45,'Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto a merchant man, seeking goodly pearls:'),
(23587,40,'Matthew','NT',13,46,'Who, when he had found one pearl of great price, went and sold all that he had, and bought it.'),
(23588,40,'Matthew','NT',13,47,'Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto a net, that was cast into the sea, and gathered of every kind:'),
(23589,40,'Matthew','NT',13,48,'Which, when it was full, they drew to shore, and sat down, and gathered the good into vessels, but cast the bad away.'),
(23590,40,'Matthew','NT',13,49,'So shall it be at the end of the world: the angels shall come forth, and sever the wicked from among the just,'),
(23591,40,'Matthew','NT',13,50,'And shall cast them into the furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.'),
(23592,40,'Matthew','NT',13,51,'Jesus saith unto them, Have ye understood all these things? They say unto him, Yea, Lord.'),
(23593,40,'Matthew','NT',13,52,'Then said he unto them, Therefore every scribe {which is} instructed unto the kingdom of heaven is like unto a man {that is} an householder, which bringeth forth out of his treasure {things} new and old.'),
(23594,40,'Matthew','NT',13,53,'And it came to pass, {that} when Jesus had finished these parables, he departed thence.'),
(23595,40,'Matthew','NT',13,54,'And when he was come into his own country, he taught them in their synagogue, insomuch that they were astonished, and said, Whence hath this {man} this wisdom, and {these} mighty works?'),
(23596,40,'Matthew','NT',13,55,'Is not this the carpenter\'s son? is not his mother called Mary? and his brethren, James, and Joses, and Simon, and Judas?'),
(23597,40,'Matthew','NT',13,56,'And his sisters, are they not all with us? Whence then hath this {man} all these things?'),
(23598,40,'Matthew','NT',13,57,'And they were offended in him. But Jesus said unto them, A prophet is not without honour, save in his own country, and in his own house.'),
(23599,40,'Matthew','NT',13,58,'And he did not many mighty works there because of their unbelief.'),
(23600,40,'Matthew','NT',14,1,'At that time Herod the tetrarch heard of the fame of Jesus, {tetrarch: or, governor over four provinces}'),
(23601,40,'Matthew','NT',14,2,'And said unto his servants, This is John the Baptist; he is risen from the dead; and therefore mighty works do shew forth themselves in him. {do...: or, are wrought by him}'),
(23602,40,'Matthew','NT',14,3,'For Herod had laid hold on John, and bound him, and put {him} in prison for Herodias\' sake, his brother Philip\'s wife.'),
(23603,40,'Matthew','NT',14,4,'For John said unto him, It is not lawful for thee to have her.'),
(23604,40,'Matthew','NT',14,5,'And when he would have put him to death, he feared the multitude, because they counted him as a prophet.'),
(23605,40,'Matthew','NT',14,6,'But when Herod\'s birthday was kept, the daughter of Herodias danced before them, and pleased Herod. {before...: Gr. in the midst}'),
(23606,40,'Matthew','NT',14,7,'Whereupon he promised with an oath to give her whatsoever she would ask.'),
(23607,40,'Matthew','NT',14,8,'And she, being before instructed of her mother, said, Give me here John Baptist\'s head in a charger.'),
(23608,40,'Matthew','NT',14,9,'And the king was sorry: nevertheless for the oath\'s sake, and them which sat with him at meat, he commanded {it} to be given {her}.'),
(23609,40,'Matthew','NT',14,10,'And he sent, and beheaded John in the prison.'),
(23610,40,'Matthew','NT',14,11,'And his head was brought in a charger, and given to the damsel: and she brought {it} to her mother.'),
(23611,40,'Matthew','NT',14,12,'And his disciples came, and took up the body, and buried it, and went and told Jesus.'),
(23612,40,'Matthew','NT',14,13,'When Jesus heard {of it}, he departed thence by ship into a desert place apart: and when the people had heard {thereof}, they followed him on foot out of the cities.'),
(23613,40,'Matthew','NT',14,14,'And Jesus went forth, and saw a great multitude, and was moved with compassion toward them, and he healed their sick.'),
(23614,40,'Matthew','NT',14,15,'And when it was evening, his disciples came to him, saying, This is a desert place, and the time is now past; send the multitude away, that they may go into the villages, and buy themselves victuals.'),
(23615,40,'Matthew','NT',14,16,'But Jesus said unto them, They need not depart; give ye them to eat.'),
(23616,40,'Matthew','NT',14,17,'And they say unto him, We have here but five loaves, and two fishes.'),
(23617,40,'Matthew','NT',14,18,'He said, Bring them hither to me.'),
(23618,40,'Matthew','NT',14,19,'And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the grass, and took the five loaves, and the two fishes, and looking up to heaven, he blessed, and brake, and gave the loaves to {his} disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.'),
(23619,40,'Matthew','NT',14,20,'And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the fragments that remained twelve baskets full.'),
(23620,40,'Matthew','NT',14,21,'And they that had eaten were about five thousand men, beside women and children.'),
(23621,40,'Matthew','NT',14,22,'And straightway Jesus constrained his disciples to get into a ship, and to go before him unto the other side, while he sent the multitudes away.'),
(23622,40,'Matthew','NT',14,23,'And when he had sent the multitudes away, he went up into a mountain apart to pray: and when the evening was come, he was there alone.'),
(23623,40,'Matthew','NT',14,24,'But the ship was now in the midst of the sea, tossed with waves: for the wind was contrary.'),
(23624,40,'Matthew','NT',14,25,'And in the fourth watch of the night Jesus went unto them, walking on the sea.'),
(23625,40,'Matthew','NT',14,26,'And when the disciples saw him walking on the sea, they were troubled, saying, It is a spirit; and they cried out for fear.'),
(23626,40,'Matthew','NT',14,27,'But straightway Jesus spake unto them, saying, Be of good cheer; it is I; be not afraid.'),
(23627,40,'Matthew','NT',14,28,'And Peter answered him and said, Lord, if it be thou, bid me come unto thee on the water.'),
(23628,40,'Matthew','NT',14,29,'And he said, Come. And when Peter was come down out of the ship, he walked on the water, to go to Jesus.'),
(23629,40,'Matthew','NT',14,30,'But when he saw the wind boisterous, he was afraid; and beginning to sink, he cried, saying, Lord, save me. {boisterous: or, strong}'),
(23630,40,'Matthew','NT',14,31,'And immediately Jesus stretched forth {his} hand, and caught him, and said unto him, O thou of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?'),
(23631,40,'Matthew','NT',14,32,'And when they were come into the ship, the wind ceased.'),
(23632,40,'Matthew','NT',14,33,'Then they that were in the ship came and worshipped him, saying, Of a truth thou art the Son of God.'),
(23633,40,'Matthew','NT',14,34,'And when they were gone over, they came into the land of Gennesaret.'),
(23634,40,'Matthew','NT',14,35,'And when the men of that place had knowledge of him, they sent out into all that country round about, and brought unto him all that were diseased;'),
(23635,40,'Matthew','NT',14,36,'And besought him that they might only touch the hem of his garment: and as many as touched were made perfectly whole.'),
(23636,40,'Matthew','NT',15,1,'Then came to Jesus scribes and Pharisees, which were of Jerusalem, saying,'),
(23637,40,'Matthew','NT',15,2,'Why do thy disciples transgress the tradition of the elders? for they wash not their hands when they eat bread.'),
(23638,40,'Matthew','NT',15,3,'But he answered and said unto them, Why do ye also transgress the commandment of God by your tradition?'),
(23639,40,'Matthew','NT',15,4,'For God commanded, saying, Honour thy father and mother: and, He that curseth father or mother, let him die the death.'),
(23640,40,'Matthew','NT',15,5,'But ye say, Whosoever shall say to {his} father or {his} mother, {It is} a gift, by whatsoever thou mightest be profited by me;'),
(23641,40,'Matthew','NT',15,6,'And honour not his father or his mother, {he shall be free}. Thus have ye made the commandment of God of none effect by your tradition.'),
(23642,40,'Matthew','NT',15,7,'{Ye} hypocrites, well did Esaias prophesy of you, saying,'),
(23643,40,'Matthew','NT',15,8,'This people draweth nigh unto me with their mouth, and honoureth me with {their} lips; but their heart is far from me.'),
(23644,40,'Matthew','NT',15,9,'But in vain they do worship me, teaching {for} doctrines the commandments of men.'),
(23645,40,'Matthew','NT',15,10,'And he called the multitude, and said unto them, Hear, and understand:'),
(23646,40,'Matthew','NT',15,11,'Not that which goeth into the mouth defileth a man; but that which cometh out of the mouth, this defileth a man.'),
(23647,40,'Matthew','NT',15,12,'Then came his disciples, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the Pharisees were offended, after they heard this saying?'),
(23648,40,'Matthew','NT',15,13,'But he answered and said, Every plant, which my heavenly Father hath not planted, shall be rooted up.'),
(23649,40,'Matthew','NT',15,14,'Let them alone: they be blind leaders of the blind. And if the blind lead the blind, both shall fall into the ditch.'),
(23650,40,'Matthew','NT',15,15,'Then answered Peter and said unto him, Declare unto us this parable.'),
(23651,40,'Matthew','NT',15,16,'And Jesus said, Are ye also yet without understanding?'),
(23652,40,'Matthew','NT',15,17,'Do not ye yet understand, that whatsoever entereth in at the mouth goeth into the belly, and is cast out into the draught?'),
(23653,40,'Matthew','NT',15,18,'But those things which proceed out of the mouth come forth from the heart; and they defile the man.'),
(23654,40,'Matthew','NT',15,19,'For out of the heart proceed evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, fornications, thefts, false witness, blasphemies:'),
(23655,40,'Matthew','NT',15,20,'These are {the things} which defile a man: but to eat with unwashen hands defileth not a man.'),
(23656,40,'Matthew','NT',15,21,'Then Jesus went thence, and departed into the coasts of Tyre and Sidon.'),
(23657,40,'Matthew','NT',15,22,'And, behold, a woman of Canaan came out of the same coasts, and cried unto him, saying, Have mercy on me, O Lord, {thou} Son of David; my daughter is grievously vexed with a devil.'),
(23658,40,'Matthew','NT',15,23,'But he answered her not a word. And his disciples came and besought him, saying, Send her away; for she crieth after us.'),
(23659,40,'Matthew','NT',15,24,'But he answered and said, I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Israel.'),
(23660,40,'Matthew','NT',15,25,'Then came she and worshipped him, saying, Lord, help me.'),
(23661,40,'Matthew','NT',15,26,'But he answered and said, It is not meet to take the children\'s bread, and to cast {it} to dogs.'),
(23662,40,'Matthew','NT',15,27,'And she said, Truth, Lord: yet the dogs eat of the crumbs which fall from their masters\' table.'),
(23663,40,'Matthew','NT',15,28,'Then Jesus answered and said unto her, O woman, great {is} thy faith: be it unto thee even as thou wilt. And her daughter was made whole from that very hour.'),
(23664,40,'Matthew','NT',15,29,'And Jesus departed from thence, and came nigh unto the sea of Galilee; and went up into a mountain, and sat down there.'),
(23665,40,'Matthew','NT',15,30,'And great multitudes came unto him, having with them {those that were} lame, blind, dumb, maimed, and many others, and cast them down at Jesus\' feet; and he healed them:'),
(23666,40,'Matthew','NT',15,31,'Insomuch that the multitude wondered, when they saw the dumb to speak, the maimed to be whole, the lame to walk, and the blind to see: and they glorified the God of Israel.'),
(23667,40,'Matthew','NT',15,32,'Then Jesus called his disciples {unto him}, and said, I have compassion on the multitude, because they continue with me now three days, and have nothing to eat: and I will not send them away fasting, lest they faint in the way.'),
(23668,40,'Matthew','NT',15,33,'And his disciples say unto him, Whence should we have so much bread in the wilderness, as to fill so great a multitude?'),
(23669,40,'Matthew','NT',15,34,'And Jesus saith unto them, How many loaves have ye? And they said, Seven, and a few little fishes.'),
(23670,40,'Matthew','NT',15,35,'And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the ground.'),
(23671,40,'Matthew','NT',15,36,'And he took the seven loaves and the fishes, and gave thanks, and brake {them}, and gave to his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.'),
(23672,40,'Matthew','NT',15,37,'And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken {meat} that was left seven baskets full.'),
(23673,40,'Matthew','NT',15,38,'And they that did eat were four thousand men, beside women and children.'),
(23674,40,'Matthew','NT',15,39,'And he sent away the multitude, and took ship, and came into the coasts of Magdala.'),
(23675,40,'Matthew','NT',16,1,'The Pharisees also with the Sadducees came, and tempting desired him that he would shew them a sign from heaven.'),
(23676,40,'Matthew','NT',16,2,'He answered and said unto them, When it is evening, ye say, {It will be} fair weather: for the sky is red.'),
(23677,40,'Matthew','NT',16,3,'And in the morning, {It will be} foul weather to day: for the sky is red and lowring. O {ye} hypocrites, ye can discern the face of the sky; but can ye not {discern} the signs of the times?'),
(23678,40,'Matthew','NT',16,4,'A wicked and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be given unto it, but the sign of the prophet Jonas. And he left them, and departed.'),
(23679,40,'Matthew','NT',16,5,'And when his disciples were come to the other side, they had forgotten to take bread.'),
(23680,40,'Matthew','NT',16,6,'Then Jesus said unto them, Take heed and beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees.'),
(23681,40,'Matthew','NT',16,7,'And they reasoned among themselves, saying, {It is} because we have taken no bread.'),
(23682,40,'Matthew','NT',16,8,'{Which} when Jesus perceived, he said unto them, O ye of little faith, why reason ye among yourselves, because ye have brought no bread?'),
