(23698,40,'Matthew','NT',16,24,'Then said Jesus unto his disciples, If any {man} will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me.'),
(23699,40,'Matthew','NT',16,25,'For whosoever will save his life shall lose it: and whosoever will lose his life for my sake shall find it.'),
(23700,40,'Matthew','NT',16,26,'For what is a man profited, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul? or what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?'),
(23701,40,'Matthew','NT',16,27,'For the Son of man shall come in the glory of his Father with his angels; and then he shall reward every man according to his works.'),
(23702,40,'Matthew','NT',16,28,'Verily I say unto you, There be some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till they see the Son of man coming in his kingdom.'),
(23703,40,'Matthew','NT',17,1,'And after six days Jesus taketh Peter, James, and John his brother, and bringeth them up into an high mountain apart,'),
