(23757,40,'Matthew','NT',18,28,'But the same servant went out, and found one of his fellowservants, which owed him an hundred pence: and he laid hands on him, and took {him} by the throat, saying, Pay me that thou owest. {pence: the Roman penny is the eighth part of an ounce, which after five shillings the ounce is seven pence halfpenny; about fourteen cents}'),
(23758,40,'Matthew','NT',18,29,'And his fellowservant fell down at his feet, and besought him, saying, Have patience with me, and I will pay thee all.'),
