(27028,44,'Acts','NT',4,9,'If we this day be examined of the good deed done to the impotent man, by what means he is made whole;'),
(27029,44,'Acts','NT',4,10,'Be it known unto you all, and to all the people of Israel, that by the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom ye crucified, whom God raised from the dead, {even} by him doth this man stand here before you whole.'),
(27030,44,'Acts','NT',4,11,'This is the stone which was set at nought of you builders, which is become the head of the corner.'),
(27031,44,'Acts','NT',4,12,'Neither is there salvation in any other: for there is none other name under heaven given among men, whereby we must be saved.'),
(27032,44,'Acts','NT',4,13,'Now when they saw the boldness of Peter and John, and perceived that they were unlearned and ignorant men, they marvelled; and they took knowledge of them, that they had been with Jesus.'),
(27033,44,'Acts','NT',4,14,'And beholding the man which was healed standing with them, they could say nothing against it.'),
(27034,44,'Acts','NT',4,15,'But when they had commanded them to go aside out of the council, they conferred among themselves,'),
(27035,44,'Acts','NT',4,16,'Saying, What shall we do to these men? for that indeed a notable miracle hath been done by them {is} manifest to all them that dwell in Jerusalem; and we cannot deny {it}.'),
(27036,44,'Acts','NT',4,17,'But that it spread no further among the people, let us straitly threaten them, that they speak henceforth to no man in this name.'),
(27037,44,'Acts','NT',4,18,'And they called them, and commanded them not to speak at all nor teach in the name of Jesus.'),
(27038,44,'Acts','NT',4,19,'But Peter and John answered and said unto them, Whether it be right in the sight of God to hearken unto you more than unto God, judge ye.'),
(27039,44,'Acts','NT',4,20,'For we cannot but speak the things which we have seen and heard.'),
(27040,44,'Acts','NT',4,21,'So when they had further threatened them, they let them go, finding nothing how they might punish them, because of the people: for all {men} glorified God for that which was done.'),
(27041,44,'Acts','NT',4,22,'For the man was above forty years old, on whom this miracle of healing was shewed.'),
(27042,44,'Acts','NT',4,23,'And being let go, they went to their own company, and reported all that the chief priests and elders had said unto them.'),
