(27683,44,'Acts','NT',21,22,'What is it therefore? the multitude must needs come together: for they will hear that thou art come.'),
(27684,44,'Acts','NT',21,23,'Do therefore this that we say to thee: We have four men which have a vow on them;'),
(27685,44,'Acts','NT',21,24,'Them take, and purify thyself with them, and be at charges with them, that they may shave {their} heads: and all may know that those things, whereof they were informed concerning thee, are nothing; but {that} thou thyself also walkest orderly, and keepest the law.'),
(27686,44,'Acts','NT',21,25,'As touching the Gentiles which believe, we have written {and} concluded that they observe no such thing, save only that they keep themselves from {things} offered to idols, and from blood, and from strangled, and from fornication.'),
(27687,44,'Acts','NT',21,26,'Then Paul took the men, and the next day purifying himself with them entered into the temple, to signify the accomplishment of the days of purification, until that an offering should be offered for every one of them.'),
(27688,44,'Acts','NT',21,27,'And when the seven days were almost ended, the Jews which were of Asia, when they saw him in the temple, stirred up all the people, and laid hands on him,'),
(27689,44,'Acts','NT',21,28,'Crying out, Men of Israel, help: This is the man, that teacheth all {men} every where against the people, and the law, and this place: and further brought Greeks also into the temple, and hath polluted this holy place.'),
