(27731,44,'Acts','NT',22,30,'On the morrow, because he would have known the certainty wherefore he was accused of the Jews, he loosed him from {his} bands, and commanded the chief priests and all their council to appear, and brought Paul down, and set him before them.'),
(27732,44,'Acts','NT',23,1,'And Paul, earnestly beholding the council, said, Men {and} brethren, I have lived in all good conscience before God until this day.'),
