(27867,44,'Acts','NT',27,15,'And when the ship was caught, and could not bear up into the wind, we let {her} drive.'),
(27868,44,'Acts','NT',27,16,'And running under a certain island which is called Clauda, we had much work to come by the boat:'),
(27869,44,'Acts','NT',27,17,'Which when they had taken up, they used helps, undergirding the ship; and, fearing lest they should fall into the quicksands, strake sail, and so were driven.'),
(27870,44,'Acts','NT',27,18,'And we being exceedingly tossed with a tempest, the next {day} they lightened the ship;'),
(27871,44,'Acts','NT',27,19,'And the third {day} we cast out with our own hands the tackling of the ship.'),
(27872,44,'Acts','NT',27,20,'And when neither sun nor stars in many days appeared, and no small tempest lay on {us}, all hope that we should be saved was then taken away.'),
(27873,44,'Acts','NT',27,21,'But after long abstinence Paul stood forth in the midst of them, and said, Sirs, ye should have hearkened unto me, and not have loosed from Crete, and to have gained this harm and loss.'),
(27874,44,'Acts','NT',27,22,'And now I exhort you to be of good cheer: for there shall be no loss of {any man\'s} life among you, but of the ship.'),
