(27892,44,'Acts','NT',27,40,'And when they had taken up the anchors, they committed {themselves} unto the sea, and loosed the rudder bands, and hoised up the mainsail to the wind, and made toward shore. {taken...: or, cut the anchors, they left them in the sea}'),
(27893,44,'Acts','NT',27,41,'And falling into a place where two seas met, they ran the ship aground; and the forepart stuck fast, and remained unmoveable, but the hinder part was broken with the violence of the waves.'),
(27894,44,'Acts','NT',27,42,'And the soldiers\' counsel was to kill the prisoners, lest any of them should swim out, and escape.'),
