(28281,45,'Romans','NT',14,4,'Who art thou that judgest another man\'s servant? to his own master he standeth or falleth. Yea, he shall be holden up: for God is able to make him stand.'),
(28282,45,'Romans','NT',14,5,'One man esteemeth one day above another: another esteemeth every day {alike}. Let every man be fully persuaded in his own mind. {fully persuaded: or, fully assured}'),
(28283,45,'Romans','NT',14,6,'He that regardeth the day, regardeth {it} unto the Lord; and he that regardeth not the day, to the Lord he doth not regard {it}. He that eateth, eateth to the Lord, for he giveth God thanks; and he that eateth not, to the Lord he eateth not, and giveth God thanks. {regardeth: or, observeth}'),
(28284,45,'Romans','NT',14,7,'For none of us liveth to himself, and no man dieth to himself.'),
(28285,45,'Romans','NT',14,8,'For whether we live, we live unto the Lord; and whether we die, we die unto the Lord: whether we live therefore, or die, we are the Lord\'s.'),
(28286,45,'Romans','NT',14,9,'For to this end Christ both died, and rose, and revived, that he might be Lord both of the dead and living.'),
(28287,45,'Romans','NT',14,10,'But why dost thou judge thy brother? or why dost thou set at nought thy brother? for we shall all stand before the judgment seat of Christ.'),
(28288,45,'Romans','NT',14,11,'For it is written, {As} I live, saith the Lord, every knee shall bow to me, and every tongue shall confess to God.'),
(28289,45,'Romans','NT',14,12,'So then every one of us shall give account of himself to God.'),
(28290,45,'Romans','NT',14,13,'Let us not therefore judge one another any more: but judge this rather, that no man put a stumblingblock or an occasion to fall in {his} brother\'s way.'),
(28291,45,'Romans','NT',14,14,'I know, and am persuaded by the Lord Jesus, that {there is} nothing unclean of itself: but to him that esteemeth any thing to be unclean, to him {it is} unclean. {unclean: Gr. common}'),
(28292,45,'Romans','NT',14,15,'But if thy brother be grieved with {thy} meat, now walkest thou not charitably. Destroy not him with thy meat, for whom Christ died. {charitably: Gr. according to charity}'),
(28293,45,'Romans','NT',14,16,'Let not then your good be evil spoken of:'),
(28294,45,'Romans','NT',14,17,'For the kingdom of God is not meat and drink; but righteousness, and peace, and joy in the Holy Ghost.'),
(28295,45,'Romans','NT',14,18,'For he that in these things serveth Christ {is} acceptable to God, and approved of men.'),
(28296,45,'Romans','NT',14,19,'Let us therefore follow after the things which make for peace, and things wherewith one may edify another.'),
(28297,45,'Romans','NT',14,20,'For meat destroy not the work of God. All things indeed {are} pure; but {it is} evil for that man who eateth with offence.'),
(28298,45,'Romans','NT',14,21,'{It is} good neither to eat flesh, nor to drink wine, nor {any thing} whereby thy brother stumbleth, or is offended, or is made weak.'),
(28299,45,'Romans','NT',14,22,'Hast thou faith? have {it} to thyself before God. Happy {is} he that condemneth not himself in that thing which he alloweth.'),
(28300,45,'Romans','NT',14,23,'And he that doubteth is damned if he eat, because {he eateth} not of faith: for whatsoever {is} not of faith is sin. {doubteth: or, discerneth and putteth a difference between meats} {damned: or, condemned, or liable to punishment}'),
(28301,45,'Romans','NT',15,1,'We then that are strong ought to bear the infirmities of the weak, and not to please ourselves.'),
(28302,45,'Romans','NT',15,2,'Let every one of us please {his} neighbour for {his} good to edification.'),
(28303,45,'Romans','NT',15,3,'For even Christ pleased not himself; but, as it is written, The reproaches of them that reproached thee fell on me.'),
(28304,45,'Romans','NT',15,4,'For whatsoever things were written aforetime were written for our learning, that we through patience and comfort of the scriptures might have hope.'),
(28305,45,'Romans','NT',15,5,'Now the God of patience and consolation grant you to be likeminded one toward another according to Christ Jesus: {according to: or, after the example of}'),
(28306,45,'Romans','NT',15,6,'That ye may with one mind {and} one mouth glorify God, even the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(28307,45,'Romans','NT',15,7,'Wherefore receive ye one another, as Christ also received us to the glory of God.'),
(28308,45,'Romans','NT',15,8,'Now I say that Jesus Christ was a minister of the circumcision for the truth of God, to confirm the promises {made} unto the fathers:'),
(28309,45,'Romans','NT',15,9,'And that the Gentiles might glorify God for {his} mercy; as it is written, For this cause I will confess to thee among the Gentiles, and sing unto thy name.'),
(28310,45,'Romans','NT',15,10,'And again he saith, Rejoice, ye Gentiles, with his people.'),
(28311,45,'Romans','NT',15,11,'And again, Praise the Lord, all ye Gentiles; and laud him, all ye people.'),
(28312,45,'Romans','NT',15,12,'And again, Esaias saith, There shall be a root of Jesse, and he that shall rise to reign over the Gentiles; in him shall the Gentiles trust.'),
(28313,45,'Romans','NT',15,13,'Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, through the power of the Holy Ghost.'),
(28314,45,'Romans','NT',15,14,'And I myself also am persuaded of you, my brethren, that ye also are full of goodness, filled with all knowledge, able also to admonish one another.'),
(28315,45,'Romans','NT',15,15,'Nevertheless, brethren, I have written the more boldly unto you in some sort, as putting you in mind, because of the grace that is given to me of God,'),
(28316,45,'Romans','NT',15,16,'That I should be the minister of Jesus Christ to the Gentiles, ministering the gospel of God, that the offering up of the Gentiles might be acceptable, being sanctified by the Holy Ghost. {offering up: or, sacrificing}'),
(28317,45,'Romans','NT',15,17,'I have therefore whereof I may glory through Jesus Christ in those things which pertain to God.'),
(28318,45,'Romans','NT',15,18,'For I will not dare to speak of any of those things which Christ hath not wrought by me, to make the Gentiles obedient, by word and deed,'),
(28319,45,'Romans','NT',15,19,'Through mighty signs and wonders, by the power of the Spirit of God; so that from Jerusalem, and round about unto Illyricum, I have fully preached the gospel of Christ.'),
(28320,45,'Romans','NT',15,20,'Yea, so have I strived to preach the gospel, not where Christ was named, lest I should build upon another man\'s foundation:'),
(28321,45,'Romans','NT',15,21,'But as it is written, To whom he was not spoken of, they shall see: and they that have not heard shall understand.'),
(28322,45,'Romans','NT',15,22,'For which cause also I have been much hindered from coming to you. {much: or, many ways, or oftentimes}'),
(28323,45,'Romans','NT',15,23,'But now having no more place in these parts, and having a great desire these many years to come unto you;'),
(28324,45,'Romans','NT',15,24,'Whensoever I take my journey into Spain, I will come to you: for I trust to see you in my journey, and to be brought on my way thitherward by you, if first I be somewhat filled with your {company}. {with...: Gr. with you}'),
(28325,45,'Romans','NT',15,25,'But now I go unto Jerusalem to minister unto the saints.'),
(28326,45,'Romans','NT',15,26,'For it hath pleased them of Macedonia and Achaia to make a certain contribution for the poor saints which are at Jerusalem.'),
(28327,45,'Romans','NT',15,27,'It hath pleased them verily; and their debtors they are. For if the Gentiles have been made partakers of their spiritual things, their duty is also to minister unto them in carnal things.'),
(28328,45,'Romans','NT',15,28,'When therefore I have performed this, and have sealed to them this fruit, I will come by you into Spain.'),
(28329,45,'Romans','NT',15,29,'And I am sure that, when I come unto you, I shall come in the fulness of the blessing of the gospel of Christ.'),
(28330,45,'Romans','NT',15,30,'Now I beseech you, brethren, for the Lord Jesus Christ\'s sake, and for the love of the Spirit, that ye strive together with me in {your} prayers to God for me;'),
(28331,45,'Romans','NT',15,31,'That I may be delivered from them that do not believe in Judaea; and that my service which {I have} for Jerusalem may be accepted of the saints; {do not...: or, are disobedient}'),
(28332,45,'Romans','NT',15,32,'That I may come unto you with joy by the will of God, and may with you be refreshed.'),
(28333,45,'Romans','NT',15,33,'Now the God of peace {be} with you all. Amen.'),
(28334,45,'Romans','NT',16,1,'I commend unto you Phebe our sister, which is a servant of the church which is at Cenchrea:'),
(28335,45,'Romans','NT',16,2,'That ye receive her in the Lord, as becometh saints, and that ye assist her in whatsoever business she hath need of you: for she hath been a succourer of many, and of myself also.'),
(28336,45,'Romans','NT',16,3,'Greet Priscilla and Aquila my helpers in Christ Jesus:'),
(28337,45,'Romans','NT',16,4,'Who have for my life laid down their own necks: unto whom not only I give thanks, but also all the churches of the Gentiles.'),
(28338,45,'Romans','NT',16,5,'Likewise {greet} the church that is in their house. Salute my wellbeloved Epaenetus, who is the firstfruits of Achaia unto Christ.'),
(28339,45,'Romans','NT',16,6,'Greet Mary, who bestowed much labour on us.'),
(28340,45,'Romans','NT',16,7,'Salute Andronicus and Junia, my kinsmen, and my fellowprisoners, who are of note among the apostles, who also were in Christ before me.'),
(28341,45,'Romans','NT',16,8,'Greet Amplias my beloved in the Lord.'),
(28342,45,'Romans','NT',16,9,'Salute Urbane, our helper in Christ, and Stachys my beloved.'),
(28343,45,'Romans','NT',16,10,'Salute Apelles approved in Christ. Salute them which are of Aristobulus\' {household}. {household: or, friends}'),
(28344,45,'Romans','NT',16,11,'Salute Herodion my kinsman. Greet them that be of the {household} of Narcissus, which are in the Lord. {household: or, friends}'),
(28345,45,'Romans','NT',16,12,'Salute Tryphena and Tryphosa, who labour in the Lord. Salute the beloved Persis, which laboured much in the Lord.'),
(28346,45,'Romans','NT',16,13,'Salute Rufus chosen in the Lord, and his mother and mine.'),
(28347,45,'Romans','NT',16,14,'Salute Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermas, Patrobas, Hermes, and the brethren which are with them.'),
(28348,45,'Romans','NT',16,15,'Salute Philologus, and Julia, Nereus, and his sister, and Olympas, and all the saints which are with them.'),
(28349,45,'Romans','NT',16,16,'Salute one another with an holy kiss. The churches of Christ salute you.'),
(28350,45,'Romans','NT',16,17,'Now I beseech you, brethren, mark them which cause divisions and offences contrary to the doctrine which ye have learned; and avoid them.'),
(28351,45,'Romans','NT',16,18,'For they that are such serve not our Lord Jesus Christ, but their own belly; and by good words and fair speeches deceive the hearts of the simple.'),
(28352,45,'Romans','NT',16,19,'For your obedience is come abroad unto all {men}. I am glad therefore on your behalf: but yet I would have you wise unto that which is good, and simple concerning evil. {simple: or, harmless}'),
(28353,45,'Romans','NT',16,20,'And the God of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ {be} with you. Amen. {bruise: or, tread}'),
(28354,45,'Romans','NT',16,21,'Timotheus my workfellow, and Lucius, and Jason, and Sosipater, my kinsmen, salute you.'),
(28355,45,'Romans','NT',16,22,'I Tertius, who wrote {this} epistle, salute you in the Lord.'),
(28356,45,'Romans','NT',16,23,'Gaius mine host, and of the whole church, saluteth you. Erastus the chamberlain of the city saluteth you, and Quartus a brother.'),
(28357,45,'Romans','NT',16,24,'The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ {be} with you all. Amen.'),
(28358,45,'Romans','NT',16,25,'Now to him that is of power to stablish you according to my gospel, and the preaching of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery, which was kept secret since the world began,'),
(28359,45,'Romans','NT',16,26,'But now is made manifest, and by the scriptures of the prophets, according to the commandment of the everlasting God, made known to all nations for the obedience of faith:'),
(28360,45,'Romans','NT',16,27,'To God only wise, {be} glory through Jesus Christ for ever. Amen. «{Written to the Romans from Corinthus, and sent} by Phebe servant of the church at Cenchrea.}»'),
(28361,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,1,'Paul, called {to be} an apostle of Jesus Christ through the will of God, and Sosthenes {our} brother,'),
(28362,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,2,'Unto the church of God which is at Corinth, to them that are sanctified in Christ Jesus, called {to be} saints, with all that in every place call upon the name of Jesus Christ our Lord, both theirs and ours:'),
(28363,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,3,'Grace {be} unto you, and peace, from God our Father, and {from} the Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(28364,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,4,'I thank my God always on your behalf, for the grace of God which is given you by Jesus Christ;'),
(28365,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,5,'That in every thing ye are enriched by him, in all utterance, and {in} all knowledge;'),
(28366,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,6,'Even as the testimony of Christ was confirmed in you:'),
(28367,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,7,'So that ye come behind in no gift; waiting for the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ: {coming: Gr. revelation}'),
(28368,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,8,'Who shall also confirm you unto the end, {that ye may be} blameless in the day of our Lord Jesus Christ.'),
(28369,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,9,'God {is} faithful, by whom ye were called unto the fellowship of his Son Jesus Christ our Lord.'),
(28370,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,10,'Now I beseech you, brethren, by the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that ye all speak the same thing, and {that} there be no divisions among you; but {that} ye be perfectly joined together in the same mind and in the same judgment. {divisions: Gr. schisms}'),
(28371,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,11,'For it hath been declared unto me of you, my brethren, by them {which are of the house} of Chloe, that there are contentions among you.'),
(28372,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,12,'Now this I say, that every one of you saith, I am of Paul; and I of Apollos; and I of Cephas; and I of Christ.'),
(28373,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,13,'Is Christ divided? was Paul crucified for you? or were ye baptized in the name of Paul?'),
(28374,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,14,'I thank God that I baptized none of you, but Crispus and Gaius;'),
(28375,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,15,'Lest any should say that I had baptized in mine own name.'),
(28376,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,16,'And I baptized also the household of Stephanas: besides, I know not whether I baptized any other.'),
(28377,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,17,'For Christ sent me not to baptize, but to preach the gospel: not with wisdom of words, lest the cross of Christ should be made of none effect. {words: or, speech}'),
(28378,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,18,'For the preaching of the cross is to them that perish foolishness; but unto us which are saved it is the power of God.'),
(28379,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,19,'For it is written, I will destroy the wisdom of the wise, and will bring to nothing the understanding of the prudent.'),
(28380,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,20,'Where {is} the wise? where {is} the scribe? where {is} the disputer of this world? hath not God made foolish the wisdom of this world?'),
(28381,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,21,'For after that in the wisdom of God the world by wisdom knew not God, it pleased God by the foolishness of preaching to save them that believe.'),
(28382,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,22,'For the Jews require a sign, and the Greeks seek after wisdom:'),
(28383,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,23,'But we preach Christ crucified, unto the Jews a stumblingblock, and unto the Greeks foolishness;'),
(28384,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,24,'But unto them which are called, both Jews and Greeks, Christ the power of God, and the wisdom of God.'),
(28385,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,25,'Because the foolishness of God is wiser than men; and the weakness of God is stronger than men.'),
(28386,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,26,'For ye see your calling, brethren, how that not many wise men after the flesh, not many mighty, not many noble, {are called}:'),
(28387,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,27,'But God hath chosen the foolish things of the world to confound the wise; and God hath chosen the weak things of the world to confound the things which are mighty;'),
(28388,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,28,'And base things of the world, and things which are despised, hath God chosen, {yea}, and things which are not, to bring to nought things that are:'),
(28389,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,29,'That no flesh should glory in his presence.'),
(28390,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,30,'But of him are ye in Christ Jesus, who of God is made unto us wisdom, and righteousness, and sanctification, and redemption:'),
(28391,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',1,31,'That, according as it is written, He that glorieth, let him glory in the Lord.'),
(28392,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,1,'And I, brethren, when I came to you, came not with excellency of speech or of wisdom, declaring unto you the testimony of God.'),
(28393,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,2,'For I determined not to know any thing among you, save Jesus Christ, and him crucified.'),
(28394,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,3,'And I was with you in weakness, and in fear, and in much trembling.'),
(28395,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,4,'And my speech and my preaching {was} not with enticing words of man\'s wisdom, but in demonstration of the Spirit and of power: {enticing: or, persuasible}'),
(28396,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,5,'That your faith should not stand in the wisdom of men, but in the power of God. {stand: Gr. be}'),
(28397,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,6,'Howbeit we speak wisdom among them that are perfect: yet not the wisdom of this world, nor of the princes of this world, that come to nought:'),
(28398,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,7,'But we speak the wisdom of God in a mystery, {even} the hidden {wisdom}, which God ordained before the world unto our glory:'),
(28399,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,8,'Which none of the princes of this world knew: for had they known {it}, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory.'),
(28400,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,9,'But as it is written, Eye hath not seen, nor ear heard, neither have entered into the heart of man, the things which God hath prepared for them that love him.'),
(28401,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,10,'But God hath revealed {them} unto us by his Spirit: for the Spirit searcheth all things, yea, the deep things of God.'),
(28402,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,11,'For what man knoweth the things of a man, save the spirit of man which is in him? even so the things of God knoweth no man, but the Spirit of God.'),
(28403,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,12,'Now we have received, not the spirit of the world, but the spirit which is of God; that we might know the things that are freely given to us of God.'),
(28404,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,13,'Which things also we speak, not in the words which man\'s wisdom teacheth, but which the Holy Ghost teacheth; comparing spiritual things with spiritual.'),
(28405,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,14,'But the natural man receiveth not the things of the Spirit of God: for they are foolishness unto him: neither can he know {them}, because they are spiritually discerned.'),
(28406,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,15,'But he that is spiritual judgeth all things, yet he himself is judged of no man. {judgeth: or, discerneth} {judged: or, discerned}'),
(28407,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',2,16,'For who hath known the mind of the Lord, that he may instruct him? But we have the mind of Christ. {may: Gr. shall}'),
(28408,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,1,'And I, brethren, could not speak unto you as unto spiritual, but as unto carnal, {even} as unto babes in Christ.'),
(28409,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,2,'I have fed you with milk, and not with meat: for hitherto ye were not able {to bear it}, neither yet now are ye able.'),
(28410,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,3,'For ye are yet carnal: for whereas {there is} among you envying, and strife, and divisions, are ye not carnal, and walk as men? {divisions: or, factions} {as men: Gr. according to man?}'),
(28411,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,4,'For while one saith, I am of Paul; and another, I {am} of Apollos; are ye not carnal?'),
(28412,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,5,'Who then is Paul, and who {is} Apollos, but ministers by whom ye believed, even as the Lord gave to every man?'),
(28413,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,6,'I have planted, Apollos watered; but God gave the increase.'),
(28414,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,7,'So then neither is he that planteth any thing, neither he that watereth; but God that giveth the increase.'),
(28415,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,8,'Now he that planteth and he that watereth are one: and every man shall receive his own reward according to his own labour.'),
(28416,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,9,'For we are labourers together with God: ye are God\'s husbandry, {ye are} God\'s building. {husbandry: or, tillage}'),
(28417,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,10,'According to the grace of God which is given unto me, as a wise masterbuilder, I have laid the foundation, and another buildeth thereon. But let every man take heed how he buildeth thereupon.'),
(28418,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,11,'For other foundation can no man lay than that is laid, which is Jesus Christ.'),
(28419,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,12,'Now if any man build upon this foundation gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, stubble;'),
(28420,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,13,'Every man\'s work shall be made manifest: for the day shall declare it, because it shall be revealed by fire; and the fire shall try every man\'s work of what sort it is. {it shall be: Gr. it is}'),
(28421,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,14,'If any man\'s work abide which he hath built thereupon, he shall receive a reward.'),
(28422,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,15,'If any man\'s work shall be burned, he shall suffer loss: but he himself shall be saved; yet so as by fire.'),
(28423,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,16,'Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and {that} the Spirit of God dwelleth in you?'),
(28424,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,17,'If any man defile the temple of God, him shall God destroy; for the temple of God is holy, which {temple} ye are. {defile: or, destroy}'),
(28425,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,18,'Let no man deceive himself. If any man among you seemeth to be wise in this world, let him become a fool, that he may be wise.'),
(28426,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,19,'For the wisdom of this world is foolishness with God. For it is written, He taketh the wise in their own craftiness.'),
(28427,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,20,'And again, The Lord knoweth the thoughts of the wise, that they are vain.'),
(28428,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,21,'Therefore let no man glory in men. For all things are yours;'),
(28429,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,22,'Whether Paul, or Apollos, or Cephas, or the world, or life, or death, or things present, or things to come; all are yours;'),
(28430,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',3,23,'And ye are Christ\'s; and Christ {is} God\'s.'),
(28431,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,1,'Let a man so account of us, as of the ministers of Christ, and stewards of the mysteries of God.'),
(28432,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,2,'Moreover it is required in stewards, that a man be found faithful.'),
(28433,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,3,'But with me it is a very small thing that I should be judged of you, or of man\'s judgment: yea, I judge not mine own self. {judgment: Gr. day}'),
(28434,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,4,'For I know nothing by myself; yet am I not hereby justified: but he that judgeth me is the Lord. {know: or, I am not conscious of any fault}'),
(28435,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,5,'Therefore judge nothing before the time, until the Lord come, who both will bring to light the hidden things of darkness, and will make manifest the counsels of the hearts: and then shall every man have praise of God.'),
(28436,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,6,'And these things, brethren, I have in a figure transferred to myself and {to} Apollos for your sakes; that ye might learn in us not to think {of men} above that which is written, that no one of you be puffed up for one against another.'),
(28437,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,7,'For who maketh thee to differ {from another}? and what hast thou that thou didst not receive? now if thou didst receive {it}, why dost thou glory, as if thou hadst not received {it}? {maketh...: Gr. distinguisheth thee}'),
(28438,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,8,'Now ye are full, now ye are rich, ye have reigned as kings without us: and I would to God ye did reign, that we also might reign with you.'),
(28439,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,9,'For I think that God hath set forth us the apostles last, as it were appointed to death: for we are made a spectacle unto the world, and to angels, and to men. {us...: or, us the last apostles, as} {spectacle: Gr. theatre}'),
(28440,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,10,'We {are} fools for Christ\'s sake, but ye {are} wise in Christ; we {are} weak, but ye {are} strong; ye {are} honourable, but we {are} despised.'),
(28441,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,11,'Even unto this present hour we both hunger, and thirst, and are naked, and are buffeted, and have no certain dwellingplace;'),
(28442,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,12,'And labour, working with our own hands: being reviled, we bless; being persecuted, we suffer it:'),
(28443,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,13,'Being defamed, we intreat: we are made as the filth of the world, {and are} the offscouring of all things unto this day.'),
(28444,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,14,'I write not these things to shame you, but as my beloved sons I warn {you}.'),
(28445,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,15,'For though ye have ten thousand instructors in Christ, yet {have ye} not many fathers: for in Christ Jesus I have begotten you through the gospel.'),
(28446,46,'1 Corinthians','NT',4,16,'Wherefore I beseech you, be ye followers of me.'),
