(28863,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,7,'But we have this treasure in earthen vessels, that the excellency of the power may be of God, and not of us.'),
(28864,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,8,'{We are} troubled on every side, yet not distressed; {we are} perplexed, but not in despair; {in despair: or, altogether without help, or, means}'),
(28865,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,9,'Persecuted, but not forsaken; cast down, but not destroyed;'),
(28866,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,10,'Always bearing about in the body the dying of the Lord Jesus, that the life also of Jesus might be made manifest in our body.'),
(28867,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,11,'For we which live are alway delivered unto death for Jesus\' sake, that the life also of Jesus might be made manifest in our mortal flesh.'),
(28868,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,12,'So then death worketh in us, but life in you.'),
(28869,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,13,'We having the same spirit of faith, according as it is written, I believed, and therefore have I spoken; we also believe, and therefore speak;'),
(28870,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,14,'Knowing that he which raised up the Lord Jesus shall raise up us also by Jesus, and shall present {us} with you.'),
(28871,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,15,'For all things {are} for your sakes, that the abundant grace might through the thanksgiving of many redound to the glory of God.'),
(28872,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,16,'For which cause we faint not; but though our outward man perish, yet the inward {man} is renewed day by day.'),
(28873,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,17,'For our light affliction, which is but for a moment, worketh for us a far more exceeding {and} eternal weight of glory;'),
(28874,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',4,18,'While we look not at the things which are seen, but at the things which are not seen: for the things which are seen {are} temporal; but the things which are not seen {are} eternal.'),
(28875,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',5,1,'For we know that if our earthly house of {this} tabernacle were dissolved, we have a building of God, an house not made with hands, eternal in the heavens.'),
(28876,47,'2 Corinthians','NT',5,2,'For in this we groan, earnestly desiring to be clothed upon with our house which is from heaven:'),
